(1064, '“Decentralized Systems: Leveraging Blockchain for Secure IoT Networks”', 'MR.SHAHZAIB ALI', '“Enhancing IoT Security and Data Integrity Through Blockchain Technology”', '1', 1, 'The rapid growth of the Internet of Things (IoT) has introduced significant challenges in device security, data integrity, and system scalability. Traditional centralized IoT architectures are prone to single points of failure, unauthorized access, and data tampering. This paper presents DecentraSense, a blockchain-enabled framework designed to enhance the security, scalability, and interoperability of IoT ecosystems. By leveraging blockchain’s decentralized ledger, smart contracts, and consensus mechanisms, DecentraSense ensures that IoT device registration, access control, and data transmission are both transparent and tamper-proof. The proposed system integrates real-time data collection from heterogeneous IoT devices with a secure, immutable blockchain backend, allowing authorized users to monitor and control devices dynamically. Experimental results demonstrate improved security, reduced reliance on centralized servers, and reliable device-to-device communication. DecentraSense provides a practical and scalable approach for deploying secure IoT solutions in various applications, including smart homes, industrial automation, and smart cities.', 1, 2025, 3, 18, 'Blockchain Technology'),
(1065, 'ddd', 'dd', 'dd', '2', 22, '222222', 1, 22, 2, 14, '22');
