INSERT INTO `people` (`people_id`, `url_name`, `user_id`, `designation_id`, `group_id`, `post_id`, `title`, `fname`, `lname`, `url`, `email`, `off_no`, `ext`, `cell_no`, `fax_no`, `image_name`, `seqno`, `biography`, `research_interest`, `status`, `is_core_team`) VALUES
(3, 'DrWaqarMahmood', 3, 11, 1, 73, 'Dr.', 'Waqar', 'Mahmood', '', 'director@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-99029450', '805', '', '', 'Dr_Waqar.jpg', 0, '<p>Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood received his Bachelor&rsquo;s degree from University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore in 1989, Masters and PhD from Georgia Tech USA in 1992 and 1996 respectively, all in Electrical Engineering. He has served in industry as well as academia in the North America and Pakistan. He served as Director Process Development in CIENA Corporation, Maryland; He was selected as voting member and US delegate to the IEC committee on optical interconnect standardization. He is currently serving as Sultan Qaboos IT Chair at UET, Lahore. In addition, he is the Director of Al-Khwarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) - a center of excellence for ICT research and development in UET, Lahore. He is also the Director of Center for Energy Research and Development (CERAD) at the same University. He has served as faculty member in National University of Science and Technology (NUST) prior to joining KICS. His research interests include optical communications, process technology development, discrete event systems, Networking systems, wireless systems, energy optimization, power systems and renewable energy. He has consistently won research funding in a number of IT and renewable energy technologies. He has published over 80 reviewed papers and has 12 US patents to his credit.</p>\r\n<p>Dr. Waqar Mahmood is an expert and holds leadership position in the research and development organizations in the areas of information technology and&nbsp; renewable energy. He has build vibrant R&amp;D organizations from ground up in these critical areas of technology. He is the founding member and director for the Center for Energy Research and Development (CERAD), which is a leading research center in Pakistan for renewable technologies development, energy systems evaluation, component testing and validation, training and certification. The center also provides services for energy auditing, demand management, and consultancy for energy conservation in buildings, factories and homes. Under his leadership the Center has established Solar PV testing and validation facility, the only in Pakistan. The Center has developed solar concentrated power solutions, low cost invertors for PV systems, bio-fuel solutions based on the biomass available in the region, low head hydro power generation solutions, micro wind turbines and many more. The solutions developed by the center are focused on solving energy problem of the country through low cost viable indigenous technologies.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Dr. Waqar has initiated training programs in energy at Bachelors, Masters, and vocational level. The training at vocational level is most popular, as it helps create workforce for upcoming energy projects in the country.&nbsp; Dr. Waqar advises the energy department Punjab on various technology choices. He is a frequent speaker on choices of energy technologies and related policy matters. He is author of more then eighty peer reviewed papers and holds twelve US patents.</p>', '<ol>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Modeling, Control and Optimization</li>\r\n<li>Discrete Event Systems</li>\r\n<li>Communication Systems</li>\r\n<li>Digital Signal Processing</li>\r\n<li>Integrating Technology and Business Planning</li>\r\n<li>Power Electronics</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div>\r\n<p>Patents:</p>\r\n<ol type=\"circle\">\r\n<li>Applied: Polishing Fixture Assembly for a Fiber Optic Cable Connector Polishing Apparatus.</li>\r\n<li>Method of simultaneously polishing a plurality of diverse fiber optic cable connectors.</li>\r\n<li>Method and System for Controlling Splice Attenuation.</li>\r\n<li>Polishing Pad Assembly for Fiber Optic Cable Connector Polishing Apparatus.</li>\r\n<li>System for Controlling a Process for Interconnection of Optical Fibers Including a Fuzzy Logic Control and Optimization Architecture.</li>\r\n<li>Attenuating Splice System and Method there for using Estimation Algorithm and Closed Loop Intelligent Control.</li>\r\n<li>Attenuation Splice System and Method Therefore.</li>\r\n<li>Apparatus for Comparing Tensile or Compressive Stresses Imposed on Different Parts of Optical Fiber.</li>\r\n<li>Apparatus for Integrating Steps of a Process for Interconnecting Optical Fiber.</li>\r\n<li>Apparatus and method for calibrating pressure existing between optical fibers and a polishing pad during a polishing process .</li>\r\n<li>Fiber Bragg Gratings Based Strain Measurement Apparatus, System and&nbsp;Method.</li>\r\n<li>Automated Apparatus for Counting Pilings in Textile Fabric.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;Honors and awards:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Chair IEEE Computer Society Lahore Section since 2012.</li>\r\n<li>Chaired ICOSST for last ten years 2006-2016.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Won nomination to HEC mentor group detailed for developing plans for establishment of 4 institutes of higher learning in Pakistan 2005.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Won nomination to the Standard&rsquo;s Council of Canada as Canadian Expert, a voting member and as Canadian delegate to the IEC SC86B committee, 2003.</li>\r\n<li>Won US Technical Advisory Group (TAG) membership and US Expert nomination for the IEC SC86B committee on standardization of optical interconnects and passive components, 2000.</li>\r\n<li>Won nomination by International Society of Optical Engineers as one of the top 100 global optical experts.</li>\r\n<li>Won nomination as Executive Officer for the Washington / Northern Virginia Chapter of the IEEE Laser and Electro-Optical Society (LEOS). 2002</li>\r\n<li>Nominated as Chair for session on Optical Components and Systems Process Technologies at the 6th World Multi-conference on Systematics, Cybernetics and Informatics, Florida USA, July 2002</li>\r\n<li>Hosted IEC technical forum on global telecommunications standardization in Annapolis, MD USA, 2000</li>\r\n<li>B.Sc. Engineering with Honors securing top 1% position at the University of Engineering and Technology, 1989.</li>\r\n<li>Won nomination for the &ldquo;Summer School in Science for Talented Students&rdquo; by the Lahore Board of Intermediate education 1981.</li>\r\n<li>Position holder and Merit Scholarship winner during F.Sc. and Matriculation examinations</li>\r\n<li>Gold Medal winner Matriculation Examination, Govt. High School Chauburji Gardens, Lahore, 1980.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong> PhD Thesis Supervised</strong></p>\r\n<table class=\"table\" width=\"99%\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"6%\">\r\n<p><strong>Sr.</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"24%\">\r\n<p><strong>Name of students</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"14%\">\r\n<p><strong>Discipline</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"35%\">\r\n<p><strong>Thesis Area</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"18%\">\r\n<p><strong>Status</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"6%\">\r\n<p>1. &nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"24%\">\r\n<p>Ghulam Mustafa</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"14%\">\r\n<p>PhD, CS</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"35%\">\r\n<p>Multi-core processor bench marking</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"18%\">\r\n<p>On going</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"6%\">\r\n<p>2. &nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"24%\">\r\n<p>AbidGhaffar</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"14%\">\r\n<p>PhD, CS</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"35%\">\r\n<p>Data mining and visualization</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"18%\">\r\n<p>On going</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"6%\">\r\n<p>3. &nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"24%\">\r\n<p>M.WaseemBhalli</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"14%\">\r\n<p>PhD, CS</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"35%\">\r\n<p>Behavioral model development through social media</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"18%\">\r\n<p>Ongoing</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"6%\">\r\n<p>4. &nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"24%\">\r\n<p>SajidIqbal</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"14%\">\r\n<p>PhD, CS</p>\r\n</