(11, 'Dr.ShafeyShumail', 11, 12, 1, 10, 'Dr.', 'Shafey', 'Shumail', '', '@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, '', '', 1, 0),
(12, 'Dr.MuhammadAkmalButt', 12, 130, 1, 11, 'Dr.', 'Muhammad', 'Akmal Butt', '', 'akmal<code>@</code>kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029350', '815', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'akmalbutt.jpg', 0, 'Dr. Muhammad Akmal Butt received his bachelor degree from University of Engineering and Technology in 1990. Master degree from University of Wisconsin, Madison, USA in 1993 and PhD degree from Georgia Institute of Technology, Atlanta, USA in 1998, respectively.', '<div align=\"justify\">Digital Singal / Image Processing<br />\r\n  and their application in telecommunication. <br />\r\n  <br />\r\n   <font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Achievements & Honors</font>\r\n   <ul type=\"circle\">\r\n     <li><strong>2006</strong>	Invited speaker in First International Conference on Graphics Multimedia and Imaging, GRAMI, Taxila, Pakistan. </li>\r\n     <li><strong>2005</strong>	Invited speaker in First International Conference on Information and Communication Technology, ICICT, Karachi, Pakistan. </li>\r\n     <li><strong>2003</strong>	Invited speaker in 2nd International Bhourban Conference on Applications of Science and Technology, IBCAST, Bhourban, Pakistan.</li>\r\n     <li><strong>1996</strong>	Active member of the organizing committee for the International Symposium on Mathematical Morphology, Atlanta, USA</li>\r\n     <li><strong>1992</strong>	Won the nation-wide competition for the award 4-year scholarship for higher studies in USA.</li>\r\n     <li><strong>1990</strong>	Finished B.Sc. Electrical Engineering securing 8th position in a batch of 150.</li>\r\n     <li><strong>1989</strong>	Project Advisor of the Electronics Society. Helped other students with design and implementation of electronics projects.</li>\r\n     <li><strong>1985</strong> Dean’s merit scholarship during four years of undergraduate studies.</li>\r\n   </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Academic Experience</font></p>\r\n<ul type=\"circle\"><li><p align=\"justify\"> 12/03  - 07/06   <strong>Associate Professor</strong><strong> </strong>¾ <em>FAST</em><em> National  University, Lahore, Pakistan</em><br />\r\n      Taught undergraduate and graduate level  courses in Digital Signal Processing, Digital Image Processing, Computer  Graphics, Control Systems, and Stochastic Processes. Developed undergraduate  teaching labs for Telecommunication Program. Served as coordinator of Ph.D.  program and head of Library committee.    </p>\r\n  </li>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <p align=\"justify\">3/01 - 9/03    <strong>Assistant Professor</strong> ¾ <em>Lahore  Univ. of Management Sciences, Lahore,   Pakistan</em> <br />\r\n                   Involved in planning of M.Sc.  Computer Engineering curriculum. Developed the Digital Signal Processing stream  of courses. Taught undergraduate and graduate courses in the fields of Digital  Signal Processing, Digital Image Processing, and Stochastic Processes.  Developed and supervised a Linux-based computing cluster for scientific  computing and research in operating systems, data acquisition, and parallel  processing. </p>\r\n  </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Research and Development  Experience</font></p>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n  <ul type=\"circle\">\r\n    <li>(Juluy 2006 -  Present) <strong>Research  Professor </strong>¾ <em>Al-Khawarizmi  Institute, UET, Lahore, Pakistan</em><br />\r\n      Leading a group of 8 researchers working  on industry-sponsored research projects related to implementation of telecommunications  algorithms on FPGA and DSP chips. Currently developing telemetry system based  on QAM-4 modulation and a low-end OFDM modem. Planning to develop WiMAX  compliant OFDMA modem.</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <ul type=\"circle\">\r\n    <li>(Sep.2003   - Dec2003) <strong>Consultant</strong> ¾ <em>Al-Khawarzmi  Institute, UET, Lahore, Pakistan</em><br />\r\n      Developed and implemented algorithms for  initial synchronization and subsequent timing recovery of QAM-4 and QAM-16  signals of a multichannel digital radio modem.</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <ul type=\"circle\">\r\n    <li>(Oct.1999 – Jan.2001) <strong>Senior Scientist</strong> ¾ <em>Communications  Enabling Technologies, Irvine,   CA, USA</em> <br />\r\n                     Developed new algorithms for  acoustic and line echo cancellation, IIR modeling of fading channels, efficient  and optimal design of polyphase and polynominal interpolators. Implemented a  linear programming based package for linear-phase FIR filter design with  arbitrarily complex amplitude  and phase  response. A new technique was developed to design a combined decimation and  timing-recovery filter using continuous domain modeling of the interpolators.</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <ul type=\"circle\">\r\n    <li>(Jun1998 – Oct.1999) <strong>Research  Engineer</strong> ¾ <em>Appalachian  Elect. Instruments, Ronceverte,   WV, USA</em> Developed an  intelligent high-speed inspection system for automatic detection and  classification of weaving defects in different fabrics. The hardware setup  included multiple line-scan cameras synchronized with textile transportation  system using optical shaft encoders. The defect detection algorithm was based  on fast wavelet transforms and the defect classification algorithm was based on     <em>Radon Transform.</em> The inspection  system was integrated with customer network for monitoring, planning, and  quality control of the weaving and finishing processes. Also developed an image  acquisition and false-color rendering system for infra-red images. The system  was used to detect and monitor the internal injuries of race horses.</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <ul type=\"circle\">\r\n    <li>(Feb.1997  – Apr.1998)<strong>Consultant</strong> ¾ <em>Micro  Enterprises, Norcross, GA, USA</em>Developed and implemented image analysis algorithms  for a multi-layer paint thickness measurement system for sheet metal finishing  process. The system consisted of a precision microscope attached with a colour  CCD camera and a frame grabber. The image analysis algorithm was based on image  segmentation, vector quantization, data clustering and other pattern  classification techniques.</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <ul type=\"circle\">\r\n    <li>  (Aug.1995 – March1998)<strong> Research Assistant</strong> ¾ <em>Georgia</em><em> Institute of Technology, Atlanta, GA, USA</em>Worked on research projects sponsored by Joint  Services Electronics Program (JSEP) and National Science Foundation (NSF). The  research involved modeling and analysis of image analysis operators using  mathematical morphology, differential geometry, and nonlinear partial  differential equations. This Ph.D. research resulted in development of accurate  and efficient algorithms for image analysis problems like distance transforms,  curvature flow, and image segmentation.</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Publications</font></p>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n  <ul type=\"square\">\r\n          <li><font size=\"2\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\"><strong>Books</strong></font>\r\n              <ul type=\"circle\">\r\n                <li>Petros Maragos, Ronald Schafer, and Muhammad Akmal Butt, “Mathematical Morphology and its applications to Image and Signal Processing”, Kluwer Academic Press, 1996.</li>\r\n              </ul>\r\n          </li>\r\n    <li><font size=\"2\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\"><strong>Journal Papers</strong></font>\r\n      \r\n              <ul type=\"circle\">\r\n                <li><strong>Muhammad Akmal Butt</strong> and Petros Maragos, “Optimum Design of Chamfer Distance Transforms”, IEEE Transactions on Image Processing, October 1998</li>\r\n                <li>Petros Maragos and <strong>Muhammad Akmal Butt</strong>, “Curve Evolution, Differential Morphology, and Distance Transforms Applied to Multiscale and Eikonal Problems”, Fundamens Informaticae, July 1998</li>\r\n              </ul>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li><font size=\"2\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\"><strong>Conference Papers</strong></font>\r\n          <ul type=\"circle\">\r\n              <li><strong>Muhammad Akmal Butt</strong> and Petros Maragos, “Comparison of Mutiscale Morphology Approaches: PDE Implemented via Curve Evolution versus Chamfer Distance Transform,” Proc. International Symposium on Mathematical Morphology, 1996</li>\r\n            <li>Petros Maragos and <strong>Muhammad Akmal Butt</strong>, “Partial differential equations in image analysis: Continuous modeling, discrete processing,” Proc. IEEE International Conference on Image Processing, 1996</li>\r\n            <li><strong>Muhammad Akmal Butt</strong>, and Petros Maragos, “Advances in Differential Morphology: Image Segmentation via Eikonal PDE & Curve Evolution and Reconstruction via Constrained Dilation Flow,” Proc. International Symposium on Mathematical Morphology, 1998</li>\r\n            <li>Petros Maragos, <strong>Muhammad Akmal Butt,</strong> and Lucio Pessoa, “Two Frontiers in Morphological Image Analysis: Differential Evolution Models and Hybrid Morphological/Linear Neural Networks,” Proc. SIBGRAPI, October 1998</li>\r\n            <li><strong>Muhammad Akmal Butt</strong>, Sherjil Ahmad, Amjad Luna, and Mohammad Usman, “Polynomial vs. Polyphase Interpolators: Analysis, Comparison, and Implementation”, Proc. ICSPAT, October 2000 </li>\r\n            <li>Amjad Luna, Sherjil Ahmad, <strong>Muhammad Akmal Butt</strong>, and Mohammad Usman, “The Design and Implementation of a Multiple Data-rate BPSK/QPSK Coherent Burst Satellite Modem”, Proc. ICSPAT, October 2000</li>\r\n            <li><strong>Muhammad Akmal Butt </strong>and Umair bin Saeed, “A Robust Shading Scheme using Continuous-domain Modeling of Specular Reflection”, Proc. International Multi-topic Conference, December 2004</li>\r\n            <li>Atif Hashmi and <strong>Muhammad Akmal Butt</strong>,“Multi-channel Data Acquisition for Real-Time Signal Processing Algorithms”, Proc. International Multi-topic Conference, December 2004</li>\r\n          </ul>\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <br />\r\n  \r\n</div>\r\n', 1, 0),
(13, 'DrAbdulWaheed', 13, 13, 7, 13, 'Dr.', 'Abdul', 'Waheed', '', 'awaheed@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, '<p>Dr. Abdul Waheed received his bachelor degree from University of Engineering and Technology in 1991, Master degree from Michigan State University, East Lansing, MI in 1993 and PhD degree from Michigan State University, East Lansing, MI in 1997, respectively.</p>', '', 1, 4),
(14, 'ZubairAKhan', 14, 13, 1, 13, 'Dr.', 'Zubair', 'A Khan', '', 'zubair.khan', '+92-42-99029300, 99029450', '823', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'DrZubair.jpg', 0, '<p>Dr. Zubair Ahmad Khan received his bachelor\'s degree from University of Engineering and Technology, UET, Lahore in 1975. Master and PhD degrees from UMIST, Manchester, England in 1987 and 1990, respectively.</p>', '<p align=\"justify\">Research related to Microprocessor/ microcontroller/DSP processors and FPGA/CPLD based system development and designing. Research areas for above activities are instrumentation, protection, control, telecommunication and wireless systems and other areas of Electrical Engineering.<br /> <span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: \'Times New Roman\', Times, serif; font-size: large;\">Publications</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>Fahad A Khan, Aurangzeb and <strong>Zubair A Khan </strong> \" DNA Sequence matching system based on hardware accelerators utilized efficiently in a multi-threaded environment ICEE 2008 10-11 April, 2009</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>Saad A. Khan, Fahad A. Khan, Arslan Shahid,<strong>Zubair A.Khan,</strong> \"Reconfigurable Cluster Tree Topology for a Zigbee Home Area Network, IEEE SENSORCOMM 2009, 3rd IEEE Computer Society Conference on Sensor Technologies &amp; Applications, Athens Greece, June 18-23, 2009.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>Saad A. Khan, Fahad A. Khan, Arslan Shahid, <strong>Zubair A Khan</strong>, \"Load Balanced Clustering Algorithm For Energy Efficient Home Area Networking, Sensors Application Symposium, Proceeding of IEEE SAS 2009, 4th IEEE Instrumentation &amp; Measurement Society Sensor Application Symposium, New Orleans, LA, February 17-19, 2009</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>Ali Faisal Murtaza, <strong>Z A khan</strong>, \" Starvation Free Controller Area Network using Master Node ICEE 2008 25-26 March 2008 <strong>IEEE Catalog Number:</strong> CFP0896B-DR<strong> ISBN:</strong> 978-1-4244-2293-7<strong> Library of Congress:</strong> 2008902131 Paper ID : CN-11<strong> </strong>15- K.Anwar, Z A Khan \"On Simulating Dynamic prioritiesin Controller Area Network January, IBCAST 2009</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>K.Anwar, <strong>Z A Khan</strong> \"On Simulating Dynamic prioritiesin Controller Area Network January, IBCAST 2009</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>Ali Faisal Murtaza, <strong>Z A khan</strong>, \" Starvation Free Controller Area Network using Master Node ICEE 2008 25-26 March 2008 <strong>IEEE Catalog Number:</strong> CFP0896B-CDR<strong> ISBN:</strong>978-1-4244-2293-7<strong> Library of Congress:</strong> 2008902131 Paper ID : CN-11</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>Ehsan Ullah, <strong>Zubair A. Khan</strong>, Shahid Awan, Abdurehman \" Platform Independent Implementation of Java Telephony API (JTAPI) for data calls ICOST 2007 17-18 December 2007. IEEE Catalog Number : 13451 <strong></strong>Paper ID: <a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\">07-118</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>M. Akbar, <strong>Z. A. Khan</strong> \"Modified Nonintrusive Appliance Load Monitoring For Nonlinear Devices INMIC 2007, 28-30 December 2007 ISBN : 1-4244-1553-5 (Conference CD-ROM Version) ISBN : 1-4244-1552-7 (Conference Print Version)</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>Taha Sajjad, <strong>Dr. Zubair Ahmed Khan</strong> \"Comparison of speech response of normal hearing listener and cochlear implanted patient using model for chaotic system. INMIC 2007, 28-30 December 2007. ISBN : 1-4244-1553-5 (Conference CD-ROM Version) ISBN : 1-4244-1552-7 (Conference Print Version)</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>K.Anwar, <strong>Z.A.Khan</strong> \" Dynamic Priority Based Message on Controller Area Network.ICEE 2007, 11-12 APRIL 2007. IEEE Catalog Number 07EX1653C ISBN: 1-4244-0893-8 Paper ID : 104 Library of Congress : 2006939760</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>M. A. Jamil, <strong>Dr. Zubair Ahmed Khan</strong> \"Design and Development of Communication Adapterfor Legacy Substation Devices ICEE 2007, 11-12 APRIL 2007. IEEE Catalog Number 07EX1653C ISBN: 1-4244-0893-8 Paper ID : 206 Library of Congress : 2006939760</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>Experimental observation of Series Resonance Using ABBC Microcomputer <strong>Khan Z.A.</strong> M.Sc thesis UMIST Manchester , England January ,1987.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>\" Microprocessor Based Protection Scheme of a Grid Station (Jaranwala). (M.Sc. Thesis ) <strong>Khan Z.A</strong>, M.Sc thesis UET , Lahore September 1985.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p><strong>Khan Z.A</strong> \" Calibration and Zero Adjustment Procedure for Harmonic Measurement in a power Meter \".Publication Journal of IEEEP 1997.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p><strong>Khan Z.A</strong>, Shami T.A \" Cost Reduction Factors of the Cheaper Multifunction kWh Meter \".. Journal of the IEEP Volume XXXIV pages 21-26 1997 January December 1996.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p><strong>Khan Z.A</strong> \" Microprocessor based Techniques To Measure Accurate Harmonic level in Energy Mater \".. Journal of the IEEEP , Volume XXXIV pages 27-29 Journal December 1996.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>\". <strong>Khan Z.A</strong> \" An Economical Microprocessor Based Design for Energy Recording Multimeasuring and Tariff Matering. Journal of the IEEP Volume XXI pages 4-9 April December 1992.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p><strong>Khan Z.A</strong> \" Increasing Accuracy of Frequency Measurement in a Microprocessor Based Multimeasuring System. . Journal of the IEEP Volume XXIII pages 4-8 January March, 1993.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<p>D.Lidgate., <strong>Khan Z.A.</strong> \"A low cost microprocessor based multi-function energy matter \".27th UPEC (Universities Power Engineering Conference ) Bath , U.K Volume 2 Pages 325-328 September , 1992.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: \'Times New Roman\', Times, serif; font-size: large;\">Rsearch Grants as Principal Investigator</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: \'Times New Roman\', Times, serif; font-size: small;\"> (other than the research grant given by the parent University) :</span></p>\r\n<p>Won various grants from local industry and USAID for the following .research projects. Detail of these is given below</p>\r\n<p><strong>Projects completed for Private Sector:</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Won US Aid Grant to work on the following Projetcs.( 1994-95)</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Stabilized Regulated Power Supply</li>\r\n<li>Variable Speed AC Motor Controller</li>\r\n<li>Energy and Mutimetering System</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>Won grants from local industry to carry out work on the following projects.</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>1- Project Title: Invoice Processing Automation System (I.P.A.S) Customization</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Client</strong>: Sapphire Electric Company Limited (Independent Power Producer)</p>\r\n<p><strong>URL:</strong> <a href=\"http://www.sapphire.com.pk/home.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sapphire.com.pk/home.htm</a></p>\r\n<p><strong>Duration:</strong> Sep 2010 to Present</p>\r\n<p><strong>Platform</strong>: Windows XP/2003 Enterprise Server</p>\r\n<p><strong>Description:</strong></p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\">KICS has developed the Software IPAS which is a network and web based application that covers the commercial and technical aspects as contained in the Power Purchase Agreement (\"PPA) 2002 entered in to between Company and National Transmission &amp; Dispatch Company. The Sapphire Electric Company Limited intended for the Customization of IPAS as per its local requirements that facilitates the company in its future operations after the commercial operations date. The project scope covers the collection of the meter readings, weather station information, complex events information, etc. from the SECL power plant, located at Sheikupura Muridke Road, Lahore. This project also covers the scope of the integration of the IPAS software with the International Standards based system Oracle Financial &amp; Company Pie Server in accordance with the customized requirements of the Client. Followed by the Implementation, support, training and maintenance of the customized IPAS for Orient Power containing all the modules and any additional modules of the application.</p>\r\n<p><strong>2- Project Title: Invoice Processing Automation System (I.P.A.S) Customization</strong><br /> <strong>Client</strong>: Orient Power Ltd. (Independent Power Producer)<br /> <strong>URL:</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.orientpower.com.pk/\">http://www.orientpower.com.pk/</a><br /> <strong>Duration:</strong> Aug 2009 to Present<br /> <strong>Platform</strong>: Windows XP/2003 Enterprise Server</p>\r\n<p><strong>Description:</strong></p>\r\n<p>KICS has developed the Software IPAS which is a network and web based application that covers the commercial and technical aspects as contained in the Power Purchase Agreement (\"PPA) 2002 entered in to between Company and National Transmission &amp; Dispatch Company. The Orient Power Company intended for the Customization of IPAS as per its local requirements that facilitates the company in its future operations after the commercial operations date. Followed by the Implementation, support, training and maintenance of the customized IPAS for Orient Power containing all the modules and any additional modules of the application.</p>\r\n<p><strong>3- Project Title: Load Forecasting System for Pakistan WAPDA<br /> </strong><strong>Funding</strong>: ICT R&amp;D FUND</p>\r\n<p><strong>Description:</strong></p>\r\n<p>Electric Energy Load Forecasting research for Pakistan WAPDA is being carried out at AL-KICS, UET Lahore, to develop a load forecasting system for WAPDA. Recent years have increased the demand for such a system that can predict future energy loads, which is a very important component for energy management. We are interested in developing a self learning, adaptive, transparent, intelligent decision making system that can forecast short term, medium term and long term energy requirement,</p>\r\n<p>Load forecasting has always been important for economics of electrical supply companies in terms of cost saving, planning and operational decision making. The power industry requires forecasts not only from the production side but also from a financial perspective. It is necessary to predict hourly loads as well as daily peak loads. Accurate tracking of the load at all times is a basic requirement in the operation of power systems and must be accomplished for various time intervals. Since electricity cannot be stored efficiently in large quantities, the amount generated at any given time must cover all of the demand from consumers as well as line losses. Forecasts of the load are used to decide whether extra generation must be provided by increasing the output of online generators, by committing one or more extra units, or by the interchange of power with neighboring systems. Similarly, forecasts are used to decide whether the output of an already running generation unit should be decreased or switched off, which is determined by generation control functions, such as scheduling, unit-commitment, coordination, and interchange evaluation.</p>\r\n<p><strong>4- Project Title: Invoice Processing Automation System (EMIS) </strong><br /> <strong>Client</strong>: CPPA, NTDC WAPDA Pakistan. <br /> <strong>URL:</strong> <a href=\"http://www.ntdc.com.pk/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.ntdc.com.pk</a> <br /> <strong>Duration:</strong> Jan 2006 to Present<br /> <strong>Platform</strong>: Windows 2000 Advanced Server/XP/2003 Enterprise Server</p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><strong>Description:</strong><br /> The IPAS is an Enterprise Management Information System being design and architecture for the CPPA, NTDC, WAPDA Pakistan. Under the Policy for Power Generation Projects, 2002 announced by the Government of Pakistan, NTDC has developed a new Standard Power Purchase Agreement (PPA) for the upcoming power projects. This new regime for projects came to surface which now revolves around the Availability Based, Data Processing and Invoicing System. In order to support this new regime of PPA, there is a demand identified for Data Processing and Invoice Processing Automation System (IPAS), which is an Enterprise Management Information System (EMIS). The objective is to implement the Rules and Regulations specified in the Standard Power Purchase Agreement (PPA) by NTDC, WAPDA Pakistan and Tariff Determination by NEPRA. The system will fetch data in real time from IPPs and process<br /> it in a central location.</p>\r\n<p>The system has been designed and developed recently and now it is in implementation phase in WAPDA.</p>\r\n<p><strong>5- Project: KTAPI The</strong> <strong>Data Collection System from Power Generators and Weather Stations. </strong><br /> <strong>Client</strong>: CPPA, NTDC WAPDA Pakistan. <br /> <strong>URL:</strong> <a href=\"http://www.ntdc.com.pk/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.ntdc.com.pk</a> <br /> <strong>Duration:</strong> Jan 2006 to Present<br /> <strong>Platform</strong>: Windows 2000 Advanced Server/XP/2003 Enterprise Server</p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><strong>Abstract:</strong> <br /> <br /> This project has been developed to be an autonomous, adaptive and standalone part of Pakistan WAPDA&rsquo;s energy metering and management system (EMIS). This software application collects data from meters installed on power stations and weather stations. Based on this timely reading. It support and can communicate with meters on all available communication channels (PSTN, GSM, GPRS, and IP Networks). <br /> This data collection system queries each modem installed on all IPP&rsquo;s and collects data from each meter connected to same modem and transfers recorded reading to EMIS central database. Other supporting features are installation of modems, remote configurations of modems/meters, dynamic selection of communication medium, error recovery and fault tolerance.</p>\r\n<p><strong>6- Project Title: Automated Meter Reading (MIS)</strong><br /> <strong> Client</strong>: Syed Bhais, Pakistan. <br /> <strong> URL:</strong> <a href=\"http://www.syedbhais.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.syedbhais.com</a> <br /> <strong> Duration:</strong> Apr 2005 to Dec 2006<br /> <strong> Platform</strong>: Windows 2000 Advanced Server/XP/2003 Enterprise Server</p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><strong>Description:</strong><br /> WAPDA intends to arrange for a remote system capable of measuring electricity consumption/customer usage, besides generating all other information and data needed to run its specific MIS, without those glitches inherent to the existing normal system. The system also plans to control the administrative losses i.e. pilferage, theft and stealing of energy, constricted recording due to improper installation of energy meters, by-passing of the same and other such internal and external features. The &lsquo;AMR-API&rsquo; provides an application layer to communicate with meters using GSM unit \"Telit GM862-GPRS through micro controller ATMEL 89C52 Series. Using API, MIS can access meter parameters. The connectivity is provided using SMS. MIS can send short message request to meters individually and in response to the request meters reply with short message which is decoded by the API and required parameters are returned to the MIS. The JSF/J2EE based MIS includes implementation of the Existing Commercial Procedures for WAPDA. Also User Management, Equipment Management and Management of Tariff Categories are the integral parts of MIS.</p>\r\n<p><strong>7- Project Title: EMV-3-Phase Electronic Vector Meter </strong><br /> <strong> Software.</strong><br /> <strong>Client</strong>: Syed Bhais, Pakistan. <br /> <strong> URL:</strong> <a href=\"http://www.syedbhais.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.syedbhais.com</a> <br /> <strong> Duration:</strong> Jul 2005 to Sep 2005<br /> <strong> Platform</strong>: Windows XP</p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><strong>Description:</strong><br /> Configuration software for 3-Phase electronic vector meter, facilitate users with creating and applying new settings and configurations for 3-Phase vector meters. The major features provided with this software are administrating users, setting time of use of meter, setting demand metering and notifications to the meter and programming meter with these settings.</p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><strong>8- Project Title: Vehicle Tracking and Fleet Management </strong><br /> <strong> System. (UTrack)</strong><br /> <strong>Client</strong>: Utrack <br /> <strong> Duration:</strong> Dec 2007<br /> <strong> Platform</strong>: Windows XP<br /> <strong> </strong><strong></strong><br /> <strong>Description:</strong><br /> Vehicle Tracking Systems using electronic devices installed in vehicles enables vehicle owners or third parties to track the location, status of a vehicle and allow them to control the vehicle remotely using GSM or/and GPRS. It uses GPS modules to allow for easy and accurate location of the vehicle. It also combines a communications component such as cellular or satellite transmitters to communicate the vehicle&rsquo;s location to a remote user. Vehicle information can be viewed on electronic maps via the Internet by this specialized software.</p>\r\n<p><strong>9- Real Time Data proceesing System of CDPs (Common </strong><br /> <strong> Delivery Points) for WAPDA</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Client</strong>: CPPA, NTDC WAPDA Pakistan. <br /> <strong>URL:</strong> <a href=\"http://www.ntdc.com.pk\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.ntdc.com.pk</a> <br /> <strong>Duration:</strong> Year 2008<br /> <strong>Platform</strong>: Windows 2000 Advanced Server/XP/2003 <br /> Enterprise Server<br /> (Work is in progress)</p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\">The basic objective of this system is monitor energy consumption, power load at common delivery points. This will help for the management of load and keep an eye on DISCOs.</p>', 0, 2);
INSERT INTO `people` (`people_id`, `url_name`, `user_id`, `designation_id`, `group_id`, `post_id`, `title`, `fname`, `lname`, `url`, `email`, `off_no`, `ext`, `cell_no`, `fax_no`, `image_name`, `seqno`, `biography`, `research_interest`, `status`, `is_core_team`) VALUES
(16, 'Mr.MuzammilBaig', 16, 17, 1, 55, 'Mr.', 'Muzammil', 'Baig', 'http://member.acm.org/~muzammilbaig', 'muzammil@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029450', '826', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'muzamil.jpg', 0, 'Mr. Muzammil Baig received his ‘Master in Computer Science’ degree from University of Central Punjab in 2003 and MSCS from University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore in 2007 respectively.<br />\r\nMuzammil Baig is a well-known researcher at Al-Khawarzmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS), UET Lahore. During his ongoing experience at KICS he has successfully completed many research projects like FALCON-A Processor, Digital Rights Management/ Digital Content Protection (DCP/DRM), Non-Signature base Anti-Key Logging and Digital Rights Management (DRM) Implementation in P2P Networks. He is the only fellow at KICS who have five publications after his joining, four of them are International. He also has the honor to get the Higher Education Commission (HEC) scholarship three times to attend International conferences in Greece, Italy and Australia. He is also the professional member of IEEE, IEEE Computer Society and ACM.<br />', '<p>Digital Rights Management (DRM)<br /> Information Security and Privacy<br /> Digital Steganography and Digital Watermarking<br /> Digital Copyright Protection</P>\r\n<font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Achievements & Honors</font>\r\n<uL><li>Got 6th NCR National IT Excellence Award and Gold Medal, in the category of IT Media & Publication for the year 2003-2004.  Youngest winner in any professional category in the history of NCR awards.  (http://teradataitawards.com/winners2004.asp).  NCR awards are the most recognized awards on national level in Pakistan. </li>  \r\n<li>Worked as active member of organizing committee for the First International Conference on Open Source Technologies (ICOST 06), held from 28-29 December 2006 in University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore. (http://uet.edu.pk/icost2006)</li>\r\n<li>Worked as active member of organizing committee for the Second International Conference on Open Source Systems and Technologies (ICOSST 2007), held from 17-18 December 2007 in University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore. (http://uet.edu.pk/icosst2007)</li>\r\n<li>	Honor to get Higher Education Commission (HEC) scholarship three times to attend and present research papers in International conferences in Greece (2004), Italy (2004) and Australia (2007).  HEC awards these scholarships only to top researchers.  The only researcher at Al-Khawarzmi awarded this scholarship three times.</li>\r\n<li>	Received Appreciation Letter from Intellectual Property Organization (IPO) of Pakistan, in recognition of R&D activities done in Pakistan, in the discipline of Digital Rights Management (DRM). </li>\r\n<li>	Got Higher Education Commission (HEC) Indigenous scholarship for MS Leading to Phd Program in 2004.  Top researchers are selected for this scholarship each year after national level test. </li>\r\n<li>	Got “Honorable Mention Award” in 4th All Pakistan Software Competition held from 23-25 September 2004 at Ghulam Ishaq Khan Institute of Engineering and Technology, Topi Pakistan.</li>\r\n<li>	Got 3rd prize in 1st in-house software competition held from 13-14 December, 2002 at Punjab College of Information Technology, Lahore, Pakistan.\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n <br />\r\n<font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Publications</font>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<strong>Muzammil M. Baig</strong>, Waqar Mehmood, “Robust Technique of Anti-Key Logging   \r\n       using Key-Logging Mechanism”, IEEE International conference on Digital Eco-\r\n      Systems and Technologies (DEST 2007), February 2007, Cairns Australia. Pages \r\n      314–318. ISBN:1-4244-0470-3.</li>\r\n<li>	M. Aslam, Naveed Idrees, <Strong>Muzammil Baig</Strong>, Asif Arshad, “Anti-Hook Shield against Software Key-loggers” National Conference on Emerging Technologies, December, 2004, SZABIST Karachi. Pages 189–191.</li>\r\n<li>   <strong>Muzammil Baig</strong>, Muhammad Razeen,  Anjum Ali, Noor M. Sheikh, “Pooling Implementation in Steganography – Providing BMP Protection Solution” WSEAS Transactions on Information Science And Applications, Issue 6, Volume 1,  December 2004. ISSN:1790-0832. Pages 1518–1523.</li>\r\n<li>    Muhammad Razeen, <strong>Muzammil Baig</strong>, Anjum Ali, Noor M. Sheikh, “A Robust Technique for Intellectual Property Protection of Digital Media through Steganography” IASTED International conference on Signal and Image Processing (SIM 2004). August 2004, Hawaii, USA. Pages 36–41. ISBN: 0-88986-434-9</li>\r\n<li>   Anjum Ali, <strong>Muzammil Baig</strong>, Amna Nasir, “Software Learning Tools for FALCON-A” IASTED International Conference on Applied Simulation and Modeling (ASM 2004), June 2004, Rhodes, Greece. Pages 498–503. ISBN: 0-88986-397-0 </li></ul>\r\n\r\n  <font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Patents</font>\r\n</p>\r\n<ol><li>Secure System Input Mechanism Parallel with Keyboard, submitted to Patent Office, application # 868/2007, Intellectual Property Organization of Pakistan.</li>\r\n<li>Digital Rights Management (DRM) Architecture for Audio/Video in Computers, Electronics and Portable Devices. Submitted to Patent Office, application # 869/2007, Intellectual Property Organization of Pakistan.</li> \r\n<li>First Architecture in Learning Computer Organization and Networks (FALCON-A).  Submitted to Copyright Office, Intellectual Property Organization of Pakistan</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n', 1, 9),
(17, 'Mr.EhsanUllah', 17, 17, 1, 55, 'Mr.', 'Ehsan', 'Ullah', '', 'ehsan.ullah@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '823', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, '', '', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO `people` (`people_id`, `url_name`, `user_id`, `designation_id`, `group_id`, `post_id`, `title`, `fname`, `lname`, `url`, `email`, `off_no`, `ext`, `cell_no`, `fax_no`, `image_name`, `seqno`, `biography`, `research_interest`, `status`, `is_core_team`) VALUES
(18, 'JamshaidIqbalJanjua', 18, 143, 2, 148, 'Dr.', 'Jamshaid', 'Iqbal Janjua', '', 'jamshaid.janjua', '+92-42-99029300, 99029450', '826', '+92-42-36843748', '+92-42-99250246', 'JamshaidIqbal Janjua162jpg', 1, '<p><strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong> established his &lsquo;MSCS&rsquo; degree from PICS, Faculty of Information Technology, University of Central Punjab, Lahore in 2009. Previously he received the &lsquo;Master in Computer Science&rsquo; degree from Institute of Management Sciences (Pak-Aims) in 2002. He also holds a &lsquo;MBA in Human Resource Management&rsquo; degree from Institute of Management Sciences (Pak-Aims) in 2007. He has Ph.D. in Computer Science specilizing in Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science. He is working as Principal Manager Technical Research at KICS.</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li>Enterprise Management Information Systems</li>\r\n<li>Machine Learning &amp; Data Science</li>\r\n<li>Blockchain Technology Research Frontiers</li>\r\n<li>Cross Disciplinary Research Avenues in Machine Learning</li>\r\n<li>Business Intelligence over Internet of Things (IoT)</li>\r\n<li>E-Infrastructure Development</li>\r\n<li>Software Design &amp; Architecture</li>\r\n<li>Energy Management Systems</li>\r\n<li>Software Technology Innovation Parks&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Surveillance Science &amp; Related research areas</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: \'Times New Roman\', Times, serif; font-size: large;\">Publications</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\"><strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, Ch. Faisal Nazir, \"Predicting Energy Consumption in Smart Homes Using Time-Series Analysis of Environmental Factors and Appliance Usage,\" 2025 IEEE International Conference on Data-Driven Social Change (ICDDSC-2025), ISBN 979-8-3315-1105-0, February&nbsp;18-19, 2025, Tando Jam, <strong>Pakistan</strong>.</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\"><strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, Muhammad Kaleem, Muhammad Azhar Mushtaq, Sadaqat Ali Ramay, Anaum Ihsan, Sayyid Kamran Hussain, \"Comparative Study of RSA and ECC Algorithm,\" 2025 IEEE International Conference on Data-Driven Social Change (ICDDSC-2025), ISBN 979-8-3315-1105-0, February&nbsp;18-19, 2025, Tando Jam, <strong>Pakistan</strong>.</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Anaum Ihsan, <strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, Tahir Abbas, \"Molecular Property Prediction through Machine Learning and Chemical Feature Analysis,\" 2025 IEEE International Conference on Data-Driven Social Change (ICDDSC-2025), ISBN 979-8-3315-1105-0, February&nbsp;18-19, 2025, Tando Jam, <strong>Pakistan</strong>.</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Amna Anwar, <strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, Anaum Ihsan, Tahir Abbas, \"Exploratory Data Analysis of Energy Deficit from Consumption and Generation Patterns,\" 2025 IEEE International Conference on Data-Driven Social Change (ICDDSC-2025), ISBN 979-8-3315-1105-0, February&nbsp;18-19, 2025, Tando Jam, <strong>Pakistan</strong>.</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Rathore, S. A., Salam, M. H. u, Sayyed, A., Nasrullah, <strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, &amp; Abbas, T., \"Applications of Neural Networks and Machine Learning Techniques in Medicine and Urology\", Published: 18 February&nbsp;2025, HEC Y-Category Journal, ISSN:2959-0809, Journal Volume 5(1), The Asian Bulletin of Big Data Management (ABBDM), Islamabad, <strong>Pakistan</strong>.</span></span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Shujaat Ali Rathore, Muhammad Hammad u Salam, Ali Sayyed, Dr. Nasrullah, <strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, &amp; Tahir Abbas, \"Enhancing Reaction Yield Predictions with Machine Learning Models for Organic Synthesis\", Published: 13 February&nbsp;2025, HEC Y-Category Journal, ISSN:3007-3138, Journal Volume 3(2), Spectrum of Engineering Sciences (SES), <strong>Pakistan</strong>.</span></span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\">Shujaat Ali Rathore, Muhammad Hammad u Salam, Qamar Muhay-ud-din, <strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, Sidra Zulfiqar, Tahir Abbas, \"Reducing Urban Pollution and Health Risks with Big Data for Predictive Environmental Monitoring Learning\", Published: 9 Feburary 2025, HEC Y-Category Journal, ISSN:3006-709X, Journal Volume 3(1), Competitive Research Journal Archive (CRJA), <strong>Pakistan</strong>.</span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\">Muhammad Hammad u Salam, Shujaat Ali Rathore, Fateh Hayat Maken, Qamar Muhay-ud-din, <strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, Muhammad Irfan, \"Harnessing Big Data and IoT for Enhanced Resource Optimization in Sustainable Construction within Smart Cities\", Published: 9 Feburary 2025, HEC Y-Category Journal, ISSN:3006-2640, Journal Volume 2(1), The Journal of Research Review (JRR), <strong>Pakistan</strong>.</span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\">Rubia, Aasif Shah,&nbsp;<strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, \"Transformative AI in Health Information Exchange for Predictive Analytics Enhancing Patient Outcomes,\" 2024 IEEE 6th International Conference on Computer and Applications (ICCA), ISBN 979-8-3503-XXXX-6, December 17-18, 2024, Cairo,&nbsp;<strong>Egypt</strong>.</span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Asif Ahamed, Nisher Ahmed, </span><strong style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">, Zakir Hossain, Ekramul Hasan, Tahir Abbas, \"Advances and Evaluation of Intelligent Techniques in Short-Term Load Forecasting,\" 2024 IEEE 6th International Conference on Computer and Applications (ICCA), ISBN 979-8-3503-XXXX-6, December 17-18, 2024, Cairo, </span><strong style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Egypt</strong><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">.</span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\">Abdulrahman Alqarafi, Hina Batool, Tahir Abbas, <strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, Sadaqat Ali Ramay, Munir Ahmed, \"Estimating Uncertainty in Deep Learning Methods and Applications,\" 2024 IEEE 6th International Conference on Computer and Applications (ICCA), ISBN 979-8-3503-XXXX-6, December 17-18, 2024, Cairo, <strong>Egypt</strong>.</span></span></li>\r\n<li><strong style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">, M. Irfan, T. Abbas, A. Ihsan and B. Ali, \"Enhancing Contextual Understanding in Chatbots and NLP,\" 2024 IEEE 4th International Conference on TVET Excellence &amp; Development (ICTeD), ISBN 979-8-3503-6910-6, December 16-17, 2024, Melaka, </span><strong style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Malaysia</strong><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">.</span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\">Taher M. Ghazal, <strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, Walid Abushiba, Muhammad Salah-ud-Din Iqbal, Waqas Iqbal, Munir Ahmad, Muhammad Saleem, \"Deep Learning and CNN-Based Approach for Efficient Detection of Potato Leaf Diseases,\" 2024 7th IEEE Asia-Pacific Conference on Geoscience, Electronics and Remote Sensing Technology (AGERS), ISBN 979-8-3503-XXXX-6, December 13-14, 2024, Manado, <strong>Indonesia</strong>.</span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, S. Kousar, A. Khan, A. Ihsan, T. Abbas and A. Q. Saeed, \"Enhancing Scalability in Reinforcement Learning for Open Spaces,\" 2024 IEEE 6th International Conference on Decision Aid Sciences and Applications (DASA), ISBN 979-8-3503-6910-6, December 11-12, 2024, Manama,&nbsp;<strong>Bahrain</strong>.</span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">A. Rehman, F. Noor, </span><strong style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">, A. Ihsan, A. Q. Saeed and T. Abbas, \"Classification of Lung Diseases Using Machine Learning Technique,\" 2024 IEEE 6th International Conference on Decision Aid Sciences and Applications (DASA), ISBN 979-8-3503-6910-6, December 11-12, 2024, Manama, </span><strong style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Bahrain</strong><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">.</span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\">B. Y. Almansour, A. Y. Almansour, <strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, M. Zahid and T. Abbas, \"Application of Machine Learning and Rule Induction in Various Sectors,\" 2024 IEEE 6th International Conference on Decision Aid Sciences and Applications (DASA), ISBN 979-8-3503-6910-6, December 11-12, 2024, Manama, <strong>Bahrain</strong>.</span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\">A. M. A. Al-Tarawneh, R. A. AlOmoush, T. ul Islam, <strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, T. Abbas and A. Ihsan, \"Current Trends in Artificial Intelligence for Educational Advancements,\" 2024 IEEE 6th International Conference on Decision Aid Sciences and Applications (DASA), ISBN 979-8-3503-6910-6, December 11-12, 2024, Manama, <strong>Bahrain</strong>.</span></span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Taher M. Ghazal, </span><strong style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">, Walid Abushiba, Munir Ahmad, Tahir Abbas, Karamath Ateeq, \"Cutting-Edge Predictive Methods for Enhancing Short-Term Load Prediction,\" 2024 6th IEEE International Conference on Electrical and Computer Engineering Researches (ICECER 2024), ISBN 979-8-4503-XXXX-9, December 4-6, 2024, Gaborone, </span><strong style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">Botswana</strong><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;\">.</span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7.5pt;\">Taher M. Ghazal, <strong>Jamshaid Iqbal Janjua</strong>, Walid Abushiba, Munir Ahmad, Anuam Ihsan, Nidal A. Al-Dmour, \"Cybersecurity Revolution via Large Language Models and Explainable AI,\" 2024 17th IEEE International Conference on Security of Info