(38, 'Mr.ShoukatAli', 38, 15, 1, 69, 'Mr.', 'Shoukat', 'Ali', '', '@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '812', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'Shaukat_Ali.jpg', 0, '', '', 1, 0),
(39, 'Mr.MuhammadHasanJamal', 39, 17, 7, 55, 'Mr.', 'Muhammad', 'Hasan Jamal', '', 'hasan.jamal@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '823', '+92-321-4121491', '+92-42-9250246', 'Hussan_Jammal.jpg', 0, '  <p>Mohammad  Hasan Jamal received his Bachelors degree with honors in Computer and  Information Engineering from International Islamic University Malaysia, Kuala    Lumpur, Malaysia  in 2005. He received his Masters degree from Electrical  Engineering Department, University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore, Pakistan,  specializing in Computer Engineering in December 2008. Mohammad Hasan Jamal has been working at  Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) in University  of Engineering and technology, Lahore, as a Research  Associate since June 2006.<br />\r\nCurrently  he is attached with High Performance Computing and Networking Lab. He is  actively involved in setup of a High Performance Computing and Networking Lab,  equipped with high end multi-core servers and a cluster of around 200 PCs  connected through 1 Gbps Networks.<br />\r\nHe is currently leading the ICT R&D funded project titled  “Characterization, Evaluation, and Development of High Performance Network  Services on Multi-Core Architectures”. His tasks include </p>\r\n  <ul>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Development  of micro benchmark kernels in ANSI C on UNIX based systems, specifically  focusing on Multi-core architectures. </li>\r\n    <li>Performance  Characterization, Evaluation and Benchmarking of Multi-core processor based  systems.</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <p>. <br />', ' <ul>\r\n      <li>Performance  evaluation and benchmarking of Multi-core processor based systems</li>\r\n      <li>Development  of performance measuring and profiling tools</li>\r\n      <li>High  performance computing and networking systems</li>\r\n      <li>Parallel  and distributed systems, grid and cluster computing</li>\r\n    </ul>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Publications</font></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n  <li><strong>M.   H. Jama</strong>l, G. Mustafa, W. Mahmood, and A. Waheed, &ldquo;An Extensible Infrastructure   for Benchmarking Multi-Core Processor based Systems,&rdquo; Accepted to   appear&nbsp;in SPECTS\'09, Istanbul, Turkey, July 2009.</li>\r\n  <li>&nbsp;<strong>M. H. Jama</strong>l, A. Qadeer,   A. Waheed, J. Ding, and W. Mahmood, &ldquo;Virtual   Machine Scalability on Multi-Core Processor based Servers for Cloud Computing   Workloads,&rdquo;   Accepted to   appear in NAS\'09, Hunan, China, July 2009.</li>\r\n  <li><strong>&nbsp;M. H. Jamal</strong>, and A.   Waheed, &ldquo;Precise Measurement of Execution Time of Concurrent, Symmetric,   and Short Tasks,&rdquo; in the Proceedings of CMG&rsquo;08, Las Vegas, Nevada, 7-12   December, 2008, pp. 149-160.  </li>\r\n  <li><strong>M. H. Jamal</strong>,  A. Waheed, and W. Mahmood, “Manifold: A Benchmark for Multi Core Processors  based Systems”, 1st International Conference on Open-Source Technologies, Lahore (ICOST’06), PAKISTAN, December 2006.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><br />\r\n', 1, 0),
(43, 'Mr.MMusharafDar', 43, 15, 1, 67, 'Mr.', 'Muhammad', 'Musharaf Dar', '', 'musharaf.dar@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '818', '+92-300-4135334', '+92-42-9250246', 'MuhammadMusharaf Dar387', 0, '<p>Muhammad Musharaf Dar received his <strong>&ldquo;Master in Information Technology&rdquo;</strong> degree from University of Punjabb, Lahore, Pakistan in 2008. Muhammad Musharaf Dar has been working at Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) in University of Engineering and technology, Lahore, as a <strong>&ldquo;Network Administrator&rdquo;</strong> since March 2007.<br /> His job responsibilities include Servers Hardware and Software Maintenance, Virus Protection, Regular Backups, Upgrade and Maintenance and 24/7 on call to attend to any problem in the Servers and the Systems. He is currently supporting over 250 Computers in all aspect, like Installation, Configuration, Backup and virus protection, which includes around 7 Servers (ISA, Squid Server, DC Server, RIS Server, File Server, Mailing Server and DHCP Server).<br /> Installation and Supervision of Networking Equipments, Network Cabling etc. Designing, Implementing and trouble-shooting of TCP/IP based Local Area Networks. Installation and configuration of Cisco based Routers &amp; Switches.<br /> He is also attached with &ldquo;High Performance Computing and Networking&rdquo; group. He is actively involved in setup of a High Performance Computing and Networking Lab, equipped with high end multi-core servers and a cluster of around 200 PCs connected through 1 Gbps Networks.</p>', '<ol>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Network Security</li>\r\n<li>Data Base</li>\r\n<li>Internet Programing</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</ol>', 1, 0),
(44, 'Mr.MuhammadJaved', 44, 135, 1, 71, 'Mr.', 'Muhammad', 'Javed', '', '@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '812', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'Muhammad_javed.jpg', 0, '', '', 1, 0),
(45, 'Mr.NazarHussain', 45, 135, 1, 101, 'Mr.', 'Nazar', 'Hussain', '', 'nazar', '+92-42-9029450', '812', '0321-4539032', '+92-42-9250246', 'NazarHussain405jpg', 0, '', '', 0, 0),
(46, 'Mr.MuhammadAsifRaza', 46, 17, 1, 55, 'Mr.', 'Muhammad', 'Asif Raza ', '', 'Muhammad.asif@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '810', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, '<br>Muhammad Asif Raza received his MS degree in Information Technology from NUST School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science, National University of Sciences Technology, in 2008. Previously, he received his BS in Computer Science from University of Central Punjab, Lahore in 2003. Since March 2008 he has been working as a Research Associate and Ph.D Candidate at Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS), UET, Lahore. <br><br>', 'Optical networks, Wireless sensor networks,Computer Networks, Network Programming<br><br>\r\n<font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">\r\n\r\nAchievements and Honors</font>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li> Scholarship from NUST School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science to work on Grid Enabling Technologies in collaboration with Caltech University, USA\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Selected by Scalable Agent Grooming Environment (SAGE) governing body to design security architecture for SAGE Platform (first South-Asian open source Multi-Agent System developed at NUST School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science in collaboration with Comtec Japan)</li>\r\n<li>Won Lab Strengthening Project funding from Higher Education Commission, Pakistan to establish and enhance wireless sensor networking lab facility at Alkhawarizmi Institute of Computer Science, UET, Lahore, Pakistan.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n<font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\" align=\"justify\">Publications</font>\r\n<ul>\r\n<font size=\"2\"><em><u>Journal</u></em></font><br><br>\r\n<li>Muhammad A. Raza, W. Mahmood and A. Ali, “Hybrid Control and Reservation Architecture for Multi-Domain Burst Switched Network”, IEEE / OSA Journal of Lightwave Technology, Vol. 26, No. 14, July 15, 2008<br>\r\n<li>M. A. Raza, W. Mahmood and A. Ali, “Hybrid Control Architecture for Optical Burst Switching Networks”, WSEAS Journal on Communications, Issue 8, Vol. 5 Aug. 2006 \r\n</li><br><br>\r\n<font size=\"2\"><em><u>Conference</u></em></font><br><br>\r\n\r\n<li>M. A. Raza, W. Mahmood and A. Ali, “A New Control Architecture for Optical Burst Switching Networks”, 10th WSEAS Intl. Conference on Communications, Greece July 12-15, 2006</li>\r\n<li>M. A. Raza, W. Mahmood and A. Ali, “Just-Enough-Time Domain Level Signaling (JET-DS) For Optical Burst Switching Networks”, 4th IASTED Intl. Conference on Communications, Internet, and Information Technology (CIIT 2006) St. Thomas, USVI, USA Nov. 29-Dec. 1, 2006. </li>\r\n<li>M. A. Raza, W. Mahmood and A. Ali, “Dynamic Resource Management in Hybrid Architecture for OBS Control Plane”, International Conference on Electrical Engineering (IEEE Lahore Chapter) UET, Lahore, April 11-12, 2007.\r\n.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 1, 0),
(47, 'Mr.NiamatAli', 47, 135, 1, 91, 'Mr.', 'Niamat', 'Ali', '', 'niamat.ali', '+92-42-9029450', '812', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'Niamat_Ali.jpg', 0, '', '', 0, 0),
(49, 'Mr.WasifTanveer', 49, 17, 3, 55, 'Mr.', 'Wasif', 'Tanveer', '', 'wasif.tanveer@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '813', '0321-4106323', '+92-42-9250246', 'wasif.jpg', 0, '<br>Mr. Wasif Tanveer graduated from Punjab University, College of Information Technology and currently working as Lecturer / Research Associate in Al-Khwarizmi Institute of Computer Science, UET Lahore. He is pursuing his MS in Computer Science from University of Engineering and Technology Lahore.<br><br>', 'Mobile Development and Communication<br>\r\nSoftware   Engineering<br>\r\nNetworking<br>\r\nNew Tools and Technologies<br>\r\nUbiquitous   Computing<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Publications</font>\r\n<br>\r\n<ul>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">\r\n      <div align=\"justify\"><strong>Wasif Tanveer</strong>, Martinez-Enriquez A. M, Escalada-Imaz G., and Muhammad Aslam, <strong>&ldquo;Sensing WithSense &ndash; An Intelligent Interface for Participatory Sensing&rdquo;</strong>, The Fifth International Conference on Software Engineering Advances (ICSEA), Nice, France, 22-27 August, 2010.</div>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </li>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">\r\n      <div align=\"justify\">M. Imran Sarwar<span title=\"imsarwar\" height=\"12px\" width=\"15px\"></span> , <strong>Wasif Tanveer</strong>, and Imran Sarwar<span title=\"imsarwar\" height=\"12px\" width=\"15px\"> </span>,   \"<strong>Performance   of MI Tools in Perspective of Open Source Software</strong>\", <em>2nd IEEE</em> <em>International Conference on Computer, Control &amp; Communication</em> (IEEE-IC4 2009), Pakistan Marine Engineering College, Karachi, Pakistan   February   17-18, 2009. </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </li>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">M. Imran Sarwar , <strong>Wasif Tanveer</strong>, Imran Sarwar, Dr. Waqar   Mahmood, \"<strong>A Comparative Study of MI Tools: Defining the Roadmap to MI   Tools   Standardization</strong>\", <em>IEEE International Multitopic Conference</em> (IEEE   INMIC   2008), Bahria University, Karachi, Pakistan December 23-24, 2008.</div>\r\n  </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 1, 0),
(50, 'Ms.FarzeenAbass', 50, 17, 3, 55, 'Ms.', 'Farzeen', 'Abass', '', 'farzeen.abass@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '813', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'farzeen_abass.jpg', 0, '<p>Farzeen Abbas has received her    BCSE degree form UET, Lahore.    Currently she is pursing MS in Computer Science from UET, Lahore.She have    more than two years of experience in IT industry.&nbsp;She has sound    professional/technical background .She is part of the team developing N-Tier    architecture based projects for foreign and local clients. She is also    working with the High Performance Computing Group in Distributed Systems    Domain.</p>', '<ul>\r\n      <li>Distributed Systems </li>\r\n      <li>Information Retrieval</li>\r\n      <li>Enterprise    Software&nbsp;Development</li>\r\n    </ul>', 1, 0),
(51, 'Ms.MariaChaudhry', 51, 17, 1, 55, 'Ms.', 'Maria', 'Chaudhry', '', 'maria.chaudhry @kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '813', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, '              Maria Chaudhry received her BS degree in Computer Engineering from University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore in 2007. She is pursuing her MS in Computer Engineering from UET Lahore, while working as Research Associate at Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS). She is currently working in the domain of Service Oriented Architecture (SOA) based RFID middleware. She is also a member of Wireless Sensor Networks (WSNs) group at KICS, UET Lahore', 'Service-Oriented Architectures (SOAs)<br>\r\nMiddlewares in Sensor Networks<br>\r\nEmbedded System Development (ESD)<br>\r\nSoftware Quality Assuance (SQA)<br>\r\n', 1, 0),
(52, 'Dr.AniqaDilawari', 52, 13, 3, 13, 'Dr.', 'Aniqa', 'Dilawari', '', ' aniqa.dilawari@kics.edu.pk', '', '', '', '', 'AniqaDilawari468jpg', 0, '<p>Ms. Aniqa Dilawari received her Bachelor&acirc;&euro;&trade;s degree from Lahore College for Women University, Lahore in 2004 and Master&acirc;&euro;&trade;s degree from FAST-NU, Lahore in 2007.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Quality Assurance<br /> Software Process Management<br /> Agile Software Development<br /> Requirements Engineering</p>\r\n<p><br /><span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: \'Times New Roman\', Times, serif; font-size: large;\">Achievements &amp; Honors</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Inscribed in Academic Roll Of Honor, Lahore College for Women University, Lahore in the year 2004.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', 1, 0),
(53, 'Mr.GhulamMustafa', 53, 132, 7, 38, 'Dr.', 'Ghulam', 'Mustafa', '', 'ghulam.mustafa@kics.edu.pk', '+92- 42-9250228-9, 9029450', '810', '+92-333-4374262', '+92-42-9250246', 'GhulamMustafa477', 0, '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ghulam Mustafa received his Bachelors degree in Civil Engineering from University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Taxila in 1998. He earned his Masters degree in Computer Science from University of Management and Technology (UMT), Lahore in 2007. He had taught at Punjab University College of Information Technology (PUCIT), Punjab University, Lahore as Visiting Faculty from October, 2006 till February, 2008. GhulamMus tafa has been working at KICS since March, 2008 as Senior Research Associate.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Currently he is attached with High Performance Computing and Networks group. The research focus of this group is to:</p>\r\n<ul style=\"margin-top: 0in;\" type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo3;\">Setup a high performance computing laboratory, equipped with Multicore and Many-core systems connected through 1Gbps network.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo3;\">Establish a Cluster of about 200 PCs</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo3;\">Develop microbenchmark kernels in ANSI C on Unix based systems, specifically focusing on Multicore architectures</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo3;\">Benchmarking and Performance Evaluation of Multicore / Many-core systems</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li><span class=\"MsoNormal\">Benchmarking and Performance Engineering</span></li>\r\n<li><span class=\"MsoNormal\"> High Performance Computing</span></li>\r\n<li><span class=\"MsoNormal\"> Parallel Programming</span></li>\r\n<li><span class=\"MsoNormal\"> Scientific Computing and Visualization</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: Times New Roman,Times,serif; font-size: large;\">Publications</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">K. Butt, <strong>G. Mustafa</strong>, A. Qadeer, A. Waheed, \"<em>Runtime Analysis of Application Binaries for Function Level Parallelism Potential Using QEMU</em>,\" 2012 (accepted in ICCOST 2012 to be&Acirc;&nbsp; held in December 2012).</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>G. Mustafa</strong>, A. Waheed, W. Mahmood, &ldquo;SeekBin: An Automated Tool for Analyzing Thread Level Speculative Parallelization Potential,&rdquo; in proceedings of 7th IEEE International Conference on Emerging Technologies (ICET), Islamabad, Pakistan, 2011, pp. 196-201.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>G. Mustafa</strong>, A. Waheed, W. Mahmood, \"Performance Characterization of a GPU as a Ubiquitous Accelerator in Commodity Multiprocessor Systems,\" Technical Report, 2010, http://www.kics.edu.pk/hpcnl/images/hpcnl_kics_tr_03.pdf.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">M. H. Jamal, <strong>G. Mustafa</strong>, W. Mahmood, and A. Waheed, &ldquo;An Extensible Infrastructure for Benchmarking Multi-Core Processor based Systems,&rdquo; Accepted to appear&nbsp;in SPECTS\'09, Istanbul, Turkey, July 2009.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', 1, 26),
(54, 'Ms.ShafiaKiran', 54, 134, 1, 55, 'Ms.', 'Shafia', 'Kiran', '', 'shafia.kiran@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '807', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, 'Ms. Shafia Kiran  graduated from Punjab University, College of Information Technology and currently working as Research Assistant in Al-Khwarizmi Institute     of Computer Science, UET Lahore.', '<ul>\r\n<li>Software Engineering</li>\r\n<li>Databases</li>\r\n<li>New Tools and Technologies</li>\r\n\r\n</ul>', 1, 0),
(55, 'Mr.MuhammadImranAfzal', 55, 17, 1, 55, 'Mr.', 'Muhammad Imran', 'Afzal', '', 'imran.afzal@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', 'N/A', '+92-321-5023925', '+92-42-9250246', 'imran_afzal.jpg', 0, '<br>Mr. Imran has earned his bachelors degree in 2003 and Masters  degree in 2006 from COMSATS Institute of Information technology,  Islamabad.<br><br>', '<br>Optical Wireless Communication (OWC) Modeling in Distributed Micro and Nano Sensors i.e. Smart Dust, The Sensors Everywhere.<br>\r\nFree Space Quantum Cryptography and Quantum Noise.<br>\r\nFiber Optics and Optoelectronics Devices.<br>\r\nAtmospheric and Oceanic Probing By Using OWC Modeling.<br>', 1, 0),
(56, 'Mr.MuhammadIdrees', 56, 17, 7, 55, 'Mr.', 'Muhammad', 'Idrees', '', 'idrees@kics.edu.pk', '+92- 42-9250228-9, 9029450', '810', '+92-300-4590301', '+92-42-9250246', 'muhammad_idrees.jpg', 0, '<br>Muhammad Idrees has received his M.SC. Degree in Computer Science from Punjab University College of Information Technology (PUCIT), Lahore in  2004. He earned his M.S. Degree in Computer Science from University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore in 2008. He is enrolled for his Ph. D. in Computer Science in University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore in 2008. He has been teaching at Institute of Engineering and Technology (IET), Allama Iqbal Open University in Lahore Campus, as Computer Science Lecturer Since  January, 2006 to February, 2008. He  has been working at KICS since March, 2008 as a Research Associate. He also has the honor to get the HEC scholarship. \r\nCurrently he is attached with “High Performance Computing and Networking Research” group. The research focus of this group is to:<br>\r\n<UL><li>Setup a high performance computing laboratory, equipped with Multi core and Many-core systems connected through 1Gbps network.</li>\r\n<li>Establish a Cluster of about 200 PCs</li>\r\n<li>Develop micro benchmark kernels in ANSI C on Unix based systems, specifically focusing on Multi core architectures</li>\r\n<li>Benchmarking and Performance Evaluation of Multi core / Many-core systems</li><ul><br><br>', '<br>Content Searching Algorithms and Parallel Programming<br>\r\nHigh Performance Computing and Networking<br>\r\nBenchmarking and Performance Measurement<br>\r\nDistributed Computing and Clustering<br>\r\nMulti-Core Systems\r\n<br>', 1, 0),
(57, 'Ms.MamoonaTasadduq', 57, 17, 1, 55, 'Ms.', 'Mamoona', 'Tasadduq', '', 'mamoona.tasadduq@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029450', 'NA', '+92-321-4384570', '+92-42-9250246', 'mamoona_Tasadduq.jpg', 0, '<br>Mamoona Tasadduq received her bachelor’s degree in BS (CS) from NU- FAST in 2006. She has almost one year of working experience as a Java Developer in Sigma Tech Solutions.<br><br>', '<br>Database Management Systems<br>\r\nSoftware Engineering<br>\r\nComputer Vision<br>\r\n<br>\r\n', 1, 0),
(58, 'Engr.SaadAhmadKhan', 58, 17, 1, 55, 'Engr.', 'Saad', 'Ahmad Khan ', '', 'saad.ahmad@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', 'NA', '+92 345 4737204', '+92-42-9250246', 'saad_ahmad.jpg', 0, '<br>\r\nSaad Ahmad Khan received his Bachelors degree in Electrical Engineering (specialization in telecommunication) from University Of Engineering & Technology, Lahore in 2007. He is currently pursuing his Masters degree from same university, specializing in Computer Engineering.<br>\r\nHis current work is in the domain of “Wireless Sensor Networks”. He is currently among team lead of zigbee networking group. He is also involved in research activities in the 6LowPan’s group.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nCurrent projects are:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\nEfficient image routing over zigbee networks\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\nShooter Localization using clustering in Sensor Networks\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nProjects completed:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\nImplementation of Zigbee Protocol\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\nHome Area Networking (HAN) using Zigbee Protocol\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\nEfficient implementation of H.264 codec for multi-core system\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<br><br>', '<font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Publications</font><br>\r\n  <div align=\"justify\">\r\n      <ol>\r\n        <li>Saad Ahmad Khan, Hajra Aziz, Samia Maqsood, Saleha Faisal, “Clustered Home Area Network: A Beacon Enabled IEEE\r\n          802.15.4 Approach”, Emerging Technology Conference, IEEE ICET 2008, 4th International Conference on, ISBN: 978-1-\r\n          4244-2211-1, IEEE Catalogue Number: CFP08617, Oct 19-18 2008.<a href=\"include/ATT00012.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">[ Download in PDF ]</a></li>\r\n        <li> Saad A. Khan, Fahad A. Khan, Arslan Shahid, &ldquo;Load Balanced Clustering Algorithm For Energy Efficient Home Area\r\n          Networking&rdquo;, to be presented at the, Sensors Application Symposium, Proceeding of IEEE SAS 2009, New Orleans, LA,\r\n        February 17-19, 2009.<a href=\"include/PID797485.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">[ Download in PDF ]</a></li>\r\n        <li> Saad A. Khan, Fahad A. Khan, Arslan Shahid, Zubair A. Khan, &ldquo;Zigbee Beacon Enabled Reconfigurable Cluster Tree\r\nTopology for a Multi-hop network&rdquo;, submitted to, IEEE SECON 2009, 6th International Conference on, June 22-26 2009. </li>\r\n        <li>Saad A. Khan, Fahad A. Khan, Zubair A. Khan, &ldquo;Performance Analysis of a Zigbee Cluster Tree Network&rdquo;, submitted to, IEEE\r\n          SENSORCOMM 2009, 3rd IEEE Computer Society Conference on Sensor Technologies &amp; Applications, Athens Greece, June<br>\r\n        18-23 2009.</li>\r\n        <li> Saad A. Khan, Fahad A. Khan, Arslan Shahid, Zubair A. Khan, &ldquo;Zigbee Beacon Enabled Reconfigurable Cluster Tree Topology for a\r\n          Multi-hop network&rdquo;, submitted to, IEEE SECON 2009, 6th Annual IEEE Communication Society International Conference on, June<br>\r\n          22-26 2009.</li>\r\n      </ol>\r\n</div>\r\n  <div align=\"center\">[<a href=\"include/SAAD_CV5.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download CV</a>] </div>\r\n\r\n', 1, 0),
(59, 'Ms.KauserJamal', 59, 134, 7, 55, 'Ms.', 'Kauser', 'Jamal', '', 'kauser @kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029450 - 823', '808', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, '<br><p> <strong>Kauser Jamal</strong> received her Bachelors degree with honors   in Electrical Engineering from University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore   in 2008. She has been working at Al-Khawarizmi   Institute of Computer Science (KICS) in University of Engineering and   technology, Lahore, as a Research Assistant since July   2008.</p>\r\n<p>Currently she is attached   with High Performance Computing and Networking Lab. Her tasks include the   development of micro benchmarks in Java specifically focusing on Multi-core   architectures.</p>\r\n<br />', '<br/>\r\n<ul><li>Benchmarking of   Multi-core processor based systems. </li></ul>\r\n<ul><li>High performance   computing and networking systems</li></ul>\r\n<font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Achievements &amp; Honors</font></p>\r\n  <p>Fifth Position  UET Lahore for  BSc Electrical Engineering<br />\r\n    First Position  UET Lahore, for  Term 5<br />\r\n    Merit  Scholarship UET Lahore, for Terms 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7 &amp; 8</p>', 1, 0),
(87, 'Mr.Naveed_Nawaz', 87, 13, 6, 13, 'Mr.', 'Naveed ', 'Nawaz', '', 'naveed@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'naveed1.jpg', 0, '<p>Mr. Naveed Nawaz received his degree in B.Sc. Electrical Engineering with honors from University of Engineering and technology, Lahore in 2006 and later on, completed M.Sc. in Electrical Engineering with specialization in telecommunication from the same institute in 2008.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>He remained on frontline during operation and maintenance of GSM equipment at HUAWEI-UET Joint Telecom IT Center (HUTIC) for 2 years and now has been managing installation and commissioning activities of new versions of GSM equipment of HUAWEI-technologies, with a team of six members. Also he has been conducting various trainings on BTS and BSC.</p>', '', 1, 0),
(88, 'Ms.ArfaDilawari', 88, 132, 6, 38, 'Ms.', 'Arfa', 'Dilawari', '', 'arfa.dilawari@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '829', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'ArfaDilawari792', 0, '<p>Arfa graduated from University of Engineering and Technology Lahore in Electrical Engineering with Electronics and Communications as her specialization. She joined KICS as a Research Assistant in August 2009. She is currently working at HUTIC on various modules of Huawei&rsquo;s GSM/GPRS Network equipment.</p>', '', 1, 28),
(89, 'Ms.MadihaManzoor', 89, 132, 6, 38, 'Ms.', 'Madiha ', 'Manzoor', '', 'madiha.manzoor@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'Madiha Manzoor801', 0, '<p>Madiha graduated from EME (NUST) in Computer System Engineering in 2007 and is doing her MS from UET Lahore in Electrical Engineering with specialization in Computers Engineering. She joined KICS in June, 2007. She has been conducting trainings on Huawei&rsquo;s GSM M900/M1800 BSS. <br /> Currently, she is working at HUTIC on BTS3012, BSC6000, PCU6000 and SmartAX MA5600 of Huawei&rsquo;s GSM/GPRS Network equipment.</p>', '', 1, 24),
(90, 'Ms.SabaShahid', 90, 134, 6, 55, 'Ms.', 'Saba ', 'Shahid', '', 'saba@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '829', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, 'Saba Shahid received her Bachelors degree in Electrical Engineering with a specialization in Electronics and Communications, from University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore in the year 2008. She joined KICS in July 2008 as a Research Assistant. \r\nCurrently she is working at HUTIC on HLR9820, M2000, SG7000, SGSN and GGSN of Huawei’s GSM/GPRS Network equipment.\r\n', '', 1, 0),
(92, 'Mr.AbdurRehman', 92, 133, 2, 53, 'Mr.', 'Abdur', 'Rehman', '', 'a.rehman @kics.edu.pk', ' +92-42-9029450 ', '827', '+92-3338418450', '+92-42-9250246', 'arehman.jpg', 0, '<p>Abd ur Rehman received his &tilde;Master in Computer Science\" degree from Punjab University College of Information Technology in 2003. He also has &tilde;MS Computer Sceinces\" degree from Department of Computer Sciences, University of Engineering &amp; Technology, Lahore. He has been working as J2EE developer at KICS for one and a half year.</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Machine Learning &amp; Pattern Matching</li>\r\n<li>Artificial Intelligence</li>\r\n</ul>', 1, 27),
(93, 'Mr.SajidMahmood', 93, 13, 2, 13, 'Dr.', 'Sajid ', 'Mahmood', '', 'sajid.mahmood@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-684-2430, +92-42-902-9450-', '827', '+92-321-451-1087', '+92-42-9250246', 'Sajid Mahmood837', 2, '<p>Sajid Mahmood received his MS degree in Computer Science from department of Computer Science and Engineering, University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore in 2007. He has also received MSc. degree in Computer Science from University of the Punjab, Lahore in 2003. He is currently working as Research Associate at Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS). During this tenure, he worked on research based development projects, N-Tier Enterprise Web Applications using Open-Source Softwares and Technologies.<br /> <strong><br /></strong></p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Feature Extraction &amp; Selection</li>\r\n<li>Classification from Imbalanced Data Sets</li>\r\n</ul>', 1, 15),
(95, 'Mr.ImranAbbas', 95, 134, 2, 55, 'Mr.', 'Imran ', 'Abbas', '', 'imran.abbas @kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'imranabbas.jpg', 0, 'Mr. M.Imran Abbas received his Bachelor’s in Computer Science degree from \r\nUniversity of the Punjab, Lahore in 2005. He also has Masters in Information \r\nTechnology degree from Punjab University College of Information Technology, \r\nLahore in 2008. Currently he is attached with “Embedded System & Software\r\n” group \r\n', '<br />Project Management \r\n<br />Software Engineering \r\n<br />Software Quality Assurance \r\n<br />Database Management Systems & <br />Recovery mechanisms \r\n', 1, 0),
(98, 'usmansaeed', 98, 130, 4, 79, 'Dr.', 'Usman', 'Saeed', '', 'u.saeed@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029350, 9029450', '', '', '+92-42-9250246', '', 0, '<p>.</p>', '<p>.</p>', 1, 0),
(100, 'Ms.SarahSaleem', 100, 134, 1, 55, 'Ms.', 'Sarah', 'Saleem', '', '@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, '<br/><p>Received my Bachelor’s degree from University of Engineering and Technology , Lahore in 2005. Currently i am a student of MSc in Computer Science in Department of Computer Science and Engineering, University of Engineering and Technology.Lahore. At Kics , currently working with the research group WATCH Nets ( Wireless Sensor Network group). The MS thesis topic is the Fault Tolerance in Wireless Sensor Networks.</P><br/> ', '<ul>\r\n<li>Mobile Communication</li>\r\n<li>Optical Wireless and Wireless Sensor Networks</li></ul>', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO `people` (`people_id`, `url_name`, `user_id`, `designation_id`, `group_id`, `post_id`, `title`, `fname`, `lname`, `url`, `email`, `off_no`, `ext`, `cell_no`, `fax_no`, `image_name`, `seqno`, `biography`, `research_interest`, `status`, `is_core_team`) VALUES
(101, 'Dr.AliHammadAkbar', 101, 13, 5, 13, 'Dr.', 'Ali  Hammad ', 'Akbar', '', 'ahakbar@gmail.com,hammad@ajou.ac.kr ', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'ali_hammad.jpg', 0, '<p><br />Ali Hammad Akbar obtained his bachelors degree with distinction in telecommunications from NUST, Pakistan in 1997. As an intern, he worked at Pakistan Communications Industries, wherein he proposed and incorporated enhancements in the Norwegian telephone set, VIVO-II and its in-circuit tester. Later in 1998, he was awarded merit scholarship for MS in UNSW Australia, which concluded with his research findings in DWDM systems in optical communication systems. While in Australia, he also worked as a consultant to Eztel Corporation, a telco that compares in service provisioning with giants like Optus and Telstra. In 1999, he joined his alma mater as a lecturer. For his academic accomplishments, he was declared as a star laureate by South Asia Publications&Acirc;&reg; for the year of 2003. In 2004, he joined Ajou University for pursuing the PhD studies. He worked on the architectural issues of wireless sensor networks that define the role and mechanisms for addressing the constraints and challenges purported in these networks. After the completion of his PhD, he is currently working as an assistant professor at UET Pakistan, a premier university in engineering and technology. His topics of interest include wireless networks such as MANETs and sensor networks.</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Wireless sensor networks</li>\r\n<li>Mobile Ad Hoc Networks</li>\r\n<li>6LoWPANs</li>\r\n<li>IEEE802.15.4</li>\r\n<li>Wireless Mesh Networks</li>\r\n<li>Fibre optics</li>\r\n<li>Wave division multiplexing</li>\r\n<li>Gratings (Fabry-Perot and BRAGG)</li>\r\n<li>IKE Infrastructure for wireless networks</li>\r\n<li>Location and target tracking in WSNs</li>\r\n<li>Mobility management in WSNs</li>\r\n<li>Policy-based management of WSNs</li>\r\n<li>Wireless sensor grids for surveillance</li>\r\n<li>Service discovery protocols for WSNs</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: \'Times New Roman\', Times, serif; font-size: x-large;\">Publications:</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: \'Times New Roman\', Times, serif; font-size: large;\">Book chapters</span></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, and Ki-Hyung Kim&ldquo;A Proxy-Enabled Service Discovery Architecture to Find Proximity-Based Services in 6LoWPAN&rdquo;, in book titled &ldquo;Ubiquitous Computing and Communications&rdquo; by IDEAS Group, USA (2007)</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Hamid Mukhtar, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Shafique Ahmad Chaudhary, Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;Network Management in Wireless Sensor Networks&rdquo; in book titled, &ldquo;RFID and Sensor Networks; Architectures and applications&rdquo;, by CRC Press 2008.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: \'Times New Roman\', Times, serif; font-size: large;\">Patents</span></p>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><ol>\r\n<li>USN Service Provisioning INfrastructurE (U-Spine) Submitted to US Patent Office USPTO (2009)</li>\r\n<li>USN Key management INfrastructure (U-KIN) Submitted to Korea Patent Office (Jan, 2007)</li>\r\n</ol></div>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: \'Times New Roman\', Times, serif; font-size: large;\">Papers</span></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Maria Chaudhary, Qanita Ahmad, Imran Sarwar, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;Comparative Study of RFID Middlewares&mdash;Defining the roadmap to SOA-based Middleware&rdquo; IEEE ICIT 2009, Chile. (Conference organized by IEEE Transactions on Industrial Technologies)</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Muhammad Asif Raza, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Waqar Mehmood, &ldquo;Optimal Cluster Head Election for Efficient Resource Discovery Mechanism in Wireless Sensor Networks,&rdquo; IEEE LCN2009, Switzerland. (A class conference)</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Mohsin Javed, Rizwan Butt, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Anoar-al-Omar, &ldquo;A lexicon-based cost evaluation for multi-metric routing protocols in WSNs,&rdquo; IEEE INMIC2009, Islamabad.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Hina Khalid, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar </strong>et. al, &ldquo;LEGATE: Location managEment system for logical Group-bAsed Tracking of mobilE nodes in retailing malls,&rdquo; IEEE Innovations, 2009, Al-Ain UAE.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Anwar Alomar, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;C&#1103;C; Carrefour Routing for cluster-based sensor networks to support multiple applications in multiple gateway environments&rdquo; 5th Intl Conf. IEEE <em>MSN&rsquo;09,</em> China. (Top ranked conference in sensor networks)&nbsp;</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Anwar Alomar, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;Carrefour Cast: A new routing protocol to support multiple applications in multiple gateway environments of wireless sensor networks&rdquo; <em>world congress on science, Engineering and technology,</em> 2009 Singapore. &nbsp;&nbsp;</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;Joining the IETF Folds,&rdquo; IETF Journal, Volume 4 Issue 2 (October 2008).</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Rabia Riaz, Ayesha Ikram, Attiya Naureen, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;A Unified Security Framework with Three Key Management Schemes for Wireless Sensor Networks&rdquo;, Computer Communications, Elsevier Sciences, 2008. (Impact factor: 1)</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Taqi Raza, Zeeshan Mir, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;An adaptive Yaw Rate Aware Sensor Wakeup Protocol (YAP) for Energy Efficient Target Tracking in Sensor Networks&rdquo; IEICE Transactions on Communications 2008. (Impact factor: 0.48)</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Gargi Bag, Saif Shams, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;Network Assisted Mobility Support Architecture for 6LoWPANs, CCNC2008 (A ranked conference)</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Mustafa Hasan, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;NOMADIC: A new mobility management protocol for sensors in web portal-baseD multi-tier architecture,&rdquo; NCM 2008, Korea. (Acceptance rate &lt;25%)</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Hamid Mukhtar, Gargi Bag, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;LNMP: Management architecture for IPv6 based low power wireless personal area networks (6LoWPANs),&rdquo; NOMS2008 (Top tier conference in network management).</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Mustafa Hasan, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;A scheme to support mobility for IP-based sensor networks&rdquo;, InfoScale2008, Italy.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Ali Tufail, Fraser, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo; An empirical study to analyze the feasibility of WIFI for VANETs,&rdquo; CSCWD2008, China.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Imran Afzal, Waqar Mahmood, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;A Battery Recharge Model for WSNs using Free-Space Optics (FSO)&rdquo; IEEE INMIC2008, Pakistan.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Seuk Jung, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Byeong-hee Roh, Ki-hyung Kim, &ldquo;Multiple Routers-based Architecture for IPv6-Based Wireless Sensor Networks (6LoWPANs),&rdquo; NEXT2007</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Kim Ki-Hyung, &ldquo;On the Interplay of Proximity and Ubiquity,&rdquo; IEICE Transactions on Communications, 2008 (Impact factor: 1)</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Muhammad Taqi Raza H. M., <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, Gargi Bag, Seung-wha Yoo, and Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;A Yaw Rate Aware Sensor Wakeup Protocol (YAP) for Energy Efficient Target Tracking in Sensor Networks,&rdquo; Milcom 2007, USA.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Rabia Riaz, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Mustafa Hasan, Ki-Hyung Kim, Kyungsuk Lhee, Hafiz Farooq Ahmed, &ldquo;Key Management Scheme for Sensor Networks with Proactive Key Revocation and Sleep State Consideration,&rdquo; ATNCTA Workshop in IFIP NPC2007, China, Sep. 2007.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Mustafa Hasan, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Rabia Riaz, Subir Biswas, Ki-Hyung Kim, Seung W. Yoo, Byeong-hee Roh, &ldquo;Key Management in IP-based Ubiquitous Sensor Networks: Issues, Challenges and Solutions&rdquo;, IEEE ICUT2007 Dubai, Feb 2007.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ahmad Ali Iqbal, Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, Chaudhary Sajjad Hussain, and Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;A routing overlay for wireless sensor networks with multiple service support,&rdquo; <em>The Journal of Korean Institute of Next Generation Computing</em>, ISSN 1738-8341 Vol. 1, No. 2.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;On self management of wireless mesh and MANETs&rdquo;, <em>The Journal of Korean Institute of Next Generation Computing</em>, ISSN 1738-8341 Vol. 2, No. 2.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Ki-Hyung Kim, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;IPv6 over IEEE 802.15.4 : Bridging Over the Ubiquity Vision to Reality, &ldquo; Korean American Scientists and Engineers, Aug. 10th-13th, 2006, Teaneck, New Jersey, USA.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Won-Sik Yoon and Jai-Hoon Kim, &ldquo;Effect of transmission power adjustments on network availability,&rdquo; <em>Information Technology Journal </em>4(3): 271-273, 2005.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Shafique Ahmad Chaudhary, Ali Kashif, and Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;Sustaining network availability of wireless sensor networks,&rdquo; Technical Paper Collections, IT International Student Fair August 2005, South Korea.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ahmad Ali Iqbal, Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, Chaudhary Sajjad Hussain, Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;A Routing Overlay for Wireless Sensor Networks with Multiple Services Support,&rdquo; (<strong><em>Outstanding Paper Award</em></strong>) Korea International Next Generation Personal Computer Conference (KINGPC), Seoul, 3-4 Nov, 2005, pp. 171-175.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Ki-Hyung Kim, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ali Kashif Bashir, &ldquo;Are Low Pans a Pan or an Internet of Pans?,&rdquo; Korea International Next Generation Personal Computer Conference (KINGPC), Seoul, 3-4 Nov, 2005, pp. 182-186.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Waleed Mansoor, Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, Ali Kashif, and Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;Longevity techniques for sensor grids,&rdquo; Korea International Next Generation Personal Computer Conference (KINGPC), Seoul, 3-4 Nov, 2005, pp 20-24.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Jung Won-Do, Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Sohn Young-Do,&nbsp; and Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;Route Error Reporting Schemes for 6lowPANs,&rdquo; Korea International Next Generation Personal Computer Conference (KINGPC), Seoul, 3-4 Nov, 2005, pp. 25-29.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Ali Kashif Bashir, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, Chauhdary Sajjad Hussain, and Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;Collaborative Detection and Agreement Protocol for Routing Malfunctioning in Wireless Sensor Networks,&rdquo; IEEE International Conference on Advanced Communications Technology (ICACT), 20-22 Feb. 2006, pp. 327-332.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Waleed Mansoor, Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, Ali Kashif, and Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;Node-link-failure Resilient Routing Architecture for Sensor Grids,&rdquo; IEEE International Conference on Advanced Communications Technology (ICACT), 20-22 Feb. 2006, pp. 131-135.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Ki-Hyung Kim and <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;Are Low PANs a PAN or An Internet of PANs?,&rdquo; Grid and Pervasive Computing Conference GPC2006 (<strong>SCIE:</strong> <strong><em>LNCS SPRINGER VERLAG </em></strong>), Taiwan 3-5 May 2006.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ki-Hyung Kim, Seung-Jin Bang, Waleed Mansoor, and Won-Sik Yoon, &ldquo;Availability Considerations for Wireless Sensor Grids,&rdquo; Grid and Pervasive Computing Conference GPC2006 (<strong>SCIE:</strong> <strong><em>LNCS SPRINGER VERLAG</em></strong>), Taiwan 3-5 May 2006.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ahmad Ali Iqbal, and Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;Binding Multiple Applications on Wireless Sensor Networks,&rdquo; Grid and Pervasive Computing Conference GPC2006 (<strong>SCIE:</strong> <strong><em>LNCS SPRINGER VERLAG</em></strong>), Taiwan 3-5 May 2006.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ki-Hyung Kim, Shaokai Yu, and Won-Sik Yoon, &ldquo;On the Effect of Heterogeneous Traffic Sources on the Network Availability for Wireless Sensor Grids,&rdquo; International Conference on Computational Science ICCS2006 (<strong>SCIE:</strong> <strong><em>LNCS SPRINGER VERLAG</em></strong>), UK 28-31 May 2006.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ki-Hyung Kim, Won-Do Jung, Ali Kashif Bashir, and Seung-Wha Yoo, &ldquo;GARPAN: Gateway-Assisted Inter-PAN Routing for 6LoWPANs,&rdquo; The 2006 International Conference on Computational Science and its Applications ICCSA 2006 (<strong>SCIE:</strong> <strong><em>LNCS SPRINGER VERLAG</em></strong>), Scotland, 8-11 May, 2006.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Shoaib Mukhtar, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, Won-Sik Yoon, Ki-Hyung Kim, and Suk-Kyo Hong, &ldquo;Mitigating Broadcast Storms in Stateless Address Auto-Configuring MANETs,&rdquo; The 2006 International Conference on Computational Science and its Applications ICCSA 2006 (<strong>SCIE:</strong> <strong><em>LNCS SPRINGER VERLAG</em></strong>), Scotland, 8-11 May, 2006.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ahmad Ali Iqbal, Waleed Mansoor, Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, and Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;Longevity Enhancing Measures for Sensor Grids,&rdquo; KNOM Review (Korean Institute of Communications Sciences), Vol. 8, No. 2, February 2006, pp. 26-31.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, Won Do Jung, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, and Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;Proxy-based Service Discovery and Network Selection in 6LoWPAN,&rdquo; The 2006 International Conference on High Performance Computing and Communications HPCC-06, (<strong>SCIE:</strong> <strong><em>LNCS SPRINGER VERLAG</em></strong>) 13th-15th Sep, 2006.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, Won-Do Jung, Chaudhary Sajjad Hussain, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, and Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;A Proxy-Enabled Service Discovery Architecture to Find Proximity-Based Services in 6LoWPAN,&rdquo; International Conference on Embedded And Ubiquitous Computing (EUC\'2006), (<strong>SCIE:</strong> <strong><em>LNCS SPRINGER VERLAG</em></strong>) Aug. 01-04, 2006.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><ol>\r\n<li>Shafique Chaudhry, Faisal Siddiqui, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;NETSAQ: Network State Adaptive QoS Provisioning for MANETs,&rdquo;&nbsp; 9th Asia-Pacific Network Operations and Management Symposium (APNOMS), (<strong>SCIE:</strong> <strong><em>LNCS SPRINGER VERLAG</em></strong>) Sep, 27th-29th, 2006.</li>\r\n<li>Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Faisal Siddiqui, and Ki-Hyung Kim, &ldquo;Autonomic Network Management for Wireless Mesh and MANETs,&rdquo; International Workshop on Self-Organizing Systems (IWSOS), (<strong>SCIE:</strong> <strong><em>LNCS SPRINGER VERLAG</em></strong>), Sep., 18th-20th 2006.</li>\r\n<li>Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Ki-Hyung Kim, <br /> Suk-Kyo Hong, and Won-Sik Yoon, &ldquo;HYWINMARC: An Autonomic Management Architecture for Hybrid Wireless Networks,&rdquo; International Conference on Embedded And Ubiquitous Computing (EUC\'2006), (<strong>SCIE:</strong> <strong><em>LNCS SPRINGER VERLAG</em></strong>) Aug. 01-04, 2006.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Faysal Adeem Siddiqui, Shoaib Mukhtar, &ldquo;Network management of uZone networks,&rdquo; <em>Q-2 Technical Report </em>submitted to u-Frontier Project Ministry of Science and Technology (MoST), Korea 2005.</li>\r\n<li>Shafique Ahmad Chaudhry, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Faysal Adeem Siddiqui, and Won-Sik Yoon, &ldquo;Autonomic Network Management for u-Zone Network,&rdquo; UbiCNS2005, Cheju Korea.</li>\r\n<li>Shafique Ahmad Chaudhary, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Chaudhary Sajjad, and Kim Ki-Hyung, &ldquo;Autonomic remote management architecture for smart homes,&rdquo; Technical Paper Collections, IT International Student Fair August 2005, Korea.</li>\r\n<li>Muhammad Wajid, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Muhammad Hasan Zaidi, &ldquo;On the Evaluation of Active Queue Management Issues in MANETs,&rdquo; GIKITech 19th Dec, Swabi Pakistan 2004.</li>\r\n<li>Ramla Ahmad, Dr. Zaidi, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;Wavelength Assignment using Closest Wavelength Tuning&rdquo;, HONET 2004, Islamabad Pakistan.</li>\r\n<li>Saud Mukhtar, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;Proposal for Implementing Firewall for NIIT Intranet,&rdquo; PGD-IT Thesis NUST Pakistan, 2003.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, Faran Qadir, Baqir Hussnain, &ldquo; Data Communications and Security Simulator; An educational tool,&rdquo; International Conference on Technology Revamping &amp; Upgradation 12-13 April 2004, Lahore Pakistan.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar,</strong> &ldquo;A Simulation Tool; Data Communications for IT Professionals&rdquo;, Dawn Lifestyle Exhibition, Islamabad 20 Jan, 2004</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;An Indigenous Data Communications simulator for Public Sector Universities of Pakistan&rdquo;, Final Selection in SofTech, FAST NU Pakistan 21-22 March, 2004.</li>\r\n<li>Monographs</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;Student-teacher-student; A respite?&rdquo; Gazette, Graduate School of Information Studies, Jan. 2005 Ajou University, South Korea.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;PhD is a journey&hellip;not a destination&rdquo; Ajou Globe, May. 2005 Ajou University, South Korea.</li>\r\n</ol></div>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: \'Times New Roman\', Times, serif; font-size: large;\">Before 2004</span></p>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar,</strong> &ldquo;TCP Protocols in MANETs; Evaluation and Enhancement&rdquo;, One Day Workshop on Advanced Networks, NUST Pakistan15 Dec, 2003</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar, </strong>&ldquo;Optical Filtering using Bragg Gratings and Fabry-Perot Cavity in DWDM Networks&rdquo;, International Seminar on Broadband Networks, ZTE-NUST 15 July, 2002.</li>\r\n<li>Riaz Mehmood, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong><strong>, </strong>&ldquo;Mitigating Denial of Service Attacks using Dynamic Ingress Filtering Technique&rdquo;, IEEE Student Conference, LUMS Pakistan May, 2002.</li>\r\n<li>Ramla Ahmed, Muhammad Hasan Zaidi, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;An Evaluation of Routing and Wavelength Assignment Algorithms in IP over DWDM Networks,&rdquo; IEEE Student Conference, LUMS Pakistan May, 2002</li>\r\n<li>Muhammad Hasan Zaidi, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;Pakistan Academic Intranet: Technology Solution,&rdquo; ITU Telecom Asia 2000 Hong Kong - December, 2000</li>\r\n<li>Muhammad Hasan Zaidi, <strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;Pakistan Academic Intranet- A Technology Solution,&rdquo; Report submitted to PITB and MoST Pakistan, Nov 2000.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong>, &ldquo;Electronic Payment Mechanisms in Ecommerce Implementation for Pakistan&rdquo;, Keynote Speaker, Jan 2000.</li>\r\n<li>Ramla Ahmad, Dr. Zaidi, Ali Hammad, &ldquo;Performance Analysis of Wavelength Assignment algorithms in IP over DWDM Networks&rdquo;, IADIS WWW/Internet Conference 2002, Lisbon Portugal.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ali Hammad Akbar</strong> and Gang Ding Peng, &ldquo;Fibre Fabry-Perot E&rsquo;talong; the marvel unveiled,&rdquo; MS Thesis, Dept of Electrical Engineering, University of New South Wales, 1999.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>', 1, 0),
(102, 'Ms.SidraShafique', 102, 134, 1, 55, 'Ms.', 'Sidra', 'Shafique', '', 'sidrah.shafique@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, '<br>Completed bachelors in electrical engineering with a specialization in Electronics and Communications with Honors, from University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore in august 2008.Currently serving as a research assistant under the supervision of Dr. Muhammad Akmal Butt since august.<br><br>', '<br>embedded systems,development of time varying channel and extending it for MIMO systems <br><br>\r\n<font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Achievements & Honors</font><br><br>\r\n\r\n1.	received Shamshad Majeed gold medal for mathematics from Lahore College for Women University <br>\r\n2.	completed Bachelors in electrical engineering with honors ', 1, 0),
(104, 'Ms.AmaraTariq', 104, 134, 1, 55, 'Ms.', 'Amara', 'Tariq', '', 'amara.tariq@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '103', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'AmaraTariq936', 0, '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>I received my Bachelor\'s degree with honors in Electrical Engineering (specialization in Electronics and Telecommunication) from University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore in 2008. I have been working at Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) in University of Engineering and technology, Lahore, as a Research Assistant since August 2008. Currently I am working on the project of FlexTrainer ,under the supervision of Dr. Muhammad Akmal Butt. <br /><br /></p>', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>DSP algorithm implementation</li>\r\n<li>embedded systems</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: Times New Roman,Times,serif; font-size: large;\">Achievements &amp; Honors</span></p>\r\n<p>secured 3rd position in B.Sc. engineering</p>', 1, 0),
(107, 'Mr.AbdulQadeer', 107, 16, 7, 18, 'Mr.', 'Abdul', 'Qadeer', '', 'qadeer@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450 - 823', '--', '--', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, '<p><br /> Abdul Qadeer received his Bachelors degree in Computer Science from FAST (Foundation for Advancement of Science and Technology), Lahore in 2001. He received his M.S. Degree in Computer Science in February 2006 from Lahore University of Management Sciences (LUMS), Pakistan. Moreover he received his Master Degree M.S.in Computer Science from University of Southern California (USC), Los Angeles, CA</p>\r\n<p>His core competencies are Software Systems development (Conceiving to Deployment) and Technical Training. He has done a lot of work in the different areas like Requirement analysis, System development, Unit testing, Workflow development.and System design. He is currently working as a Research Manager in Al-Khawarizmi Institure of Computer Science, UET, Lahore. </p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: \'Times New Roman\', Times, serif; font-size: large;\">Project Compeleted </span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Development of Map Reduce framework: He developed a whole map reduce frame work mainly based on the ideas of Google&acirc;&euro;&trade;s MapReduce framework. He used framework network data analysis. This analysis was mainly about the current IPv4 allocation status. data is the IP ping experiment data conducted by John Heidemann at ISI.<br /><br /><br /></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Parallel &amp; Distributed Computing, Cloud Computing</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color: #1b68b0; font-family: \'Times New Roman\', Times, serif; font-size: large;\">Publications</span></p>\r\n<div align=\"justify\"><ol>\r\n<li>K. Butt, Ehsan-ul-Haq, A. Qadeer, and A. Waheed, \"MIPS64 User Mode Emulation: A Case Study in Open Source Software Engineering,\" in proceedings of 7th IEEE International Conference on Emerging Technologies (ICET), Islamabad, Pakistan, 2011, pp. 78-83.<br /> </li>\r\n<li>\"The website census\"Qadeer, Abdul&nbsp;&nbsp; Mahmood, Waqar&nbsp;&nbsp; Waheed, Abdul, Paper to appears in: Internet Technology and Secured Transactions, 2009. ICITST 2009. International Conference for Publication Date: 9-12 Nov. 2009 On page(s): 1 - 6 Location: London, United Kingdom ISBN: 978-1-4244-5647-5 Current Version Published: 2010-01-29<br /> </li>\r\n<li>M. H. Jamal, A. Qadeer, A. Waheed, J. Ding, and W. Mahmood, \"Virtual Machine Scalability on Multi-Core Processor based Servers for Cloud Computing Workloads,\" Accepted to appear in NAS\' 09, Hunan, China, July 2009.<br /> </li>\r\n<li>\r\n<div align=\"left\">\"Software Automated Testing Guidelines\".Proceedings of 3rd CIIT Workshop on Research in Computing (CWRC\"06).It discusses specific to the regional software industry ranging from management to technical incorporate automation.</div>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol></div>', 1, 0),
(108, 'Ms.AnamAli', 108, 17, 7, 55, 'Ms.', 'Anam', 'Ali', '', 'anum.ali@kics.edu.pk', '', '', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, 'Ms. Anum Ali received her Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science from Sir Syed University of Engineering and Technology, Karachi in 2004 and Master’s degree in Satellite & Space Environment from Lancaster University, UK in 2006.', '<ul><li>Parallel & Distributed Computing</li></ul>', 1, 0),
(110, 'Ms.FasihaAshraf', 110, 134, 7, 55, 'Ms.', 'Fasiha ', 'Ashraf ', '', 'Fasiha.ashraf@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029450', '823 - 808', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, 'Ms. Fasiha Ashraf received her Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science from University of Agriculture, Faisalabad in 2007 and is pursuing her Master’s degree from University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore.', 'Virtualization\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n <br>\r\n              <strong><em><br>  \r\n              <br>\r\n          Currently she is doing PhD degree from University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore </em></strong>', 1, 0),
(111, 'Mr.ZahoorurRehman', 111, 16, 3, 38, 'Mr.', 'Zahoor ur', 'Rehman', '', 'zahoor@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300', '813', '+92-321-9676940', '+92-42-9250246', 'Zahoor_rehman.jpg', 0, '<p>Mr. Zahoor ur Rehman received his MS-CS from Foundation University Islamabad in 2007. He is currently enrolled in PhD at department of Computer Science and Engineering at University of Engineering and Technology. He has completed his course work and now working on his PhD dissertation. \r\nZahoor ur Rehman has versatile experience of programming, teaching and research. He has joined KICS in Dec 2008 as Senior Research Associate and working on Koha an ILS project and also preparing feasibility for data analysis center establishment. He is an active researcher and has a journal publication and his two publications are in review stage at IEEE Toronto conference. \r\n</p><br>', '<ul>\r\n  <li>Data Mining and Wireless Sensor  Network</li><br>\r\n  <li> Context-aware Ubiquitous Data mining</li><br>\r\n  <li> Sensor Stream Mining</li><br>\r\n  <li> Pervasive Computing</li><br>\r\n  <li> Educational Data Mining</li><br>\r\n  <li> Data Analysis</li><br>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span class=\"headingcolor\">Publications</span></p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\"><ul>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\"><strong>Rehman, Z.</strong>, Shahbaz, M.,&nbsp;Shaheen, M., Mehmood, S., 2010.,&nbsp;<em>Context Aware Ubiquitous Data Mining Framework to predict Malicious Activities</em>., Journal of American Science, Vol. 6 (8), pp. 161-171.</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">\r\n      Shaheen, M.,  Shahbaz, M., Guergachi, A.,<strong> Rehman, Z.,</strong> 2010., <em>Data Mining Applications in Hydrocarbon Exploration</em>., Springer Link  Artificial Intelligence Review, Vol. 34, Number.4, Dec 2010.</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">\r\n      Mehmood, T., <strong>Rehman, Z.</strong>, Jameel, Tariq., 2010.,<span lang=\"EN-US\"><em>A Review of the Problems Faced by AIOU Regional Centers in Pakistan.,&nbsp;</em></span>Journal of American Science, Vol. 7(1), pp.&nbsp;92-99</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">\r\n      Shaheen,M.,  Shahbaz, M., <strong>Rehman, Z.,</strong> Aurangzeb, S., 2010., <em>Issues in Interacting with GIS for Hydrocarbon Exploration</em>., Journal  of American Science, Vol. 6(7)., pp. 262-271.</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">\r\n      Shaheen, M.,  Shahbaz, M.,<strong> Rehman, Z.,</strong> Mehmood, S., 2010., <em>A Method of Data Mining for Sustainable Hydrocarbon Exploration.,  Accepted in: Journal of Engineering &amp; Applied Sciences</em>, UET Peshawar.</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">\r\n      Shaheen, M.,  Aslam, M., Shahbaz, M., Martinaquez, A., <strong>Rehman, Z.</strong>, 2010., <em>An Intelligent Mechanism for GIS Contract  Automation</em>., Accepted in: Journal of Research in Computing Mexico, Vol. 47.</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">\r\n      Shaheen, M.,  Shahbaz, M., Guergachi, A., <strong>Rehman, Z</strong>., 2010., <em>Context Based Positive and Negative Spatio Temporal Association Rule  Mining</em>., Submitted to: Elsvier Journal of Data and Knowledge Engineering.</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">\r\n      Shaheen, M.,  Shahbaz, M., Guergachi, A., <strong>Rehman, Z</strong>., 2010., <em>Mining Sustainability Indicators to Classify Hydrocarbon Development</em>.,  Submitted to: IEEE Intelligent Systems Special Issue: AI and Power Markets.</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\"><strong>Zahoor  ur Rehman</strong>, M.Shahbaz, M. Shaheen, Aziz Guergachi.,  &quot;Situation-awareness and Sensor Stream Mining for Sustainable  Society&quot; (2009) International Conference on Soft Computing and Pattern  Recognition (Malaysia) Vol:ISBN-13: 978-0-7695-3879-2</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\"><strong>Zahoor  ur Rehman</strong>, M. Imran, M.Aslam, M. Shaheen., &ldquo;An Inatelligent Mathematical  Production Assistant&rdquo; (2009)&nbsp;  International Conference on Frontier of Information Technology  (Pakistan)</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">M.  Shaheen, M.Shahbaz, <strong>Zahoor ur Rehman</strong>, M. Sarshar Aurangzeb.,  &quot;Issues in Interacting with GIS in Hydrocarbon Exploration Industry&quot;  (2010) Journal of American Science USA Vol:6(7) pp:262-271</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">M.  Shaheen, M.Shahbaz, <strong>Zahoor ur Rehman.</strong>, Aziz Guergachi &quot;Mining  Sustainability Indicators to Predict Optimal Hydrocarbon Exploration Rate&quot;  (2010) International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Applications  (Austria) Vol:ISBN: 978-0-88986-817-5</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">M.  Shaheen, <strong>Zahoor ur Rehman.,</strong> &ldquo;Critical Skills for Computer  Academician-Course Proposal&quot; (2008) Informing Science Society Conference  (Bulgaria) as well as in &quot;journal of Information Technology California  USA&quot;</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">M.  Shaheen, M.Shahbaz, <strong>Zahoor ur Rehman.,</strong> &quot;Data Mining Applications in  Hydrocabron Exploration&quot; (2010) Springer Link:: Artificial Intelligence  Reviews Vol:Submitted for Peer Review</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  </ul>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\"><strong>Rehman, Z.</strong>, Shahbaz, M., Shaheen, M., Guergachi, A., 2009., <em>Situation Awareness and Sensor Stream Mining  for Sustainable Society</em>., International Conference on Soft Computing and  Pattern Recognition Malaysia.</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\"><strong>Rehman, Z.</strong>, Imran, M., Aslam, M., Shaheen, M., 2009., <em>An Intelligent Mathematical Production Assistant</em>.,  International Conference on Frontiers of Information Technology (FIT),  Pakistan.</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">Shaheen, M., Shahbaz, M.,&nbsp;<strong>Rehman, Z</strong>., Guergachi, A., 2010.,&nbsp;<em>Mining Sustainability Indicators to Predict Optimal Hydrocarbon Exploration Rate</em>., IASTED International Conference on Artificial intelligence and Applications., Innsbruck, Austria, pp.394-400.</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\"> Shaheen, M.,&nbsp;<strong>Rehman, Z.</strong>, 2008.,&nbsp;<em>Critical Skills for Computer Academicians</em>., Proceedings of Informing Science &amp; IT Education Conference (InSITE) 2008, Bulgaria, pp. 405-421.</div>\r\n  </li><br>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', 1, 0),
(112, 'wasimbhalli', 112, 132, 3, 38, 'Mr.', 'Muhammad', 'Wasim', '', 'wasim@kics.edu.pk', '', '', '+92 333 8639639', '+92 42 9250246', 'MuhammadWasim1008', 1, '<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: helvetica; font-size: small;\">Mr. Muhammad Wasim is team lead of data science lab and pursuing his PhD in Computer Science from University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore. He has industry experience of 6+ years and academic background of 4+ years. He has taught various subjects at UET, FC College, and UMT.</span></p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Data Science</li>\r\n<li>Big Data</li>\r\n<li>Natural Langauge Processing</li>\r\n<li>Information Retreival</li>\r\n</ul>', 1, 0),
(114, 'Dr.SyedMuhammadAhsan', 114, 13, 8, 13, 'Dr.', 'Syed Muhammad', 'Ahsan', '', 'ahsancs@hotmail.com', '+92-42-9029260', '', '92-322-4379469', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, 'Syed Muhammad Ahsan received his Ph.D Degree in Computer Science in 2009 from University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore. His Area of Specialization is  Bioinformatics. His Thesis Title is Development of an Extensible Database Management System for Biological Data.\r\n<br>\r\nMoreover he has done Master in Computer Science from University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore in 1994.\r\n', '<br><ul type=\"square\">\r\n\r\n<li>Bioinformatics</li>\r\n\r\n<li>Distribute Databases</li>\r\n<li> Data  Provenance</li>\r\n<li> Semantic Web<br />\r\n  <br />\r\n  <font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Publications</font></li>\r\n<li><font size=\"2\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\"><strong>Book Chapters </strong></font></li>\r\n<ul type=\"circle\">\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\">Ahsan, S. and Shah, A., ‘Quality Metrics for Evaluating Data Provenance’.   Designing Software-Intensive Systems: Methods and Principles. Information Science Reference, USA, April 2008</div>\r\n  </li>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\"> Ahsan S. and Shah A., ‘Web Services for Bioinformatics’. Methodologies for Non-Functional   Requirements in Service Oriented Architecture. Information Science Reference, USA (Accepted)</div>\r\n  </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<li><font size=\"2\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\"><strong>Journal and Conference Papers</strong></font>\r\n<ul type=\"circle\">\r\n    <li>\r\n      <div align=\"justify\">Ahsan S. and Shah, A. ‘An Agile Development Methodology for the Development of Bioinformatics’. The journal of American Science” Volume 4 (1), 2008, USA. ISSN 1545-1003</div>\r\n    </li>\r\n   <li >\r\n     <div align=\"justify\">Syed Ahsan, and Abad Shah. Data Mining, Semantic Web and Advanced Information Technologies for Fighting Terrorism’ ? IEEE International Symposium on Biometrics & Security Technologies, ISBAST Karachi, March 2008. </div>\r\n   </li>\r\n      <li>\r\n        <div align=\"justify\">Syed Ahsan, and Abad Shah. Quality Metrics for Semantic Web in Bioinformatics. The 2007 International Conference on Information and Knowledge Engineering (IKE, 07). Las Vegas, USA</div>\r\n      </li>\r\n   <li>\r\n     <div align=\"justify\">	Syed Ahsan, and Abad Shah. Biological Databanks: Distribution, Heterogeneity, Diversity and Provenance. 7th Workshop on Distributed Data and Structures. Santa Clara, California, January 4-5, 2006</div>\r\n   </li>\r\n  	<li>\r\n  	  <div align=\"justify\">Syed Ahsan and Abad Shah. Problems and Issues in Managing Biological data.BIC’05, International Symposium on Bio-Inspired Computing. Malaysia, September 5-7, 2005.</div>\r\n  	</li>\r\n   </ul>\r\n</li>\r\n\r\n<li><font size=\"2\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\"><strong>Conferences Organized</strong></font>\r\n	<ul type=\"circle\">\r\n		<li>\r\n		  <div align=\"justify\">Conference Chair for IKE’07, WorldComp 07 Las Vegas, USA. June 2007.</div>\r\n		</li>\r\n    </ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><font size=\"2\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\"><strong>Papers/ Book Chapters  Reviewed</strong></font>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <div align=\"justify\">&ldquo;A service based Quality Model Web Services&rdquo; for ACIT  2005 Al-Zaytoonah University of Jordon.</div>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <div align=\"justify\">&ldquo;A High Performance Computing Method for Data  Allocation in Distributed Database Systems&rdquo;. Journal of Super Computing,  U.S.A.,&nbsp;&nbsp; </div>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <div align=\"justify\">&ldquo;Differentiated Process Support for Large Software  Support&rdquo;. Journal of E-Supply Chain Management.</div>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <div align=\"justify\">&ldquo;Risk Assessment for Evolutionary Development of  Complex Real-Time Software System. Journal of E-Supply Chain Management.</div>\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <br />\r\n  <font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Collaborative Research/ Faculty Research:   </font>\r\n  <p align=\"justify\">Co-Principal  Investigator for HEC funded project, &lsquo;Development of Analysis Node for  Establishment of Bioinformatics Resource Facility&rsquo; at U.E.T., Lahore, Pakistan.<br />\r\n</p>\r\n  </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO `people` (`people_id`, `url_name`, `user_id`, `designation_id`, `group_id`, `post_id`, `title`, `fname`, `lname`, `url`, `email`, `off_no`, `ext`, `cell_no`, `fax_no`, `image_name`, `seqno`, `biography`, `research_interest`, `status`, `is_core_team`) VALUES
(115, 'Dr.AbadAliShah', 115, 13, 8, 13, 'Dr.', 'Abad Ali ', 'Shah', '', 'abadshah@uet.edu.pk;abad_shah@hotmail.com', '+92-42-902-9499 ;+92-42-925-0220 ;+ 92-42-669-6793-3022 ', '', '   +92-300-478-2122 ', '', 'malePic.jpg', 0, '<div align=\"justify\">Prof. Dr. Abad Ali Shah is an HEC foreign faculty at Department of Computer Science& Engineering U.E.T., Lahore. He did is Ph. D. in Computer Science from Wayne State University, Michigan USA and his Master in Computer Science from Renseller Polytechnique Institute, New York USA. He is also the Principal Investigator for HEC funded project, ‘Development of Analysis Node for Establishment of Bioinformatics Resource Facility’ at U.E.T., Lahore, Pakistan. Dr. Abad has more then twenty five years of teaching experience at Wayne State University and later at King Saud University, Saudi Arabia. His research interests include Database Systems, Software Engineering, Bioinformatics, Semantic Web, Ontologies and Distribute Databases which has resulted in almost hundred research publications in international books, journals and conferences.  Dr. Abad is a Quaid-e-Azam Award holder from Quaid-e-Azam University., Islamabad. </div>\r\n', '<br />\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n    <ul>\r\n        <li>Database  Management Systems</li>\r\n      <li> Bioinformatics</li>\r\n      <li> Web Databases</li>\r\n      <li> Hypermedia Systems</li>\r\n      <li> Semantic  Web</li>\r\n      <li> Web Engineering</li>\r\n      <li>Information Retrieval (IR) Software Engineering&nbsp; </li>\r\n      <li>Software Development Methodologies</li>\r\n      <li> Software  Metrics Data Modeling</li>\r\n      <li>Information Systems</li>\r\n    </ul>\r\n	\r\n    <p><font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\">Publications</font></p>\r\n  <ul  type=\"square\">\r\n    <li><font size=\"2\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\"><strong>Book Chapters </strong></font>\r\n      <ul>\r\n        <li>Ahsan, S. and Shah, A., Book Chapter Entitled &ldquo;Quality Metrics for Evaluating  Data Provenance,&rdquo; the book entitled,&ldquo; <strong><em>Chapter XV</em></strong> Designing Software-Intensive Systems:  Methods and Principles&rdquo; the <em>I</em>dea  Group Publishing<em>, </em>USA, 2008. </li>\r\n        <li>Shah, A., Adeniyi, J. and Al- Twairqi &ldquo;An  Algorithm For Transforming XML Documents Schema Into Relational Database  Schema,&rdquo; Chapter VII of the Book Entitled &ldquo;<em>Transformation of Knowledge,  Information and Data: Theory and Applications</em>&rdquo;, the <em>I</em>dea Group Publishing<em>, </em>USA,  Pp 171-189., 2005 </li>\r\n        <li>Shah, A., &ldquo;OODM: An Object-Oriented Design  Methodology for Development of Web Applications,&rdquo; Chapter X of the book Entitled<em>&ldquo;Information Modeling For Internet Applications,&rdquo;</em> <em>I</em>dea  Group Publishing<em>, </em>USA, 2003, ISBN:1-591-40050-3, Pp 189-229.</li>\r\n        <li>Ahsan S.  and Shah A., &lsquo;Web Services for Bioinformatics&rsquo;. Methodologies for  Non-Functional&nbsp;&nbsp; Requirements in Service  Oriented Architecture. Information Science Reference, USA  (Accepted)</li>\r\n      </ul>\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n  <ul type=\"square\">\r\n    <li><font size=\"2\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\"><strong>Jounals </strong></font> </li>\r\n  \r\n        <ul>\r\n          <li>Shah,  A., Adeniyi, J. and Al- Twairqi &ldquo;An Efficient Algorithm For Transforming XML  Documents Schema Into Relational Database Schema,&rdquo; <em>the International  Journal of Computer Science (IJCS), USA </em>(commutated)</li>\r\n          <li>Mustafa, G.,  Shah, A., and Vashishta, A., &ldquo;Visual Data Mining subject to Positivity  Constraint,&rdquo; <em>the Journal of Universal  Computer Science</em>, a publication of the <a href=\"javascript:ol(\'http://www.know-center.at/\');\">Know-Center </a>in  cooperation with <a href=\"javascript:ol(\'http://www.springer.de/\');\">Springer  Publishers </a>, <a href=\"javascript:ol(\'http://www.joanneum.at/\');\">JOANNEUM RESEARCH </a>and <a href=\"javascript:ol(\'http://www.iicm.edu/\');\">IICM,  Graz University of Technology</a> (communicated)</li>\r\n          <li>Singhera, Z., Horowitz, E.,  and Shah, A., &ldquo;A Graphical User Interface (GUI) Testing Methodology&rdquo; <em>the International Journal of </em><em>Information Technology &amp; Web  Engineering, 3(2)</em>, April-June, 2008, Pp. 1-17. </li>\r\n          <li>Ahsan, S. and Shah, A. &ldquo;A  Framework For Agile Methodologies For Development of Bioinformatics<em>,&rdquo;&nbsp;&nbsp; the  Journal of American Science, Volume<br>\r\n            4 - Number 1 (ISSN 1545-1003)</em>, January  2008 Pp.20-32.</li>\r\n          <li>Shah, A., Fotouhi, F. and Grosky, W.,&ldquo;A Temporal Object  System&nbsp; for a&nbsp; Clinical&nbsp;  Environment,&rdquo; <em>the International  Journal of Software Engineering, 1(1), 2007</em>, Pp. 2-11.</li>\r\n          <li>Abdul-Nasir and Shah, A., &ldquo;Digitization&rsquo;s of Legal  Documents,&rdquo; the <em>E:Gov Magazine, India, February 2007 Issue, Pp. 32-35.</em></li>\r\n          <li>Shah, A., Fotouhi, F., and Grosky, W., &ldquo;Operators of  the Temporal Object-Oriented System and their Implementation,&rdquo; <em>the  International Journal of Information Sciences (INS), </em>Elsevier Publisher,  the Netherlands,  158(2004) Pp 37-68.</li>\r\n          <li>Shah, A., &ldquo;A Methodology For  Transferring Huge Raw Multimedia Data of an Application and Its Design Into a  Web-Based Information System,&rdquo; <em>the  Egyptian Computer Science Journal</em>,  Vol. 25, No. 2, 2003, Pp. 69-87.</li>\r\n          <li>Shah, A., &ldquo;A Framework for Life-Cycle of the  Prototype-Based Software Development Methodologies,&rdquo;<em> the Journal of King   Saud University</em>, <em>Vol.  13</em>, Pp. 105-125, 2001.</li>\r\n          <li>Shah,  A., &ldquo