.74.</li>\r\n        <li>Shoaib, M. and  Shah, A. &ldquo;Indexing Technques for Information Retreival,&rdquo; <em>the International Journal of Software Engineering, 1(1), 2007</em>, Pp.  73.</li>\r\n      </ul>\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<ul>\r\n  <li><font size=\"2\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\"><strong>Conferences </strong></font></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <ul>\r\n      <li>Shah, A. &ldquo;A New  Dynamic Weight Assignment Schema for Index Terms Based on Statistical  Approach,&rdquo; (to be communicated)</li>\r\n      <li>Shah, A., Khalid,  H., Ahsan, S. and Naseer I., &ldquo;Query Model for Object-Oriented Data Model  of Protein Structures,&rdquo; <em>the 2008  International Conference on Bioinformatics and  Computational Biology</em> (BIOCOMP\'08: uly  14-17, 2008), USA  (accepted)</li>\r\n      <li>Farooq, A. and  Shah, A. &ldquo;Structured-Based Similarity Measuring Between Ontologies,&rdquo; <em>the Proceedings of the  2nd International Conference on Information and Communication  Technologies (ICICT 2007)</em> Karachi, 15-16 December, Pp. 85-91.</li>\r\n      <li>Ahsan S. and  Shah, A., &ldquo;A Software Engineering Methodolgy for&nbsp; Evolutionary Domains&quot; <em>the Proceedings of the 25th International Conference  on Conceptual Modeling&nbsp; (ER2006)</em> Tucson, Arizona,   USA. November 6  - 9, 2006.(communicated)</li>\r\n      <li>Asif, K., Shah,  A. and Farooq, A. &ldquo;Modeling Ontology Evolution Using the Temporal Object  System,&rdquo; <em>the Proceedings of the 2nd  International Conference on Information and Communication Technologies (ICICT  2007)</em> Karachi, 15-16 December, Pp. 99-104.</li>\r\n      <li>Ali, K.,&nbsp; Shah,  A., Farooq, H. and Ali, A., &ldquo;A Bernoulli Process Approximation for the Reverse  Translation of Protein to DNA/mRNA,&rdquo; <em>the  Proceedings of International Conference on Bioinformatics &amp; Computational  Biology, Monte Carlo Resort  BIOCOMP\'07- The 2007</em>, Las Vegas, Nevada, USA, June 25-28, 2007, Pp. 446-451. &nbsp;</li>\r\n      <li>Ahsan, S. and  Shah, A., &rdquo;Quality Metrics for Semantic Web in Bioinformatics,&rdquo; <em>the Proceedings of the 2007 International  Conference on Information and Knowledge Engineering (IKE\'07),</em> June 25-28, 2007), Las Vegas, USA,  Pp. 359-272.</li>\r\n      <li>&nbsp;Shah, A. Amjad Farooq and Kashif Talib, &ldquo;User-Oriented Identity  Management Model for Web-Services,&rdquo; <em>the  Proceeding of the 4th International Symposium on High Capacity  Optical Networks and Enabling Technologies</em>, November 18-20, 2007, UAE, Pp 1-8. </li>\r\n      <li>Farooq, A., Shah,  A. and Asif, K., &ldquo;Designing of Ontology Semantic Web Engineering Provess,&rdquo; <em>the Proceeding of the 4th  International Symposium on High Capacity Optical Networks and Enabling  Technologies (HONET)</em>, November 18-20, 2007, UAE, Pp 1-6. </li>\r\n      <li>Syed  W., &nbsp;Shah, A. and Syed W., &ldquo;Challenges  of Quality in Higher Education and their Solutions,&rdquo; the  2007 International Conference on Information and Knowledge Engineering (IKE\'07:  June 25-28, 2007),  Las Vegas, USA, Pp. 351-358.</li>\r\n      <li>Farooq, A. Shah, A. and Akram, Q. &ldquo; Web-ontology Populating Methodology,&ldquo; the 2007 International Conference on Information and Knowledge Engineering(IKE\'07: June 25-28, 2007), Las Vegas, USA, Pp. 297-302. </li>\r\n      <li>Shah, A. and&nbsp; Mohammad A. ALGhalayini, &ldquo;Introducing The (POSSDI) Process:&nbsp;  The Process of Optimizing the Selection of The Scanned Document Images,&rdquo; the International Joint Conferences on Computer, Information, and Systems  Sciences, and Engineering (CIS2E 06), Technically Co-Sponsored  by:&nbsp; Institute  of Electrical &amp; Electronics Engineers (IEEE) University of Bridgeport,  December4-14, 2006, Pp. 313-324.</li>\r\n      <li><strong>Mustafa G., Shah A. and Asim M. &ldquo;Gridding Multivariate Positive Data for  Real Time Visualization,&rdquo; <em>the </em></strong><em>Proceedings  of the International Conference on Computer Graphics, Imaging and Visualization</em>, Sydney Australia 2006, ISBN:0-7695-2606-3, IEEE Computer  Society&nbsp; Washington, DC, USA  &nbsp;Pp. 496 &ndash; 502.&nbsp; </li>\r\n      <li>Shoaib, M. Arshad, S. Shah, A. &ldquo;Data Representation,  Extraction and Integration Process for&nbsp;  Web and Databases,&rdquo; <em>the 2006  International Conference on Information and Knowledge Engineering (IKE\'06)</em>June 26-29, 2006, Las Vegas, USA,  pp. 56-62.</li>\r\n      <li>Farooq, A., Shah, A. and Qasim Akram, &ldquo;A Technique for  Generating Semantic Web Documents.&rdquo; <em>the  2006 International Conference on Information and Knowledge Engineering (IKE\'06:  June 26-29, 2006,</em> Las Vegas, USA, pp, 264-269.&nbsp;</li>\r\n      <li>Asif, K. and Shah, A. &ldquo;Alignment and Integration of  Ontologies: Challenges and Problems,&rdquo; <em>the  International Conference on Software Engineering (ISE06)</em>, April 14-15, 2006, Pp.  32-35.</li>\r\n      <li>Ahsan, S., and Shah, A., &ldquo;Front Line States in Fight  Against Terrorism and Role of IT: Failures, Challenges and Initiatives,&rdquo; <em>the Proceeding of Dependability Aspects on  Data Warehousing and Mining Applications (DAWAN 2006) Conference, Austria, &nbsp;April 20-22, 2006. </em></li>\r\n      <li>Farooq, A., Asif, K. and Shah, A, &ldquo;Ontology  Construction For Semantic Web,&rdquo; the International Conference on Software  Engineering (ISE06), April 14-15,   2006, Pp. 40-45.</li>\r\n      <li>Arshad, S., Shoaib, M. and Shah, A. &ldquo;Intellectual  Property Right Issues From Software Engineering Perspective,&rdquo; the International  Conference on Software Engineering (ISE06), April 14-15, 2006, Pp. 118-121.</li>\r\n      <li>Singhera, Z. and Shah, A. &ldquo;Extended Web Services Framework to Model  Non-Functional Requirements,&rdquo; the Web Services  Modeling and Implementation using sound Web Engineering Practices (SMIWEP  2006)&nbsp; (Workshop held in conjunction with ICWE 2006 July 11, 2006 Palo  Alto, California, USA. </li>\r\n      <li>Arshad, S., Shoaib M. and Shah, A.,&rdquo;  Testing and Validation of Web-Based Software&rsquo;s,&rdquo; the National Computer  Conference (NCC), Saudi    Arabia, 2006, pp. 151-158.</li>\r\n      <li>Shoaib, M., Arshad, S., Shah, A. and Ali, A. &ldquo;A  Methodology For Indexing and Retrieval Information From XML Documents,&rdquo; the National Computer Conference (NCC), Saudi Arabia,  2006, pp. 147-150.</li>\r\n      <li>Shoaib M, and Shah, A., &ldquo;A Technique for Making Dynamic Index Files of IR  Systems,&rdquo; <em>the third International  Conference on Innovative Applications of formation Technology For Developing World, Nepal</em>,  Dec 10-12, 2005.  (accepted) </li>\r\n      <li>Arhad, S., Mohammad, S. and Sghah, A. &quot;Proposed  Life-Cycle Model &nbsp;For Web-Based Hypermedia Applications Development Methodologies.&rdquo; <em>the Proceedings of the International  Conference on Systems, </em><em>Computing  Sciences and Software Engineering (SCSS</em> 2005, CT, USA </li>\r\n      <li>Shah, A. and Ahsan, S. &ldquo;Problems and Issues in  Managing Biological Data,&rdquo; <em>the Proceedings  of </em><em>International Symposium on Bio-Inspired Computing 2005(</em><em>BIC 05)</em>, Malaysia.  September 6- 10, 2005, pp. 206-210. </li>\r\n      <li>Shoaib, M.&nbsp; and  Shah, A., &ldquo;Remote Information Retrieval Using Cell Phone,&rdquo; <em>the International Conference on Software  Engineering Research &amp; Practice (SERP\'05</em> June 27-30, 2005,  Las Vegas, US, Pp. 890-896.</li>\r\n      <li>Ahsan, S and&nbsp;&nbsp;  Shah, A., &rdquo;Identification of Biological Data Issues and Challenges  through Real World Examples&rdquo; <em>the International Arab  Conference on Information Technology (ACIT 2005)</em> Amman, Jordon. December 6-8, 2005), pp. 344-348. </li>\r\n      <li>Shah, A. and Shoaib, M., &ldquo;Sources  of Irrelevancy in Information Retrieval Systems,&rdquo;<em> the International Conference on Software Engineering Research &amp;  Practice (SERP\'05 </em>June27-30, 2005, Las Vegas, USA,  Pp 877-883.</li>\r\n      <li>Ahsan, S. and Shah, A. &ldquo;Need for  Cooperation between Academia and Industry in&nbsp;Developing Countries,&rdquo; <em>the  International Arab Conference On Information Technology (ACIT 2005)</em> Amman,  Jordon. December 6-8, 2005),  pp. 467-470. </li>\r\n      <li>Shoaib, M., Shah, A., and Vashishta, A. &ldquo;A Dynamic  Indexing Technique for IR Systems,&rdquo; the<em> First International Conference of Information and Communication Technologies, Pakistan</em>, August 27-28, 2005. Pp.  272-275.</li>\r\n      <li>Shoaib, M., Habib-ur-Rehman and Shah, A. &ldquo;Visualization of Retrieved  Positive Data Using Blending Function ,&rdquo; <em>the  First International Conference of Information and Communication Technologies,  Pakistan</em>, August 27-28, 2005, Pp. 255-262.</li>\r\n      <li>Vashishta, A. and Shah, A., &ldquo;An Approach For  Extracting Information From Narrative Web Information Sources,&rdquo; <em>the 37th  Annual Midwest Instruction and Computer  Symposium, </em>Morris MN, USA,April 16-17, 2004</li>\r\n      <li>Shah, A. and Mathkour, H., &ldquo;Modeling of A Medical  Information System Using the Temporal Object System,&rdquo; the 8th Asian  Pacific Conference on Communications, Information and Communication Technology,  17-20 September 2002, Indonesia...</li>\r\n      <li>Mathkour H. and Shah A., &ldquo;Framework For Development of  Web Applications,&rdquo; the joint meeting of the 5th World Multi-conference on  Systemics, Cybernetics and Informatics (SCI 2001) and the 7th International  Conference on Information Systems Analysis and Synthesis (ISAS 2001), USA,  2001. pp. 480-485.</li>\r\n      <li>Shah A., and Mathkour, H., &ldquo;SELF Programming Language  as an Implementation Tool,&rdquo; <em>Proceedings of the 16th National  Conference for Computers,</em> Saudi    Arabia, February 4-7, 2001, Pp. 347-358.</li>\r\n      <li>Jawed, M., Shah, A., and Mathkour, H., &ldquo;Knowledge  Discovery in Databases (KDD) - An Overview,&rdquo; <em>Symposium of Saudi Computer Society on Computer Networking and  Distributed Databases</em>, March 1998, Pp 143-151. </li>\r\n      <li>Singhera, Z., Shah, A., Al-Bargi, M., &ldquo;Islamic  Information on CyberSpace - Issues and Challenges,&rdquo; the Symposium of Saudi  Computer Society on Networking and Distributed Databases, March 1998, Pp  183-194. </li>\r\n      <li>Shah A., and Mathkour, H., &ldquo;Developing an Application  Using SELF Programming Language,&rdquo; <em>ECOOP\'96  Workshop WS14,</em> Linz, Austria, July 9, 1996. (accepted) </li>\r\n      <li>Singhera, Z., Agrawal, J., Shah, A., Martin, J.,  Adeniyi, J., and Mathkour, H., &ldquo;Should IS be Split into Two Independent  Disciplines?&rdquo;<em> Proceedings of the World  Wide</em> <em>IS Educators Conference  (WISE&rsquo;95)</em>, <em>World Wide</em>, Denver, Colorado,   USA, June 10-14, 1995, Pp.  165-169.</li>\r\n      <li>Agrawal,J., Adeniyi, J., Singhera,&nbsp; Z., Shah, A., Mathkour, H., and. Martin,, J,  &ldquo;Need for Special Industry-University Cooperative Programs,&rdquo;<em> Proceedings of the World Wide</em> <em>IS Educators Conference (WISE&rsquo;95)</em>, Denver, Colorado,   USA, June 10-14, 1995. Pp  124-128.</li>\r\n      <li>Martin, J., Agrawal, J., Adeniyi, J., r Singhera,&nbsp; Z., Shah, A., and Mathkour, H., &ldquo;Bridging the  Gap between Industry Experience and the Classroom,&rdquo; <em>Proceedings of the World Wide</em> <em>IS  Educators Conference (WISE&rsquo;95)</em>, Colorado, USA, June 10-14, 1995, Pp  110-115.</li>\r\n      <li>Mathkour, H., Agrawal. J., and Shah, A., &ldquo;Complexity  Measure for OOD Programs in Ada,&rdquo; <em>Proceedings of the 13th Annual National  Conference on Ada  Technology, Pennsylvania, USA, March 13-16, 1995,  Pp 179-184.</em></li>\r\n      <li>Zakzouk, T. S.&nbsp; Mathkour,  H., and Shah, A., &ldquo;Design of the Plan Manager for the STDT,&rdquo; <em>Proceedings of the</em> <em>IASTED International Conference on Modeling and Simulation</em>, July 26-28, 1995, Sri Lanka, Pp.  241-244.</li>\r\n      <li>Zakzouk, T. S.&nbsp;  Mathkour, H., and Shah, A., &ldquo;STDT: A Self-Tuning Tool for Database  Systems &ndash; <em>A Design of the Conceptual  Hierarchy Manager</em>,&rdquo;<em> Proceedings of  the Third International Conference on Artificial Intelligent Applications</em>, Cairo, Egypt,  January 4-7, 1995,  Pp 263-272. </li>\r\n      <li>Al-Khudair, A., Shah, A., and Mathkour, H., &ldquo;Design of  Class-History Management System in Object-Oriented Databases,&rdquo;<em> Proceedings of the VIII International  Symposium in Informatics Application (INFONOR&rsquo;94)</em>,  Antofagasta,   Chile, November 21-25, 1994, Pp  95-101. </li>\r\n      <li>Al-Harbi, S., Shah, A., and Mathkour, H., &ldquo;The FTD-OOD  Methodology with Case Study,&rdquo; <em>Proceedings  of the VIII International Symposium in Informatics Application (INFONOR&rsquo;94)</em>,  Antofagasta, Chile, November 21-25, 1994, Pp 211-217. </li>\r\n      <li>&nbsp;Al-Sayegh, T.,  Shah, A., and Farag, I., &ldquo;Design of Object  Manager for the TOS,&rdquo;<em> Proceedings of the  VIII International Symposium in Informatics Application (INFONOR&rsquo;94)</em>, Antofagasta, Chile, November 21-25, 1994, Pp 103-109.</li>\r\n      <li>Zakzouk, T. S.&nbsp;  Mathkour, H., and Shah, A., &ldquo;A Self Tuning Database Tool,&rdquo;<em> Proceedings of the VIII International  Symposium in Informatics Application (INFONOR&rsquo;94)</em>, Antofagasta, Chile,  November 21-25, 1994,  Pp 79-86.</li>\r\n      <li>Al-Khudair, A., Shah, A., and Mathkour, H., &ldquo;Issues in  Management of Class History in Object-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Oriented  Databases,&rdquo;<em> Proceedings of the Third  International Conference on Intelligent Systems</em>, Las Vegas, Nevada, USA,  June 6-8, 1994, Pp 823-831.</li>\r\n      <li>Al-Harbi, S., Shah, A., and Mathkour, H.,&nbsp; &ldquo;Methodology to Convert a Traditional Design  to an Object-Oriented Design,&rdquo;<em> Proceedings of the Third International Conference on Intelligent Systems</em>,  Las Vegas, Nevada, USA, June 6-8, 1994, Pp 833-842.</li>\r\n      <li>Al-Sayegh, T., Shah, A., and Farag, I., &ldquo;Design Issues  of Object Manager For the TOS,&rdquo;<em> Proceedings of the Third International Conference on Intelligent Systems</em>,  Las Vegas, Nevada, USA, June 6-8, 1994, Pp. 813-822. </li>\r\n      <li>Shah, A., Fotouhi, F., and Grosky, W., &ldquo;Knowledge  Sharing Mechanism for the TOS,&rdquo; <em>Proceedings  of the VIII Brazilian Symposium of Software Engineering (VIII SBES)</em>, Curitba, Brazil,  October 25-28, 1994,  Pp. 211-219.</li>\r\n      <li>Shah, A., Mathkour, H., Fotouhi, F., and Grosky, W.,  &ldquo;A Categorical Formalism for the TOS,&rdquo; <em>Proc.  of the Tenth Conference on Applied Mathematics (CAM-94)</em>, Edmond, Oklahoma, USA, February 4-5, 1994, Pp 212-224.</li>\r\n      <li>Mathkour H., and Shah, A., &ldquo;An Intelligent, and Arabic  SQL Query Processor,&rdquo; <em>Proc. of</em> <em>the Second International Conference on AI  Applications</em>, Cairo, Egypt, January 22-24, 1994, Pp 521-531.</li>\r\n      <li>Shah, A., Fotouhi, F., Grosky, W., Al-Dehlan, A., and  Vashishta, A., &ldquo;A Temporal Object System for a Construction Environment,&rdquo; <em>Proc. of the XIII Conference of the  Brazilian Computer Society&nbsp;&nbsp; (SEMISH-90)</em>,  September, 1993, Pp 211-225.</li>\r\n      <li><strong>*</strong>Shah, A., Fotouhi, F., Grosky, W., Rana, S.P. and&nbsp; Vashishta, A., &ldquo;Offstage Objects and their  Renovations in the Temporal Object System,&rdquo; <em>Proc.  of</em> <em>the third International Symposium  on Database Systems for Advanced Applications</em>, Dejeon, Korea, April 6-8,  1993, Pp 306-312.</li>\r\n      <li><strong>*</strong>Shah, A., Fotouhi, F., and Grosky, W., , &ldquo;Renovation  of Complex Objects in the TOS,&rdquo; <em>Proceedings  of the Twelfth Annual IEEE International Phoenix Conference on Computers &amp;  Communications</em>, Scottdale, Arizona, March&nbsp;  23-26, 1993, Pp 203-209.</li>\r\n      <li>Fotouhi, F., Shah A., and Grosky, W., &ldquo;TOS: A Temporal  Object System,&rdquo; <em>Proceedings of the Fourth  International Conference on Computing &amp; Information (ICCI\'92)</em>, Toronto, Canada,  May 28-30, 1992,  Pp&nbsp; 351-354.</li>\r\n      <li>Fotouhi, F., Shah A., and Grosky, W., &ldquo;Complex Objects  in the Temporal Object System,&rdquo;<em> IEEE  Post-Conference Proceedings of the Fourth International Conference on Computing  &amp; Information</em>, 1992, Pp&nbsp; 381-384.</li>\r\n      <li>Shah A., and. Kaushal, R. P, &ldquo;A Methodology For  Converting An Imperative Design to An Object-Oriented Design,&rdquo; <em>Proceedings of the 23rd Pittsburgh  Conference on Modeling and Simulation</em>, Pittsburgh, April 30-May 1, 1992, Pp  1505-1512.</li>\r\n      <li>Vashishta, A., Shah, A., and Kundur, V. K. R.,  &ldquo;Methods Implementation in Object-Oriented DBMS,&rdquo;<em>Proceedings of Conference Computer Solutions Expo\'90</em>, Michigan, USA, September,  1990, Pp 109-118.</li>\r\n      <li>Ramzan, M., and Shah, A., &ldquo;Design Considerations For  Strain Gauge Pressure Transducers,&rdquo; Presented in the <em>Seminar on Explosive and Propellants</em>, Defense Science &amp;  Technology Organization, Chaklala, Rawalpindi, 24-27 July, 1978.</li>\r\n    </ul>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<ul type=\"square\">\r\n  <li><font size=\"2\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\"><strong>Collaborative Research/ Faculty Research: </strong></font></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n  <blockquote>\r\n    <p align=\"left\">Principal  Investigator for HEC funded project, &lsquo;Development of Analysis Node for Establishment  of Bioinformatics Resource Facility&rsquo; at U.E.T., Lahore, Pakistan. </p>\r\n  </blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n<ul type=\"square\">\r\n  <li><font size=\"2\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color:#1b68b0;\"><strong>Work included in Bibliography and cited in Papers</strong></font></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<div align=\"justify\">\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <ul>\r\n      <li>\r\n        <div align=\"left\">In the       bibliography of ACM-SIGMOD RECORD, Vol. 25, No. 1, 1996</div>\r\n      </li>\r\n      <li>\r\n        <div align=\"left\">Salvatore       T. March, Charles A. Wood, Gove N. Allen, &quot;Research Frontiers in       Object Technology&quot;, Information Systems Frontiers Vol. 1 No. 1, pp.       51-74, 1999.<strong># 1.&nbsp; </strong>Included  in Bibliography of Mathematical Review (@004), USA</div>\r\n      </li>\r\n    </ul>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>', 1, 0),
(117, 'Ms.FaizaIftikhar', 117, 134, 7, 55, 'Ms.', 'Faiza', 'Iftikhar', '', 'faiza.iftikhar@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029450', ' - 823 - 80', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'malePic.jpg', 0, 'Ms. Faiza Iftikhar received her Bachelor’s degree in electrical engg. from University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore in 2008.She has been working at Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) in University of Engineering and technology, Lahore, as a Research Assistant since April 2009.\r\n\r\nCurrently she is attached with High Performance Computing and Networking \r\nLab. Her tasks include the development of cluster using commodity PCs. \r\n', '<ul><li>Computer Networks</li>\r\n<li>Distributed Systems\r\n</li></ul>', 1, 0),
(118, 'Ms.HinaJaved', 118, 133, 6, 53, 'Ms.', 'Hina', 'Javed ', '', 'hina.javed@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '829', '', '+92-42-9250246', 'HinaJaved 1062', 0, '<p>Hina Javed received her degree in BS(CS) Computer Science Engineering from Bahauddin Zakariya University, Multan and has done her MS(CS) with specialization in telecommunication in 2009.</p>\r\n<p>She remained on frontline during operation and maintenance of GSM equipment at HUAWEI-UET Joint Telecom IT Center (HUTIC) for 1 year. Currently, she is working at HUTIC on MSOFTX3000, UMG8900, NGN System, Softswitch3000, SGSN and GGSN of Huawei\'s s GSM/GPRS Network equipment.</p>', '', 1, 29),
(121, 'Dr.SarmadHussain', 121, 13, 10, 13, 'Dr.', 'Sarmad', 'Hussain', '', 'sarmad.hussain', '+92-42-99029300, 99029450 - ', '809', '', '+92-42-99250246', 'sarmad_1.JPG', 0, '<p>PhD in Speech Science, Department of Communication Sciences, Northwestern University, Evanston, IL., USA. 1993-1997. Thesis in Experimental Phonology and Phonetics: &acirc;&euro;&oelig;Phonetic Correlates of Lexical Stress in Urdu.&acirc;&euro;? Advisor: Janet Pierrehumbert. Visiting Scholar, Phonetics Laboratory, Oxford University, Oxford, UK.Advisor: John Coleman. MPhil in Computer Speech and Language Processing, Department of Engineering, Cambridge University, Cambridge, UK. 1992-1993. Thesis: &acirc;&euro;&oelig;Synthesis of Urdu Consonants Using Infovox Text-to-Speech System.&acirc;&euro;? Advisor: Sarah Hawkins. BSEE (with Honors) in Electrical Engineering (Computer Eng.), Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, University of Texas at Austin, TX., USA. 1988-1992.</p>', '<div align=\"justify\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family: Times New Roman,Times,serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Publications</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A Novel Approach for Ranking Spelling Error Corrections for Urdu, in Language Resources and Evaluation, Special issue on Asian language technology, Naseem, T. and Hussain, S<span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">.</span> (2007).</li>\r\n<li>Journal Publications A Novel Approach for Ranking Spelling Error Corrections for Urdu, in Language Resources and Evaluation, Special issue on Asian language technology, Naseem, T. and Hussain, S. (2007).</li>\r\n<li>Developing Lexicographic Sorting: An Example for Urdu, in ACM Transactions on Asian Languages Information Processing (2007).</li>\r\n<li>Phonological Processing for Urdu Text to Speech System, in Contemporary Issues in Nepalese Linguistics (eds. Yadava, Bhattarai, Lohani, Prasain and Parajuli), Linguistics Society of Nepal (2005). ISBN 99946-57-69-0. Localisation in Pakistan, in Localisation Focus: The International Journal for Localisation 3(4), LRC, Univ. of Limerick, Ireland (2004). Pan Localisation Regional Initiative: Developing Local Language Computing, in I4D: Information for Development II(6), www.I4Donlinet.net, S. Hussain (2004).</li>\r\n<li>A Longitudinal Investigation of Duration and Temporal Variability in Children&acirc;&euro;&trade;s Speech Production, in Journal of Acoustic Society of America (99) 4. pp. 2344-2349. B. Smith, M. Kenney &amp; S. Hussain (1996).</li>\r\n<li>Large Vocabulary Continuous Speech Recognition for Urdu, submitted to Frontiers of Information Technology (FIT), Islamabad. Sarfraz, H., Hussain, S., Raza, A.A., Ullah, I., Sarfraz, Z (2010).</li>\r\n<li>An ASR System for Spontaneous Urdu Speech, submitted to O-COCOSDA\'10, Nepal, Sarfraz, H., Hussain, S., Raza, A.A., Ullah, I., Sarfraz, Z (2010).</li>\r\n<li>Speech Corpus Development for a Speaker Independent Spontaneous Urdu, submitted to O-COCOSDA\'10, Nepal, Raza, A.A., Hussain, S., Sarfraz, H., Ullah, I., Sarfraz, Z (2010).</li>\r\n<li>Dzongkha Word Segementation, in the Proceedings of the 8th Workshop on Asian Language Resources, COLING2010, Beijing, China. Norbu, S., Choejey, P., Dendup, T., Hussain, S. and Muaz, A. (2010).</li>\r\n<li>Word Segmentation for Urdu OCR, in the Proceedings of the 8th Workshop on Asian Language Resources, COLING2010, Beijing, China. Akram, M. and Hussain, S. (2010).</li>\r\n<li>A hybrid approach to Urdu Verb Phrase chunking, in the Proceedings of the 8th Workshop on Asian Language Resources, COLING2010, Beijing, China. Awan, W. and Hussain, S. (2010). Urdu</li>\r\n<li>Word Segmentation, in Proceedings of NAACL HLT 2010, USA, Durrrani, N. and Hussain, S. (2010).</li>\r\n<li>Transliterating Urdu for a Broad-Coverage Urdu/Hindi LFG Grammar, in the Proceedings of LREC 2010, Malta.</li>\r\n<li>Improving Nastalique Specific Pre-Recognition Process for Urdu OCR, in the Proceedings of 13th IEEE International Multitopic Conference 2009 (INMIC 2009), Islamabad, Pakistan, Javed, S.T, Hussain, S.(2009).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Design and development of phonetically rich Urdu Speech Corpus, in the Proceedings of O-COCOSDA\'09, 10-13 Aug 2009, at the School of Information Science and Engineering of Xinjiang University, Urunqi, China (URL: http://o-cocosda2009.xju.edu.cn), Raza, A.A., Hussain, S., Sarfraz, H., Ullah, I., Sarfraz, Z. (2009).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Assas-band, an Affix-Exception-List Based Urdu Stemmer, in the Proceedings of the 7th Workshop on Asian Language Resources, IJCNLP&acirc;&euro;&trade;09, Suntec City, Singapore (URL: http://www.acl-ijcnlp-2009.org/index.html), Akram, Q., Naseer, A., Hussain, S. (2009).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Analysis and Development of Urdu POS Tagged Corpora, in the Proceedings of the 7th Workshop on Asian Language Resources, IJCNLP&acirc;&euro;&trade;09, Suntec City, Singapore (URL: http://www.acl-ijcnlp-2009.org/index.html), Muaz, A., Ali, A., Hussain, S. (2009).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Semi-Automatic Lexical Functional Grammar Development, in Conference on Language and Technology 2009, CRULP, NUCES, Lahore. U. Khalid, N. Karamat, S. Iqbal and S. Hussain (2009).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Arabic Script Internationalized Domain Names, in CIIT Workshop on Research in Computer (CWRC), Lahore, S. Hussain, N. Karamat and A. Mansoor (2008).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Resources for Urdu Language Processing, in the Proceedings of Workshop on Asian Language Resources, IJCNLP 2008, IIIT Hyderabad, India (2008).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Corpus Based Urdu Lexicon Development, in the Proceedings of Conference on Language Technology 2007, University of Peshawar, Pakistan T. Naseem and S. Hussain (2007).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Spelling Error Trends in Urdu in the Proceedings of Conference on Language Technology 2007, University of Peshawar, Pakistan T. Naseem and S. Hussain (2007).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">SSML for Urdu Speech Synthesis, in the Proceedings of Third Workshop on Internationalizing SSML, World Wide Web Consortium, IIIT Hyderabad, India (2007).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Challenges of Script and Style for Inputting Urdu, at the Meeting of Localization Working Group of 8th Asian Open Source Software, Bali, Indonesia (2007).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Context Sensitive Shape-Substitution in Nastaliq Writing System: Analysis and Formulation, A. Wali and S. Hussain. In the Proceedings of International Joint Conferences on Computer, Information, and Systems Sciences, and Engineering (CIS2E 06) (2006).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Urdu Internationalized Domain Names, in Proceedings of the IEEE International Multi-Topic Conference, Islamabad. S. Hussain, N. Durrani (2006).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Status and Issues of NLP in Developing Asian Countries, Panel on NLP in Developing Asian Countries, Second International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing (IJCNLP), Jeju, Korea (2005).</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Urdu Spell Checker, &acirc;&euro;&oelig;From Localization to Language Processing,&acirc;&euro;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>', 1, 3),
(122, 'Dr.MuhammadTahir', 122, 13, 5, 13, 'Dr.', 'Muhammad', 'Tahir', '', 'tahir', '', '', '', '', 'MuhammadTahir1098jpg', 0, '<p>Dr. Muhammad Tahir is a Ph.D holder</p>', '<p>Research</p>', 0, 5),
(124, 'Mr.SohaibAMalik', 124, 16, 1, 38, 'Mr.', 'Sohaib', 'A. Malik', '', '@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450 - 813', '', '', '', 'malePic.jpg', 0, 'Mr. Sohaib A. Malik ', '<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n1\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n2\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n3\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n4\r\n</li>\r\n', 1, 0),
(125, 'Mr.UmarAkram', 125, 134, 3, 55, 'Mr.', 'Umar', 'Akram', '', 'umar.akram @kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450', '832', '+92-321-7606869', '+92-42-9250246', 'umarakram.jpg', 0, '<p><strong>Mr. Umar Akram</strong> received his BS in computer science from Agriculture   University of Faisalabad in 2007. He has versatile experience of   programming, teaching and   research. He has joined KICS in Jan 2009 as&nbsp; Research Assistant&nbsp;   and since then he played an active role in many research projects.   Currently he is working on uhands: Ubiquitous Help and Disaster System   project and also participating in other research projects like&nbsp; HUMS. He   is an active researcher and&nbsp; his paper publication is in review stage   at   IEEE conference. </p>', '<ul>\r\n  <li>Ubiquitous   Computing</li>\r\n  <li>Artificial  intelligence/ Autonomous Systems/Intelligent Agents</li>\r\n  <li> Distributed Systems</li>\r\n  <li>&nbsp;Information Fusion</li>\r\n  <li> Software   Engineering</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<font size=\"4\" face=\"Times New Roman, Times, serif\" style=\"color: rgb(27, 104, 176);\">Publications</font>\r\n<ul>\r\n  <li>\r\n    <div align=\"justify\"><strong>Imran Sarwar, Wasif Tanveer</strong>, Umar Akram , 2011, &mu;HandS: Ubiquitous Help and Safety services in emergencies.</div>\r\n  </li>\r\n</ul>', 1, 0),
(126, 'Mrs.Quratulain', 126, 134, 1, 55, 'Mrs.', 'Quratulain', '', '', 'quratulain @kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-99029450', '825', '', '+92-42-99250246', 'Quratulain1134', 0, '<p align=\"justify\">Quratulain received her Bachelors degree in Electrical Engineering with a specialization in Telecommunication and Electronics from University of Engineering and technology, Lahore in 2009 and doing her Masters in Telecommunication and Electronics Engineering from the same institute.<br /> She joined Al-Khawarzmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS), UET Lahore in November 2009. During her enduring experience at KICS she has successfully completed many research oriented tasks on Crossbow motes in Sensor Networks Lab. She also has publications in international journals and conferences.</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Remote code update management</li>\r\n<li>Application-specific groups management</li>\r\n<li>Multi-metric routing</li>\r\n</ul>', 1, 0),
(127, 'Ms.FatimaMaqbool', 127, 134, 2, 56, 'Ms.', 'Fatima', 'Maqbool', '', 'fatima.maqbool@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450 ', '829', '', '', 'malePic.jpg', 0, 'Fatima Maqbool received her Bachelors degree in Computer Engineering from University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore in 2009 and doing her Masters in Computer Science \r\nfrom UET Lahore . She joined KICS as a Research Assistant in August 2010 and currently working at Embedded Systems & Enterprise Software Solutions Lab. Currently she is working on Invoice Processing Automation System (I.P.A.S) project.\r\n', '', 1, 0),
(128, 'Ms.MehwishNadeem', 128, 132, 2, 38, 'Ms.', 'Mehwish', 'Nadeem', '', 'mehwish.nadeem@kics.edu.pk', '+92-42-9029300, 9029450 ', '829', '', '', 'MehwishNadeem1152', 3, '<p>Mehwish Nadeem received her Master degree in Information Technology from Punjab University of Information Technology (PUCIT), Lahore in 2009. She is doing her MS/M.Phil in Computer Science from UET Lahore . She has joined KICS as a Research Assistant in July 2010 and is currently working at Embedded Systems &amp; Enterprise Software Solutions Lab. Currently, she is working on Invoice Processing Automation System (I.P.A.S) project.</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Information Retrieval Methodologies</li>\r\n<li>Programming Languages</li>\r\n<li>Web Technologies</li>\r\n</ul>', 1, 0),
