(262, 'dr_imran_mehmood', 262, 13, 1, 13, 'Dr.', 'Imran', 'Mahmood', '', 'imahmood@kics.edu.pk', '', '', '', '', 'Ahsan SaleemKhan2358', 0, '<p><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Career Summary</strong></span><br /><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Working as Assistant Professor at Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science, UET, Lahore; Performed teaching duties and supervised ongoing research projects as Lead researcher at the Center for Visual Analytics Research; Earned Doctoral degree in Computer Systems at School of Information and Communication Technology (ICT), <strong>KTH-Royal Institute of Technology Sweden</strong> in 2013; Earned <strong>MS degree in Software Engineering of Distributed Systems</strong> from the same university in 2007; More than 7 years of experience as academic researcher. Comprehensive knowledge of <strong>Modeling &amp; Analysis of Complex systems</strong>, derived from extensive academic &amp; industrial training. Worked in collaboration with <strong>Swedish Defense research agency (FOI)</strong> during the Masters and Doctoral research; Published quality research papers and delivered different workshops, lectures and invited talks; has served in IT industry earlier at various leading roles, at different private and governmental organizations.</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>PhD Thesis:</strong> A Verification Framework for Component Based Modeling and Simulation - \"Putting the pieces together\"</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Research Focus:</strong> Component based Modeling and Simulation; Formal Verification, Model Checking, System Theory, Dynamical Systems, Real-Time Systems, Stochastic Systems, Composability and Probabilistic Verification.</span></p>\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Research Domains:</span></strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Defnese Modeling and Simulation</span></li>\r\n<li><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Healthcare Modeling and Simulation <br /></span></li>\r\n</ul>', 1, 0),
(263, 'ali.ayyaz', 354, 134, 24, 54, 'Mr.', 'Ali', 'Ayyaz', '', 'ali.ayyaz@kics.edu.pk', '', '', '03214747974', '', 'AliAyyaz2367', 0, '<p>Ali is a UET graduate (BS-Elect-2008 and MS-CS-2015). Ali joined KICS in 2013 and has been working as a Research Officer/Developer since then. His interest in game development led to the desire to set up a Game Development Center at UET, the idea of which was put forward by him in January 2016. After months of planning, the dream finally came into being on 18th July, 2016. Currently Ali is the program coordinator at UET Game Studio, leading the design and development of games, as well as providing trainings to students in the field of Game Development.</p>', '<p>Visual Analytics, Data Science, Information Visualization</p>', 1, 0),
