, 1),
(36, 6, 'KICS is offering a short course \"Programming Multi-Core Processors, A Hands-On Approach for Embedded, Mobile, and Distributed Systems Development\" from July 18-29, 2011 ', '<p>Multicore processors are being adopted not only in servers and desktops but also in mobile devices. However, multicore processor adoption for software developers is not a free lunch. It introduces a unique set of challenges to software development, debugging, tuning, deployment, and maintenance. This short course will focus on state-of-the-art technologies and programming environments for leading multicore processors: Cavium Networks&rsquo; Octeon Processor using Octeon SDK, ARM multicore processors based mobile devices using Android, General Purpose Nvidia GPUs using CUDA (Compute Unified Device Architecture), IBM Cell Processor using Cell-SDK, Cloud Computing using Hadoop/MapReduce, and Virtualization using KVM hypervisor. </p>\r\n<p>To Download Flyer <a href=\"images/pmcp2011.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">&lt;&lt;click here&gt;&gt; </a></p>\r\n<p>For Online Registration <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/pmcp.php\" target=\"_blank\">&lt;&lt;click here&gt;&gt; </a></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '2011-07-15', 0, 1),
(34, 3, 'For the first time, UET technical societies (IEEE-UET,  IET-UET, EC-UET, WIE-UET, ACM-UET and ASME-UET) are organizing a 4-day mega event, <strong>UET Techno Fest &rsquo;11 </strong>(<strong>18-21 May, 2011</strong>) at UET, Lahore', '<p><br />\r\n  <strong>UET TECHNO FEST &rsquo;11</strong></p>\r\n<p>  For the first time, the technical societies from the  faculties of Electrical, Computer Science and Mechanical Engineering at  University of Engineering and Technology Lahore (IEEE-UET, IET-UET, EC, WIE-UET,  ACM-UET and ASME-UET) are organizing a 4-day  event, <strong>UET Techno Fest &rsquo;11 </strong>(<strong>18-21 May, 2011</strong>). It will feature different  signature events of all the collaborating societies in one package, providing  exactly what an enthusiastic participant wants. The event will feature a wide  variety of; &nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n  <li>Competitions</li>\r\n  <li>Aawareness  conferences</li>\r\n  <li>Seminars on  non-technical topics</li>\r\n  <li>Women forum </li>\r\n  <li>Job fair &nbsp;and Entertainment </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The  purpose of the event is to provide students with an opportunity to showcase  their engineering skills such as circuit designing, programming and coding in a  wide variety of competitions, learn about the latest business trends, highlight  their abilities in non-technical skills such as delivering presentations,  drawing and photography, gain experience by interacting with professionals from  the industry, and much more&hellip;.! <a href=\"http://theiet.org.pk/uettechnofest/\">&lt;readmore&gt;  </a> | <a href=\"http://www.uet.edu.pk/export/sites/UETWebPortal/newsannouncement/newssection/Advertisement/finale1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">&lt;Even Poster&gt;</a></p>\r\n', NULL, '2011-05-10', 0, 1),
(35, 5, 'Sealed quotations are invited from the authorized dealers for the supply of Servers, <strong>Computer Systems, Laptops, Rack, KVM switch and</strong> <strong>UPS</strong> for Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science, University of the Engineering and Technology, Lahore. ', '<div align=\"center\"><strong>Tender Notice </strong></div>\r\n<p>Sealed quotations are invited from the authorized dealers for the supply of Servers, <strong>Computer Systems, Laptops, Rack, KVM switch and</strong> <strong>UPS</strong> for Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science, University of the Engineering and Technology, Lahore. </p>\r\n<p><strong>The supply items include:&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong></p>\r\n<div align=\"center\">\r\n  <table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n    <tbody>\r\n      <tr>\r\n        <td width=\"49\"><p><strong>Sr.#</strong></p></td>\r\n        <td width=\"328\"><p><strong>Item/Description</strong></p></td>\r\n        <td width=\"59\"><p><strong>Qty</strong></p></td>\r\n      </tr>\r\n      <tr>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"49\"><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;</p></td>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"328\"><p>Server Machines &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; (DELL, IBM, HP)</p></td>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"59\"><p align=\"center\">6</p></td>\r\n      </tr>\r\n      <tr>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"49\"><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;</p></td>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"328\"><p>Laptops &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; (Sony, DELL, IBM)</p></td>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"59\"><p align=\"center\">12</p></td>\r\n      </tr>\r\n      <tr>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"49\"><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;</p></td>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"328\"><p>Computers &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; (DELL, HP, IBM)</p></td>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"59\"><p align=\"center\">40</p></td>\r\n      </tr>\r\n      <tr>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"49\"><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;</p></td>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"328\"><p>Server Rack</p></td>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"59\"><p align=\"center\">1</p></td>\r\n      </tr>\r\n      <tr>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"49\"><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;</p></td>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"328\"><p>6KVA/3950W UPS / Batteries</p></td>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"59\"><p align=\"center\">1</p></td>\r\n      </tr>\r\n      <tr>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"49\"><p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;</p></td>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"328\"><p>KVM Switch</p></td>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"59\"><p align=\"center\">1</p></td>\r\n      </tr>\r\n      <tr>\r\n        <td valign=\"top\" width=\"49\"><p>&nbsp;</p></td>\r\n        <td width=\"328\"><p align=\"right\"><strong>Total Rs.</strong></p></td>\r\n        <td width=\"59\"><p align=\"center\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p></td>\r\n      </tr>\r\n    </tbody>\r\n  </table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>The detailed specifications of the supply items and terms and conditions for the purchase are given in <strong>Tender Documents</strong> that may be <strong>obtained, effective from 4th July, 2011,</strong> during normal working hours, from the office of the Director, Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science on the <strong>payment of Rs.2,000/-</strong> (by Bank Draft in favor of the <strong>Director, Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science, UET, Lahore</strong> or cash deposited in HBL UET Branch).</p>\r\n<p>The sealed quotations along with the bank draft against earnest money will be <strong>received </strong>in the office of the Director, Al-Khawarizmi Institute <strong>by 18th July, 2011 till 11:00am </strong>and will be <strong>opened</strong>, by the Chairman Pur&shy;chase Committee, <strong>on the same day at 11:30am</strong> in the Seminar Hall, Al-Khawarizmi Institute in the presence of the bidders or their representative.</p>\r\n<p>The   Chairman Purchase Committee may reject any quotation without assigning   any reason and may change the above mentioned quantities. </p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>(Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood)</strong></p>\r\n<p>Director</p>', NULL, '2011-07-11', 0, 1),
(33, 1, 'Center for Language Engineering at KICS-UET, is co-organizing Conference on Human Language Technology for Development 2011 at Bibliotheca Alexandrina, in Alexandria, Egypt. ', 'Human Language Technology (HLT) is a growing field of research and development, converging multiple disciplines including computer science, engineering, linguistics, sociology and cognitive sciences, striving to develop a natural, easy and effective user interaction with Information and Communication Technology.&nbsp; HLT, including localization, is particularly relevant for addressing access to information by the disadvantaged communities, including the illiterate, the rural poor, and the physically challenged population, especially in the developing countries.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\">HLTD 2011 (<a href=\"http://www.hltd.org/\" target=\"_blank\">www.HLTD.org</a>) aims to promote interaction among researchers and professionals working on language technology, language computing industry, civil society engaged with deployment of language technology to end-users, and policy makers planning the use of HLT in national development projects. It is hoped that the Conference will highlight HLTD challenges in the developing regions, especially in Asia and Africa.</p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\">The Conference is jointly organized by the PAN Localization Network (PAN L10n,<a href=\"http://www.panl10n.net/\" target=\"_blank\">www.PANL10n.net</a>) of Asia at CLE (<a href=\"http://www.cle.org.pk/\" target=\"_blank\">www.CLE.org.pk</a>), KICS, UET, &nbsp;and the African Network for Localization (ANLoc,<a href=\"http://www.africanlocalisation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">www.africanlocalisation.net</a>) Zuza Software Foundation.&nbsp; It is supported by Canada&rsquo;s International Development Research Centre (IDRC,&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.idrc.ca/\" target=\"_blank\">www.idrc.ca</a>) Canada, and hosted by Bibliotheca Alexandrina, Egypt.', NULL, '2011-04-09', 0, 1),
(32, 2, 'On the occasion of International Mother Language Day (21st February 2011), Center for Language Engineering (CLE) at KICS-UET, Lahore is pleased to announce the launch of Online Torwali Dictionary (OTD).\r\n', '<table width=\"100%\" border=\"1\">\r\n\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td class=\"topheading\">Release of Online Torwali Dictionary</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td><p align=\"left\" class=\"titleheading\"><span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\">Announcing release of </span> <strong><span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\">Online Torwali Dictionary</span></strong> <a href=\"http://www.cle.org.pk/software/ling_resources/otd.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cle.org.pk/software/ling_resources/otd.htm</a></p>\r\n      <DIV align=\"justify\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n        <p align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\">This year International Mother Language Day (21st February  2011,</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span><a href=\"http://www.un.org/en/events/motherlanguageday/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.un.org/en/events/motherlanguageday/</a><span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\">)</span><span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\"> </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\">focuses on using  &ldquo;information and communication technologies for the safeguarding and promotion  of languages and linguistic diversity&rdquo;:</span></p>\r\n          <p><em>&quot;Information and communication technologies can be  especially useful in promoting mother languages. We must harness the power of  progress to protect diverse visions of the world and to promote all sources of  knowledge and forms of expression. These are the threads that weave the  tapestry of humanity&rsquo;s story. &quot;</em></p>\r\n          <p><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Irina  Bokova, Director-General of UNESCO<br />\r\n\r\n            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Message for International Mother Language Day 2011</em></p>\r\n          <p><span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\">On the occasion of  International Mother Language Day (21st February  2011), Center for </span>Language<span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\"> Engineering (CLE&nbsp;; <a href=\"http://www.cle.org.pk/\" target=\"_blank\">www.cle.org.pk</a>)</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"> at Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (<a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/\" target=\"_blank\">www.kics.edu.pk</a>), University  of Engineering and Technology, Lahore (<a href=\"/\" target=\"_blank\">www.uet.edu.pk</a>) is </span>pleased<span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\"> to</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"> announce</span><span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\"> the</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"> launch</span><span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\"> of Online Torwali</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"> Dictionary</span><span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\"> (OTD). </span></p>\r\n\r\n          <p><span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\">Torwali is a  less studied</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"> indigenous language</span><span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\"> spoken by about one hundred thousand people in Bahrain </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\">and  Chail areas of the beautiful valley of Swat district in the north of Pakistan.  It is an Indo-Aryan language, known as &lsquo;Kohistani&rsquo; among locals.&nbsp; </span></p>\r\n          <p><span lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\">This  pioneering work of Torwali dictionary is an essential resource for language  learning and instruction for the community and researchers, particularly  because Torwali was previously unwritten. This addresses issues of orthography,  documentation, and language preservation for future generations and promotes  the community&rsquo;s identity and culture. This project has been recognized by  UNESCO as &lsquo;Good Practice in Language Preservation.&rsquo; </span><span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n          <p><span lang=\"fr\" xml:lang=\"fr\">This</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"> dictionary can be accessed from <a href=\"http://www.cle.net.pk/otd/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cle.net.pk/otd/</a>.</span></p>\r\n          <p><span lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\">This work  has been undertaken by CLE researcher Mr. Inam Ullah, who is a native speaker,  and supported by Torwali community.&nbsp; The project is funded by The  Genographic Project (<a href=\"http://genographic.nationalgeographic.com/\" target=\"_blank\">genographic.nationalgeographic.com</a>) of National Geographic  and PAN Localization Project (<a href=\"http://www.panl10n.net/\" target=\"_blank\">www.PANL10n.net</a>)  of International Development Research Centre, Canada.</span></p>\r\n          <p align=\"right\"></p>\r\n\r\n        </div>\r\n    </DIV></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n', NULL, '2011-02-21', 0, 1),
(31, NULL, '<p>KICS-UET, Lahore in collaboration with Pakistan  Software Export Board (PSEB) is arranging full day short courses on Entrepreneurship for Engineers and Scientists \r\nand \r\nTen Hottest Trends in Silicon Valley\r\non 17th January, 2011</p>', '<p>\r\nIt  is notified for the information of all concerned that the Al-Khawarizmi  Institute of Computer Science, UET, Lahore in collaboration with Pakistan  Software Export Board (PSEB) is arranging full day short courses on Entrepreneurship for Engineers and Scientists \r\n  and \r\n  Ten Hottest Trends in Silicon Valley\r\n  will be held on 17th January, 2011</p>\r\n<p align=\"center\"><strong> By </strong></p>\r\n<p align=\"center\"><strong>Mr. Naeem Zafar  Haas  Business School, University of California Berkeley, USA </strong></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3>Course Discription: </h3>\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Timings:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 09:30 AM &ndash; 01:00 PM</strong></p>\r\n<p> </p>\r\n<table width=\"100%\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n  <tbody>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><p align=\"center\"><strong>S. No.</strong></p></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p align=\"center\"><strong>Module-I</strong></p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Scientists and Engineers as Entrepreneurs</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"2\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Recognizing and Screening Technology Opportunities</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"3\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Designing and Developing a Technology Start-up</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"4\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Tea</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"5\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Building an Effective Team</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"6\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Developing and Protecting Intellectual Property</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"7\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>High Technology Development Strategies</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"8\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Lunch and Prayer Break</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n  </tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Timings:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 02:00 AM &ndash; 04:00 PM</strong></p>\r\n<p> </p>\r\n<table width=\"100%\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n  <tbody>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><p align=\"center\"><strong>S. No.</strong></p></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p align=\"center\"><strong>Module-II</strong></p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Technology Transition and Entry Strategies</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"2\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Technology Adoption Patterns and Marketing Strategy</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"3\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>The Business Model</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"4\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Funding the Technology Start-up</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"5\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Funding Growth</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"6\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Technology Valuation</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"7\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Ten Hottest Trends in Silicon Valley</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><ol start=\"8\" type=\"1\">\r\n        <li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n      </ol></td>\r\n      <td valign=\"top\" width=\"84%\"><p>Wrap-up &amp; Tea</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n  </tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\n  <strong>Venue: </strong>Seminar  Hall, Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science, U.E.T., Lahore, <br />\r\n  <strong>Days:  </strong>17th  January, 2010, Monday<br />\r\n  <strong>Timings:  </strong>09:30 AM – 01:00  PM<br />\r\n  01:00  PM – 02:00 PM (Lunch and Prayer Break)<br />\r\n  <strong>  </strong>02:00 PM – 04:00  PM</p>\r\n<p align=\"left\"><a href=\"Course_reg.php\">Get Registered Here.... </a></p>\r\n<p align=\"right\"><strong>(Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood)</strong><br />\r\n  Director</p>', NULL, '2011-01-13', 0, 1),
(23, NULL, 'Jobs applications are required for the post of \"Research Assisstant\" in HUAWEI UET Join Telocom IT Center', '<p align=\"left\">Jobs applications are required for the post of \"Research Assisstant\" in HUAWEI UET Join Telocom IT Center</p>', NULL, '2001-10-08', 0, 1);
INSERT INTO `star_news` (`news_id`, `order`, `news_des`, `news_detail`, `newsthumb`, `news_stamp`, `group_id`, `active`) VALUES
(27, NULL, '<img src=\"../hutic/images/new9.gif\" border=\"0\"></img>Open Source Series Workshops (OSSW-2010) and 4th International Conference on Open Source Systems and Technology (ICOSST-2010) is being held on 22-24 December 2010, at KICS-UET, Lahore, Pakistan', '<div align=\"justify\">\r\nOpen Source Series Workshops (OSSW-2010) and 4th International Conference on Open Source Systems and Technology (ICOSST-2010) is being held on 22-24 December 2010, at KICS-UET, Lahore, Pakistan</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>O</strong>pen-Source Software has now established as a  cross-disciplinary paradigm for distributed enterprise computing and  e-Government. It is helping organizations both Governmental and  non-Governmental to keep a control on the cost of development and deployment.  OSSs have not only changed the way software applications are architected,  deployed, and consumed but also they are engineered to provide large  distributed cross-platforms and frameworks. Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer  Science, University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore, is organizing a  two-day conference to invite researchers and practitioners from across the  world to share their ideas and experiences related to the state-of-the-art and  the future of open-source software like virtualization, knowledge-bases,  surveillance, automation, etc. ICOSST-2010 will create a scientific venue where  participants can share ideas, strategies, and policies for tackling the development,  research and adaptation challenges related to open-source tools and open-source  development environments for the customized and enterprise grade applications.  ICOSST-2010 will address:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n                <li>Development of open-source stand-alone software tools,  toolsets, and IDEs for open, complex, and robust enterprise and e-Government information  systems.</li>\r\n                <li>Development of tools like modeling editors, build  automation, continuous integration , logging, debugging, tracing, performance,  code generators, document generators, installers, search & rule engines,  databases, and information management.</li>\r\n              </ul>\r\n              \r\n</div>\r\n<a target=\"_blank\" href =\"http://www.uet.edu.pk/Conferences/icosst2010/index.html\">...Read More...</a>', NULL, '2010-10-08', 0, 1),
(16, NULL, 'A Seminar on Research Areas on Wireless Sensor Networks and Hands-On Workshop on Embedded Networked Devices will be held from 18th to 20th June, 2009', '<p>All the faculty members of Electrical Engineering, Computer Science Departments and the Graduate students are encouraged to attend the workshop.</p>\r\n<p><b>Venue:</b>&nbsp;Seminar Hall, Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science, U.E.T., Lahore,\r\n<p> <strong>Days:</strong>	18th To 20th June, 2009\r\n  <p><strong>Time: </strong>9:00 AM (Sharp)', NULL, '2009-06-17', 0, 1),
(17, NULL, 'RFID Tag Writing Inauguration at National Library of Engineering Sciences, UET Lahore', 'National Library of Engineering Sciences UET Lahore started RFID tag  writing process to fully automate check-in and check-out process at its  circulation desk. After successful deployment of KOHA Dhoom, an  Integrated Library System (ILS) developed by LMS group <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk\">Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science</a> , another mile stone was achieved by National Library of Engineering  Sciences UET Lahore. it is first deployment of its nature in any  library in Pakistan and will improve circulation process as well as  enhance security. RFID tag pasting on books is in progress and self  check-in/check-out functionality will be fully operational in September  2009 (inshAllah)', NULL, '2009-06-19', 0, 1),
(18, NULL, 'Jobs applications are required for the post of \"Research Assisstant\" in HUAWEI UET Join Telocom IT Center.', 'Jobs applications are required for the post of \"Research Assisstant\" in HUAWEI UET Join Telocom IT Center.<br />Mail your resume with confidence upto 11th of july, 2009 at <a href=\"mailto:hutic@kics.edu.pk\">hutic@kics.edu.pk</a>, <a href=\"mailto:admin@kics.edu.pk\">admin@kics.edu.pk</a> or <a href=\"mailto:kashif@kics.edu.pk\">kashif@kics.edu.pk</a>\r\n<P>For further Information .<a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/Careers.php\">....readmore...... </a></p>\r\n', NULL, '2009-06-23', 0, 1),
(19, NULL, '<p>A Short Course on Parallel Programming Paradigms for Multi-Core Processors Based Systems, A Hands-On Experience on Intel and Sony Playstation 3 Platforms starts on August 10-13, 2009</p><br/>', '<p dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\r\n<table width=\"544\" border=\"0\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"375\"><strong>Instructors:</strong></td>\r\n    <td width=\"159\" align=\"center\" valign=\"top\"> </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td colspan=\"2\"><p align=\"justify\">Dr.  Abdul Waheed, Adjunct Professor, Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science  (KICS), University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore, PAKISTAN</p>\r\n      <p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Abdul  Qadeer, Research Manager, Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS), University of Engineering  and Technology (UET), Lahore,   PAKISTAN</p>\r\n      <p align=\"justify\" class=\"bodytext\" dir=\"ltr\">Hasan  Jamal, Sr. Research Associate, Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science  (KICS), University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore, PAKISTAN</p>\r\n    <p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Ghulam  Mustafa, Sr. Research Associate, Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science  (KICS), University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore, PAKISTAN</p>    <a href=\"hpcnl/register.php\"></a></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td><p><strong>Contact  Information:</strong></p>\r\n      <table width=\"364\" border=\"0\" align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"9\" cellspacing=\"2\" class=\"mian\">\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td width=\"73\" valign=\"top\" class=\"texto4\"><strong>Office</strong>: </td>\r\n          <td width=\"249\" valign=\"top\" class=\"texto5\"><p>KICS, UET, Lahore</p></td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td valign=\"top\" class=\"texto4\"><strong>Phone:</strong></td>\r\n          <td valign=\"top\" class=\"texto5\">9250450-9250228</td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td width=\"73\" valign=\"top\" class=\"texto4\"><strong>Email</strong>:</td>\r\n          <td width=\"249\" valign=\"top\" class=\"texto5\"><p><a href=\"mailto:admin@kics.edu.pk\">admin@kics.edu.pk</a></p></td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td width=\"73\" valign=\"top\" class=\"texto4\"><strong>Course    Schedule:</strong></td>\r\n          <td width=\"249\" valign=\"top\" class=\"texto5\"><p>August 10, 2009 – August 13, 2009, 4 pm – 8 pm daily</p></td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td width=\"73\" valign=\"top\" class=\"texto4\"><strong>Classroom</strong></td>\r\n          <td width=\"249\" valign=\"top\" class=\"texto5\"><p>:    Computer Lab, KICS, UET, Lahore</p></td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td width=\"73\" valign=\"top\" class=\"texto4\"></td>\r\n          <td width=\"249\" valign=\"top\" class=\"texto5\"><p> </p></td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n      </table></td>\r\n    <td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\"><a href=\"hpcnl/register.php\"></a></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  \r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td colspan=\"2\"><p> </p>\r\n      <strong>Course  Description:</strong>\r\n      <p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Multiple  cores per processor has emerged as an architecture of choice to allow continued  benefits due to Moore\'s  Law. However, this choice brings along some of the unique challenges to memory  architecture design and software development to the main-stream that were once  hallmarks of high-end, high-performance, and high-price parallel computing.  This short-duration course will focus on state-of-the-art programming paradigms  that are useful for software development for multi-core architectures: explicit  message-passing, shared address space based computing, multi-threading,  map-reduce, and Compute Unified Device Architecture (CUDA). We shall provide a  brief introduction to each of these paradigms with emphasis on hands-on  experience to enable students to become familiar with them for developing  parallel applications. Students will have a unique opportunity to learn parallel  application development on Intel quad-core processor based servers and Sony  Playstation 3 games console as target multi-core platform.</p>\r\n      <strong>Prerequisite: </strong>\r\n      <p dir=\"ltr\">C and  Java programming languages on Linux. </p>\r\n      <strong>Course  Objectives:</strong>\r\n      <ul>\r\n\r\n        <li>To  introduce the students to following state-of-the-art parallel  programming paradigms: message-passing, shared-memory multiprocessing,  multithreading, map-reduce,  and CUDA; </li>\r\n        <li>To initiate  the students into developing parallel applications on multi-core processor  based systems using suitable programming paradigms; and</li>\r\n        <li>To provide  students with a unique opportunity to learn using Sony Playstation 3 as a  cost-effective multi-core  processor  based parallel computing architecture. </li>\r\n      </ul>\r\n      <strong>Learning  Outcomes:</strong><br />\r\nAt  the end of the course, a student will:\r\n<ol start=\"1\" type=\"1\">\r\n  <li dir=\"ltr\">Demonstrate basic understanding of parallel programming paradigms; </li>\r\n  <li dir=\"ltr\">Show ability to write parallel       applications for multi-core processor based systems; and</li>\r\n  <li dir=\"ltr\">Be       aware of performance implications of multi-core architectures to their parallel       applications.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<strong>Textbook: </strong>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n  <li dir=\"ltr\">None </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>References: </strong>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n  <li dir=\"ltr\">Course material </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Grading  Policy:</strong>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n  <li dir=\"ltr\">Lectures                       40%</li>\r\n  <li dir=\"ltr\">Labs                             50% </li>\r\n  <li dir=\"ltr\">Quizzes                        10% </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Students  are responsible to attend all lectures and laboratory sessions to fulfill the  completion requirements of this short course. Due to short duration, no make up  lectures, labs, or quizzes can be arranged. Absence from a lab or quiz will  result in zero credit. Each quiz will be conducted at the end of the subsequent  lecture.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><br />\r\n</p>\r\n<div align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">\r\n  <table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"5\" cellspacing=\"0\" bordercolor=\"#0066CC\">\r\n    <tr >\r\n      <td colspan=\"4\"><p align=\"left\"><strong><u>Course Syllabus</u></strong></p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr class=\"headingcolor1\">\r\n      <td width=\"80\"><br />              <strong>Day</strong><strong> </strong> </td>\r\n      <td width=\"64\"><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Duration</strong></p></td>\r\n      <td width=\"162\"><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Topics</strong><strong> </strong></p></td>\r\n      <td width=\"65\"><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Presenter</strong></p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr class=\"texto4\">\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Monday, August 10,    2009 </p></td>\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">4 Hours (lecture)</p></td>\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Overview    of parallel computing:</p>\r\n          <div align=\"left\">\r\n            <ul type=\"disc\">\r\n              <li dir=\"ltr\">Parallel         architectures and terminology</li>\r\n              <li dir=\"ltr\">Applications of         parallel computing</li>\r\n              <li dir=\"ltr\">Context of         current interest in parallel computing</li>\r\n              <li dir=\"ltr\">Programming         paradigms</li>\r\n              <li dir=\"ltr\">Logistics of the         course</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n          </div></td>\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Dr. Waheed</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr class=\"texto5\">\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Tuesday, August 11,    2009 </p></td>\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">4 Hours (1 hour    lecture followed by 3 hours for lab)</p></td>\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">An    overview of explicit message-passing, shared address space based computing, and    multi-threading on</p>\r\n          <div align=\"left\">\r\n            <ul>\r\n              <li>Intel multi-core systems; and</li>\r\n              <li>Sony Playstation 3 </li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n          </div>\r\n        <p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Lab    exercises on Intel and Playstation 3 platforms using MPI, OpenMP, and    Pthreads:</p>\r\n        <div align=\"left\">\r\n            <ul type=\"disc\">\r\n              <li dir=\"ltr\">HelloWorld</li>\r\n              <li dir=\"ltr\">Matrix         multiplication</li>\r\n              <li dir=\"ltr\">Numerical         computation of pi</li>\r\n              <li dir=\"ltr\">Parallel sort</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n        </div></td>\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Hasan Jamal</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr class=\"texto4\">\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Wednesday, August 12,    2009 </p></td>\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">4 Hours (1 hour    lecture followed by 3 hours for lab)</p></td>\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Introduction to    MapReduce:</p>\r\n          <div align=\"left\">\r\n            <ul>\r\n              <li>What is MapReduce</li>\r\n              <li>Word counting example </li>\r\n              <li>Applicability of MapReduce as a parallel programming    paradigm </li>\r\n              <li>Introduction to Hadoop</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n          </div>\r\n        <p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">MapReduce lab    exercises:</p>\r\n        <div align=\"left\">\r\n            <ul>\r\n              <li>HelloWorld</li>\r\n              <li>Weather database</li>\r\n              <li>Parallel sort </li>\r\n              <li>Numerical computation of pi</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n        </div></td>\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Abdul Qadeer</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr class=\"texto5\">\r\n      <td rowspan=\"2\"><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Thursday, August 13,    2009</p></td>\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">3 Hours (1 hour    lecture followed by 2 hours for lab)</p></td>\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Introduction to CUDA    on multi-core processors</p>\r\n          <div align=\"left\">\r\n            <ul type=\"disc\">\r\n              <li dir=\"ltr\">Memory architecture</li>\r\n              <li dir=\"ltr\">Host to GPU workload         partitioning </li>\r\n              <li dir=\"ltr\">Programming paradigm</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n          </div>\r\n        <p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">CUDA    based lab exercises: </p>\r\n        <div align=\"left\">\r\n            <ul>\r\n              <li>HelloWorld </li>\r\n              <li>Matrix multiplication </li>\r\n              <li>Numerical computation of pi </li>\r\n              <li>Parallel sort </li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n        </div></td>\r\n      <td><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Ghulam Mustafa</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td class=\"texto5\"><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">1 Hour (lecture)</p></td>\r\n      <td class=\"texto5\"><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Closing    remarks about programming paradigms: </p>\r\n          <div align=\"left\">\r\n            <ul>\r\n              <li>Ease of use </li>\r\n              <li>Performance and tools </li>\r\n              <li>Some case studies </li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n          </div></td>\r\n      <td class=\"texto5\"><p align=\"left\" dir=\"ltr\">Dr. Waheed</p></td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n  </table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p><strong>Registration Fee:</strong>\r\n</p>\r\n<p dir=\"LTR\">Students:           Rs. <strong>500</strong>/=<br>\r\n  Professional:     Rs <strong>2000</strong>/=</p>\r\n<p><strong>Instructor’s  Short Biography: </strong></p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Dr. Abdul Waheed</strong> is currently working as a senior  performance engineer at Cisco Systems in San    Jose, California, USA. He was an assistant professor  in Computer Engineering (COE) Department at KFUPM, Dhahran, Saudi Arabia  from 2001 to 2004. Before joining the KFUPM, he was working at Inktomi  Corporation in Foster City,   California, USA,  as a performance engineer in network products division. He was a research staff  member at NASA Ames  Research Center,  Moffett Field, California, USA,  from May 1997 until July 2000. He held a summer position in Concurrent  Computing Division at Hewlett-Packard Research Laboratories in Palo Alto, California,   USA in 1994. He  received a B.Sc. degree with honors in Electrical Engineering from University of Engineering  and Technology, Lahore, Pakistan in 1991. He received MS and  PhD degrees in Electrical Engineering from Michigan State University (MSU), East Lansing, Michigan,   USA in 1993 and 1997, respectively.  His research interests span performance evaluation  of high performance computing and networking architectures, parallelization for  multi-core architectures, cloud computing, and performance tools. He initiated High  Performance Computing and Networking (HPCN) effort at KICS/UET in the summer of  2006 and has been providing mentoring and leadership support to the group. HPCN  team developed Multi-core Processor Architecture and Communication (MPAC)  benchmark under his leadership and released to the open source community in  August 2008. He has published  over thirty refereed conference and journal papers on related topics. He is a  member of the IEEE Computer Society.</p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Abdul Qadeer</strong> received a B.Sc. degree  in Computer Science from FAST (Foundation for Advancement of Science and  Technology), Lahore, Pakistan in 2001. He received a  M.S. Degree in Computer Science in 2006 from Lahore University of Management  Sciences (LUMS), Pakistan.  Moreover he received a M.S. degree in Computer Science from University of  Southern California (USC), Los Angeles, CA  in 2008. Abdul Qadeer’s areas of interest are large scale distributed systems  and cloud computing. Currently he is involved in a project related to domain  specific search strategies to build effective search engine seeds. He developed a framework for web data analysis that mainly  covers the current IPv4 allocation, which is primarily based on Google’s  MapReduce paradigm.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong> </strong></p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Mohammad Hasan Jamal</strong> received a B.Sc. degree  with honors in Computer and Information Engineering from International Islamic  University Malaysia, Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia in 2005. He received a MS  degree from Electrical Engineering Department, UET, Lahore, Pakistan,  specializing in Computer Engineering in December 2008. Hasan works in the general areas of performance engineering,  HPC, and parallel and distributed systems. He is currently working on the  development of performance measurement and profiling tools. He was actively  involved in the setup of High Performance Computing and Networking Lab (HPCNL)  at KICS in UET, Lahore.  He was one of the leading contributors to the recently completed, ICT R&D  funded, project titled “Characterization, Evaluation, and Development of High  Performance Network Services on Multi-Core Architectures”. He has three  publications in peer reviewed conferences based on this effort. He is a member of the  IEEE Computer Society. </p>\r\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Ghulam Mustafa</strong>’s areas of  interest are HPC, scientific computing & visualization, parallel programming,  and energy efficient programming. Recently, he has completed the development of  multithreaded benchmarking suite (MPAC) for performance analysis of multi/many  core systems. He was the lead developer to enable its initial release in 2008  and current release of version 1.1 to open source. He is a PhD candidate in  Computer Science Department at UET. </p>\r\n<p>For further detail <a href=\"images/Poster_06_aug_09.pdf\">Click Here..</a> </p><p> </p></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td> </td>\r\n    <td> </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\r\n', NULL, '2009-08-06', 0, 1),
(20, NULL, 'Series of Courses on Advances GSM Network for the groups of BSS, HLR,and, MSC Courses  is being Started in January 2010', 'Huawei Technologies, in its second phase, provides state of the art wireless and mobiles communication equipment consisting of NGN, Broadband, soft switches etc. of  worth  5.2 million USD to UET Lahore in order to promote training and research in wireless communication sector in Pakistan. Get a chance to have hands on experience on Huawei Technologies latest GSM Equipment to gain the knowledge of BTS (Base Transceiver Station), BSC (Base Station Controller),HLR(Home Location Register) and MSC (Mobile Switching Center) installation, configuration, operation and maintenance.\r\n<p>\r\nThe schedule and details of the course is available <a  href=\"hutic/images/poster.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Here>>>></a>\r\n<p>\r\n<table width=\"417\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" bordercolor=\"#336699\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td colspan=\"5\"><div align=\"center\" class=\"subheading\">January 2010 Schedule </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"68\" rowspan=\"4\" class=\"subheading1\"><div align=\"center\"></div>      <div align=\"center\">Group 1 </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"77\" class=\"titleheading\"><div align=\"center\">Courses </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"80\" class=\"titleheading\"><div align=\"center\">Dates  </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"90\" class=\"titleheading\"><div align=\"center\">Timings </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"80\" class=\"titleheading\"><div align=\"center\">Fee</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">BSS</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\"> Jan 18-22  </div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">3 pm-7 pm</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Rs 5,000 </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">MSC</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\"> Jan 25-29   </div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">3 pm-7 pm</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Rs 5,000 </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">HLR</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\"> Feb01-05   </div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">3 pm-7 pm</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Rs 5,000 </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  \r\n</table>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n<table width=\"416\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" bordercolor=\"#5A7BA6\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td colspan=\"2\"><div align=\"center\">Discount</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"190\"><div align=\"center\">Option A </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"216\"><div align=\"center\">Option B </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>For any two courses the combined fee of Rs. 10,000 is discounted to Rs. 9,000 </td>\r\n    <td>For BSS, HLR, and MSC the combined fee of Rs.15,000 is discounted to Rs. 12,000. </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td colspan=\"2\"><div align=\"center\">Contact Person </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td valign=\"top\"><p align=\"center\">Kashif Bashir</p>\r\n    <p align=\"center\"><a href=\"mailto:kashif@kics.edu.pk\">kashif@kics.edu.pk</a> </p>\r\n    <p align=\"center\">+92-42-9029450<br />+92-42-9250229<br />+92-345-4117221<br />\r\n    +92-323-4480000</p></td>\r\n    <td valign=\"top\"><p align=\"center\">Naveed Nawaz</p>\r\n    <p align=\"center\"><a href=\"mailto:naveed@kics.edu.pk\">naveed@kics.edu.pk </a></p>\r\n    <p align=\"center\">+92-333-6031735</p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n', NULL, '2010-01-12', 6, 1),
(30, 4, 'Get a chance to have hands on experience on Telecom (Advanced GSM Technology)including BSS, HLR, MSC & IP Networks (Routing & Switching) with latest equipment to gain the depth knowledge of Networks & Telecom Technologies starting from 06 June 2011.', '<p>Al-Khwarizmi Institute of Computer Science University of Engineering and Technology Lahore organizes series of courses on advanced GSM Technology including BSS, HLR and MSC. Now it is introducing a series of new courses on Radio Network Optimization (RNO)and Networks (Router & Switching) on different vendor\'s hardware in its Huawei UET Telecom and IT Centre (HUTIC). Get a chance to have hands on experience on telecom (Advanced GSM Technology) & IP Networks (Routing & Switching) with latest equipment to gain the depth knowledge of Networks & Telecom Technologies. The purpose of these courses is to prepare professionals having a variety of technology orientation, not specific to certain hardware, to meet the market demands. Worldwide recognized certificates will also be provided after completion of these courses.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n  <li> <a href=\"doc/gsm_june_2011.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">[Download Registration Form]\r\n  </a></li>\r\n  <li>Online Registration Starts Soon...... <br>\r\n    <br>\r\n  <br>\r\n      <table width=\"200\" border=\"0\" align=\"center\">\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td><div align=\"center\"><strong>Telecom Courses </strong></div></td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n      </table>\r\n  \r\n  </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p align=\"center\"><img src=\"images/news/huawei/telecom_schedule2.jpg\" width=\"412\" height=\"350\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<img src=\"images/news/huawei/discount1.jpg\" width=\"212\" height=\"320\" /></p>\r\n<p align=\"center\"><a href=\"images/news/huawei/Poster-courses1.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download Poster [.pdf] </a>\r\n<table width=\"200\" border=\"0\" align=\"center\">\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td><div align=\"center\"><strong>Network Courses </strong></div></td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n<div align=\"center\"><br>\r\n  &nbsp;\r\n  </p>\r\n  <img src=\"images/news/huawei/networkk.jpg\" width=\"440\" height=\"268\" /></div>\r\n<p align=\"center\"><a href=\"images/news/huawei/Posternet.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download Poster [.pdf] </a> (Discount for group only) </p>\r\n', NULL, '2011-05-13', 6, 1),
(24, NULL, 'ICOSST-2010, Registration for Open Source Series Workshop (OSSW-2010), is now open', '<p>ICOSST-2010, Registration for Open Source Series Workshop (OSSW-2010), is now open</p>\r\n<a target=\"_blank\" href =\"http://www.uet.edu.pk/Conferences/icosst2010/_registration.html\">Get Registration...</a>', NULL, '2010-10-08', 0, 1),
(10, NULL, 'HUTIC celebrates World Telecom Day on 16th May 2009', 'Huawei UET joint Telecom & IT Center (HUTIC) is organizing World Telecom Day – 2009 on 16th May, 2009 at 10:00AM in Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science, University of Engineering & Technology, Lahore.  The Chinese and Pakistani experts on Telecommunication Technologies from various industry and academia are participating in the event.\r\n', NULL, '2009-05-16', 6, 1),
(11, NULL, 'Certificate Distribution Ceremony of HUTIC to be held on 16th May 2009 in the presence of Minister of Education, Mr. Mujtaba Shujja-ur-Rehman ', 'HUTIC organizes the certificate distribution ceremony for the professionals and students who have successfully completed the technical training courses on BSC, BTS, HLR and MSC. The Honorable Minister of Education, Mr. Mujtaba Shujja-ur-Rehman is invited as Chief Guest for the ceremony. Other dignitaries from the leading telecom industry are also invited. ', NULL, '2009-05-16', 6, 1),
(12, NULL, 'A workshop on Next Generation Computing Paradigms: Cloud Computing; Map Reduce; Parallel Programming; Multi-core Architecture; Virtualization, Configware ', 'A workshop on Next Generation Computing Paradigms: Cloud Computing; Map Reduce; Parallel Programming; Multi-core Architecture; Virtualization, Configware is being held on  Saturday, May 09, 2009 \r\n\r\nHigh Performance Computing & Networking Lab (HPCNL) at KICS-UET, Lahore presents this workshop the need for next generation computing paradigms along with the demonstration of some of the leading techniques <A href=\"hpcnl/workshop/ngcp.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">....read more...</A> \r\n\r\n', NULL, '2009-05-09', 0, 1),
(13, NULL, 'Third International Conference on Open-Source Systems and Technologies (ICOSST-2009) is starting on dated  19-22 December 2009, Lahore, Pakistan.', 'For further information please visit the following website of ICOSST...  \r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://www.uet.edu.pk/Conferences/icosst2009/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">3rd International Conference   ICOSST-2009</a>', NULL, '2009-05-09', 0, 1),
(14, NULL, 'Huawei-UET Center Offers a Course on Huawei GSM Equipment from 1st Week of April, 2009.', 'Huawei-UET Joint Telecom IT Center, HUTIC, starts a course on Huawei latest GSM Equipment from the 7th June, 2009.\r\n<p>The schedule and details of the course is available <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/hutic/hutnews.php\">Here...</a></p> ', NULL, '2009-03-27', 6, 1),
(25, NULL, 'Series of Courses on Advances GSM Network for the groups of BSS, HLR, MSC and RNP Courses is being Start in Nov, Dec 2010', 'Huawei Technologies, in its second phase, provides state of the art wireless and mobiles communication equipment consisting of NGN, Broadband, soft switches etc. of  worth  5.2 million USD to UET Lahore in order to promote training and research in wireless communication sector in Pakistan. Get a chance to have hands on experience on Huawei Technologies latest GSM Equipment to gain the knowledge of BTS (Base Transceiver Station), BSC (Base Station Controller),HLR(Home Location Register) and MSC (Mobile Switching Center) installation, configuration, operation and maintenance.\r\n<p>\r\nThe schedule and details of the course is available <a  href=\"hutic/images/summer3.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Here>>>></a>\r\n<p><span class=\"subheading\"><strong>Nov 2010 Schedule </strong></span>\r\n<table width=\"417\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" bordercolor=\"#336699\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td colspan=\"5\"><div align=\"center\" class=\"subheading\">November 2010 Schedule </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"68\" rowspan=\"4\" class=\"subheading1\"><div align=\"center\"></div>      <div align=\"center\">Group 1 </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"61\" class=\"titleheading\"><div align=\"center\">Courses </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"123\" class=\"titleheading\"><div align=\"center\">Dates  </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"85\" class=\"titleheading\"><div align=\"center\">Timings </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"58\" class=\"titleheading\"><div align=\"center\">Fee</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">BSS</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\"> Nov 01-05</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">3 pm-7 pm</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Rs 5,000 </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">HLR</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Nov 08-12</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">3 pm-7 pm</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Rs 5,000 </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">MSC</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Nov 15-19</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">3 pm-7 pm</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Rs 5,000 </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n<p><strong>Dec 2010 Schedule </strong> </p>\r\n<table width=\"417\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" bordercolor=\"#336699\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td colspan=\"5\"><div align=\"center\" class=\"subheading\">Dcember 2010 Schedule </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"68\" rowspan=\"4\" class=\"subheading1\"><div align=\"center\"></div>\r\n        <div align=\"center\">Group 2 </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"61\" class=\"titleheading\"><div align=\"center\">Courses </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"123\" class=\"titleheading\"><div align=\"center\">Dates </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"85\" class=\"titleheading\"><div align=\"center\">Timings </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"58\" class=\"titleheading\"><div align=\"center\">Fee</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">BSS</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\"> Dec 20-24</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">3 pm-7 pm</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Rs 5,000 </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">HLR</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Dec 27-31</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">3 pm-7 pm</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Rs 5,000 </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">MSC</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Jan 03-07</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">3 pm-7 pm</div></td>\r\n    <td class=\"texto4\"><div align=\"center\">Rs 5,000 </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n<table width=\"416\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" bordercolor=\"#5A7BA6\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td colspan=\"2\"><div align=\"center\">Discount</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"190\"><div align=\"center\">Option A </div></td>\r\n    <td width=\"216\"><div align=\"center\">Option B </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>For any two courses the combined fee of Rs. 10,000 is discounted to Rs. 9,000 </td>\r\n    <td>For BSS, HLR, and MSC the combined fee of Rs.15,000 is discounted to Rs. 12,000. </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td colspan=\"2\"><div align=\"center\">Contact Person </div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td valign=\"top\"><p align=\"center\">Kashif Bashir</p>\r\n    <p align=\"center\"><a href=\"mailto:kashif@kics.edu.pk\">kashif@kics.edu.pk</a> <br>\r\n      <a href=\"mailto:kashif818@yahoo.com\">kashif818@yahoo.com</a></p>\r\n    <p align=\"center\">+92-42-9029450<br />+92-42-9250229<br />+92-345-4117221<br />\r\n    +92-323-4480000</p></td>\r\n    <td valign=\"top\"><p align=\"center\">Naveed Nawaz</p>\r\n    <p align=\"center\"><a href=\"mailto:naveed@kics.edu.pk\">naveed@kics.edu.pk </a></p>\r\n    <p align=\"center\">+92-333-6031735</p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n', NULL, '2010-05-13', 6, 1),
(28, NULL, 'Center for Language Engineering (CLE) at KICS-UET, LHR has released an Urdu version of the flood relief website for the Government of Punjab to provide greater access to this information to local population.', 'We are pleased to announce that the Center for Language  Engineering at Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science, University of  Engineering and Technology, Lahore (<a href=\"http://www.cle.org.pk/\" target=\"_blank\">www.cle.org.pk</a>)  has released an Urdu version of the flood relief website <a href=\"http://floodrelief.punjab.gov.pk/urdu/\" target=\"_blank\">http://floodrelief.punjab.gov.pk/urdu/</a> for the Government of Punjab to provide greater access to  this information to local population.&nbsp; This is a parallel site to the  English version already available at&nbsp;<a href=\"http://floodrelief.punjab.gov.pk/\" target=\"_blank\">http://floodrelief.punjab.gov.pk/</a>.&nbsp;  The website has detailed information on the damages in various sectors caused  by the flood (including education, health, agriculture, livestock, etc.),  detailed status of the relief and rehabilitation efforts underway and how  others can participate in the process.&nbsp; The information in both versions  of the website is being update on daily basis and based on data being received  by different departments and districts of the Government of Punjab,  Pakistan.&nbsp;', NULL, '2010-10-14', 0, 1),
(29, NULL, 'HEC Chairman visited HUAWEI-UET TELECOM and IT Center.', '<p>\r\nThe Honorable Chairperson Higher Education Commission, Mr. Javed Laghari visited the Huawei UET Telecom IT Center (HUTIC) along with the Vice- Chancellor, University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore and Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Director, Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science. He visited the high-tech 2.S/2.75G GSM facility available for training and research. He also admired the state-of-the-art spacious facility organized by\r\nthe UET with the collaboration of Huawei Technologies, China\r\n</p>', NULL, '2010-12-08', 6, 1),
(46, 14, '					KICS is offering a short course on DS / CDMA Systems, Implementation and Issues (A hands on approach for understanding CDMA systems) starting from Sept 17th, 2012\r\n', '\r\n<h3>Description </h3>\r\n<p>Importance of DS/CDMA systems in the field of communication can hardly be overemphasized. This technology forms the backbone of various communication standards being used internationally. This course does not focus on any particular technology; it rather introduces detailed implementation of generic CDMA systems. Initially a fundamental single user DS/CDMA system will be implemented using C language. Effect of spreading sequences and pertinent interesting results will be presented. Code acquisition in CDMA systems will be discussed in detail. Synchronous and asynchronous systems in single user and multiuser scenarios will be discussed and simulated successively and research opportunities in this domain will be explored towards the end of this course. </p>\r\n<p> Each session will include one lecture and lab practice. Approximately one hour lecture will be followed by a two hours lab practice where software implementation of the discussed concepts will be carried out using C language and Matlab. </p>\r\n<table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td><strong>Session</strong></td>\r\n    <td><strong>Topic</strong></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td><p>Monday Sept 17, 2012 </p></td>\r\n    <td><p>Introduction to multiple access communications and working principle of DS/CDMA systems </p></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td><p>Tuesday Sept 18, 2012 </p></td>\r\n    <td>Multiple access interference (MAI) minimization and code acquisition</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td><p>Wednesday Sept 19, 2012 </p></td>\r\n    <td>Single user chip-synchronous system </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td><p>Thursday Sept 20, 2012 </p></td>\r\n    <td>Multiuser chip-synchronous system </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td><p>Friday Sept 21, 2012 </p></td>\r\n    <td>Chip-asynchronous systems and research issues to be explored </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n<p><strong>Instructor : Dr. M Tahir Abbas Khan</strong></p>\r\n<p>Dr. M Tahir Abbas Khan received his PhD in communications from Kyushu University, Japan in 2005. He was a research fellow for Japan Society for Promotion of Science (JSPS) from 2005-2007. He has been working in Ritsumeikan Asia Pacific University as Associate professor since 2007. Currently he is at Al-Khwarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS), UET Lahore. </p>\r\n<p>Office: KICS, UET Lahore Email: <a href=\"mailto:admin@kics.edu.pk\"> admin@kics.edu.pk</a> Phone: +92 42 9250450 </p>\r\n<p> Training room: Android Lab, KICS, UET Lahore </p>\r\n<p>For registration, please send an email to <a href=\"mailto:admin@kics.edu.pk\"> admin@kics.edu.pk</a> <br>\r\n</p>\r\n<a href=\"downloads/DSCDMA_poster.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Poster</a>\r\n', NULL, '2012-09-10', 0, 1),
(49, 50, 'Careers Opportunities in Al-Khwarizmi Institute of Computer Science UET Lahore', '<a href=\"http://kics.edu.pk/career\" target=\"_blank\">Careers Opportunities in Al-Khwarizmi Institute of Computer Science UET Lahore.</a>', NULL, '2013-02-01', 0, 1),
(51, 55, 'Congratulations! ICOSST-2012 has now been officially Approved and Confirmed by IEEE for appearance as IEEE Xplore publication.', 'Al-Khawarizimi Institute of Computer Science (KICS), UET, Lahore   organized the &quot;IEEE 2012 International Conference on Open Source Systems   &amp; Technologies (ICOSST-2012)&quot; with associated Open Source Series   Workshops (OSSW-12) &amp; Open Source Projects Exhibition (OSPE-12).   ICOSST 2012 was technically co-sponsorship by IEEE Computer Science,   Lahore Section. The Conference was held on 20-22 December,2012 at UET,   Lahore, Pakistan.</div>\r\n<div><br />\r\n</div>\r\n<div>ICOSST was   initially organized by KICS in 2006 afterwards it has   been regularly organized in 2007,2009,2010,2011 &amp; then 2012. IEEE   recognized and approved ICOSST-2012 for the appearance and indexing on   IEEE Xplore for the first time in its history.<br />\r\n    <br />\r\n  The Conference Proceedings for ICOSST 2012 are now available online at IEEE Xplore, under the following link:<br />\r\n  <br />\r\n  <a href=\"http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/xpl/tocresult.jsp?isnumber=6472819\" target=\"_blank\">http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/xpl/tocresult.jsp?isnumber=6472819</a><br />\r\n  <br />\r\n  This benchmark is achieved as a collective effort of KICS Staff   &amp; Conference Organizing Committees. We are determined to take ICOSST   2013 to higher levels of standards with the continued spirit and   dedication.</div>\r\n', NULL, '2013-04-18', 0, 1),
(52, 56, 'Invitation For Workshop On Software Defined Radio (SDR)', '<p> Al - Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS),&nbsp; UET, Lahore &nbsp;is organizing a workshop with collaboration of IEEE CS and HEC on &ldquo;<strong>Wireless receiver design using Software Defined Radio (SDR)&rdquo;.&nbsp;</strong>The&nbsp;outline&nbsp;and schedule of&nbsp; the &nbsp;workshop is&nbsp;available at <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/\">http://www.kics.edu.pk/</a> . &nbsp; <u><a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk//downloads/Poster_SDR.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download Poster </a></u><u><strong></strong></u></p>\r\n<p><strong>Date and Venue:</strong></p>\r\n<p> The workshop will begin on&nbsp; Monday, October 28&nbsp;( 3:30PM) and end at&nbsp; noon&nbsp;on Friday,&nbsp;November 01, 2013&nbsp; at \r\n  Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS), UET, Lahore.  <u><a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk//downloads/Schedule_%20Workshop%20_SDR.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download Schedule </a></u></p>\r\n<p><strong>Eligibility&nbsp;Criteria:</strong></p>\r\n<p> The intended audience for this workshop is&nbsp; Final Year students&nbsp;of Electrical/Telecom or Computer Engineering. Nevertheless, fresh graduates or early career researchers are also particularly welcome to &nbsp;t his workshop.&nbsp; &nbsp; </p>\r\n<p><strong>Objective:</strong></p>\r\n<p> The&nbsp; objective &nbsp;of this workshop &nbsp; is &nbsp; to provide hands-on experience with designing and developing software defined radio based systems. Moreover, the audience will get the opportunity to learn how to build modern and state-of-the art wireless receiver using USRPs and GNU Radio Platform in real-time settings.&nbsp;Participation in this workshop will help the audience to enhance their software and hardware skills and thus will be beneficial in the current job market. </p>\r\n<p><strong>Speaker\'s Profile:</strong></p>\r\n<p> Dr. Muhammad Mahboob-ur-Rahman is the key speaker of this workshop. He has been working as a researcher in wireless group of Nokia Research Centre, Berkeley, CA, USA since May 2013. He has recently completed his PhD in Electrical and Computer Engineering from the University of Iowa, Iowa City, USA. His recent research interests include distributed MIMO,&nbsp;software-defined radios for rapid prototyping of novel wireless concepts, stability of consensus based algorithms. He has a vast experience in design and development of SDR modems, wireless camera sensor networks and digital filters. He has published several journal articles and presented his results in international conferences and seminars. He got best demo award at I EEE International Symposium on a World of&nbsp;Wireless, Mobile and Multimedia Systems, 2012. </p>\r\n<p><strong>Registration:</strong></p>\r\n<p> The registration fee&nbsp;is&nbsp; &nbsp;<strong> Rs.1000 /-</strong> (non-refundable) &nbsp;for each participant,&nbsp;<strong>UET students </strong>&amp;<strong> IEEE CS members </strong>will be granted a special concession of <strong>50%</strong>.&nbsp;The&nbsp;interested&nbsp;students and professionals may submit the registration form along with fee till&nbsp; <strong>25 th Oct</strong><strong>, 2013</strong>; registration form is available at KICS reception. <u><a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk//downloads/Registration_Form_SDR.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download Registration Form</a></u></p>\r\n<p> All the resources (including computers) required for this workshop will be provided by &nbsp; the&nbsp;institute . <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk//downloads/outline.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Purposed Outline and Profile</a></p>\r\n<p>\r\n<p><strong>Contact: </strong></p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>\r\nFor general info:\r\nNoor-ul-Wara @ 0321-4152275 \r\n<p> For technical info: Dr. Omer Waqar @ 0333-0453147 </p>', NULL, '2013-10-07', 0, 1),
(55, 59, 'Workshop on Scientific Writing and Research Methodology (SWARM) Starting from 9th April, 2014\r\n', '<p>An important workshop has been scheduled by KICS for the enhancement of of the technical and scientific writing skills of KICS staff members. Four lectures each of 2 hours will be delivered on 9th, 10th,16th and 17th April, 2014 at KICS Seminar Hall. Speaker is Dr. Imran Mahmood, Assistant Professor KICS.</p>\r\n<p>For more details please <a href=\"http://kics.edu.pk/doc/Workshop_SWARM.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">click here</a></p>', NULL, '2014-04-07', 0, 1),
(56, 62, 'KICS announces TICK, and the activity to build its creative team of First UET startup leaders', '<p><strong> &nbsp;</strong><strong>UET Startup Leader (USL) </strong></p>\r\n<p>The TICK- Technology incubation Centre of Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Sciences providing you an opportunity to be one of the first \"UET Startup Leaders\" (USL). It&rsquo;s a platform where you all can:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Become Ambassador for the first Acceleration &amp; Incubation cycle of KICS</li>\r\n<li>Participate in a series of professional development &amp; entrepreneurship workshops &amp; group activities (Phase I)</li>\r\n<li>Connect with other leaders on campus &amp; outside</li>\r\n<li>Get training from industry entrepreneurs as mentors</li>\r\n<li>Get trained as a Trainer on the first boot camp for the Startup Challenge</li>\r\n<li>Develop a team to explore the skill set of yours and your team members</li>\r\n<li>Participate in professional Phase II incubation activities of KICS Startups</li>\r\n<li>Get a chance to become one of the first incubates of KICS technology incubation center</li>\r\n<li>All USL shall be awarded with certificates of participation and selected trainers will be awarded separate certificates</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<div><img src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/doc/tick.jpg\" alt=\"sitecK_flyer KICS\" width=\"700\" height=\"1150\" /></div>\r\n<h2>How to apply</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Student of any year, be a freshman, sophomore or out of the most senior batch of CE, CS, EE, Mechatronics is welcome to apply to this program.</li>\r\n<li>Selection will be done by following the procedure below:</li>\r\n<li>A psychometric test of 30 minutes</li>\r\n<li>An interview of 10 minutes with a panel of 2 to 3 core incubation team members</li>\r\n<li>Apply by 20th April online at <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/incubations/usl_reg\">http://www.kics.edu.pk/incubations/usl_reg</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>For any queries and information, if required.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Saman Tariq <a href=\"mailto:saman.tariq@kics.edu.pk\"> saman.tariq@kics.edu.pk</a></li>\r\n<li>Muhammad Zeeshan <a href=\"mailto:syed.zshan75@gmail.com\"> syed.zshan75@gmail.com</a> 0342-7725288</li>\r\n<li>Ahsan Saleem Khan <a href=\"mailto:ahsan.khan@kics.edu.pk\"> ahsan.khan@kics.edu.pk</a> 0322-4456333</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '2014-04-14', 0, 1),
(57, 63, '2G/3G/4G Mobile Networks and Technologies \r\nFast- Track Training \r\n', '<p align=\"center\"><strong> Get hands-on practice on Huawei\'s equipment modules installed at HUTIC</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Mobile Network Fundamentals and Evolution of Mobile Technologies towards 3G/4G Architectural Advancements and Hardware Upgrades from GSM/GPRS to UMTS and LTE</li>\r\n<li>Functions and evolution of BTS towards NodeB/e-NodeB and Site Designing</li>\r\n<li>Mobility and Resource Management and Optimization in the BSS/UTRAN with BSC/RNC</li>\r\n<li>Evolution of 2G MSC towards MSS in 3G/3G Core Networks</li>\r\n<li>Enhancement of HLR towards HSS with Evolving Mobile Networks</li>\r\n<li>Signalling Flows and Data configuration on online BSC, MSC and HLR LMT Softwares</li>\r\n</ol>', NULL, '2014-05-28', 6, 1);
INSERT INTO `star_news` (`news_id`, `order`, `news_des`, `news_detail`, `newsthumb`, `news_stamp`, `group_id`, `active`) VALUES
(58, 64, 'HUTIC KICS is going to start a series of Telecom and Network Courses (2G / 3G / 4G) from Feb, 09.', '<p>HUTIC KICS is going to start a series of Telecome and Network Courses (2G, 3G, 4G) from Feb, 09.<br /><br />Mobile Network Fundamentals and Evolution of Mobile Technologies towards 3G/4G Architectural, Advancements and Hardware Upgrades from GSM/GPRS to UMTS and LTE Functions and evolution of BTS towards NodeB/e-NodeB and Site Designing Mobility and Resource Management and Optimization in the BSS/UTRAN with BSC/RNC Evolution of 2G MSC towards MSS in 3G/3G Core Networks Enhancement of HLR towards HSS with Evolving Mobile Networks Signalling Flows and Data configuration on online BSC, MSC and HLR LMT Softwares.<br /><br /><a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/trainings/course_schedule/1\" target=\"_blank\">View Course Schedule</a></p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://kics.edu.pk/hutic/documents/poster.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Download Poster</a><br /><br /></p>', NULL, '2015-02-16', 6, 1),
(59, 67, 'Free Solar Energy Training at KICS', '<p>KICS UET Lahore is offering three month\'s free Solar Energy Training Session for the students of Matric with the cooperation of \"Punjab Skill Development Fund (PSDF)\"</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/doc/solar_energy_training_matricl_Admission_form.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download Admission Form</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><strong><a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/doc/solartraining_matric.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Download Adverstisement</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</strong><strong><a title=\"Download Schedule\" href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/doc/Schedule-PSDF.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download Schedule&nbsp;</a></strong></p>\r\n<p><img src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/doc/solartraining_matric.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div id=\"__if72ru4sdfsdfrkjahiuyi_once\" style=\"display: none;\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div id=\"__if72ru4sdfsdfruh7fewui_once\" style=\"display: none;\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div id=\"__hggasdgjhsagd_once\" style=\"display: none;\">&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2015-03-10', 0, 1),
(60, 66, 'Center for Language Engineering (CLE), KICS, UET, Lahore is organizing a research seminar.', '<div style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;\">\r\n<div>Center for Language Engineering is conducting the seminars on bi-weekly basis where CLE researchers present their research work on difference aspects of linguistics, computer science and social science and share their research experiences with the audience. These seminars are intended to be a forum for sharing new research and gaining valuable feedback.<br /><br /></div>\r\nPlease note the details for the Upcoming Seminar:<br /><br /></div>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;\"><strong>Date:</strong>&nbsp;<span class=\"aBn\" style=\"border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-style: dashed; border-bottom-color: #cccccc; position: relative; top: -2px; z-index: 0;\" data-term=\"goog_134668170\"><span class=\"aQJ\" style=\"position: relative; top: 2px; z-index: -1;\">13th January, 2015</span></span><br /></span></p>\r\n<div style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;\"><strong>Time:&nbsp;</strong><span class=\"aBn\" style=\"border-bottom-width: 1px; border-bottom-style: dashed; border-bottom-color: #cccccc; position: relative; top: -2px; z-index: 0;\" data-term=\"goog_134668171\"><span class=\"aQJ\" style=\"position: relative; top: 2px; z-index: -1;\">11:30 am-12:00 pm</span></span><br /><br /></div>\r\n<div style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;\"><strong>Venue:</strong>&nbsp;Seminar Hall, KICS<br /><br /></div>\r\n<div style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;\"><strong>Presenter:&nbsp;</strong>Ms. Rida Hijab<br /><br /></div>\r\n<div style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;\"><strong>Topic:</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Classification of Clauses in Non-Disclosure Agreements (NDAs)</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;\">\r\n<div><strong>Abstract:</strong></div>\r\n<div>Written contracts consist of various clauses which are a fundamental framework for commercial and cooperative transactions and relationships. Legal contracts are huge documents and searching through them to get the desired clauses is a cumbersome task. To solve this problem, many systems are being developed that automates this process of finding desired clauses in the legal documents. Classification of clauses in contracts is an automatic process of assigning correct labels/classes to each sentence present in the contract. With the help of this, one can simply get the similar clauses in the contract without going through the trouble of manually skimming through them. Our recent research has been focused on developing one such system. The distinguishing feature of our system is that it covers a large set of classifying labels. The label set of 29 labels consists of primary and secondary labels due to which two-level classification method has been adopted. Similar labels have been grouped together as secondary labels and classified later at level 2. Two-level classification method has overall accuracy of about 78.60%.&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', NULL, '2015-01-13', 10, 1),
(61, 68, 'Friendly Cricket Match Between Team IoT and Team Admin', '<p>A friendly cricket match series was held on April 29, 2015 at UET Stadium between Team IoT &nbsp;and Team Admin.&nbsp;<br />Team IoT and Admin was led by Sheraz and Raheel respectivley. Series of two matches was played and Team Admin won the series by 2-0 &nbsp;</p>', NULL, '2015-04-29', 0, 1),
(62, 115, 'Certificate Distribution Ceremony of Solar Photovoltaic System Installation and Pumping Training', '<p>Certificate distribution ceremony was organizes at Chemical seminar hall, UET Lahore on April 6th, 2015 where honorable Vice chancellor UET Lahore Prof. Dr Fazal Ahmad Khalid was invited as a chief guest. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/assets/images/news/solar.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"900\" height=\"1300\" /></p>', NULL, '2015-05-11', 6, 1),
(63, 117, 'Certificate Distribution Ceremony of 2nd Batch of Solar Photovoltaic System Installation and Pumping Training ', '<p>Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) and Center for Energy Research and Development (CERAD), University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore has been conducting Solar Photovoltaic Installation and Pumping Training for the underprivileged youth of Punjab with association of Punjab Skills Development Fund (PSDF) since December 2014. Course is consisted of three months duration delivering extensive theoretical as well as practical training to youth of Punjab. Two batches of this training have been completed under the flag of KICS-CERAD. Second batch (April-July 2015) has just finished with fifty-eight (58) passed out trainees and Certificate distribution ceremony was executed on 7th July, 2015.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>A number of dignitaries from solar industries in Pakistan joined the event to provide their support and prayers to the passed out trainees. It became an excellent opportunity for trainees to meet with the industry experts; share their experiences and to discuss their future plans in the scope of solar technology. The Honorable Chief Guest Additional Secretary Energy Department Punjab Mr. Khalid Awais Ranjha and Distinguished Guest Mr. Muhammad Aamir Chief Executive Officer from Tesla Industries Pvt. Ltd; Mr. Shahid Awan Chief Executive Officer Solar tech Pvt. Ltd.; Mr. Baqar Bilal Chief Executive Officer GET Technologies, Mr. Omar Akhtar Communication Team Punjab Skills Development Fund; and Mr. Mou from ZTE graced the occasion.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2015/july/ceretificate_dist_cerm_photovoltaic2.JPG\" alt=\"\" width=\"750\" height=\"399\" /></p>\r\n<p>Ceremony started with Tilawat-e-Quran Majeed; and proceeded with addresses from present dignitaries. First of all, Dr. Waqar Mahmood Director KICS-CERAD, gave introduction of the PSDF training and wished trainees Good Luck for their careers. Mr. Baqar Bilal from GET technologies shared his experiences with old and new batch of PSDF trainees and rest of the audience. He encouraged students to take step ahead of their seniors, to learn from their experiences and to work whole heartedly. He appreciated the work of KICS-CERAD team and added that technology does not fail, it&rsquo;s the skills which need to be developed and polished by hard work.</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Aamir from Tesla Industries gave his appreciation and regard to UET. He admitted the hard work in developing skills of the youth and part played by UET. Furthermore, he provided open opportunities of funding for research and development in solar technology which is need of the hour.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Omar Akhtar from communication team PSDF enlightened with current and future skill development programs of PSDF and gave the count of skilled persons at the end of these programs. He briefed about new scheme of PSDF Skills for Employability 2015 in which 79 Training service providers have been awarded contract and 14 districts are targeted in this scheme. He emphasized on the slogan of PSDF which is to develop skillful youth for brighter Pakistan.</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Mou from ZTE also appreciated work of UET as largest public university. He excitedly admit the friendship of Pak-China in various domains and shared his pleasant experience working with Pakistan Government.</p>\r\n<p>Honorable secretary Energy Mr. Khalid Awais Ranjha addressed with the trainees and guests of the ceremony. He said that the UET, Lahore has always played a vital role in the field of technology dissemination and training of young individuals for their brighter future. He appreciated the help received from KICS-CERAD team in various Government Projects. Additional Secretary gave timeline of Solar Park Project of 1000MW which would be in generation line by March 2016. He insisted that Government is working hard in serious energy conditions and recently, about 200 Engineers will be sent for thermal power plants, solar and wind technology trainings to China. He added best wishes for PSDF trainees and encouraged them by saying that Pakistan has faced worst energy crisis; and solar technology as well as coal technology will prove to be the brighter ray in this darkest hour, for our nation. He appreciated the work of PSDF and Trainers team in Al-KICS who understood the need of nation in this energy calamity and set forth the way of spreading technological expertise to youth of Punjab.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Ceremony moved on with distribution of certificates to the passed trainees in order of their grade ranking. Training Instructors were also encouraged for their efforts in this intensive training and were awarded with Appreciation certificates. Ceremony ended with group photo with honorable guests, teams and trainees.</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2015/july/ceretificate_dist_cerm_photovoltaic3.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"750\" height=\"399\" /></p>', NULL, '2015-07-14', 0, 1),
(64, 118, 'Huawei-UET Certificate Distribution Ceremony', '<p>Huawei UET Telecom &amp; IT Centre (HUTIC) signifies a remarkable collaboration between Huawei Technologies, China and UET Lahore. This centre is focused to bridge the gap between industry and academia by providing the industry with well-equipped and trained young graduates and facilitating the professionals with training and experimentation on the telecom, video conferencing and networking equipment. Huawei Technologies has provided the centre with the latest Telecom and networking equipment of worth 10 Million USD.</p>\r\n<p>In last 13 years the centre has awarded 7000 certificates to the professionals, graduates and under-grad students from industries and from several prestigious universities across Pakistan and abroad.</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/assets/images/gallery/huticcermony1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"699\" height=\"465\" /></p>\r\n<p>To award certificates to the successful trainees HUTIC organized a certificate distribution ceremony on Aug 28, 2015. Mr. Jeffery Chen, Managing Director Huawei was invited as the distinguished guest and Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid Vice Chancellor of UET Lahore was invited as chief guest.</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/assets/images/gallery/huticcermony2.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"699\" height=\"465\" /></p>\r\n<p>The event started with the recitation of Holy Quran. Director HUTIC Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood welcomed the guests and students, and briefed them about the trainings conducted at the centre. Then the respected guest Mr. Jeffery Chen addressed the students. He expressed his views about the current state of Telecom industry in Pakistan and the impact of the courses conducted at the centre. He also expressed his views about technology gap and encourage the students to fill this gap by attending professional trainings. He also said that the hands-on experience during the telecom and networks trainings will help the students to enter the industry. Then the chief guest Prof.Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid Vice Chancellor of UET Lahore showed appreciation to Mr. Jeffery Chen and Huawei for such a strong collaboration with educational institute like UET. Afterwards the guests distributed certificates to the successful students from Afghanistan and Gomal University KPK.</p>\r\n<p>Director HUTIC Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood thanked the honorable dignitaries for attending the event.</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/assets/images/gallery/huticcermony3.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"699\" height=\"465\" /></p>', NULL, '2015-09-02', 6, 1),
(65, 119, 'Building Beautiful Minds. A motivational talk organized by KICS', '<p><img src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/assets/images/gallery/Flyer_BBM.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"699\" height=\"800\" /></p>', NULL, '2015-09-04', 0, 1),
(66, 120, 'Reserch Seminar on NLP Implementation on Quran Text & AI Base Systems for Arabic Language', '<p>Center for Language Engineering is conducting the seminars on bi-weekly basis where CLE researchers present their research work on difference aspects of linguistics, computer science and social science and share their research experiences with the audience. These seminars are intended to be a forum for sharing new research and gaining valuable feedback.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/assets/images/news/NLPseminar.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"700\" height=\"396\" /></p>\r\n<p>Please note the details for the Upcoming Seminar:</p>\r\n<p><strong>Topic:</strong> NLP Implementation on Quran Text &amp; AI Base Systems for Arabic Language</p>\r\n<p><strong>Presentation Date:</strong> Friday, 30th October, 2015<br /><strong>Venue:</strong> KICS Seminar Hall<br /><strong>Time:</strong> 11-30 am &ndash; 12.30 pm</p>\r\n<p><strong>ABSTRACT</strong></p>\r\n<p>Quran text and Arabic Language - Classical Arabic (CA), Modern Standard Arabic (MSA) are important areas for the researchers of Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Artificial Intelligence (AI). Various research groups around the globe are working over these areas in educational institutes as well as in industry. Arabic language is also under consideration of researchers, there are lot of high quality research works and tools available in this regard. Arabic is language of Quran and Hadith, but efforts to structure and promote friendly learning environment for Arabic is still needed to be worked like a charm. There is need to develop the friendly learning environment for Arabic language learning, and also to produce research tools for researchers to improve the speed and quality of the research.</p>\r\n<p>This discussion will be focused on the covers following two areas&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>1. NLP techniques applied on Quran text.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Conventional computational techniques for Quran.</li>\r\n<li>Advance level efforts in this area.</li>\r\n<li>Development phases and current position of presenter&rsquo;s work of Quran text morphological tagging.</li>\r\n<li>Future working dimensions.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>2. AI base systems for Classical Arabic and Modern Standard Arabic.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Development of Algorithms for Arabic Conjugations systems.</li>\r\n<li>Development of translation systems for these conjugation systems for Urdu and English.</li>\r\n<li>Development of teaching modules.</li>\r\n<li>Development of examination modules.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>ABOUT PRESENTER</strong></p>\r\n<p>Mr. Haq Nawaz is a Software Engineer, and 8th year (Final Year) student of Dars-e-Nizami in Jamia Ashrafia Lahore. His research areas are Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques applied on Quran text, &nbsp;and Artificial Intelligence (AI) base systems for teaching and evaluation of Arabic Language, both Modern Standard Arabic and Classical Arabic. And also to develop the research tools for researchers of said domains. He has presented his work in several universities and institutes in Pakistan as well as in international conferences including.</p>\r\n<p>NOORIC 2013 Taibah University International Conference on Advances in Information Technology for the Holy Quran and its Sciences, &nbsp;Madinah Munawara.<br />UCREL Corpus Linguistics 2013 WACL-2 Lancaster University UK.<br />IMAN2014 &nbsp;2nd international conference on Islamic Applications in Computer Sciences &nbsp;Amman Jordan.<br />The 5th Annual International Qur\'anic Conference 2015<br />MUQADDAS 5 University of Malaya Kuala Lumpur Malaysia.</p>\r\n<p>He also is senior member, and consultant of different Unicode base Urdu projects including famous Quran and Hadith desktop software &ldquo;Easy Quran Wa Hadees&rdquo;. Web base Unicode project of &ldquo;Tanzeem Islami Digital &nbsp;library &ldquo; and Online Unicode Hadith project. <a title=\"http://cacpak.com/\" href=\"http://cacpak.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://cacpak.com/</a></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '2015-10-27', 10, 1),
(67, 121, 'Dr. Waqar, Director KICS UET, Attends GITEX 2015 in Dubai\r\n\r\n', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #073763;\">GITEX (Gulf Information Technology Exhibition) is a well-attended technology event that is called the third largest technology fiesta on the planet. The most lucrative about participation in the event is that you bump into more than 130,000 technology professionals with real buying power. It takes place in Dubai World Trade Center in Dubai, UAE annually. GITEX is a colossal business show, exhibition and conference, which turns out to be a mammoth forum for the technologists, entrepreneurs and scientists, who attend to display their products, start up ideas and services.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #073763;\"><img style=\"vertical-align: top;\" src=\"http://blog.getujobs.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/10/8091982067_634b1484f8_b.jpg\" alt=\"GITEX 2015, Dubai\" width=\"700\" height=\"600\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #073763;\"><br /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #073763;\">This year&rsquo;s event, GITEX 2015, was held at Dubai World Trade Center from 18<sup>th</sup> to 22<sup>nd</sup> October, 2015. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director at KICS, UET) attended the event, where he delivered the speech in addition to his presentation and discussion of the research work conducted by KICS at various conferences and panel discussions on IoT (Internet of Things), Big Data, Cloud Computing, Security and other research projects.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #073763;\">Dr. Waqar was invited by Huawei to attend the program discussion and awards&rsquo; ceremony organized by HCIE (Huwaei Certified Internetwork Expert), which is called the highest achievable technical certification offered by Huawei.</span></p>', NULL, '2015-11-02', 1, 1),
(68, 122, '5th Most Downloaded Paper, The Latest Distinction in KICS Pot\r\n\r\n', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">A new distinction knocks the KICS\'s door - Al-Khawarzami Institute of Computer Science grabs a new distinction in its kit. The IoT Labs Journal Paper titled \"Internet of Multimedia Things: Vision and Challenges\", published a few months back in world renowned high quality journal \"Elsevier Ad hoc Networks\", turns out to be the 5th</span><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.3333px;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp;most downloaded paper of the journal. Check out this link </span><a style=\"font-size: 12pt;\" title=\"11th Most Downloaded Journal Paper\" href=\"http://www.journals.elsevier.com/ad-hoc-networks/most-downloaded-articles/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.journals.elsevier.com/ad-hoc-networks/most-downloaded-articles/</a><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">.</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><br /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Elsevier is the world-leading provider of information solutions, which boosts the performance of science, technology professionals and health respectively. It endows the readers/professionals with the best web-based digital solutions - among them include ScienceDirect, Elsevier Research Intelligence, Scopus and ClinicalKey. It publishes more than 2000 journals including the likes of Cell and The Lancet apart from publishing more than 33,000 book titles.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><br /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Read this paper \"Internet of Multimedia Things: Vision and Challenges\" in detail by clicking on this link </span><a href=\"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1570870515000876\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1570870515000876</span></a></p>', NULL, '2015-11-10', 16, 1),
(69, 123, 'KICS Representative Attends IEEE Power and Energy Board Meeting in Thailand', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Usman Munawar, Research Officer at KICS, has recently visited Bangkok, Thailand to attend a board meeting of IEEE Power and Energy Society, USA. He was an international speaker to present a talk on the young professionals plan and update about the energy development in Asia and Pacific. It was the biggest honor for the Pakistani and USA representatives at the event when they were placed in the front rows. Members of IEEE PES Board appreciated the efforts and also revealed the ways for the development of energy in all countries.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/nov/IEEE_Thailand.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"630\" height=\"473\" /></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Munawar interacted with the top notch companies at the event such as Schneider, ABB, Siemens and Hitachi, etc. These companies are on their way to bring giant change in society through their innovative smart grid solutions in the world.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/nov/IEEE_Thailand-02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"630\" height=\"473\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Usman Munawar&rsquo;s trip to Bangkok was funded by IEEE Power and Energy Society. He now has also been added to the IEEE Scholarship plus Project USA Committee. &nbsp;Usman also shared with the attendees of the meeting as to how KICS-UET had been working in Pakistan for the development of sustainable energy. He found the opportunity to meet the professors from different universities of USA, Australia, New Zealand, UK, Europe, Bangladesh and India; with them he shared ideas for bringing the social change in society using energy plans.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/nov/IEEE_Thailand-05.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"630\" height=\"473\" /></p>', NULL, '2015-11-13', 1, 1),
(72, 125, 'Punjab Finance Minister Inaugurates Brainiac 2015 at UET, Lahore', '<p>On December 16th, 2015 the opening ceremony of Brainiac 2015 was held at University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore followed by a ceremony in commemoration of the martyrs of APS, Peshawar.&nbsp; The ceremony for the martyrs of Peshawar started with the national anthem. The ceremony consisted of a performance of Cyanite Hub followed by a video shown there which was made by PSWO.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery//news/dec/Opening%20Ceremony%20of%20Brainiac%2015.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"428\" /></p>\r\n<p>Speeches were also delivered by debating societies of the university. Dr. Ayesha Ghous , the Finance Minister of the Punjab was the chief guest at the ceremony. After Finance Minister&rsquo;s comments on the occasion, Dr. Ayesha Ghous and Prof. Dr. Fazal Khalid Ahmad, Vice Chancellor, UET inaugurated the event Brianniac 2015 by cutting the ribbon. Group photos were also taken at the entrance gate of the Auditorium Complex, UET Lahore.</p>', NULL, '2015-12-17', 1, 1),
(73, 126, 'Rana Mashood, Punjab Education Minister Inaugurates IEEE 9th ICOSST 2015 Opening Ceremony', '<p>Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS), University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore is making significant contribution towards R &amp; D in IT and Telecom sector. As part of its activities, the institute is organizing its 9th International Conference on Open Source Systems and Technologies (ICOSST-2015) from 17th to 19th December, 2015. Conference program includes technical workshops series (OSSW) and student competition (BRAINIAC 2015) with technical sponsorship from IEEE, NJ,USA in collaboration with Higher Education Commission and National ICT R&amp;D Fund Islamabad. The conference got paper submission from 17 countries including US, India, France Germany Malaysia etc. and 20 invited speakers from international countries participated in the conference. The conference consists of a number of technical paper presentation sessions headed by IT industry leaders and international delegates.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2015/dec/icosst3.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"858\" height=\"572\" /><br /><br />The opening ceremony of ICOSST 2015 was held at Seminar Hall, Chemical Department, UET Lahore on Friday, 18th December, 2015. The Chief Guest at the occasion was Rana&nbsp; Mashood Ahmad Khan, provincial Minister of Education, Govt. of the Punjab and&nbsp; Dr. Sakhawat Ali, Director General PCSIR was the distinguished guest.&nbsp; <br /><br />Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood welcomed the honorable guests at the 9th ICOSST and presented a brief introduction of ICOSST 2015 and KICS. Additionally he also revealed the history of ICOSST and the significance of open source especially for countries like Pakistan.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2015/dec/icosst2.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"851\" height=\"567\" /></p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor UET Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid thanked the honorable guests and appreciated the efforts of KICS for conducting such a giant conference. He really appreciated KICS&rsquo;s director Dr. Waqar Mahmood&rsquo;s initiative to launch ICOSST at UET, Lahore. Continuing with his comments, he also talked about the importance of information technology in 21st century. He expressed how Pakistan had been active in the progress of scientific field. Vice Chancellor concluded his speech describing about the Pak-China collaborative works going on at UET.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2015/dec/icosst4.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"568\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2015/dec/icosst5.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"852\" height=\"567\" /></p>\r\n<p>DG PCSIR, Mr. Sakhawat revealed his thoughts on the occasion saying that he congratulates the committee for the magnificent arrangement of this event of 9th ICOSST 2015. He also delivered a brief introduction of PCSIR and its works. Mr. Sakhawat extended his support by offering PCSIR&rsquo;s services to UET.<br />&nbsp;<br />The provincial minister, Rana Mashood Ahmad Khan admired the efforts of UET, Lahore and its cooperation with government of the Punjab in the field of ICT and energy. The minister went on revealing that for the first time in the history Punjab government has allocated 27% budget for education, out of which a big chunk would be consumed on information technology. He expressed that UET is taking a lead role in development and technology and its application for the benefit of common man.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2015/dec/icosst1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"853\" height=\"390\" /></p>\r\n<p>The ceremony concluded with the presentation of shields to the honorable guests followed by a group photo.</p>', NULL, '2015-12-18', 1, 1),
(74, 127, 'Chairman HEC Punjab and DG Sports Invited at the Closing Ceremony of IEEE 9th ICOSST 2015', '<p>Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS), University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore is making significant contribution towards R &amp; D in IT and Telecom sector. As part of its activities, the institute has organized its 9th International Conference on Open Source Systems and Technologies (ICOSST-2015) from 17th to 19th December, 2015. Conference program included technical workshops series (OSSW) and student competition (BRAINIAC 2015) with technical sponsorship from IEEE, NJ, USA in collaboration with Higher Education Commission and National ICT R&amp;D Fund Islamabad. The conference got paper submission from 17 countries including US, India, France Germany Malaysia etc. and 20 invited speakers from international countries participated in the conference. The conference consisted of a number of technical paper presentation sessions headed by IT industry leaders and international delegates.<br /><br />The closing ceremony of ICOSST 2015 was held at Auditorium Complex, UET Lahore on Saturday, 19th December, 2015. The Chief Guest at the occasion was Prof. Dr. Nizam-Ud-Din (Chairman HEC, Punjab) and Mr. Usman Anwar (DG Sports, Punjab) was the distinguished guest.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/ICOSST_15_closing%20ceremony-03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"828\" height=\"548\" /></p>\r\n<p>Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood welcomed the honorable guests at the closing ceremony of IEEE 9th ICOSST 2015. He delivered review and recommendations in his speech. He thanked the honorable guests and then expressed his views on the importance of research and its procedures.&nbsp; Continuing with his views, he discussed each lab&rsquo;s working at KICS in detail. Dr. Waqar Mahmood also told about ICOSST 2015&rsquo;s workshops and presentations done by international speakers.</p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor, UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, showed that he really liked the way ICOSST 2015 took place. He appreciated the efforts of Dr. Waqar and his team to make this happen in apt manner. He also appreciated the international speakers&rsquo; presence at the occasion.<br /><br />DG Sports, Mr. Usman Anwar said that UET has been much active in producing such great talents. He also showed his support for collaborations with KICS UET Lahore. Mr. Usman congratulated the team for arranging ICOSST 2015.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/ICOSST_15_closing%20ceremony-05.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"826\" height=\"548\" /><br />Chief Guest of the occasion, Prof. Dr. Nizam-Ud-Din (Chairman HEC, Punjab) expressed his views, saying that open source is close to his heart. He also described the value and importance of open source. Dr. Nizam appreciated the efforts made to arrange this event in such a fabulous manner. He invited researchers at the conference to work on data collection and data mining for medical records of large swath of the population in the country which is 6th most populous country in the world.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/ICOSST_15_closing%20ceremony-09.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"828\" height=\"559\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/ICOSST_15_closing%20ceremony-08.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"828\" height=\"558\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/ICOSST_15_closing%20ceremony-11.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"828\" height=\"549\" /></p>\r\n<p>The ceremony concluded with the presentations of shields and a group photo followed by dinner.</p>', NULL, '2015-12-19', 1, 1),
(75, 125, '1 Week Professional Solar Training at KICS ', '<p><iframe src=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1zCbKV3ZsiA5ZkZY09O8mGa_Q9hmtk_nHLtxU1mOHAek/viewform?embedded=true\" frameborder=\"0\" marginwidth=\"0\" marginheight=\"0\" width=\"700\" height=\"1000\"></iframe></p>', NULL, '2016-01-13', 11, 1),
(80, 130, 'CERAD UET and Zonergy Company Ltd. Sign an MOU for Mutual Collaborations', '<p>An MOU signing ceremony between Center for Energy Research and Development (CERAD), UET Lahore and Chinese Zonergy Company Ltd was held at Vice Chancellor&rsquo;s Office on 22nd February, 2016, where the key persons from both sides along with Vice Chancellor UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid and KICS&rsquo; Director Waqar Mahmood attended it. The MOU was signed for a mutual collaboration for development of energy solutions and technologies which are within the domain of mutual expertise and are needed for the country. The purpose of this MoU is to initiate further collaboration for the projects of mutual interest.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/MOU_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"750\" height=\"498\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/MOU_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"752\" height=\"498\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor UET chaired the meeting. Mr. Ma Yu, International Sales and Marketing Director Zonergy Company Ltd, described about their projects to the attendees. He expressed as to how efficiently his company has been working in the field. He also explained that how much this collaboration would be beneficial for both the parties.</p>\r\n<p><br />Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, VC UET, then shared his views about this collaboration between CERAD UET and Zonergy Company Ltd and liked the efforts taken by Dr. Waqar to make this happen.</p>\r\n<p><br />Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Director KICS, then briefed about this initiative and collaboration. He also expressed how successfully and effectively the projects are being done in CERAD and how the students are taking advantages of their studies in the field.</p>\r\n<p><br />On Vice Chancellor&rsquo;s suggestion about students&rsquo; trainings and internship programs, Mr. Ma Ya responded affirmatively mentioning his company was interested in hiring the internees.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/MOU_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"754\" height=\"500\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/MOU_05.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"753\" height=\"499\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/MOU_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"753\" height=\"503\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Later the MOU signing ceremony was taken place, where Dr. Waqar Mahmood from KICS UET and Mr. Ma Ya from Zonergy Company Ltd signed the deal.<br />VC UET also told about the Chinese Center and Chinese Language Training Centers functioning at the university.<br />Vice Chancellor, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, then presented a shield as a souvenir to Mr. Ma Ya, who in return also presented a souvenir to the Vice Chancellor.</p>', NULL, '2016-02-22', 1, 1),
(76, 128, 'A Delegation of University of Gujrat Pays a Technical Visit to KICS, UET, Lahore', '<p>A delegation comprising of students and faculty members of University of Gujrat (Sialkot Campus) visited KICS (Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science) , UET, Lahore on 14th January, 2016. They were given a warm welcome by the Director KICS Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Dr. Amir Mahmood, Dr Ali Hammad Akbar, Kashif Bashir (Chair IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section), Usman Munawar (Chair IEEE SAC) and the officials respectively. The delegation was taken to the Seminar Hall at KICS, where the event began with the recitation of Holy Quran followed by Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood&rsquo;s (Director KICS) speech about the research work and research activities going on at the institute. He also presented brief information to the delegation about R&amp;D, KICS Vision, facilities being conferred for research, research labs and KICS&rsquo; services being provided to the government correspondingly. He also expressed about the IEEE activities in KICS and recently held successful conference of IEEE ICOSST 2015.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/DSC_0038.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/DSC_0098.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></p>\r\n<p>Dr. Ali Hammad Akbar then delivered a speech on the topic of &lsquo;Identifying and Assessing an Indigenous ECO System for IT Industry&rsquo;.&nbsp; <br />The delegation was then taken to the tour of the research labs and research centers of KICS. After the tour, Dr Amir Mahmood delivered a speech on &lsquo;Research Trends in High Performance Computing for Regional Content&rsquo; to the delegation.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/DSC_0040.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/DSC_0062.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"839\" height=\"554\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/DSC_0066.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/DSC_0083.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"843\" height=\"585\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/DSC_0134.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec/DSC_0162.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"841\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>Certificates&rsquo; distribution ceremony was held where the students of UOG (Sialkot Campus) and KICS&rsquo; officials were presented the certificates of attendance by Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood and Mr. Kashif Bashir (Chair IEEE Comsoc, Lahore section). A group photo was then taken by the end of the ceremony. </p>', NULL, '2016-01-15', 1, 1),
(77, 129, 'Training on ARM Embedded Systems Development', '<p align=\"center\"><strong> Training on ARM Embedded Systems Development </strong></p>\r\n<p>Learn by doing training that provide hands-on experience of Embedded Systems Development with topics covered from architecture to abstraction</p>\r\n<p><strong> Learning Outcomes: </strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>ARM Cortex-M4 architecture</li>\r\n<li>Assembly language programming</li>\r\n<li>Embedded C programming</li>\r\n<li>Interfacing microcontroller modules</li>\r\n<li>Serial and parallel interfacing</li>\r\n<li>Custom extension board interfacing</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>and much more &hellip;</p>\r\n<p><strong> Why ARM Technology? </strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Higher computational capacity</li>\r\n<li>Low power consumption</li>\r\n<li>Simple instruction set</li>\r\n<li>Deployed in 95% of Smartphones</li>\r\n<li>Wide range of microcontrollers for diverse embedded applications</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong> Duration: </strong> Feb 1 st - Feb 4 th, 2016</p>\r\n<p><strong> Registration Fee: </strong> Rs. 3000/-<strong></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong> Time: </strong> 9:00 am -- 11:30 am</p>\r\n<p><strong> Contact: </strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Muhammad Abdullah</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>0345-4816456</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"mailto:muhammad.abdullah@kics.edu.pk\"> muhammad.abdullah@kics.edu.pk</a></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/ARM_training_poster_v2.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"900\" /></p>', NULL, '2016-01-21', 1, 1),
(78, 129, 'VCs Forum Held at UET, Lahore on 29th Jan, 2016', '<p>VCs Forum on Energy Technologies was held at University of Engineering and Technology Lahore in collaboration with Centre for Energy Research and Development (CERAD) UET Lahore and Energy Department Government of Punjab. The forum started with the recitation of Holy Quran in the morning at the Conference Room at Vice Chancellor&rsquo;s Office in UET and lasted till the evening laced with various activities namely speeches by Chief Guests, VC UET and Director KICS, presentations by the universities on energy technologies and shields&rsquo; conferring.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/VCs%20Forum_06.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"518\" height=\"346\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/VCs%20Forum_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"516\" height=\"364\" /><br /><br />Chief Guest at the occasion was Mr. M. Jahanzaib Khan (Chairman Planning and Development) and distinguished guest was Javed Saleem Qureshi (Chairman Pakistan Engineering Council). Vice Chancellors and the representatives of the universities from all over Pakistan graced the event including Dr. Hassan Aamir Shah (GCU Lahore), Prof. Dr. Afzal Haq (VC NED Karachi), Prof. Dr. Habeeb Ullah Jamal (GIKI Topi) and Prof. Dr. Shahab Khushnood (UET Taxila). VC UET Prof. Dr. Fazal Khalid and Director KICS, Dr. Waqar Mahmood welcomed the guests and addressed to the attendees and briefed about the forum.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/VCs%20Forum_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"520\" height=\"332\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/VCs%20Forum_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"518\" height=\"346\" /><br /><br />The forum was the need of the hour, since the energy crisis is high in Pakistan and government has to engineer a concrete, uninterrupted and comprehensive research based policy to overcome it with universities&rsquo; collaboration. In his address to the forum, Vice Chancellor, UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid said that the universities always act like think tanks for the government and its departments to prepare adequate and effective strategies for the betterment of the country. Therefore sensing the importance of this matter, UET Lahore has arranged this forum to provide a mega platform to different universities to share their thoughts and expertise on energy. He insisted that this effort will surely generate a collective approach to resolve the energy crisis faced by the nation.</p>\r\n<p>Talking to the forum, Chairman Planning and Development Muhammad Jehanzaib Khan described that result oriented planning is based on well-designed research. Thus in this regard, the universities have to encourage practical research in order to get the real target of development at macro level.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/VCs%20Forum_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"517\" height=\"365\" /><br /><br /><br />VCs and their representatives then delivered the presentations on energy efficiencies describing about as to how they have taken the measures and how they are doing the research and works to overcome this crisis.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/VCs%20Forum_07.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"518\" height=\"346\" /><br /><br /></p>\r\n<p>The closing ceremony took place with the arrival of the distinguished guest Mr. Javed Saleem Qureshi (Chairman Pakistan Engineering Council), who talked about the energy crisis in the country and mentioned as to how government could take intuitive and measures to resolve them. He also emphasized on academia&rsquo;s contribution towards taking the steps to resolve the energy crisis in the country.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/VCs%20Forum_08.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"518\" height=\"346\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/VCs%20Forum_05.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"518\" height=\"346\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/VCs%20Forum_09.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"518\" height=\"346\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/VCs%20Forum_10.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"518\" height=\"346\" /><br /><br /></p>\r\n<p>The ceremony concluded with shields&rsquo; presentation done by the distinguished guest Mr. Javed Saleem Qureshi. The shields were presented to the attendees i.e. VCs and their representatives. <br /><br /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '2016-01-29', 1, 1);
INSERT INTO `star_news` (`news_id`, `order`, `news_des`, `news_detail`, `newsthumb`, `news_stamp`, `group_id`, `active`) VALUES
(79, 130, 'Farhan Riaz from KICS Conferred with the Title of Mentor of the Year 2015 in USA', '<p>KICS&rsquo; personnel always do bravura jobs and their works are well-received and liked by the authorities and all and sundry. Distinctions and awards keep pouring on and on and KICS&rsquo; kitty keeps swelling with continuous distinctions. The latest to arrive is an award conferred to Mr. Farhan Riaz at the recently held GCIP Global Forum in Silicon Valley, USA.</p>\r\n<p><br />Mr. Farhan, who is a Program Manager, Technology Incubation and Commercialization Center (TICK) at KICS, has been declared as Mentor of the Year 2015 for GCIP Pakistan at GCIP Global Forum taken place in Silicon Valley in the United States of America.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery//news/jan16/farhan%20riaz.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"681\" height=\"438\" /></p>\r\n<p>This is undoubtedly not only a distinction for him, but also for the institute (Al-Khwarazmi Institute of Computer Science). Congratulations to Mr. Farhan on this achievement.</p>', NULL, '2016-02-03', 1, 1),
(81, 131, 'Delegation of Trevelyan University of Western Australia Visits UET Lahore ', '<p>Engineering is quite challenging field. All the stakeholders related to engineering sector including academia, industry and other concerned departments must develop mutual lines of progress and prosperity by bringing innovation. It was said by Prof. James Trevelyan University of Western Australia while meeting with Vice-Chancellor University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid at UET.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2016/march/aus_visit.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"473\" /></p>\r\n<p>He said that the gap between academics and industrial engineers should be overcome through strong collaboration between research and development to cater down all sort of challenges with proper utilization of resources in progressive manner. He further spoke that mass production always requires mass distribution and mass consumption, so in this regards engineers must have knowledge about the demands of markets and other related segments for achieving success. He said that different technologies of engineering have become interdependent to each other so universities must develop way of coordination with each related discipline to design vivid road map for attaining destination. It is pertinent to mention here that Prof. James Trevelyan is launching a book on his ideas to become successful engineer, within days. During the session Vice-Chancellor Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid talked that today&rsquo;s era is not solo flight era, it is time of collaboration, consensus and team time work. In this dimension UET is practically revising all curricula upto the mark to channelize the efforts of learners, practitioners, mentors and industry with the emergence of innovated skills and practices. He briefed about the external and internal linkages of UET to exchange the ideas, resources and approaches by signing various MoUs. He also revealed that UET is working on interdisciplinary dimension of engineering education which will definitely bring revolution in engineering. He emphasized to activate all dead and sick sectors with comprehensive, effective and result oriented strategies by ensuring the implementation of these.<br /><br />Dr. Waqar Director KICS also briefed about the working of UET at energy sectors and other projects. At this occasion, Dean Dr. Shahid Rafique, Dr. Fiaz Shah, Dr. Nasir Hayat, Dr. Neelum Naz and PRO Adnan Khaliq Bhatti were present. The meeting was ended by presenting shield to Prof. James Trevelyan from VC UET Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid.</p>', NULL, '2016-03-03', 1, 1),
(82, 132, 'Certificate Distribution Ceremony of Huawei-UET Conducted at KICS Seminar Hall', '<p>Huawei UET Telecom &amp; IT Centre (HUTIC) is a lucrative result of the significant collaboration between Huawei Technologies, China and UET Lahore. This center has been pivotal in bridging the gap between industry and academia by providing the industry with well-equipped and trained young graduates and facilitating the professionals with training and experimentation in telecom, video conferencing and networking equipment. The momentous achievement of the center is that in last 13 years or so, it has awarded 7000 certificates to the professionals, graduates and undergraduates students from industries and from several prestigious universities across Pakistan and abroad.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2016/march/huawae_certificate1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"844\" height=\"633\" /></p>\r\n<p><br />In order to award the successful trainees with certificates, a certificate distribution ceremony took place at KICS Seminar Hall in UET, Lahore on 8th March, 2016, where Mr. Stanley Zhao, Deputy Managing Director Huawei (chief guest) , and Moosa Nadeem, Director Huwaei, graced the occasion with their presence. Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, Vice Chancellor UET, Lahore and Waqar Mahmood, Director KICS were also present there.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2016/march/huawae_certificate2.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"843\" height=\"632\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2016/march/huawae_certificate3.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"844\" height=\"633\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The event started with the recitation of Holy Quran followed by a welcome speech by Dr. Waqar Mahmood delivered to the attendees. He also briefed about the trainings conducted at the center. Mr. Stanley Zhao, chief guest of the occasion, then addressed and in his speech, he talked about the current scenario of the telecom industry and the impact of the courses being held at the center. Vice Chancellor, UET, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, appreciated the collaboration between Huawei and UET, Lahore and liked the way the center has been delivering brilliant results. <br />The ceremony concluded with certificates distribution awarded to the successful trainees.</p>', NULL, '2016-03-09', 1, 1),
(83, 133, 'UET Peshawar Pays a Technical Visit to UET Lahore ', '<div>UET Peshawar paid a technical visit to University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore on 9th March, 2016. The delegation comprised of students and faculty members, who were taken to visit various departments of UET such as KICS (Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science), Mechatronics and AERIL (Alternate Energy Research and Innovation Lab) respectively. Kashif Bashir, Manager HUTIC (HUAWEI UET Telecom IT Center), headed the tour by showing and guiding the delegation.</div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/jan16/UET_Peshwar.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"492\" /></div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>In addition to their visit to KICS and Mechatronics, they were also taken to visit Huwaei Center, where they were shown the equipments and their functioning. At AERIL Lab, the delegation saw the lab&rsquo;s activities, equipments installed there and also saw how the solar system operated. The students got much inspired by the way the technical equipments were operating.</div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div>Between the two universities &ndash; UET Lahore and UET Peshawar, MOUs signing is expected in future after this technical visit.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2016-03-09', 1, 1),
(84, 132, 'Short course on IC Designing ', '<p>A short course on IC Designing is starting from April 09, 2016. Registration deadline is April 05, 2016.</p>\r\n<p><strong>How to Register: Please fill form and submit to KICS <a href=\"http://kics.edu.pk/doc/RegistrationForm_IC_Design.doc\" target=\"_blank\">&lt;Registration Form&gt;</a></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Course Website :&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/trainings/courses_detail/34\"><strong>http://www.kics.edu.pk/trainings/courses_detail/34</strong></a></p>\r\n<p><strong><br /></strong></p>\r\n<p><img src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/doc/ic_design.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"700\" height=\"1000\" /></p>', NULL, '2016-03-16', 1, 1),
(85, 133, 'KICS UET Lahore has announced Merit list of selected Candidate under the Prime Minister Hunarmand Program', '<p>Removed</p>', NULL, '2016-03-18', 1, 1),
(89, 135, 'Engr. Usman Munawar of KICS Presents Technical Talk & Workshop at IEEE Industrial Application Society International Event in Tunisia & Turkey', '<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/Usman_Tunisia_Turkey_Visit_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"832\" height=\"426\" /></p>\r\n<p>Engr. Usman Munawar, Research officer, KICS, UET Lahore, Pakistan, IEEE Industrial Application Society Young Professionals Sub Committee Asia and Pacific [IEEE Region 10] &amp; IEEE Power and Energy Society Young Professionals Representative Asia and Pacific [IEEE Region 10] and Student Activities Committee Chair IEEE Lahore Section presented a technical talk &ldquo;Smart industry academia linkage proximity model, A way to innovation, Entrepreneurship and commercialization&rdquo; and delivered a Workshop &ldquo;Industry Academia collaboration for better tomorrow&rdquo; to Scientist, Engineers and Students from Industry, academia and society. In IEEE International IAS event, Tunisian forum for industry academia partnership, Tunisia held on 1 &ndash; 3rd April, 2016.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/Usman_Tunisia_Turkey_Visit.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"831\" height=\"378\" />He</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/Usman_Tunisia_Turkey_Visit_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"832\" height=\"426\" /></p>\r\n<p>presented Proximity model for industry academia linkage and shared practices of top 5 economies of world and presented proximity model of industry academia linkage to kick start collaborative activities and advancement between academia and industry on the basics needs of society. He discussed ice breaking activities that can be really helpful to initiate partnership between academia and industry.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/Usman_Tunisia_Turkey_Visit_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"832\" height=\"426\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/Usman_Tunisia_Turkey_Visit_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"832\" height=\"426\" /></p>\r\n<p>In his Round table workshop, he made a group of Technical people with same area of interest and assigned the task to understand basic need of the country and industry. On assessment of the basic need of the country, all groups identified problems of specific field. Mr. Usman Munawar presented Collaborative Model and basic principles for industry academia interaction. All groups worked on problems of specific field and presented solutions of these problems. The aim of the workshop was to make taskforce for Industry Academia collaboration and give directions towards academia industry linkage for better future.</p>\r\n<p>He was highly appreciated and rewarded by IEEE IAS USA, IEEE Tunisian Section, National Engineering School of Gabes Certificate of recognition, Plaques.</p>', NULL, '2016-04-19', 1, 1),
(86, 134, 'Professional Training Course on PLC & HMI', '<p>A short course on IC Designing is starting from April 09, 2016. Registration deadline is April 05, 2016.</p>\r\n<p><strong>How to Register: Please fill form and submit to KICS <a href=\"http://kics.edu.pk/doc/IACL-Form.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">&lt;Registration Form&gt;</a></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Course Website :&nbsp;</strong><strong><a href=\"#\">Coming Soon</a></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong><br /></strong></p>\r\n<p><img src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/doc/plc&amp;hmi.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"700\" height=\"1000\" /></p>', NULL, '2016-03-21', 19, 1),
(87, 134, 'MOU Signed Between UET and PMD and A Mobile Weather Update Software Launched', '<p>On 24th March, 2016, an MOU (Memorandum of Understanding) was signed between University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore and Pakistan Meteorological Department. The event was held at Conference Room at Vice Chancellor&rsquo;s Office, where the VC, UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, Director KICS Waqar Mahmood along with few personnel from KICS and Director General PMD Ghulam Rasool along with personnel from PMD were present. MOU was signed by Vice Chancellor UET, Lahore and Director General PMD. The purpose of this deal is to formalize the liaison between UET Lahore and PMD to promote training exchange, workshops, research collaboration in the areas of mutual interest.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk//newsannouncement/newssection/images/2016/march/cle_mou1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"844\" height=\"561\" /><br /><br />Apart from the MOU signing, the collaboration between the two organizations has also resulted in the launch of a mobile based weather information service, which covers 139 districts of Pakistan. The significant feature of this service is to get the user updated with easy and speedy access to weather forecast. <br /><br />Talking to the participants, Prof. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, VC UET Lahore, said that it was an essential element for the welfare of public to develop strong link of cooperation and coordination among departments. He also mentioned that sharing the expertise with each other could bring up benefits. He also pointed out that UET had been quite active in making relations with government departments, industry and other organizations in order to attain the objective of knowledge based economy at large.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk//newsannouncement/newssection/images/2016/march/cle_mou2.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"838\" height=\"394\" /></p>\r\n<p>Ghulam Rasool, Director General PMD, said that the development of the software about speedy information of the weather would facilitate the masses. He also explained that this software would not only update the users about the weather, but also would let them know about earthquake and flood situations. The ceremony then concluded with the presentation of crest conferred to DG PMD by VC UET Lahore.</p>', NULL, '2016-03-25', 1, 1),
(88, 135, 'KICS UET, Lahore Participates and Displays Its Solar Equipment Stall at National Skill Show, Expo Lahore\r\n\r\n', '<p>KICS UET Lahore has recently particpiated in the National Skill Show held at Expo Center, Johar Town Lahore on 30th March, 2016, where the depertament displayed its solar equipment stall. The show was organized by NVTTC. A good amount of attendees were seen there, and KICS\' stall got central attention from the people out there. Director KICS, Dr. Waqar Mahmood along with Chinese officials attended the stall. It was a wonderful event altogather.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/marc%2016/national_skill_show_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"734\" height=\"551\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/marc%2016/national_skill_show.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"734\" height=\"551\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/marc%2016/national_skill_show_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"738\" height=\"552\" /></p>', NULL, '2016-04-01', 1, 1),
(90, 136, 'Director General NAVTTC Visits KICS, UET Lahore', '<p>Mr. Zulfiqar Cheema, Director General NAVTTC, visited KICS (Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science) today on 20th April, 2016. Director KICS, Waqar Mahmood welcomed the honorable guest, who was then taken to the conference room where a presentation by Dr. Waqar Mahmood delivered to the honorable guest Mr. Zulfiqar Cheema. In his presentation, Dr. Waqar talked about the labs and its functioning at KICS. He explained about each lab and the outcomes being generated from it. He further expressed about the research activities being done at KICS.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/DG_NAVTTC_Visit_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"832\" height=\"426\" /></p>\r\n<p><br />The discussion on NAVTTC courses being run at the institute was masticated by the honorable guest, director KICS, other guests and the participants at the occasion. It was revealed as to how the students are awarded the internships and job placements after they complete their courses. Discussions then continued on various topics such as IT and new inventions in the field of technology.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/DG_NAVTTC_Visit_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"829\" height=\"423\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/DG_NAVTTC_Visit_05.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"832\" height=\"426\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/DG_NAVTTC_Visit_06.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"832\" height=\"426\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/DG_NAVTTC_Visit_07.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"832\" height=\"426\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The Director General then shared his views on NAVTCC courses. He was then taken to visit the labs at KICS. The honorable guest liked the way the labs were working. He was also shown the classrooms where the classes for NAVTTC courses were going on. He interacted with the students and the instructor over there. He showed his satisfaction the way the classes were being conducted.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/DG_NAVTTC_Visit.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"832\" height=\"426\" /></p>\r\n<p>Few future projects were also discussed during the meeting with the Director General. Overall, it was a successful visit that concluded with a group photo.</p>', NULL, '2016-04-20', 1, 1),
(91, 138, 'Seminar on UNIDO’s Cleantech Competition Held at KICS - Application Procedure Explained', '<p>Technology Incubation and Commercialization Center (TICK) organized an orientation session on UNIDO\'s Cleantech Competition on 3rd May, 2016. The event was held at Seminar Hall, KICS in University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore. The event started off with the introduction of the program &lsquo;GCIP (Global Cleantech Innovation Program)&rsquo;. UET&rsquo;s active association with GCIP was much praised at the occasion. A video about the program&rsquo;s activities and functions was shown to the attendees. The presenters such as Dr. Shahina Waheed and Imran Hassan Zaidi along with other noted speakers delivered their views on GCIP.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/UNIDO_Cleantech_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"838\" height=\"472\" /></p>\r\n<p>Ashra, the winner of mentor of the year award, shared her experience with the attendees. Farhan Riaz of KICS, who won last year&rsquo;s Mentor of the Year Award&rsquo; in Silicon Valley, was applauded at the event. The students were explained about applying for the program, registering their business and were further explained how they could start up their own business with the through support (financial and otherwise) of UNIDO.<br />UNIDO&rsquo;s portfolio, goals, winning prices and application procedures were also discussed at the occasion. The winners of the program of last year and the runner-ups were mentioned there. Success stories were shown as well.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2016/UNIDO_cleantech.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"839\" height=\"474\" /></p>\r\n<p><br /><em>**GCIP is world&rsquo;s largest clean technology competition that is looking to help Pakistani entrepreneurs (SMEs and Startups) with the best ideas that deal with today&rsquo;s most imperative energy, environmental and economic challenges. The Cleantech Program in Pakistan is open for applications. This competition is open to all those living in Pakistan with business ideas and prototypes under the eligible categories. Application deadline is 15th May, 2016. To apply online, visit <a href=\"http://www.cleantechopen.com/Pakistan\">www.cleantechopen.com/Pakistan </a></em></p>', NULL, '2016-05-05', 1, 1),
(92, 139, 'Research Talk on CASPR and a Video Conference with Ohio State University Held at KICS', '<p>A research talk on the topic of &ldquo;Building a World-Class Research Group in Controls &amp; Signal Processing in Pakistan&rdquo; took place at Seminar Hall, KICS UET Lahore on 13th May, 2016. The talk started off with the explanation about Controls and Signal Processing Research (CASPR) &ndash; its initiatives and achievements. Prof. Aamer Iqbal Bhatti delivered a detailed lecture on the subject of &ldquo;How to build a world class research group in Controls and Signals Processing&rdquo;. He delivered his views on the topics such as &ldquo;global competitiveness index, impediments faced by the PhD students in Pakistan, evolution of CASPR and its vision, collaborations &amp; affiliations, MOU with Ohio State University USA, research findings, hybrid electric vehicles, aerospace vehicles, underground coal gasification, etc.</p>\r\n<p><br />The event then led to a video conference with the higher officials of Ohio State University, USA. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director KICS UET Lahore), Prof. Aamer Iqbal Bhatti, Dr. Tahir Izhar (Chairman EE, UET Lahore) and Dr. Nasir Hayat (Chairman ME, UET Lahore) along with few other officials attended the conference and interacted with Ohio State University&rsquo;s officials. The conference was about the hybridization of the vehicles, which was installed on the vehicles by KICS, UET and CERAD, UET. Dr. Waqar described CERAD and its activities to Ohio State University&rsquo;s members. Dr. Waqar presented his views on hybridization of rickshaw and bus done by KICS and CERAD. In his presentation, he discussed other matters also. Dr. Aamir Bhatti also described about hybridization of rickshaw and buses. Similar views on hybridization were also presented by Dr. Tahir and Dr. Nasir. The conference concluded on a good note with expected MOUs in future.<br />&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '2016-05-16', 1, 1),
(93, 140, 'Huwaei Declares KICS UET As ‘The Best HALP\' and Mr. Ahsan \'The Best Instructor\' in Middle East Region', '<p>KICS UET never leaves any stone unturned to impress and register a big impact. Honors and distinctions always ooze out every now and then, which without any single doubt make all personnel proud. Another proud moment hits the scene, as KICS UET Lahore has been selected the &lsquo;Best HALP (Huawei Authorized Learning Partners) in the Middle East Region. This really adorns the institute with splendid honor that is heart-warming yet pompous.</p>\r\n<p><br />Huwaei also announced Mr. Ahsan of KICS UET Lahore as the &lsquo;Best Huwaei Instructor in Middle East Region&rsquo;.</p>\r\n<p>In order to check complete details, please visit Huwaei&rsquo;s official website at <a href=\"http://support.huawei.com/learning/news!toNewsInfo?newsId=Node1000010230&amp;lang=en\">http://support.huawei.com/learning/news!toNewsInfo?newsId=Node1000010230&amp;lang=en</a></p>', NULL, '2016-05-25', 1, 1),
(94, 142, 'VC UET Honors Dr. Youn With a Shield for His Exceptional Contribution', '<p>On June 6th, in an event in honor of Dr. Youn from Gwangju University Korea, Vice Chancellor Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid presented shield to Dr. Youn. On KICS&rsquo; invitation, Dr. Youn&rsquo;s visit was arranged by CERAD (Center for Energy Research and Development). He came to perform testing and evaluating the batteries submitted by different vendors. He worked very hard round the clock from 28th May to 6th June on this project and completed the task successfully.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/June%2016/dr.%20youn_shield%20presentation_01%20%282%29.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"532\" /></p>\r\n<p>A meeting between Dr. Youn and VC UET Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid was arranged on a lunch to discuss future energy projects. In the meeting, Dr. Youn enlightened the beneficial funding opportunities in Korea. On the other hand, Vice Chancellor UET Lahore requested Dr. Youn to provide guidance in automating the battery testing facility and also requested him to arrange funding for UET from Korea.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/June%2016/dr.%20youn_shield%20presentation_01%20%281%29.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"532\" /></p>\r\n<p>Note: KICS&rsquo; Energy Lab is providing consultancy services to Punjab Energy Department for execution of a project &lsquo;Solar Systems for Off-Grid and Other Schools in Punjab&rsquo;. Under this project, government will provide 4321 solar systems in entire province where Grid is not available. CERAD provides testing services and KICS provides consultancy services for submitted prototypes.</p>', NULL, '2016-06-09', 1, 1),
(95, 143, 'KICS Personnel Win Global Competition in Portland, Now Invited to Demonstrate in USA', '<p>KICS&rsquo; success track keeps moving on and on, as a new distinction now emerges on its scene. The Institute&rsquo;s personnel have won the global competition. Syed Muhammad Rizwan and Usman Munawar from KICS UET Lahore have bagged second position in IEEE CMDIAS Robotics Demonstration Contest (Global Competition) held in USA. They presented two of their projects in demonstration contest and the best thing was that both the projects qualified for the final presentation in Portland, USA.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/June%2016/Global%20Competition%20USA.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"680\" height=\"596\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Of the two, one project was on Disaster Management and Rescue Robot and another one was on Robo Soccer Player.</p>\r\n<p><br />Good news is that both Syed Muhammad Rizwan and Usman Munawar have now been invited to Portland, USA to demonstrate the projects in October, 2016. We, at KICS, wish them all the best.</p>', NULL, '2016-06-23', 1, 1),
(96, 146, 'Shahid Zulfiqar and Usman Munawar from KICS Bag 3rd Position in CMD Humanitarian Contest, USA', '<p>Another success feather arrives onto the success cap of KICS UET Lahore. Two personnel of Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science namely Shahid Zulfiqar and Mentor IEEE Usman Munawar have bagged CMD Humanitarian Contest 2016. They fetched 3rd position in IEEE Industrial Applications Society CMD Humanitarian Contest 2016 held in Portland, USA. Both have been invited to present their project in Portland, USA in October 2016.</p>\r\n<p><br />The project is relevant to humanitarian and about providing safe water for school children through economical solar water RO Plants. For the preparation of this contest, the team had worked really hard and visited 16 schools for feasibility study.</p>\r\n<p>KICS wishes Shahzad Zulfiqar and Usman Munawar all the best.</p>', NULL, '2016-06-27', 1, 1),
(97, 147, 'IEEE COMSOC Summer School 2016 to Be Held at UET and Punjab University (26th to 29th July, 16)', '<p>Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) UET in collaboration with IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section has announced <strong>&ldquo;<a href=\"http://ieeecomsoclhr.kics.edu.pk/summerschool/\">IEEE COMSOC Summer School Program 2016</a>&rdquo;</strong> to be held on 26th to 29th July 2016. The program is jointly organized by UET Lahore &amp; Punjab University. The seminars during first two days will be conducted at Punjab University and the seminars during second two days will be conducted at KICS-UET Lahore.<br /><br /><strong><a href=\"http://ieeecomsoclhr.kics.edu.pk/summerschool/\">COMSOC Summer School</a></strong> is 2nd such global event after <a href=\"http://www.comsoc.org/summer-school/\">Trento Italy</a>. <br /><br />Who Can Participate? This program has been designed for fresh graduates and MS/PhD students. The program covers fundamental, advanced and hot topics in the field of communication that will enlighten young graduates about current industry trends and future opportunities.<br /><br /><a href=\"http://ieeecomsoclhr.kics.edu.pk/summerschool/invited-speakers/\">Invited Speakers</a> are from LUMS, UET, FAST, COMSATS, HITEC, and Punjab University respectively. Students from different universities from all over Pakistan are welcome to attend. <br /><br />1)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Registration Deadline: 15 July 2016 <br />Note. Registration will be awarded on merit basis. <br /><br />Registration Link is: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/WzNnJW\">https://goo.gl/WzNnJW</a>&nbsp; <br />&nbsp;<br />2)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Program:<br />26 July 2016: Day 1 Punjab University<br />27 July 2016: Day 2 Punjab University<br />28 July 2016: Day 3 UET Lahore<br />29 July 2016: Day 4 UET Lahore<br />&nbsp;<br />UET encourages students to attend <strong>&ldquo;<a href=\"http://ieeecomsoclhr.kics.edu.pk/summerschool/\">IEEE COMSOCSummer School Program 2016</a>&rdquo;</strong>. Event includes Technical Sessions, Technical Visit, Poster Competition, 4 day meals &amp; teas and social dinner. <br /><br />Program Details: <a href=\"http://ieeecomsoclhr.kics.edu.pk/summerschool/program/\">http://ieeecomsoclhr.kics.edu.pk/summerschool/program/</a><br />Facebook: <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=834575246674480\">https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=834575246674480</a><br />Invited Speaker: <a href=\"http://ieeecomsoclhr.kics.edu.pk/summerschool/invited-speakers/\">http://ieeecomsoclhr.kics.edu.pk/summerschool/invited-speakers/</a> <br />COMSOC News: <a href=\"http://www.comsoc.org/blog/ieee-comsoc-lahore-section-introduces-comsoc-summer-school-program-pakistan\">http://www.comsoc.org/blog/ieee-comsoc-lahore-section-introduces-comsoc-summer-school-program-pakistan</a></p>\r\n<p><strong>Steering Committee: <br /></strong></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '2016-07-01', 1, 1),
(98, 148, 'KICS’ Staff Wins 3rd Position in IEEE All Pakistan Final Year Competition', '<p>KICS is going on its way to grab the distinctions. The latest to rave big about is that two internees of RF Lab of KICS have bagged the 3rd position in IEEE All Pakistan Final Year Competition held in Superior University Lahore on 19th July, 2016. The names of these two shinning internees are Asfand Yaar and Syed Zeshaan Haider. The two presented 2D CNC Image Plotter at the competition. The brilliance about this image plotter is that it can plot any 2 dimensional images.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July%2016/superior%20university%20contest-001.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"624\" height=\"414\" /></p>\r\n<p>The best about this project is that it is much economical and is in range of all and sundry. It is basically a new concept for CNC machining and printing industries.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July%2016/superior%20university%20contest-01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"622\" height=\"330\" /></p>\r\n<p>In order to develop of this project, the two internees simulated on solid edge software and then prepared user interface with processing for easy understanding. Novelty of this project is that any of jpg file can be uploaded.<br />&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '2016-07-22', 1, 1),
(99, 149, 'A Sparkling Fiesta IEEE COMSOC Summer School Held in UET and Punjab University', '<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 21.6pt; background: white; vertical-align: baseline;\">&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 11.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;\">Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS), UET in collaboration with IEEE UET Lahore, IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section and IEEE Punjab University organized&nbsp;a 4-day seminar <strong><span style=\"font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; border: none windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-alt: none windowtext 0in; padding: 0in; font-weight: normal; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">&ldquo;</span></strong></span><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><a href=\"http://ieeecomsoclhr.kics.edu.pk/summerschool/\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1; border: none windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-alt: none windowtext 0in; padding: 0in; font-weight: normal; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">IEEE COMSOC Summer School Program 2016</span></strong></a></strong><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1; border: none windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-alt: none windowtext 0in; padding: 0in; font-weight: normal; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">&rdquo; from 26th July to 29th July, 2016</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;\">.First two days&rsquo; events were conducted in Punjab University whereas the third and fourth days&rsquo; events were held at KICS-UET Lahore. The best part about this event is that </span><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><a href=\"http://ieeecomsoclhr.kics.edu.pk/summerschool/\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1; border: none windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-alt: none windowtext 0in; padding: 0in; font-weight: normal; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">COMSOC Summer School</span></strong></a></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;\">&nbsp;is the 2<sup><span style=\"border: none windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-alt: none windowtext 0in; padding: 0in;\">nd<span class=\"apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span></span></sup>such global event after&nbsp;</span><a href=\"http://www.comsoc.org/summer-school/\"><span style=\"font-size: 11.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">Trento,&nbsp;Italy</span></a><span style=\"font-size: 11.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;\">. It was designed for fresh graduates and students doing MS/PhD in the fields of IT and Communication, and students from LUMS, GCU, UET, FAST, PU, NUST and COMSATS in addition to various other universities were part of this event. In total, there were 12 Technical Talks by speakers from various universities across Pakistan including LUMS, UET, FAST, COMSATS, HITEC, and Punjab University respectively. In addition to these talks, Netsol &amp; Huawei officials too delivered talks about the current industry trends and practices. </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 21.6pt; background: white; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July%2016/IEEE01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" /></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 21.6pt; background: white; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;\">On third day, the participants of the Summer School were taken to visit the Huawei Data Center, which they found beneficial. A 6-member delegation of the US State Department was invited to speak on Entrepreneurship, on the 2<sup>nd</sup> day of the Summer School. A poster competition was also held on the second day of the summer school, in which the participants of the summer school presented their projects in front of the US Delegation, VC UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid and Director KICS Dr. Waqar Mehmood. The projects presented were acknowledged by all the judges. </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 21.6pt; background: white; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July%2016/IEEE.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" /></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 21.6pt; background: white; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;\">The closing ceremony was held at Staff Club in UET Lahore, where Vice Chancellor UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, Dr. Naveed A. Malik, VC Virtual University were the chief guests of the ceremony. VC LCWU Dr. Uzma, Director KICS Dr. Waqar, Project Director Pakistan Railways and many other distinguished guests were also present at the occasion. Certificates and shields were presented to the participants, organizers and the speakers of the summer school. The chief guests while speaking on the occasion said that these kind of events are held around the world, and hopefully after this summer school, they expect the events of this kind to continue in Pakistan.</span></p>', NULL, '2016-08-01', 1, 1),
(100, 150, 'Seminar on Patents, Copyrights and Trade Marks Registration Held in KICS', '<p>KICS arranged a seminar on the topic of Patents, Copyrights and Trade Marks Registration in Pakistan on 2nd of August, 2016 at Conference Room in KICS, UET Lahore. The speaker of this seminar was Ms. Shakra Khurshid, who has an MPhil degree in Biotechnology from Quaid-e-Azam University, Islamabad. The event was attended by the key personnel of KICS. The talk was well-received by the participants.</p>\r\n<p><br />A number of topics were discussed such as IPO Pakistan, Legal Framework, Patent, Trademark, Copyrights and so on.</p>\r\n<p><br /><strong>About Speaker:</strong></p>\r\n<p><br />Ms. Shakra Khurshid has done M.Phil in Biotechnology from Quaid-Azam University, Islamabad. She joined IPO Pakistan in 2006. She has practical experience of patent examination and also expertise in relation to national and international policy issues of IP laws. She is a frequent speaker, at public conferences and seminars. She has delivered lectures and training in various</p>\r\n<p><br />Organization / institutes on Patents and particularly on Patent drafting techniques. She is a focal member on IP help line. She has foreign trainings on Patent system and Patent laws. She has done short courses on IP offered by World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO), and World Trade Organization (WTO).</p>', NULL, '2016-08-03', 1, 1),
(101, 151, 'Korean Delegation Visits UET Lahore to Ink Deals', '<p>A delegation from Gwangju University South Korea has arrived at KICS, UET Lahore on 18th August. Dr. Yoon is heading the delegation, who has earlier paid a visit to UET as well few months back for collaborative works between Gawangju University and UET Lahore. This latest tour is also targeted to joint business collaborations among UET, government departments and Gwangju University. The delegation will return to South Korea on Sunday, 21st August.</p>\r\n<p><br />On the first day of the delegation&rsquo;s visit, they were welcomed by Director KICS Dr. Waqar Mahmood at KICS. They were then taken to the Punjab Textbook Board in the company of Dr. Waqar Mahmood and other key personnel of Al-Khawarzami Institute of Computer Science.&nbsp; In the afternoon, Dr. Yoon and other members of the delegation met the students who show keen interest in studying PhD at Gwangju University South Korea on scholarship.</p>\r\n<p><br />In coming days of their stay in Pakistan, the delegation will be meeting with Secretary Energy Department Punjab, higher authorities of the companies which manufacture solar batteries and top level personnel in telecom sector in Islamabad.<br /><br /></p>', NULL, '2016-08-19', 1, 1),
(102, 152, 'Google to Visit UET to Spread Awareness about Google’s Monetization Products', '<p>Technology magnate, Google is all geared up to come to Pakistan in order to pay a visit to local universities for the very first time. The purpose behind the visit is to inspire the students interested in designing and developing the content for the website.&nbsp; There are nine universities to visit on Google&rsquo;s itinerary all over Pakistan. The delegation from Google will commence from 30th August and end on 9th September with&nbsp;&nbsp; a visit to University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July%2016/Google.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"672\" height=\"264\" /></p>\r\n<p>This 11-day visit will be an initiative to encourage the designers, developers and bloggers for making money from the websites and the apps. With this event, the students will be introduced with Google&rsquo;s monetization products such as Google AdSense and Google AdMob. The event will consist of the notable speakers like Waqas Burney (Manager Strategic Online Partnerships &ndash; Web) and Ahmad Nawaz (Strategic Online Partnerships &ndash; Apps). The enthusiasts, who want to make a good career in web designing and app development, will be benefited with this visit. <br />University of Engineering and Technology is going to host Google&rsquo;s delegation on 9th September, 2016. The proposed timing of beginning of the event will be around 3.00 p.m. The event will last till 6.00 p.m. It will witness 2 to 4 speakers who will be making a presentations on the topics like Introducing to online publishing, Introducing Google\'s publishing products (web &amp; apps), Overview on product policies, Case studies, Getting started, Best practices and to name a few.</p>\r\n<p><br />The audience at the occasion will comprise of engineering students, computer science students, sophomore years and above in addition to higher personnel, faculty members and others.</p>\r\n<p><br />In order to attend the event, the students are required to register through <a href=\"https://events.withgoogle.com/Pakistan/\" target=\"_blank\">https://events.withgoogle.com/Pakistan/</a></p>\r\n<p>Google&rsquo;s delegation&rsquo;s official itinerary is as under:</p>\r\n<p>Tue. 30th August, 2016<br />Institute of Business Administration (IBA) Karachi</p>\r\n<p>Wed. 31st August, 2016<br />NED University of Engineering &amp; Technology (NED) Karachi</p>\r\n<p>Thu. 01st September, 2016National University of Computer &amp; Emerging Sciences (FAST-NU) Islamabad</p>\r\n<p>Fri. 02nd September, 2016<br />GIK Institute of Engineering Sciences &amp; Technology (GIKI) Topi</p>\r\n<p>Mon. 05th September, 2016<br />Lahore University of Management Sciences (LUMS) Lahore</p>\r\n<p>Tue. 06th September, 2016<br />University of Gujrat (UOG) Gujrat</p>\r\n<p>Wed. 07th September, 2016<br />University of Central Punjab (UCP) Lahore</p>\r\n<p>Thu. 08th September, 2016<br />National University of Computer &amp; Emerging Sciences (FAST-NU) Lahore</p>\r\n<p>Fri. 09th September, 2016<br />University of Engineering &amp; Technology (UET) Lahore</p>', NULL, '2016-08-25', 1, 1),
(103, 153, 'South Korean Delegation’s Visit to UET Ends up with Govt. & Private Sector’s Collaborations', '<p>South Korean delegation comprises of personnel from Gwangju University South Korea, Honan University South Korea and Astronix paid a visit to University of Engineering and Technology Lahore. They were warmly welcomed by Director KICS UET Lahore, Dr. Waqar Mahmood and other high officials at the department i.e. Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science. It was an utter fruitful visit that ended up with collaborations with government and private sectors.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/August16/IMG_3630.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"600\" /></p>\r\n<p>Following collaborations were made:</p>\r\n<p><br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Industrial linkage between South Korea and Pakistan <br /><br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Installation of LED street lights to reduce power losses<br /><br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Installation of LED manufacturing plants in Pakistan to cater the country requirements <br /><br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 3D holographic game and animation development for electronic media<br /><br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Introduce state of the art technology and beat quality batteries in Telecom industry, army and submarines</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/August16/IMG_3814.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"600\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/August16/IMG_3790.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"600\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/August16/IMG_3693.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"600\" /></p>\r\n<!--[if gte mso 9]><xml>\r\n <w:WordDocument>\r\n  <w:View>Normal</w:View>\r\n  <w:Zoom>0</w:Zoom>\r\n  <w:TrackMoves/>\r\n  <w:TrackFormatting/>\r\n  <w:DoNotShowRevisions/>\r\n  <w:DoNotPrintRevisions/>\r\n  <w:DoNotShowMarkup/>\r\n  <w:DoNotShowComments/>\r\n  <w:DoNotShowInsertionsAndDeletions/>\r\n  <w:DoNotShowPropertyChanges/>\r\n  <w:PunctuationKerning/>\r\n  <w:ValidateAgainstSchemas/>\r\n  <w:SaveIfXMLInvalid>false</w:SaveIfXMLInvalid>\r\n  <w:IgnoreMixedContent>false</w:IgnoreMixedContent>\r\n  <w:AlwaysShowPlaceholderText>false</w:AlwaysShowPlaceholderText>\r\n  <w:DoNotPromoteQF/>\r\n  <w:LidThemeOther>EN-US</w:LidThemeOther>\r\n  <w:LidThemeAsian>X-NONE</w:LidThemeAsian>\r\n  <w:LidThemeComplexScript>X-NONE</w:LidThemeComplexScript>\r\n  <w:Compatibility>\r\n   <w:BreakWrappedTables/>\r\n   <w:SnapToGridInCell/>\r\n   <w:WrapTextWithPunct/>\r\n   <w:UseAsianBreakRules/>\r\n   <w:DontGrowAutofit/>\r\n   <w:SplitPgBreakAndParaMark/>\r\n   <w:DontVertAlignCellWithSp/>\r\n   <w:DontBreakConstrainedForcedTables/>\r\n   <w:DontVertAlignInTxbx/>\r\n   <w:Word11KerningPairs/>\r\n   <w:CachedColBalance/>\r\n  </w:Compatibility>\r\n  <w:BrowserLevel>MicrosoftInternetExplorer4</w:BrowserLevel>\r\n  <m:mathPr>\r\n   <m:mathFont m:val=\"Cambria Math\"/>\r\n   <m:brkBin m:val=\"before\"/>\r\n   <m:brkBinSub m:val=\"--\"/>\r\n   <m:smallFrac m:val=\"off\"/>\r\n   <m:dispDef/>\r\n   <m:lMargin m:val=\"0\"/>\r\n   <m:rMargin m:val=\"0\"/>\r\n   <m:defJc m:val=\"centerGroup\"/>\r\n   <m:wrapIndent m:val=\"1440\"/>\r\n   <m:intLim m:val=\"subSup\"/>\r\n   <m:naryLim m:val=\"undOvr\"/>\r\n  </m:mathPr></w:WordDocument>\r\n</xml><![endif]-->\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dr. Yoon from Gwangju University headed the delegation from South Korea and provided his help in school solarization project. He earlier has also visited UET Lahore few times for various collaborative works and projects.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 2.0in; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; -<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal;\">By Goher Iqbal Punn (Content Developemnt Officer, KICS UET)</em></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 2.5in; text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;<em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Profile: <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/staff/goher_iqbal_punn\" target=\"_self\">http://www.kics.edu.pk/staff/goher_iqbal_punn</a></em></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '2016-08-29', 1, 1);
INSERT INTO `star_news` (`news_id`, `order`, `news_des`, `news_detail`, `newsthumb`, `news_stamp`, `group_id`, `active`) VALUES
(104, 154, 'KICS’ Two Personnel Win 1st Prize at ASME SPDC 2016', '<p>KICS never leaves any stone unturned to sail through the waves of success. The latest to join the bandwagon are two internees namely Asfand Yar and Zeeshan Haider from RF Lab of Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS), who bagged the first prize at ASME (American Society of Mechanical Engineers) Student Professional Development Conference 2016. The event was held at NED UET Karachi on 1st to 3rd August, 2016. The competition was an Asia Pacific level, where KICS&rsquo; internees won the first prize in Student Design Competition as well as in Technical Web page Design Competition.</p>\r\n<p><br />Student Design Competition provides platform for ASME Student Members to present their solutions to a range of design problems, from everyday household tasks to groundbreaking space exploration. Each team is required to design, construct and operate a prototype meeting the requirements of an annually determined problem statement.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery//news/August16/asme.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"752\" height=\"502\" /></p>\r\n<p>The challenge for this year was to build a compact engineering system to manufacture a projectile from a standard sheet of paper and test it by propelling it a maximum distance. The testing took place on a competition course consisted of a 3 meter wide strip along the length of the room with a 1.5-m x 3-m setup area for the system at one end.</p>\r\n<p><br />The best about our projectiles was that they traveled the maximum distance of 9.8 meters and the volume of the machine was 0.0138m3 we got 708 score which happened to be the maximum score that any student section ever achieved. <br />As for web page competition, held at Asia Pacific level Student Professional Development Conferences, it is intended to encourage the delivery of visual presentations using web page technology. Our web page is related to Advance technology in mechanical engineering. <br />After winning the first prize, we are now qualified for finals of IMECE (International Mechanical Engineering Congress &amp; Exposition) which will be held on November 11 &ndash; 17, 2016 in Arizona USA.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><br /><em>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; By Goher Iqbal Punn (Content Development Officer, KICS UET)</em><br /><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Profile: <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/staff/goher_iqbal_punn\" target=\"_self\">http://www.kics.edu.pk/staff/goher_iqbal_punn</a></em></p>', NULL, '2016-08-29', 1, 1),
(105, 155, 'CERAD Applies for 4 Patents in Collaboration with NSR Energies Private Limited', '<p>Recently CERAD has applied for 4 patents in combined collaborations with NSR Energies Private Limited. A group of researchers from RF lab came up with technological advancements and innovations in the field of renewable energy.. They worked on Hydrogen Fuel Cell and Concentrated Solar Power Systems. Their research has marked novelty to their projects. The 4 patents filed for registration at Intellectual Property Organization of Pakistan are mentioned as under:</p>\r\n<p><br />1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Hydrogen generator designed with molybdenum alloy for industrial applications<br />2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Design and simulation of parabolic dish solar thermal cooker.<br />3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Integrated black body absorber of sun light for pre heating.<br />4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A novel design of stove for cooking integrated with CSP system.<br /><br />It is undoubtedly a major step by CERAD towards the development of sustainable energy resources in Pakistan. Energy crisis are much in Pakistan and with the help of advancement in hydrogen fuel cell and concentrated solar power technology, energy crisis will surely be resolved. <br /><br />The researchers, who contributed, include: <br /><br />1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Mr. Arshad MunirKazmi<br />2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Dr. Waqar Mehmood<br />3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Dr. Zulfiqar Ali<br />4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Mr. Sana Ullah Khan<br />5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Ms. Samreen Khan<br />6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Mr. Asjad Zuliqar<br />7.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Mr. Asfand Yaar<br />8.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Mr. Umer Saleem<br /><br /><em>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; By Goher Iqbal Punn (Content Development Officer KICS, UET)</em><br /><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Profile: <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/staff/goher_iqbal_punn\">http://www.kics.edu.pk/staff/goher_iqbal_punn</a></em></p>', NULL, '2016-08-30', 1, 1),
(106, 156, 'UET Students Achieve Distinction', '<p>KICS fetched another colossal distinction recently when 5 UET students were invited to DFKI Kaiserslautern, Germany to work on a joint project taking place between KICS UET and DFKI Kaiserslautern.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The 5 luminous students who departed for Germany included:</p>\r\n<p>1: Abdullah Akmal (2012-Session)<br />2: Rayyan Khalid (2013-Session)<br />3: Muhammad Hamza Sharif (2013-Session)<br />4: Maira Nadeem (2013-Session)<br />5: Ayesha Sahar (2013-Session)</p>\r\n<p><br />These students are from UET&rsquo;s Computer Engineering and Science Department. Of these five, Abdullah Akmal is currently working in KICS UET. They are on their way to work on the project.</p>\r\n<p><br />This is a collaborative research project taking place between KICS UET Lahore and Computer Science Department, Technical University Kaiserslautern (TU KL) Germany.</p>\r\n<p>Pakistan\'s major exports are fruits &amp; vegetables and textile products. Quality standards has to be maintained in order to export the items into world market. As for fruits and vegetables products, major cause of rejection in world market in particular in Europe is fruit files. Therefore to overcome this cause, there are few treatments, which are applied prior to export the products. The goal of this project called &ldquo;iFruitFlyDetector &ndash; An Intelligent System for Fruits Quality Control&rdquo; is to provide an intelligent vision based solution capable of detecting the fruits and vegetables affected by fruit flies. It is funded by DAAD.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/August16/Aisha,%20Hamza,%20Rayyan,%20Maira.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"402\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The project provides opportunities to our students to visit Germany and work on innovative thermal imaging technologies.</p>\r\n<p><br /><em><strong>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; By Goher Iqbal Punn (Content Development Officer KICS, UET)</strong></em><br /><em><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Profile: <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/staff/goher_iqbal_punn\" target=\"_self\">http://www.kics.edu.pk/staff/goher_iqbal_punn</a></strong></em></p>', NULL, '2016-08-31', 1, 1),
(107, 34, 'KICS Launch Programmable Logic Controller Courses with the collaboration of Punjab Skill Development Fund   ', '<p>KICS Launch Programmable Logic Controller(PLC)Courses with the collaboration of Punjab Skill Development Fund</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/images/2016/sep/psdf_plcAd.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"750\" height=\"625\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><a style=\"text-align: right;\" href=\"http://kics.edu.pk/images/2016/sep/PSDF_PLC_form.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"><input class=\"btn btn-primary\" type=\"button\" name=\"button\" value=\"Download Resistration Form\" /></a></div>', NULL, '2016-09-05', 19, 0),
(108, 157, 'Google’s Seminar on Adsense and Ad Mob in UET – A Well- Attended Event', '<p>Google paid a visit to University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 9th September to discuss Google&rsquo;s publishing products and to spread awareness about the same among the attendees of the event. It was an altogether a unique and really profitable event in terms of information and knowledge. The university students and other attendees took special and keen interest in this seminar arranged at university&rsquo;s auditorium. It was a full-attended event despite of the upcoming holidays of Eid Ul Azha. Two speakers from Google Singapore talked about the Google publishing products in particular and also delivered their views on some of other products Google deals with.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/August16/google_event.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"407\" /></p>\r\n<p><br />The event was targeted to unleash and open out Google Adsense and Google Ad Mob mainly. The speakers thoroughly and very comprehensively let these products loose among the attendees making them know how these products work actually and how the people like bloggers, websites&rsquo; owners and apps developers make money from these products.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/August16/google_event_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"407\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/August16/google_event_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"407\" /></p>\r\n<p><br />There was also a questions and answers session held at the occasion. Most importantly, the Google personnel also let the students of the university know about the career opportunities at Google helping them know as to how they can join in the biggie of the trade.</p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor of University of Technology Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid was the chief guest at the occasion. He presented the shields to the Google speakers. The event wrapped up with a group photo.</p>\r\n<p><br /><em><strong>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; By Goher Iqbal Punn (Content Development Officer KICS, UET)</strong></em><br /><em><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Profile: <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/staff/goher_iqbal_punn\">http://www.kics.edu.pk/staff/goher_iqbal_punn</a></strong></em></p>', NULL, '2016-09-16', 1, 1),
(109, 158, 'KICS’ Pearson Lab Awarded ‘Highest Grade of Excellent’', '<p>KICS&rsquo; lab Pearson VUE, that conducts examinations such as HCNA, CCNA, GMAT, HCNP, etc, has recently been awarded with a distinction of &lsquo;Highest Grade of Excellent&rsquo; by Pearson VUE Channel Quality. The test center was visited by a secret shopper to review center&rsquo;s operations and to check if the policies and procedures were being followed properly. After the secret inspection, the test center was conferred with the &lsquo;Highest Grade of Excellent&rsquo; that is simply an honor for the test center and KICS.</p>\r\n<p>The shopper found excellent facilities being provided there to the candidates. The testing area was rated clean and comfortable. Service was rated very high and the candidates\' comments were simply awesome.</p>', NULL, '2016-10-18', 1, 1),
(110, 159, 'Well-Awaited Seminar ‘5 Habits of Highly Successful People’ Takes Place at KICS', '<p>A seminar on &lsquo;5 Habits of Highly Successful People&rsquo; was organized at KICS&rsquo; Seminar Hall at University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 26th October, 2016. It was much-awaited event that grabbed the attention of the students and university personnel. It was well-attended seminar, where the speaker Mr. Muhammad Ali presented 5 habits, which if one uses, will be highly successful in life.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct%2016/5%20habits_kics_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"733\" height=\"487\" /></p>\r\n<p>The 5 habits mentioned at the seminar were derived from Holy Quran. The speaker insisted that if these 5 habits were used in life and career, one would be highly successful. They were as following:</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct%2016/5%20habits_kics_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"733\" height=\"487\" /></p>\r\n<p><br />1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Straight Talk<br />2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Say Only That is Good<br />3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Share Your Grief and Sorrow Only with Allah<br />4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Never Never Never Never Never Give Up<br />5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Move Forward</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct%2016/5%20habits_kics.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"733\" height=\"487\" /></p>\r\n<p>The seminar concluded with a shield presentation conferred to the speaker by the Director KICS Dr. Waqar Mahmood. </p>', NULL, '2016-10-27', 1, 1),
(111, 160, 'DG NAVTTC and CEO QA Solar,GM HR PTCL Attend NAVTTC Certificates Distribution Ceremony', '<p>On 2nd November 2016, certificate distribution ceremony for NAVTTC courses was conducted at Chemical Engineering Department Hall at University of Engineering and Technology Lahore. Distinguished guests such as CEO Dynamic Green Junaid Ishaq, CEO Quaid-E-Azam Solar Park Muhammad Amjad, GM ZTE Mr. Bing, GM HR PTCL Nadeem Nazeer and CEO Corge Aslam Azad respectively were invited. Chief Guest of the occasion was DG NAVTTC Punjab Haji Muhammad Dogar.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct%2016/DSC_0256.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"744\" height=\"367\" /></p>\r\n<p>The ceremony started with national anthem followed by the recitation of Holy Quran. Director KICS Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood welcomed the distinguished guests. He also briefed the audience and the guests with a short presentation on KICS&rsquo; overview, NAVTTC trainings, HUTIC and CERAD.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct%2016/SPP_9527.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"744\" height=\"367\" /></p>\r\n<p>A video was played, showing the audience how the training courses of NAVTTC happen at KICS.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct%2016/SPP_9638.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"744\" height=\"367\" /></p>\r\n<p>In his speech, CEO Dynamic Green Junaid Ishaq talked about the opportunities the students may avail after the professional courses. CEO Quaid-E-Azam Solar Park Muhammd Amjad said that due to electricity crisis in Pakistan, energy industry was on full boom and a number of projects were seen to produce electricty. He further mentioned that students now could see a bright future in this industry. Mr. Bing from ZTE expressed his views, saying ZTE was on its way of success with a number of ventures with Punjab Energy Department. He talked about energy crisis in Pakistan and mentioned that solar energy has much future in Pakistan. GM HR PTCL Nadeem announced that PTCL is now offering employment to fresh graduates. Mr. Aslam Azad showed the audience the solar cars and bikes designed by him.</p>\r\n<p>DG NAVTTC Haji Muhammad Dogar, in his speech, poured light on the burning issue of unemployment in the country. He thanked PM&rsquo;s efforts for initiating the professional training courses for the students, which are helping them to find employment or starting their own small businesses. He also asked Dr. Waqar to use his sources to fetch jobs for the graduated students of NAVTTC training course. DG NAVTTC also asked for the favor to find jobs for the NAVTTC trained students from other distinguished guests. In response, CEO Quaid-E-Azam Solar Park announced to take 3 to 5 top students on board. Other guests too showed their inclination towards hiring the talents of NAVTTC students. Haji Muhammad Dogar also revealed that these professional training courses are ones of their kinds and are very important for the students who want to make good career moves in life and who want to have good jobs since there is a big market out there for the students who get trained with the skills taught in these courses. Director General NAVTTC showed affable side of him to the students of NAVTTC by interacting with them. He even passed on his cell number to the students in case they would like to make contact with him in case of difficulties.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct%2016/SPP_9727.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"744\" height=\"367\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct%2016/DSC_0403.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"744\" height=\"367\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct%2016/DSC_0407.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"744\" height=\"367\" /></p>\r\n<p>The ceremony concluded with the certification distribution. All the distinguished guests presented certificates to the graduated students. Few of the students were also awarded with kits along with the certificates. Shields were presented to the distinguished guests by DG NAVTTC, whereas the chief guest was presented a shield by Director KICS Waqar Mahmood. A group photo with the guests, NAVTTC and KICS officials together with the students of NAVTTC course was taken outside the hall.</p>', NULL, '2016-11-03', 1, 1),
