 <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"39\" QFormat=\"true\" Name=\"TOC Heading\"/>\r\n </w:LatentStyles>\r\n</xml><![endif]--><!--[if gte mso 10]>\r\n<style>\r\n /* Style Definitions */\r\n table.MsoNormalTable\r\n	{mso-style-name:\"Table Normal\";\r\n	mso-tstyle-rowband-size:0;\r\n	mso-tstyle-colband-size:0;\r\n	mso-style-noshow:yes;\r\n	mso-style-priority:99;\r\n	mso-style-qformat:yes;\r\n	mso-style-parent:\"\";\r\n	mso-padding-alt:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;\r\n	mso-para-margin:0in;\r\n	mso-para-margin-bottom:.0001pt;\r\n	mso-pagination:widow-orphan;\r\n	font-size:11.0pt;\r\n	font-family:\"Calibri\",\"sans-serif\";\r\n	mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\n	mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\n	mso-fareast-font-family:\"Times New Roman\";\r\n	mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;\r\n	mso-hansi-font-family:Calibri;\r\n	mso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\n	mso-bidi-font-family:\"Times New Roman\";\r\n	mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;}\r\n</style>\r\n<![endif]-->UET in collaboration with KICS is going to organize All Pakistan DICE Energy &amp; Water 2016 event. It is certainly going to be a mega occassion of its kind to be attended by hefty amount of people from faculties, students to the people from all walks of life. Students from all departments are welcome to attend it particularly those from mechanical, chemical, environmental and mechatronics can extract the benefits from this idiosyncratic event.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct%2016/dice%20logo.png\" alt=\"\" /></p>\r\n<p>Everyone is welcome to participate at DICE 2016 that is scheduled to be held on 19th and 20th December, 2016. More details on this event including the venue, guests list and updates can be found at KICS&rsquo; website <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk\">www.kics.edu.pk</a> Keep visiting.</p>', NULL, '2016-11-09', 1, 1),
(113, 162, 'Rizwan Naqvi of KICS Honored at IEEE Conference in Portland, USA', '<p><strong>Annual General Meeting of Industry Applications Society IEEE (2016)</strong><br /><br />IEEE Industry Applications Society Annual Meeting 2016 held in Portland, United States of America from 1st to 6th October 2016 at Marriot Downtown Portland, addressed the technical interests related to industrial applications of electrical energy.<br /><br /><strong>Participants of the Meeting</strong><br /><br />The meeting witnessed representatives from 40 countries of the world. Of them, Syed Muhammad Rizwan from KICS, University of Engineering and Technology Lahore was invited.</p>\r\n<p><br /><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct%2016/received_10157483471815640.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"720\" height=\"521\" /><br /><strong></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Syed Rizwan&rsquo;s Presentation and Representation at the Conference</strong><br /><br />At this high-status and exalted meeting at Marriot in Portland, Mr. Rizwan participated and presented his projects, which had won 2nd position in Student Robotics Demonstration Contest of IAS. He also represented IAS Chapter Lahore Section in the conference. His presentation was related to &lsquo;Robo Soccer Player&rsquo; and &lsquo;Rescue Robot&rsquo;. Rizwan also discussed technical details of his projects.<br /><br /><strong>Poster Presentation at the Conference</strong><br /><br />Syed Rizwan also participated in poster presentations representing humanitarian projects of KICS (Al-Khwarazami Institute of Computer Science) UET Lahore. He represented solar and power energy project on solar water filteration being mentored by KICS&rsquo; researchers (personnel) &ndash; Mr. Usman Munawar and Mr. Shahid Zulfiqar.<br /><strong></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct%2016/20161002_203722.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"720\" height=\"521\" /></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Conclusion</strong><br /><br />It was a worthwhile conference attended by the scholars of the world. Mr. Rizwan really felt honored by representing University of Engineering and Technology Lahore and Pakistan in the conference.&nbsp; You may visit the below link to get complete schedule of the event coupled with Mr. Rizwan&rsquo;s presentation held on 3rd October.<br /><br /><a href=\"http://www.ewh.ieee.org/soc/ias/2016/include/docs/2016%20IAS%20Annual%20Meeting%20Program.pdf\">http://www.ewh.ieee.org/soc/ias/2016/include/docs/2016%20IAS%20Annual%20Meeting%20Program.pdf</a></p>', NULL, '2016-11-11', 1, 1),
(114, 163, 'KICS and IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section Arrange Seminar on Job Hunting in Gulf Countries', '<p>IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section and KICS arranged a seminar on the topic of &lsquo;Job Hunting in Gulf Countries&rsquo; for the students of University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 16th November, 2016. The event was held at Seminar Hall in KICS, UET, Lahore, where Ms. Majida Khanam was invited as a speaker to deliver the lecture. She is a gulf-based human resource professional, who runs a recruitment firm called Ribat International Overseas Employment Agency.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/DSC_0017.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"782\" height=\"520\" /></p>\r\n<p>The event started with the recitation of Holy Quran followed by the welcome note delivered by Mr. Kashif Bashir, Chair IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section and Manager HUTIC. The host of the event Rizwan Naqvi then presented the introduction of the speaker. Later Ms. Majida began her lecture with a special focus on how to find jobs in local and overseas markets such as Gulf States. She went on revealing the ways to grab job opportunities overseas. She explained the difference between assumptions and reality, which the students or job seekers often stumble upon when slipping into finding jobs in the market.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/DSC_0011.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"782\" height=\"520\" /></p>\r\n<p>Ms. Majida insisted the job-seekers to focus on the strategies to be adopted while seeking the jobs overseas and even in local market. She gave the tips as to how one can stand out among the crowd. She told the students to narrow down their choices while they were on the verge of job hunting. She mentioned to zero in their target before they go out for job fetching.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/DSC_0035.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"782\" height=\"520\" /></p>\r\n<p>She told the students to make professional CV, since this was what was seen first, as resumes were the mirrors of one&rsquo;s skills and education. Ms. Majida also pointed out the importance of social networking and social media, as the use of these platforms happened to be the best in grabbing the best opportunities in the market. The big importance of the job portals was also revealed at the occasion. In the end, she mentioned the ways to get prepared for the interviews.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/DSC_0036.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"782\" height=\"520\" /></p>\r\n<p>The event was closed with the distribution of the appreciation certificate conferred to Ms. Majida by Mr. Kashif Bashir and Mr. Usman Munawar. KICS&rsquo; tradition of taking a group photo was also observed. Want to see the photos of the event, enjoy the picture gallery by clicking this link <a href=\"https://goo.gl/cJfU9T\" target=\"_blank\">https://goo.gl/cJfU9T</a></p>', NULL, '2016-11-16', 1, 1),
(115, 164, 'KICS UET and Huwaei Telecom Sign MOU to Conduct Training Courses at Model Town Campus Lahore', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">An MOU signing ceremony took place at Vice Chancellor&rsquo;s office on 10<sup>th</sup> November, 2016, where Al-Khawarizimi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) UET and Huwaei Telecom signed a deed (MOU) to conduct training courses at P-6 Model Town, Lahore (a UET Lahore&rsquo;s sub-campus). In the light of this memorandum of understanding HUTIC Model Town Training Center will be launched, where the training courses are conducted by the highly professional instructors of KICS UET Lahore. Chief Guest of the occasion was Mr. David, Director Training Huwaei Middle East Region. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/KICS-Huwaei%20MOU-01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"688\" height=\"339\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The ceremony began with the recitation of Holy Quran followed by Dr. Waqar&rsquo;s presentation on Huwaei and UET&rsquo;s business relationship and the progresses made so far since the commencement of HUTIC (Huawei UET Joint Telecom and IT Centre). Prof. Dr. Waqar also briefed about the HUTIC&rsquo;s significant developments made so far in terms of training the students and professionals. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/KICS-Huwaei%20MOU-02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"689\" height=\"337\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Director Huawei, Mr. Sohail Akbar, praised the progress of HUTIC in big words, whereas the chief guest Mr. David said that it was a pleasure for him to be a partner of KICS UET. He further praised the state of the art networking labs established at the center and the way the center arranged successful trainings.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/KICS-Huwaei%20MOU-03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"683\" height=\"465\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Ms. Saba Iram, HUTIC personnel, who has been declared the first female student of Huawei completing the highest level of Huwaei Certification HCIE in the region after China, was conferred with a distinction certificate. The same was also awarded to Mr. Fahmeed, HUTIC personnel, who bagged his HCIE certification.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/KICS-Huwaei%20MOU-04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"689\" height=\"479\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">HUTIC Model Town Training Centre will be operational from last week of December, 2016.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The ceremony concluded with the souvenirs&rsquo; presentations to the guests of the event. <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>', NULL, '2016-11-17', 1, 1),
(116, 165, 'Huawei Conducts ICT Skill Competition to Award Free China Trip & Fabulous Prizes in UET Lahore', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><em>Participate in a Competition and Win Free Trip to China &amp; Other Fabulous Prizes...!</em><br /></span></strong></p>\r\n<p>Would you like to visit the eye-candy and breath-arresting locales of China and that too at no expense from your pocket? &lsquo;Surely yes&rsquo; is the answer! All you have to do is to participate in a competition to be conducted by Huawei and its learning partner. &lsquo;Huawei ICT Skill Competition Pakistan&rsquo; is a nationwide competition geared up to test the skills of the participants. It will provide students with an opportunity to compete in an international environment coupled with a chance to test their dexterities. <strong>The winners of the first two rounds will bag the exclusive opportunity to visit China at the expense of Huawei for the worldwide final competition.</strong> There are three other prizes to be awarded to the winners:</p>\r\n<p><br /><strong>1st Prize: Huawei P9 Smart Phone Plus HCIE Exam Voucher</strong><br /><strong>2nd Prize: Huawei Smart Watch Plus HCNP Exam Voucher</strong><br /><strong>3rd Prize: Huawei Y5 II Smart Phone &amp; HCNP Exam Voucher</strong></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.uet.edu.pk/main_slides/huawei_ict_competition.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"171\" /></p>\r\n<p>Avail this chance to learn valuable networking knowledge. Judge your potential, know your weaknesses, showcase your brainpower and create interactive networking skills.</p>\r\n<p><br />In order to be equipped with test&rsquo;s content and format, you may go through the attached brochure. The introductory session will be arranged on 21st November, 2016 at Seminar Hall in KICS, UET Lahore. Competition will be held on 22nd November, 2016 at Seminar Hall, Chemical Engineering Department in University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore.</p>\r\n<p><a class=\"btn btn-success\" href=\"https://www.huaweiacad.com/webapps/hw-toboo-BBLEARN/match/exec.do?operation=apply&amp;t=1479455715750\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Register Here</strong></a></p>\r\n<p><br />To get more details about the test and the competition, you may contact Mr. Fahmeed Akram at <a href=\"mailto:fahmeed.akram@kics.edu.pk\">fahmeed.akram@kics.edu.pk</a> and at his cell 0300-8038396<br /><br /></p>', NULL, '2016-11-18', 1, 1);
INSERT INTO `star_news` (`news_id`, `order`, `news_des`, `news_detail`, `newsthumb`, `news_stamp`, `group_id`, `active`) VALUES
(117, 166, 'CLT 16 – A Conference Laced with Paper Presentations & Talks Taken Place in UET', '<p>6th International Conference on Language and Technology 2016 (CLT16) recently took place in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 17th and 18th November. It was conducted by CLE (Center for Language Engineering), a research lab of KICS (Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science) UET Lahore. CLT 16 is a biennial conference series organized by Society for Natural Language Processing Pakistan (SNLP) and is conducted to promote the area of research, educate the masses and to make the decision making authorities realize the importance of Language and Technology in this modern age of computers. Higher Education Commission of Pakistan (HEC), Punjab Higher Education Commission (PHEC), and the German Academic Exchange Service (DAAD) were the sponsors for this conference.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/CLT16-03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"561\" /></p>\r\n<p>At the event, 38 papers were submitted &ndash; out of which, 12 were chosen for presentation and 4 for posters after a thorough review done by an international technical committee. These papers covered Pashto, Sindhi, Mewati and Urdu language specifically, and a number of other areas including linguistics and computational aspects of phonetics, phonology, syntax and semantics. The conference also witnessed exciting talks by Dr. Miriam Butt from Germany, Dr. Hassan Sajjad from Qatar and many other eminent national researchers of NLP presenting their recent research in syntax, prosody, pattern recognition and frontiers in machine translation.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/CLT16-02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"561\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/CLT16-01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"561\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/CLT16-04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"561\" /></p>\r\n<p>The last of the conference concluded with a panel discussion on Building Synergies and Collaborations, where the panelists discussed possible points of mutual collaboration among the research groups. At the closing ceremony, honorable Vice Chancellor of UET, Dr. Fazal Ahamd Khlaid and Director KICS, Waqar Mahmood appreciated the research team at CLE led by Dr. Sarmad Hussain.</p>', NULL, '2016-11-24', 1, 1),
(118, 167, '2nd International Workshop on Pattern Recognition Applications in UET – An Event to Rave Big About', '<p>2nd International Workshop on Pattern Recognition Applications took place at New Auditorium Complex in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 18th November 2016. KICS (Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science) organized the event in collaboration with Pattern Recognition Society (PPRS) and Technical University Kaiserslautern, Germany. The event was sponsored by German Academic Exchange Service (DAAD). The first workshop was organized by NUST last year (2015).</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/pattern%20applications.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"480\" /></p>\r\n<p>This workshop witnessed researchers from various application domains of pattern recognition and provided the opportunity to get familiar with the current ongoing pattern recognition research in Pakistan. It had demonstrations/presentations of ongoing DAAD collaborative research projects between different Pakistan and Germany research institutes. <br /><br />Inter Universities&rsquo; speakers delivered talks and shared their research. Additionally panel discussion was held parallel with CLE (Center for Language Engineering) speakers. The event was laced with the speakers from NUST, IST, BZU and UCP who attended with their students to explain their projects. The speakers such as Dr. Faisal Shafait (NUST), Dr. Imran Ahmad Siddiqui (Bahria University), Dr. Khurran Khurshid (Institute of Space Technology), Dr. Yasir Niaz Khan (University of Central Punjab) and Dr. Muhammad Imran Malik (NUST) graced the occasion. <br /><br /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/pattern%20applications-01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"837\" height=\"559\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/pattern%20applications-02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"837\" height=\"558\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/pattern%20applications-03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"837\" height=\"559\" /></p>\r\n<p>The ceremony concluded by the Vice Chancellor of University of Engineering and Technology Lahore, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid who arrived along with Director KICS, Waqar Mahmood. Shields were presented to the speakers and students and organizers were conferred with the certificates.</p>', NULL, '2016-11-25', 1, 1),
(119, 168, 'Chairman CGSS Lieutenant General (R) Zaheer Ul Islam Visits UET Lahore', '<p>On 24th November 2016, a delegation of Center for Excellence of Global and Strategic Studies (CGSS) led by the Chairman CGSS Lieutenant General (R) Zaheer Ul Islam paid a visit to University of Engineering and Technology Lahore. The delegation was greeted and welcomed at Conference Room at Vice Chancellor&rsquo;s office, where VC UET Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid along with other officials of varsity welcomed them. During the meeting, Chairman CGSS Lieutenant General (R) Zaheer ul Islam said that CGSS was interested in making collaboration with UET in many areas of joint ventures to stabilize and strengthen the departments for the bright future of Pakistan.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/CGSS_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"753\" height=\"467\" /></p>\r\n<p><br />Talking to the participants, the chairman said that China Pakistan Economic Corridor was a grand opportunity for all stakeholders to contribute for image building and strong economy of Pakistan. He further revealed CGSS&rsquo;s commitment to extend its relations with academia. To fulfill all this, a number of agreements are being signed by national and international organizations. He appreciated UET&rsquo;s role to contribute for Pakistan.</p>\r\n<p><br />In his address, Vice Chancellor UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmed said that communal measures were required to make Pakistan progress and prosperous in the field of science and technology. Urging the intellectuals, experts and distinguished practitioners to play vital roles of becoming think tanks, VC said that they were the big assets of Pakistan. He also mentioned that the university was fully ready to work with strategic setups through technology, skills, training and other technical assistance.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/CGSS_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"752\" height=\"500\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/CGSS_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"752\" height=\"500\" /></p>\r\n<p>Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Director KICS UET Lahore, briefed the guests about the MoUs, projects, output of research centers and joint ventures with national and international organizations.</p>', NULL, '2016-11-28', 1, 1),
(120, 169, 'KICS’ Team Honored at University of Gujrat', '<p>KICS (Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science) UET Lahore&rsquo;s delegation paid a visit to University of Gujrat on 17th November. The delegation consisted of Director KICS Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Manager HUTIC Chair IEEE COMSOC Lahore Mr. Kashif Bashir. Huawei officials too joined the delegation. They included Director Huawei Solutions Mr. Robin and Mr. Muhammad Usman Khan.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/uog_02-visit.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"819\" height=\"529\" /></p>\r\n<p>The event at the occasion began with Smart Airport Track where the team of Huawei and Sialkot Airport Team were present. Since Huawei has been offering Smart Airport Solutions around the world, they showcased the details of their services to the participants over there. Mr. Robin revealed the solutions provided by Huawei, whereas Mr. Muhammad Usman Khan further described the details of the solutions for Smart Airports.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/uog_03-visit.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"820\" height=\"518\" /></p>\r\n<p>At the occasion, KICS&rsquo; initiatives were presented by the Director KICS and Manager HUITIC respectively. Other members of the delegation from KICS UET Lahore consisted of Mr. Usman Munawar, Shahid Zulfiqar, Mr. Fahmeed Akram, Mr. Qasim Abbass, Mr. Rizwan Naqvi and Mr. Rafiq Sultan respectively.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/November,%202016/uog_01-visit.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"819\" height=\"544\" /></p>\r\n<p>The ceremony with the presentations of lapels and souvenirs &ndash; Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood presented IEEE honorary lapel pin to COO Sialkot Airport, whereas Rector UOG presented souvenir to Huawei and KICS UET team. Mr. Usman Munawar, Research Officer KICS &amp; SAC Chair IEEE Lahore Section, presented IEEE Honorary lapel pin to the Rector of UOG Mr. Rehan.&nbsp; </p>', NULL, '2016-11-30', 1, 1),
(121, 170, 'KICS’ Lab TICK Signs MOU with Pop Corn Studio', '<p>Continuing with its success journey, KICS has one more business agreement in its pocket. TICK, one of KICS&rsquo; most valuable labs, has inked an MOU with a leading interactive creative agency Pop Corn that has clients not only in Pakistan, but also abroad. The company is based at Wahdat Road, Lahore. It is a healthy partnership that has a number of benefits including the ones mentioned as under:</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/tick-popcorn.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"652\" height=\"158\" /></p>\r\n<p>1). Strengthening of brand by expansion<br />2). Giving us more space to house our non-resident incubates<br />3). Providing a central location which makes us more accessible to people living in Wapda Town, Johar Town and other parts of the city.<br />4). Giving us more room to experiment without risking our own brand.<br /><br />Another benefit is that their startups will be registered as ours. The best of the best is that it is a win-win situation and we can proudly say that we now have another branch of ours at Wahdat Road Lahore.<br /><br />This MOU between TICK and Pop Corn is going to help KICS in catalyzing KICS vision of strengthening entrepreneurial ecosystem in Pakistan.</p>', NULL, '2016-12-01', 1, 1),
(122, 171, 'Free Microsoft Certifications for UET Students and Faculty – Avail Exclusive Opportunity', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Free Microsoft Certifications for the students and faculty members of University of Engineering and Technology Lahore. Get Microsoft Certified free of cost by the well-trained instructors. Learn the skills of operating MS Word, MS Excel, Power Point, Access, Outlook, One Note and Share Point. Training will take place at HUTIC, UET Lahore. Contact Mr. Tahir through e-mail: <a href=\"mailto:tahir.naeem@kics.edu.pk\">tahir.naeem@kics.edu.pk</a> to register for these exams. You may also get yourself registered by calling at 0344-7786447.<br /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><br /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/UET%20Poster_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"893\" height=\"636\" /></span></p>', NULL, '2016-12-08', 1, 1),
(123, 180, 'UET Offers Free Technical Training Courses in collaboration with Punjab Skills Development Fund with Monthly Stipend', '<p>University of Engineering and Technology Lahore in collaboration with Punjab Skills Development Fund has started the training courses to be held at KICS (Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science) UET Lahore. It will be FREE OF COST training courses for the eligible students. Below mentioned training courses will be offered at UET Lahore.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/PSDF.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"700\" height=\"700\" /><br /><strong></strong></p>\r\n<p><a style=\"text-align: right;\" href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/assets/psdf/Final_Admission_form.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"><input class=\"btn btn-primary\" type=\"button\" name=\"button\" value=\"Download Form\" /></a></p>\r\n<p><strong>Training Courses</strong></p>\r\n<p><br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Solar Photovoltaic Installation and Pumping Training<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Mobile Application Development<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Web Designing and Development<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Applied Instrumentation and Control Automation<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The duration of these courses will be between 3 months to 1 year. 25 seats have been allocated to each course.</p>\r\n<p><br /><strong>Eligibility and Conditions to Apply</strong></p>\r\n<p><br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Matric, DAE, Fsc or above can apply for these training courses.<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Those who previously have done PSDF courses are not eligible to apply.<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Candidates with Punjab domicile can apply for these training courses.<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Along with the application form, one passport size photo, all educational documents and copy of CNIC are required to submit.<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; During studies, if anyone leaves the course, he or she will have to pay the total course fee.</p>\r\n<p><br /><strong>Stipend Offered</strong></p>\r\n<p><br />Those who are selected for the training courses will be awarded a monthly stipend.</p>\r\n<p><br /><strong>Last Date for Applications</strong></p>\r\n<p><br />26th December 2016 is the last date for submitting the applications.</p>\r\n<p><br /><strong>Interview Date, Time and Venue</strong></p>\r\n<p><br />Interviews will be held on 27th December 2016 between 8 a.m. to 4 p.m. at UET Lahore&rsquo;s Main Auditorium.</p>\r\n<p><br /><strong>How to Get Admission Forms</strong></p>\r\n<p><br />Admission forms are available from the front desk of KICS (Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science) UET Lahore and can also be downloaded from below button</p>\r\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '2016-12-09', 1, 1),
(124, 173, 'UET Game Studio (KICS) Launches Its First Mobile Game ‘Protect the Candy’', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">UET Game Studio, a Game Design and Development Center of KICS, has launched its first mobile and game titled &lsquo;Protect the Candy&rsquo; that is available on Google Play Store. This is the first step towards the big success. It is undoubtedly a wonderful and enjoyable game that can equally be pleasurable for both adults and the kids. The game can be downloaded through Google Play Store and from the below link:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><a href=\"https:/play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=pk.edu.kics.ayyaz.ali.ProtectTheCandy\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #0000ff;\">https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=pk.edu.kics.ayyaz.ali.ProtectTheCandy</span></a></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><br /> </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/game.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"856\" height=\"481\" /><br /> </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><br /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">If you face any bugs or issues in the game and while playing it, you may contact the team at <span style=\"color: #0000ff;\"><a href=\"mailto:uetgs@kics.edu.pk\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #0000ff;\">uetgs@kics.edu.pk</span></a><span style=\"color: #000000;\">.</span></span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><br /> This effort is the result of the hard work of the game design and development team at KICS UET Lahore that works under the supervision of Dr. Usman Ghani.</span></p>', NULL, '2016-12-10', 1, 1),
(125, 174, 'KICS’s HUTIC Actively Participated in Huawei ICT Skill Competition', '<p>Huawei and its learning partners recently organized a competition in Pakistan called &lsquo;Huawei ICT Skill Competition Pakistan&rsquo;. It was undoubtedly a great opportunity for the candidates to learn the valuable networking knowledge. Besides, the competition provided the candidates with an experience to compete in a competitive environment, a chance to test their skills and recognize their weaknesses, display their knowledge and create interactive networking skills respectively.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/ICT_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"829\" height=\"524\" /></p>\r\n<p>The content of the competition was primarily based on the following aspects:</p>\r\n<p><br />Network Fundamentals, Principle of Switches and Routers, TCP/IP Protocol Family, Routing Protocols, Access Control, Troubleshooting of Network Faults, Installation and Commissioning of Huawei Routing and Switching Devices.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/ICT_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"829\" height=\"391\" /></p>\r\n<p>First round of the competition took place from 15th to 23rd November 2016 in Lahore and Islamabad, where 40 students qualified for the second round. Second round of the competition happened on 11th December 2016 in Lahore, where 3 students qualified for the third round. Third round (the final round) of the competition will take place in China at Huawei Headquarters in February 2017. The second round three winners will fly to China to attend the final round at Huawei Headquarters free of cost on Huawei&rsquo;s expenditures.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/ICT_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"830\" height=\"399\" /></p>\r\n<p>Apart from China&rsquo;s return ticket for Huawei headquarters, there are other prizes offered to the candidates. First prize is Huawei P9 Smart Phone and HCIE Exam Voucher, second prize is Hauwei Smart Watch and HCNP Exam Voucher and third prize is Huawei Y5 II Smart Phone and HCNP Exam Voucher.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/ICT_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"829\" height=\"519\" /></p>\r\n<p>HUTIC (Huawei UET Telecom IT Center) KICS UET Lahore made a big participation and contribution to the first round of the competition. The seminars and interactive sessions were conducted in various universities such as University of Engineering and Technology Lahore, Lahore Garrison University, Lahore College for Women University, Kinnaird College and COMSATS Lahore. Huawei appreciated HUTIC&rsquo;s efforts consumed for this competition. </p>', NULL, '2016-12-13', 1, 1),
(126, 175, 'KICS UET Lahore Conducts Open Source Series Workshop (OSSW) 2016', '<p>Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) organizes its annual conference &lsquo;10th IEEE ICOSST 2016&rsquo; that began from 15th December 2016 at KICS, University of Engineering and Technology Lahore. Apart from the conference consisting of invited talks and paper presentations, it also carries the events such as OSSW 2016 (Open Source Series Workshop), ICT-Symposium 2016 and Brianiac 2016. OSSW 2016 - the first event of the conference took place at seminar hall at KICS UET Lahore.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/ossw-2016.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"827\" height=\"373\" /></p>\r\n<p>Five workshops were presented at the occasion namely &lsquo;Urdu Search Engine Monitoring Design, Challenges and Solution&rsquo; by Dr. Amir Mahmood (KICS) and Mr. Abdullah Zafar (KICS), &lsquo;3D Mapping and Simulation for Smart Cities&rsquo; by Dr. Murtaza Taj (LUMS, Lahore), &lsquo;Safe Campus&rsquo; by Mr. Robin Xing (Huawei, Pakistan), &lsquo;Cloud Based Services with Feature Velocity&rsquo; by Dr. Abdul Waheed (Salesforce, USA) and &lsquo;Connected Future in a Smart City&rsquo; by Mr. Muhammad Umair (KICS).</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/ossw-2016_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"828\" height=\"687\" /></p>\r\n<p>It was a thoroughly knowledgeable and informative event. The participants not only grabbed the information, but also enjoyed it completely.&nbsp; ICOSST 2016 is scheduled from 15th to 17th December 2016 at University of Engineering and Technology Lahore. Mr. Ali Raza Gillani, Minsiter HED Government of the Punjab will be the chief guest at the occasion. Distinguished guests and high government officials are slated to attend the conference as well. The official opening ceremony of ICOSST 2016 will take place on 16th December, whereas the closing ceremony is scheduled on 17th December. Brianiac 2016, another event in series of ICOSST 2016 laced with technical and non-technical competitions, happened on 14th December in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore, which winners will be announced on the opening ceremony of ICOSST 2016.</p>', NULL, '2016-12-15', 1, 1),
(127, 176, 'Punjab Minister Syed Raza Ali Gillani to Inaugurate ICOSST 2016 in UET Lahore ', '<p>10th IEEE ICOSST 2016 has started at Al-Khawarzmi Institute of Computer Science, University of Engineering and Technology Lahore with the opening event on competitions called &lsquo;Brianiac 2016&rsquo; followed by OSSW-2016 (Open Source Series Workshops). On 16th December 2016, the opening ceremony will be held at University of Engineering and Technology Lahore&rsquo;s Main Auditorium, where Mr. Raza Ali Gillani, the honorable minister HED Govt. of Punjab is the chief guest.</p>\r\n<p><br />Mr. Tariq Sultan, Member (Finance) PTA is the distinguished guest. There will be other high officials of government such as Dr. Arshad Ali, Executive Director HEC Pakistan.</p>\r\n<p><br />Apart from the addresses of the chief guest, distinguished guest and keynote speech by HEC Executive Director, the event will consist of the address by Vice Chancellor UET Lahore Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid and introduction by KICS&rsquo; director Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood.</p>\r\n<p><br />The ceremony will be concluded with shields&rsquo; distribution.</p>', NULL, '2016-12-15', 1, 1),
(128, 177, 'Syed Raza Ali Gillani, HED Minister of Punjab Inaugurates ICOSST 2016’s Opening Ceremony in UET Lahore', '<p>Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) University of Engineering and Technology Lahore is organizing its annual conference &lsquo;ICOSST 2016&rsquo; being held from 15th to 17th December 2016 at UET Lahore. The opening ceremony of the conference was held on 16th December 2016 at University&rsquo;s main auditorium hall, where the chief guest Mr. Syed Raza Ali Gillani, the honorable minister HED Govt. of Punjab, inaugurated the ceremony along with other distinguished guests such as Mr. Tariq Sultan, Member (Finance) PTA and Dr. Arshad Ali, Executive Director HEC Pakistan.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/ICOSST-Opening%20Ceremony_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>This year&rsquo;s ICOSST 2016&rsquo;s is the 10th edition of the annual conference and its theme is Smart Cities. It is a three-day conference being held from 15th to 17th December 2016 at KICS UET Lahore for the researchers and practitioners from across the world to share their ideas and experiences related to the state-of-the-art and the future of open-source software. IEEE ICOSST is a successful scientific venue where participants share ideas, strategies, and policies for tackling the development, research and adaptation challenges related to open-source tools and development environments. Nearly 200 research papers from 28 countries have been submitted in conference this year and peer reviewed by 240 reviewers from the international technical program committee from 32 countries including USA, Australia, Japan, China, Canada, India, Romania, Malaysia, UK and to name a few.</p>\r\n<p><br />The honorable minister, Mr. Syed Raza Ali Gillani said that software is the need of the hour and is much important in today&rsquo;s life. He insisted on the development of software technology. Additionally he revealed about the importance of open source technology. Gillani also appreciated the researchers came all the way from abroad to attend this conference. He liked the efforts being consumed by KICS UET for making collaborations in IT. Syed Raza said that government of Punjab and higher education department will always support research activities in UET.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/ICOSST-Opening%20Ceremony_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Mr. Tariq Sultan, Member (Finance) PTA talked about the spectrum of 3G and 4G. He excitedly told that now connectivity in rural areas was not a big problem, as now the rural areas had full connectivity. He further said now the government&rsquo;s finance ministry had made planning of year 2020 when the country would be having majority of mobile bank accounts.<br />Vice Chancellor UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid in his speech talked about the promotion and development of quality education, which the university was delivering to its students. He also revealed university&rsquo;s history and its growth over the years. Dr. Fazal said that university had good support from the government.</p>\r\n<p><br />Dr. Waqar Mahmood, KICS Director presented a brief introduction of ICOSST 2016 and KICS. Additionally he also revealed the history of ICOSST and the significance of open source especially for countries like Pakistan.<br />Other speakers such as Dr. Andrew from the University of South Wales (UK) and Dr. Kamran Iqbal from USA presented their views on the conference.</p>\r\n<p><br /><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/DSC_1711.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"564\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The ceremony concluded with shield distributions to the honorable guests and the winners of Brianiac 2016 competition were awarded with certificates and prize money by the honorable minister. </p>', NULL, '2016-12-16', 1, 1),
(129, 178, 'KICS UET’s Annual Conference ICOSST 2016 Successfully Wraps Up - Chairman PITB The Chief Guest of the Closing Ceremony', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) University of Engineering and Technology Lahore has organized its annual conference &lsquo;ICOSST 2016&rsquo; held from 15<sup>th</sup> to 17<sup>th</sup> December 2016 at UET Lahore. The opening ceremony of the conference was held on 16<sup>th</sup> December 2016, whereas the closing ceremony of the conference was held at University&rsquo;s main auditorium hall on 17<sup>th</sup> December 2016, where Dr. Omer Saif, Chairman PITB was the chief guest. Other distinguished guests such as Dr. Shafay Shamail, IEEE Lahore Section&rsquo;s Chairman and the invited speakers of the conference who came from across the globe to attend the event. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/Dice_2016_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"846\" height=\"566\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">This year&rsquo;s ICOSST 2016&rsquo;s was the 10<sup>th</sup> edition of the annual conference and its theme was Smart Cities. The event wrapped up its decade&rsquo;s activities successfully. It was a three-day conference held at KICS UET Lahore for the researchers and practitioners from across the world to share their ideas and experiences related to the state-of-the-art and the future of open-source software. IEEE ICOSST is a successful scientific venue where participants share ideas, strategies, and policies for tackling the development, research and adaptation challenges related to open-source tools and development environments. Nearly 200 research papers from 28 countries were submitted in conference this year and peer reviewed by 240 reviewers from the international technical program committee from 32 countries including USA, Australia, Japan, China, Canada, India, Romania, Malaysia, UK and to name a few.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/Dice_2016_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"843\" height=\"278\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">The honorable chief guest, Mr. Omer Saif, first of all appreciated the efforts of KICS UET to make this event happen successfully, then went on sharing his success story by letting the audience know how he studied at Cambridge university to do his PhD? He then revealed the importance of the research papers. Mr. Omer said that the bad system of the country needs to be changed in order to bring change in the country. He pointed out how badly every department of the government was working? He said this generation could bring about change in the country. He then mentioned the bitter reality of being so behind in the world mentioning Pakistan does not have even a single university among top 700 universities of the world. Mr. Omer also appreciated UET&rsquo;s efforts to produce talents and doing technological advancement works. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Vice Chancellor UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid in his speech talked about the promotion and development of quality education. He focused on the technology&rsquo;s importance in society. Vice Chancellor then talked about opeb source technology and its values in today&rsquo;s world. He talked about as to how cities can be converted into smart cities. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Dr. Waqar Mahmood, KICS Director <span style=\"color: black; letter-spacing: -.2pt;\">presented a brief introduction of ICOSST 2016 and KICS. Additionally he also revealed the history of ICOSST and the significance of open source especially for countries like Pakistan.</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 11.4pt; margin-bottom: .0001pt; margin-left: 0in; text-align: justify; line-height: 23.95pt; mso-pagination: none; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; color: black; letter-spacing: -.2pt;\">Other speakers such as Dr. Shafay Shamail and Dr. Andrew from the University of South Wales (UK) also shared their views.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 11.4pt; margin-bottom: .0001pt; margin-left: 0in; text-align: justify; line-height: 23.95pt; mso-pagination: none; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; color: black; letter-spacing: -.2pt;\">&nbsp;<img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/Dice_2016_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"846\" height=\"566\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 11.4pt; margin-bottom: .0001pt; margin-left: 0in; text-align: justify; line-height: 23.95pt; mso-pagination: none; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; color: black; letter-spacing: -.2pt;\">The ceremony concluded with shield distributions to the honorable chief guest presented by Vice Chancellor and Director KICS. The chief guest presented the shields to the organizers of the event.</span></p>', NULL, '2016-12-19', 1, 1),
(130, 179, 'All Pakistan DICE Energy and Water 2016 Begins at UET Lahore', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: Verdana;\">All Pakistan DICE Energy &amp; Water 2016 exhibition is being held in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 19<sup>th</sup> and 20<sup>th</sup> December 2016 in collaboration with Al-Khwarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) UET Lahore, ORIC Department Punjab University, CERAD, IEEE Industry Applications Society, IEEE Power and Energy Society Lahore Section and DICE USA respectively<strong>. </strong><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">The opening ceremony of this exhibition was held on 19<sup>th</sup> December at Main Auditorium of UET Lahore. The theme of the event was &lsquo;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Conserve Energy and Water for Green Pakistan&rsquo;. Program&rsquo;s objective is to establish a strong linkage between academia and industry of energy and water for providing a common platform to internet, share knowledge and collaborate on innovations and commercialization in order to grow the indigenous energy and water industry in the country. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/dice%20event_opening_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"878\" height=\"878\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: Verdana; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">The distinguished guests of the occasion include Chairman DICE Foundation Dr. Khurshid Qureshi,<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span>Chairman Dice Energy and Water USA, Dr. Ubaid, Director ORIC Punjab University, Dr. Aamir Ijaz and Dean Faculty of Engineering, Dr. Sohail Aftab.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Dr. Khurshid Qureshi said that we should foster the culture of innovations. He emphasized on the need to promote the innovations in the country in order to be successful and take steps along with the world. He said that Pakistan needed indigenous progress. About DICE, the Chairman said that we had developed DICE to foster the innovations in Pakistan. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Dr. Ubaid, in his views, first presented a brief history of DICE and narrated how since 2014 DICE had been in operations successfully. He mentioned how the issues related to energy and water could be resolved. He emphasized on the need of solar energy storage and how it could be done working with academia. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/dice%20event_opening_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"877\" height=\"877\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">UET&rsquo;s Dean of Faculty, Dr. Sohail Aftab said that we were suffering from the issues like energy and water in Pakistan. He stressed on the need of promoting solar energy in the country. He pointed out that water should not be wasted. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Director ORIC Punjab University Dr. Aamir Ijaz mentioned the mission of ORIC to launch research activities in Pakistan. He emphasized that being a good researcher could make you a good entrepreneur. He said that their (ORIC) aim was to develop students in a way that they could do jobs and create jobs being entrepreneur. Dr. Aamir said that we should utilize the water came from floods and rains, as it normally went waste as unutilized. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/dice%20event_opening_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"879\" height=\"879\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Vice Chancellor of UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid said that the needs of country related to energy and water could be fulfilled by adaptation of modern techniques of management and generation. He mentioned that through applicable research, practical solutions could be obtained with systematic planning to cater down the issues related to energy and water. He narrated that the operation of industry agriculture was entirely based on energy for working efficiently to meet the demands of national and international markets. Vice Chancellor expressed his hope that the outcomes of this mega event will be fruitful for all stakeholders to constitute comprehensive and cohesive policy for energy and water.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Director CERAD UET, Dr. Waqar Mahmood briefed the audience about DICE and revealed the motto behind this event. He told the audience that the objective of this conference was to generate positive and favorable image of Pakistan&rsquo;s energy and water industry in the eyes of the international community. He told that the country was fully capable of developing innovative energy and water products for domestic and world markets. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/dice%20event_opening_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"873\" height=\"584\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">DICE received nearly 150 students&rsquo; projects from all over Pakistan, out of which more than 60 were chosen. At the exhibition displayed at the event, 50 stalls of industry and educational institutions are installed. The guests of the occasion visited the stalls and showed their interest in the products showcased there.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/DSC_1597.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"868\" height=\"454\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">The first day&rsquo;s event concluded with a social evening, where the artists from the television industry showed their talents and singers performed to the large audience.</span></p>', NULL, '2016-12-20', 1, 1),
(131, 180, 'Ch. Sher Ali Concludes the Closing Ceremony of UET’s All Pakistan DICE Energy Event 2016', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">The 2-day mega event &lsquo;All Pakistan DICE Energy and Water 2016&rsquo; carrying the theme &lsquo;Conserve Energy and Water for Green Pakistan&rsquo; has ended up on 20<sup>th</sup> December with a colossal closing ceremony attended by the chief guest of the occasion Ch. Sher Ali Khan (Provincial Minister for Mines and Minerals), Mr. Farooq Amjad Mir (Senior Advocate of Supreme Court of Pakistan), Dr. Amjad Ijaz (Director ORIC, Punjab University) and Ms. Hania (Business Development Manager of Premier Energy, UK) respectively. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/dice_closing_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"875\" height=\"875\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">While talking to the audience, the ministers said that the government was much active in improving the situation of energy and water in Pakistan with the help of many projects going on and are in pipeline. He stated that the academia could really play a vital role in this regard. He emphasized on the need of conserving the water. Ch. Sher Ali also mentioned that the conferences of these kinds had a better role to play for developing the sense of saving water. He pointed out that government&rsquo;s project on energy &lsquo;Quaid-e-Azam Solar Park&rsquo; was on way to provide a big chunk of energy and more projects of these kinds had to be started off. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/dice_closing_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"874\" height=\"437\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Senior Advocate Supreme Court Farooq Amjad Mir emphasized on the need of water conservation. He said that water wastage should be stopped. <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Dr. Aamir Ijaz said that collaborations of the kind of UET and Punjab University that resulted into DICE 2016 could really bring up the benefits for the country. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Vice Chancellor UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid said that industry and agriculture were the major players for the progress of the country and were completely dependent on energy and water. For conservation and alternate energy like solar, wind and coal, the sense of realization must be activated for strengthening the concept of Green Pakistan.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/dice_closing_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"876\" height=\"586\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Director CERAD and KICS UET Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood delivered a presentation on the introduction, history and functions of CERAD and KICS and then gave an overview of the 2-day event of DICE 2016.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Other guests too appreciated the event and the collaboration of UET and Punjab University to launch DICE event for the first time in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/dice_closing_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"874\" height=\"584\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">The event concluded with the prize distribution among the three winners of the projects. Aeronautical Engineering, NUST bagged the 1<sup>st</sup> prize of 200,000 rupees, whereas University of Engineering and Technology Lahore won 2<sup>nd</sup> by winning 60 thousand rupees. The 3<sup>rd</sup> winner was from University of the Punjab who was awarded 30 thousand rupees. The provincial minister delivered the prizes to the students and then presented the shields to the industry personnel (who had placed the installs at the event) and then presented the souvenirs to the guests. Vice Chancellor presented the souvenir to the minister in return. <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/DSC_2566.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"876\" height=\"367\" /></span></span></p>', NULL, '2016-12-21', 1, 1);
INSERT INTO `star_news` (`news_id`, `order`, `news_des`, `news_detail`, `newsthumb`, `news_stamp`, `group_id`, `active`) VALUES
(132, 181, 'A Delegation of Government College of Technology Pindi Bhattian Visits HUTIC UET Lahore', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">A delegation of final year students of Telecom and Electronics DAE from Government College of Technology (GCT) Pindi Bhattian (district Hafizabad) recently visited Huawei UET Telecom &amp; IT Center (HUTIC) KICS UET Lahore on 19<sup>th</sup> December 2016. The delegation comprised of 45 students and 4 faculty members namely Muhammad Faisal, Arfan Zahoor, Waqas Ahmad and Mr. Zeshan Ahmad respectively.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/GCT_Visit-Featured.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"852\" height=\"852\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">KICS&rsquo; Research Officers Ayyaz Ahmed and Engr. Hafiz Tayyab Hashmi gave brief presentations to the delegation about KICS UET, Huawei and HUTIC. The students also were informed about the training and certifications being done at HUTIC (Huawei UET Joint Telecom IT Centre) in the fields of Computer Networking and Telecom sector. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\"><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/GCT%20Visit_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"848\" height=\"594\" /></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">The delegation enjoyed their visit to HUTIC UET Lahore thoroughly and also visited the departments of the university.</span></p>', NULL, '2016-12-22', 1, 1),
(134, 182, 'DICE Automotive Meeting Held in UET Lahore', '<p>Prior to the start of All Pakistan DICE Energy and Water 2016 held at UET from 19th to 20th December 2016, a meeting on DICE Automotive was conducted at Conference Room in KICS (Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science) UET Lahore on Sunday, 18th December. DICE automotives reflects the progress and innovation ongoing in the field of automotives in Pakistan. The meeting focused on the shortcomings faced by the academia and industry in automotives and strived to single out an effective solution to the problems associated with. The DICE automotive network involves several universities from Pakistan and now aims to involve UET to its network.</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/dice_auomotive_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"817\" height=\"817\" /></p>\r\n<p>Attendees of the meeting were from different entities. The ones, who attended the DICE Automotive Meeting included:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Dr. Fazal Ahmed Kahlid, Vice Chancellor, UET, Lahore</li>\r\n<li>Saad Ellahie, Chair DICE Automotive, USA</li>\r\n<li>Dr. Khurshid Qureshi, Chairman, DICE Foundation, USA</li>\r\n<li>Dr. Raziq Yaqub, Alabama A&amp;M University, USA</li>\r\n<li>Ahmed Safi, General Electric</li>\r\n<li>Executive from PAAPAM</li>\r\n<li>Salam Ullah form United Motors</li>\r\n<li>Dr. Tahir Izhar, Chairman Electrical Department, UET, Lahore</li>\r\n<li>Dr. Aamer Iqbal Bhatti, CASPR, CUST, Islamabad</li>\r\n<li>Dr. Waqar Mehmood, Director CERAD, UET</li>\r\n<li>Dr. NAsir Hayat, Chairman Mechanical Department, UET, Lahore</li>\r\n<li>Mohammad Ali, Sr. Research Manager, KICS, UET, Lahore</li>\r\n<li>Muhammad Rizwan, Research Officer, KICS, UET, Lahore</li>\r\n<li>Safi Ullah, Research Officer, KICS, UET, Lahore</li>\r\n<li>Ubaid Ullah, DICE Automotives</li>\r\n<li>Engr. Sajjad Hussain, MBA, USA</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The vision of this meeting was to articulate, agree upon, and to work on specific common goals and demonstrate a commitment to the values and benefits that guide the collaboration. The theme of this meeting was Hybird vehicles.</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/dice_auomotive_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"818\" height=\"409\" /></p>\r\n<p>Patron-in-Chief of this meeting was Vice Chancellor UET Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid and the Chair was Mr. Saad Elahi from Dice Automotive, USA. Moderator was Mr. Muhammad Ali (Senior Research Manager, EECL and KICS UET Lahore). Co-ordinator of the meeting was Mr. Safi Ullah (Research Officer, EECL, KICS UET Lahore). Agenda of the meeting was introduction of Dice Automotives, presentation on automotive projects and panel discussion.</p>', NULL, '2016-12-23', 1, 1),
(135, 183, 'Merit Lists of PSDF Technical Short Courses', '<h3>Web Design &amp; Development -- &nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/documents/psdf_web.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download List</a></h3>\r\n<h3>Mobile Application Development -- <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/documents/psdf_mobile.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download List</a></h3>\r\n<h3>Applied Instrumentation and Control Automation -- <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/documents/psdf_instrumentation.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download List</a></h3>\r\n<h3>Solar Photovoltaic Installation and Pumping Training -- <a href=\"http://kics.edu.pk/documents/psdf_solar.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download List</a></h3>', NULL, '2016-12-30', 1, 1),
(136, 183, 'KICS Organizes a Workshop on Developing Exceptional Communication Skills', '<p>KICS proudly arranged a one of its kind workshop on the topic of Developing Exceptional Communication Skills&rsquo; on 29th December 2016 at Seminar Hall. It was a 3 hours long interactive session that addressed the key elements of communications with special emphasis on trainings. The learning objectives of this workshop were plenty, but the focus was especially on the below:</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/workshop_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"864\" height=\"864\" /></p>\r\n<p>&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Managing Communication Problems<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Developing the Right content for the Audience<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Connecting with the audience<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Effective Use of Verbal/Non-Verbal Tools<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Creating effective Visual Aids</p>\r\n<p><br />The trainer of the workshop was a highly professional and experienced person named Muhammad Jahanzeb Akbar, who is a government officer, a PMO Specialist and a seasoned trainer. More than 15 countries&rsquo; students have been trained by him so far.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/dec,%2016/workshop_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"864\" height=\"864\" /></p>\r\n<p>The attendees of the workshop included the managers, senior staff and other personnel of KICS (Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science).</p>', NULL, '2016-12-30', 1, 1),
(137, 184, 'MNS University’s Delegation Visits HUTIC UET Lahore', '<p>A delegation from Muhammad Nawaz Sharif University of Engineering and Technology (MNS UET) Multan comprising of 24 students and 2 lecturers visited HUTIC (Huawei UET Joint Telecom IT Center) KICS on 27th December 2016. The delegation was invited by IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section. The ceremony began with the presentations on networking and telecom equipment delivered by telecom and networking instructors &ndash; Mr. Ayyaz and Mr. Hafiz Muhammad Tayyab Hashmi.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/MNS%20Visit.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /><br /><br />HUTIC Manager Mr. Kashif Bashir briefed the students about trainings being delivered at UET. He also told the importance of the certifications and trainings being done at the university.&nbsp; The students and the lecturers both enjoyed this study tour.</p>', NULL, '2017-01-05', 1, 1),
(138, 185, 'CERAD and VTI Faisalabad Sign an MOU', '<p>CERAD UET Lahore and VTI (Vital Trade Impex) Faisalabad have reached to an agreement on 28th December, 2016. The two parties signed JV Research Agreement at Faculty Hostel in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore where the key high officials of both sides were present. Director CERAD Dr. Waqar Mahmood delivered a brief presentation about the lab and its working before MOU signing.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/VTI-MoU.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>This joint venture is for research &amp; development and promotion &amp; marketing of waste to fuel briquettes and waste to fuel pellets.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/VTI-MoU_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"563\" /></p>\r\n<p>This Waste to Fuel JV Research Agreement between the parties &ndash; CERAD and VTI is set to bring fruitful results for the university. </p>', NULL, '2017-01-05', 1, 1),
(139, 186, 'KICS UET and HME Faisalabad Sign an Agreement for CNC 3D Platforms for Industrial Applications', '<p>KICS UET Lahore and HME (Hayat Mahal Engravers) Faisalabad have signed an agreement on 4th January 2017. The MOU signing ceremony was held in the presence of Vice Chancellor UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid at Faculty Hostel in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore, where the key personnel from both sides took part. Before signing of the agreement, Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Director KICS, delivered a presentation on KICS&rsquo; activities and its research labs.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/kics_hme_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>As for this JV-Research Agreement, HME will be a joint venture partner for research and development and promotion &amp; marketing for CNC 3D Platforms for Industrial Applications.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/kics_hme_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor was also shown the 3D Logo of the university made by HME, which the VC appreciated highly. Talking to the guests, Dr. Fazal said that this joint venture will bring really lucrative results for the benefits of the university.<br /><br /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '2017-01-05', 1, 1),
(140, 187, 'Kashif Bashir from KICS Receives IEEE Comsoc Outstanding Technical Chapter Award 2016', '<p>IEEE Lahore Section has been awarded with the distinction of Outstanding Technical Chapter Award 2016 out of 5 Technical Chapters. The event was held at the Annual General Meeting (AGM) of IEEE Lahore Section in 7th January 2017 at FAST Institute in Lahore, where Mr. Kashif Bashir, Chair IEEE Comsoc Lahore Sectio &amp; Manager HUTIC KICS UET Lahore, received the award from Dr. Amjad Hussain (Director FAST NU) and Dr. Ali Kashif Bashir (Osaka University, Japan).</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/IEEE_COMSOC-Award_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"858\" height=\"545\" /></p>\r\n<p>34 Universities&rsquo; IEEE branches and faculty members attended this event applauded by all and sundry out there.</p>\r\n<p>IEEE COMSOC Lahore Sction arranged a number of technical events in 2016 and initiated the COMSOC summer school program efficiently in Pakistan. It has bigger plans for year 2017 in store.</p>\r\n<p>It is without any doubt a big achievement that took place with the support of Director KICS UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood, who congratulated Mr. Kashif Bashir and his team for achieving this milestone and great distinction.</p>', NULL, '2017-01-18', 1, 1),
(141, 188, 'Dawer Saeed of KICS to Deliver a Workshop on Robot Building in UET Lahore', '<p>Dawer Saeed from KICS (Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science) is going to deliver a workshop on &lsquo;Robot Building&rsquo; at Electrical Department UET Lahore on 25th and 26th January 2017. This workshop is a presentation of IET UET Chapter. It will endow the participants a chance to equip themselves with knowledge of building a full-fledged robot from scratch. The main intention is to enable the students especially the newcomers to develop wireless controlled robots. The workshop will also be helpful in setting the students on the path of robot-making.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/Robotics%20Workshop.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"678\" height=\"960\" /></p>\r\n<p>The students will learn about the famous micro controller &lsquo;Arduino&rsquo; and how to interface different sensors, motors and actuators with it. This workshop will also focus on building a robot controlled with an Android phone via Bluetooth.</p>\r\n<p><br />After attending the workshop, you will be able to learn the below skills:</p>\r\n<p><br />Arduino programming skills<br />Motor control<br />Motor shields working<br />Wireless control<br />Techniques on making a completely functioning robot for our upcoming event &lsquo;Robowars&rsquo;</p>\r\n<p><br />Post the workshop, there will be an exhibition of the robots at EE Lobby on 27th of January. To register for this workshop, click the link below.</p>\r\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><a style=\"text-align: right;\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSckRsaRG3mPEkZrbAYVTr16bu_hxXwUfgTEjG5bSopjeKun2w/viewform?c=0&amp;w=1\" target=\"_blank\"><input class=\"btn btn-primary\" type=\"button\" name=\"button\" value=\"Event Registration\" /></a></div>', NULL, '2017-01-25', 1, 1),
(142, 189, 'KICS and IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section Organize Power of Idea and Execution Workshop', '<p>KICS in collaboration with in collaboration with IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section and IEEE Young Professionals organized a workshop on &lsquo;Power of Idea and Execution&rsquo; in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 21st January 2017 where a good attendance was seen. The guests of the occasion were Mr. Faisal Wahab (Corporate Trainer, Mobilink) and Mr. Hussam Sohail Ahmad (CEO, Sportcomm). The resource person of the workshop who delivered this workshop was Mr. Faisal Wahab, who is a TTT certified trainer from Harvard Business Publishing and has trained participants from leading organizations from diverse industries.</p>\r\n<p><br />The workshop was based on the below-mentioned contents:</p>\r\n<p><br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; What is the power of idea?<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; How ideas have shaped this world?<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; How to have a creative and fertile mind?<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Why fear of failure stifles us?<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; How to have a YES attitude?<br />&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; If you are not ready to FAIL you are not prepared to WIN</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/power_idea_workshop.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"823\" height=\"544\" /></p>\r\n<p>At this meet up, various ideas were discussed. Mr. Faisal talked about the power of idea besides mentioning as to how one can change one idea into reality. Further he mentioned as to how you can evaluate your ideas and test them to assure that your ideas have enough innovation for the market. Startup business plans and business models too were discussed at the workshop. The participants got the knowledge about the difference between entrepreneurship and intrepreneurship.</p>', NULL, '2017-01-25', 1, 1),
(143, 190, 'One-Day Seminar on Solar Quality Awareness and System Design in UET Lahore', '<p>AERIL Lab of KICS UET Lahore conducted a one-day seminar on the subject of &lsquo;Solar Quality Awareness and System Design&rsquo; in collaboration with German Solar Association (BSW) GIZ and Stimulus. The seminar was conducted last month on December 21st 2016 where a good amount of the participants were seen, who took wider interest in learning the techniques. All prime issues including the solar quality and common trends in today&rsquo;s market were covered in this seminar.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/solar_quality_001.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"826\" height=\"464\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/solar_quality_002.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"826\" height=\"464\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/solar_quality_003.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"826\" height=\"464\" /></p>\r\n<p>Apart from the above, the seminar also focused on case studies and extensive review of the solar system designing. It was a thorough learning experience for the participants and a joyful teaching experience for the instructors.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/solar_quality_004.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"826\" height=\"464\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/solar_quality_005.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"826\" height=\"464\" /></p>\r\n<p>The participants were made to see the projects working on solar in UET Lahore and they also visited the AERIL Lab to see how the working takes place there.</p>\r\n<p>At the end of the seminar, the certificates were distributed among the participants of the seminar.</p>', NULL, '2017-01-27', 1, 1),
(144, 191, 'SSR Group of KICS UET Signs Agreement with American University in the Emirates (UAE)', '<p>Software System Research Group* from KICS (Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science) University of Engineering and Technology Lahore has signed an MOU with College of Computer Information Technology (CCIT) of American University in the Emirates (UAE) for a number of collaborative works. As per the agreement, the two entities will collaborate in research projects, student project supervision, talks in conferences to be held at both of the universities, cultural exchange visits and online lab of students.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/MOU_Emirates%20Uni_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"832\" height=\"554\" /><br /><br /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/MOU_Emirates%20Uni_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"834\" height=\"552\" /></p>\r\n<p>It was a two-day event taken place at the American University in the Emirates (UAE). High officials from both the universities were present at the occasion. Dr. Usman Ghani from KICS UET Lahore led the delegation and signed the agreement. Dr. Usman also delivered a research talk and gave a presentation on the functionality of the research department i.e. KICS.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/MOU_Emirates%20Uni_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"836\" height=\"557\" /></p>\r\n<p>* Sofware System Research Group consists of:<br /><br />1) Software System Research Lab<br />2) Bioinformatic research Lab <br />3) Computer Vision &amp; Machine Learning Research lab<br />4) UET Game Studio</p>', NULL, '2017-01-27', 1, 1),
(145, 192, 'KICS Awarded Tier 1 Ranking for Providing Trainings in Solar Technology by PSDF', '<p>Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) UET Lahore has been awarded the tier 1 ranking for providing the trainings in solar technology by PSDF (Punjab Skill Development Fund). Among the 4 tiers (Tier 1 Green, Tier 2 Brown, Tier 3 Yellow and Tier 4 Red respectively) PSDF has developed for the TSPs (Training Service Providers), KICS grabbed the first tier performance award i.e. 1st Tier Green based on the performance criteria of trainings delivered by KICS during the engagement period with Punjab Skill Development Fund from July 2012 to December 2015.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan,%202017/PSDF_KICS.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"633\" height=\"243\" /></p>\r\n<p>KICS bagged 81 percent performance rate under its trade group &lsquo;Photovoltaic Technicians and Supervisors&rsquo; by delivering the trainings for Solar Photovoltaic Installation and Pumping.</p>', NULL, '2017-01-30', 1, 1),
(146, 193, 'IEEE UET Lahore Section Conducts Awards Ceremony in UET Lahore', '<p>IEEE UET Lahore held an awards&rsquo; ceremony at EE Department in UET recently. It was conducted to deliver the Lahore Section Awards for the ones who secured Best Student Branch Award, Runner-Up Position for the Best Student Volunteer, Best WIE Volunteer and Runner-Up for the Best WIE Affinity group respectively. At the ceremony, the members of IEEE society and the faculty members were present. Mr. Kashif Bashir (Chair IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section and Manager HUTIC) and Mr. Usman (Research Officer at KICS UET Lahore) delivered the talks.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_2017/IEEE_UET_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"425\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_2017/IEEE_UET_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"563\" /></p>\r\n<p>Apart from the talks, few discussions were also done such as on the topic of getting benefits from IEEE. 3 months&rsquo; lecture series, which was proposed at the event, was also approved by the ORIC UET. It was discussed over there that special seminars will be arranged in order to promote the research activities in the university.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_2017/IEEE_UET_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"454\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_2017/IEEE_UET_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"482\" /></p>\r\n<p>Mr. Kashif Bashir and Mr. Usman presented the awards. EE faculty appreciated the students who won the awards at the event.</p>', NULL, '2017-02-02', 1, 1),
(147, 194, 'Distinction: ICOSST 2016 Now Published in IEEE Xplore', '<p>Undoubtedly it is laudatory news that KICS&rsquo;s annual conference ICOSST (International Conference on Open Source Systems &amp; Technologies) is now published in IEEE Explore. KICS&rsquo; annual mega conference ICOSST 2016 took place in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore from 15th to 17th December, 2016. The conference was laced with technical workshops, invited talks and a number of other educational activities. Distinguished speakers from renowned universities of the world came to attend and delivered the lectures at the conference.</p>\n<p><br />IEEE Meetings, Conferences, and Events (MCE) USA, which partnered with KICS on ICOSST 2016, has appreciated KICS&rsquo; efforts to organize this giant conference successfully at UET Lahore and also showed its keen interest in partnering again on another conference.</p>\n<p><strong><br /></strong></p>\n<p><strong>All About ICOSST 2016 <a href=\"http://icosst.kics.edu.pk/\" target=\"_blank\">http://icosst.kics.edu.pk/</a></strong></p>\n<p><br />MCE USA congratulated KICS UET Lahore for being published in IEEE Xplore.</p>', NULL, '2017-02-06', 1, 1),
(148, 196, 'UET & KICS High Officials Attend LUMS Roundtable Discussion on Future of Energy in Pakistan', '<p>LUMS (Lahore University of Management Sciences) organized an Energy Roundtable Discussion that took place on 3rd February 2017 at LUMS where thought leaders from government, industry and non-profit organizations came to attend it. They shared their views and ideas on this exceptionally important and pertinent matter on the topic of Future of Energy in Pakistan. The LUMS advisory board members including Dr. Sally Benson, Professor of Energy Resources Engineering and GCEP Director, Stanford University and Dr. Khalid Aziz, Otto N. Miller Professor of Energy Resources Engineering in the School of Earth, Energy &amp; Environmental Sciences, Emeritus, lead the discussion. From KICS (Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Sciences) University of Engineering and Technology Lahore, Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Jamshed Iqbal Janjua (Senior Manager at KICS, Chair IEEE</p>\r\n<p>Computational Intelligence Society Lahore Section, Vice Chair IEEE Computer Society Lahore Section), Kashif Bashir (HUTIC UET Manager, Chair IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section), Research Office Engineer Usman Munawar and Research Officer Shahid Zulfiqar participated at the discussion and shared their valuable thoughts.</p>\r\n<p><br />The participants presented their views and discussed the areas such as:</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"https://scontent-sin6-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t31.0-8/16700519_1243570105734637_5830046766028874379_o.jpg?oh=a4c4bf552e0e5555fce3beb888db351d&amp;oe=59449C82\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"625\" /></p>\r\n<p>From the Government Organizations: What are the needs for increasing electricity supply and improving reliability, extending access to grid, use of renewable energy, off-grid-solutions, expanded natural gas supplies, etc.<br />From the Industry: What are the opportunities for expanding availability of energy supplies to support industrial growth &mdash; and what are the challenges to doing this.</p>\r\n<p><br />From the Non-Profit Organizations: What is being done to improve energy access in locations that do not have electricity or the people cannot afford it. Trend in uptake of Solar, challenges and how to make it sustainable.</p>\r\n<p><br />The list of the participants together with their association, who attended the event, is as under</p>\r\n<p><strong>Government:</strong><br /><br />Asad Rehman Gilani, Secretary Energy (Punjab Energy Department)<br /><br />Fiaz Chaudhry, Managing Director (NTDC)<br /><br />Muhammad Amjad, CEO (Q A Solar and Wind)<br /><br />&nbsp;Hasan Touqir Bokhari, CEO (PITC)<br /><br />&nbsp;Fayyaz Akram, CEO (Power Tech)<br /><br />Muhammad Qasim Khokhar, Managing Director (PEECA)</p>\r\n<p><strong>Industry:</strong><br /><br />Nadeem Babar, CEO (Orient Power Company)<br /><br />Arif Saeed, Chairman (QA Thermal and National Power Parks Mgmt. Co.)<br /><br />Nauman Saeed, CEO, MiacroTech Industries)<br /><br />Arif Bashir, Director Technical (D G Cement, Nishat Group)<br /><br />Faisal Farid, MD, Maximum International, LUMS BoD)<br /><br />Shahid Hussain, CEO (Servis Sales Corporation, LUMS BoD)<br /><br />Bilal Arif, Technical Lead (Schneider Electric)<br /><br /></p>\r\n<p><strong>Non-Profit/NGOs:</strong><br /><br />Ijaz Nabi, Country Head, IGC<br /><br />&nbsp;Asim Buksh, CEO (Buksh Energy)<br /><br />Junaid Qureshi, CEO (Dynamic Green Lahore)<br /><br />Ali Habib, Managing Partner (Hima Verte)<br /><br />Naveed Siddique, GM (DICE/Ghulam Faruque Group)<br /><br /></p>\r\n<p><strong>Academia:</strong><br /><br />Prof. Dr. Waqar Mehmood, Director (KICS UET)<br /><br />Amjad Hussain, Director (FAST, NUCES)<br /><br />Suhail Aftab Qureshi, Dean EE (UET, Lahore)<br /><br />Tahir Izhar, Chair EE (UET, Lahore)<br /><br />&nbsp;Muhammad Ghaffar Dogar, Chief Scientific Officer (Comsats Energy Center)</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"https://scontent-sin6-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/16602574_1243570235734624_7108802582840630506_n.jpg?oh=c232bb3900c22dfd875340f94c3c157f&amp;oe=594A3E74\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"625\" /></p>', NULL, '2017-02-10', 1, 1),
(149, 197, 'KICS Holds a Workshop on Introduction to SDR and Developing Next Generation 5G Communication System', '<p>A workshop on the topic of &lsquo;Introduction to SDR and Efficiently Developing Next Generation/5G Communication System&rsquo; was held in KICS, UET Lahore on 15th February. It was conducted by Mr. Fawad and Mr. Tayyab from HUTIC Telecom Lab. This research talk was an introduction to SDR and Efficiently Deploying Next Generation Wireless System like 5G prototype.</p>\r\n<p><br />The presenters &ndash; Mr. Fawad and Mr. Tayyab very skillfully covered the SDR architecture, SDR applications, components of SDR, NI platform and development tools of SDR. Apart from all this, the topics like the implementation of Massive MIMO and mm Wave in 5G prototype, 5G standardization activities in 3GPP, 5G Vectors, OFDMA with MIMO and Beam forming were also discussed in detail.</p>', NULL, '2017-02-16', 1, 1),
(150, 198, 'A Get Together Organized to Honor the Organizers of DICE 2016 ', '<p>A get together for DICE Energy &amp; Water 2016 Exhibition (held in UET Lahore on 19th &amp; 20th December 2016) was conducted at Staff Club in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 15th February 2017. The ceremony witnessed the high officials of UET, organizers of DICE 2016 and other participants. The event started with the recitation of Holy Quran. Dr. Waqar Mahmood, the chief guest of the occasion, delivered a speech and appreciated the efforts of the organizers. He also revealed the future plans of KICS UET. The ceremony concluded with certificates&rsquo; distribution among the organizers of DICE 2016.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_2017/dice%20get%20together_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"773\" height=\"517\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_2017/dice%20get%20together_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"772\" height=\"772\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_2017/dice%20get%20together_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"774\" height=\"774\" /></p>', NULL, '2017-02-16', 1, 1),
(151, NULL, 'test', '<p>test</p>', NULL, '0000-00-00', 25, 1),
(154, NULL, 'Finance for Entrepreneurship by Dr. Andrew Scheuermann, a Ph.D. from Stanford University who has been deeply involved in entrepreneurship education. Andrew was one of the early team members that built StartX, one of the top startup accelerators in the world.  Andrew is skilled in venture fundraising and is one of the \'fundraising architects\' in the StartX community to help other founders who have collectively raised over $2B dollars. ', '<p><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Cambria, serif; color: #444444; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">This talk was arranged by Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science&rsquo;s Technology Incubation and Commercialization Center (TICK). It was attended by the number of participants comprising of business executives, business students, researchers and managers respectively who all took a deep interest in the talk.</span></p>', NULL, '2017-07-18', 15, 1),
(155, NULL, 'TICK Proudly Launches Chargeable Electric Bike That Does 100 KM on a Single Charge', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria, serif; color: #444444; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-size: small;\">TICK has launched a Turbo Electric Bike called Simtaar that accelerates to 60 kilometer per hour. The brilliance of this electric bike is that it does more than 100 km on a single charge The luminous minds behind this innovation are Abdul Basit and Asra Alvi.</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria, serif; color: #444444; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">The Turbo Electric Bike Simtaar was introduced to the Vice Chancellor UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid and Director KICS, Prof. Waqar Mahmood. Other faculty members were also present at the occasion.</span></span></p>', NULL, '2017-06-19', 15, 1),
(156, NULL, ' \"Ecommerce by Amazon FBA\". ', '<p><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Great workshop organized by TICK and LOOP on How to develop a profitable business through selling products at Amazon Conducted by a 6 figure earner Muhammad Naeem Sikandar.</span></p>', NULL, '2017-07-11', 15, 1),
(157, NULL, 'All Pakistan DICE Energy & Water 2016 Exhibition', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria, serif; color: #444444; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">DICE Energy &amp; Water 2016 exhibition is going to be held at University of Engineering Technology Lahore with the collaboration of&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria, serif; color: #444444; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Al-Khwarizmi Institute of Computer Science UET Lahore, ORIC Department Punjab University, CERAD, IEEE Industry Applications Society, IEEE Power and Energy Society Lahore Section and DICE USA<strong><span style=\"font-family: \'Cambria\',\'serif\'; mso-ascii-theme-font: major-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: major-latin; mso-bidi-font-family: Helvetica;\">.&nbsp;</span></strong></span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria, serif; color: #444444; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong></strong>The program held at various universities in Pakistan every year since 2007, but for the first time UET Lahore has gained the privilege to conduct it. The idea behind DICE E&amp;W Exhibition is to motivate academia, industry, government, entrepreneurs and expatriates to come to a common platform to showcase innovations, technologies, knowledge and make further collaborations with each other for the rapid development of innovative products necessary for the economic development of the country.</span></span></p>', NULL, '2017-01-19', 15, 1),
(158, NULL, 'USL Induction Ceremony 2015 at KICS', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria, serif; color: #444444; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">A seminar on &ldquo;Leadership and Motivation&rdquo; proposed by Mr. Rehan Tariq and with the help of KICS&rsquo;s management was arranged at seminar hall KICS on Tuesday, 17th November 2015 for the UET Startup Leaders. The basic purpose of the seminar was to impart leadership skills to USLs.</span></span></p>', NULL, '2015-11-17', 15, 1),
(159, NULL, 'A Seminar on Entrepreneurship & TICK Incubation Center at University of Central Punjab , Lahore', '<h4 style=\"margin: 0in 0in 3.75pt 0.5in; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: small; font-family: Cambria, serif; color: #333333; font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</span></h4>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria, serif; color: #444444; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Riding the rampant entrepreneurial wave in Pakistan, UET has introduced its own incubation centre named TICK. It operates under the Al-Khwarizmi Institute of Computer Sciences, commonly known as KICS. For awareness and promotional purposes seminars are conducted in and outside UET. One of such events includes a seminar in UCP, the title of which was &ldquo;Entrepreneurship and TICK Incubation Centre&rdquo;</span>.</span></span></p>', NULL, '2014-05-16', 15, 1),
(160, NULL, 'A Seminar on \"Entrepreneurship and Tech Incubation Center \" in UCP', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria, serif; color: #444444; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: small;\">Al Khwarizimi Institute of Computer Sciences (KICS), UET Lahore is organizing a seminar&ldquo;Entrepreneurship and Tech Incubation Center (TICK)&rdquo; in UCP. The seminar will be an introductory session on Entrepreneurship and Startup Culture followed by how our Incubation Center &ndash;TICK, can help the students in realizing their business dreams.</span></span></p>', NULL, '2015-05-12', 15, 1),
(161, NULL, 'Seminar on \"Entrepreneurship and TICK Incubation Center\"', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria, serif; color: #000000; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-size: small;\">Al-Khwarizmi Institute of Computer Science is organizing a seminar on &ldquo;Entrepreneurship and &nbsp;&nbsp;TICK Incubation Center&rdquo; on 6th of May, 2014.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family: \'Cambria\',\'serif\'; mso-ascii-theme-font: major-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: major-latin; mso-bidi-font-family: Helvetica; color: #444444;\"><span style=\"font-size: small; color: #000000;\">Since the seminar is intended to provide a platform for exchange of good enterprising ideas in the context of our Incubation Center, we believe it will provide enriching experience for all the participants.</span></span></p>', NULL, '2014-04-28', 15, 1),
(162, NULL, 'UET Startup Leader (USL)', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 13.5pt; text-indent: -22.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Cambria, serif; color: #444444; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Cambria, serif;\">The TICK- Technology incubation Centre of</span><span style=\"line-height: 115%; font-size: 14.6667px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Cambria, serif;\">AlKhwarizimi Institute of Computer Sciences (KICS), UET Lahore is providing an opportunity to be one of the first &ldquo;UET Startup Leaders&rdquo; (USL). It&rsquo;s a platform where students can learn and participate in events; create a relation between students &amp; university.</span></p>', NULL, '2014-04-09', 15, 1),
(163, NULL, 'Seminar on Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT)', '<p><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12.8px;\">IoT lab of KICS arranged a talk on Industrial Internet of Things (</span><span class=\"il\" style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12.8px;\">IIoT</span><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12.8px;\">) on 4th August in&nbsp;</span><span class=\"il\" style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12.8px;\">Seminar</span><span style=\"color: #222222; font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12.8px;\">&nbsp;Hall of KICS UET.&nbsp;</span></p>', NULL, '2017-08-04', 16, 1),
(182, 2028, 'A Talk on Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT) Takes Place in KICS UET Lahore', '<p>IoT Lab of KICS UET Lahore arranged a talk on &lsquo;Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT)&rsquo; in Seminar Hall at KICS, University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 4th August 2017. The speaker of the event was Dr. Muhammad Moeen from USA.&nbsp; He is a UET&rsquo;s graduate and earned the engineering degree in Electronics/communications engineering in 2000. Mr. Moeen did his Masters in Communications and Signals Processing from London in 2002 later did PhD in Control Engineering from Imperial College, London. He has been working within engineering organization of Schlumberger in various engineering and management positions related to New Product Development since 2007. For last one year or so, he has been working towards identifying technology building blocks and platforms to facilitate adoption and deployment of Industrial IoT (IIoT) solutions across all product lines within Schlumberger in an effort to digitally transform oil field services operations.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/August%2017/IIOT_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>The number of internet connected devices is expected to reach 30 billion by 2020. This exponential rise in number of connected devices is set to transform businesses in consumer space as well as industrial space. Use of internet connected industrial devices, termed as, Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT), is being adopted by several enterprises across all major industrial sectors to revolutionize their businesses.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/August%2017/IIOT_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>Therefore, this talk focused on the identification of the need of IIoT being taken by the industry today. The talk made it clear that the industry today understood the importance of IIoT. It also delivered the examples from various industrial verticals demonstrating the impact IIoT was making in creating the value for their businesses. It also highlighted the end-to-end IIoT solutions and key characteristics.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/August%2017/IIOT_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"471\" /></p>\r\n<p>Researchers and faculty members took keen interest in this specially designed talk that benefited them in entirety. </p>', NULL, '2017-08-08', 1, 1),
(181, 2027, 'CLE in Collaboration with SNLP Conducts Post Graduate Certificate in Experimental Phonology Using PRAAT', '<p>A program on the topic of &lsquo;CLE Post Graduate Certificate in Experimental Phonology Using PRAAT was conducted at Center of Language Engineering (CLE) KICS, University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 4th to 5th and 11th to 12th August 2017. CLE in collaboration with Society for Natural Language Processing (SNLP) arranged this program that witnessed horde of professionals.</p>\r\n<p><br />The program was specially designed and targeted to faculty and researchers from disciplines including Urdu, English, Applied Linguistics, English Language Teaching, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering (Language Processing), Speech Pathology and related areas. In order to gran good participation from faculty, it was arranged on weekends. It is still going on and will end up on 12th August.</p>', NULL, '2017-08-08', 1, 1),
(180, 2026, 'IEEE COMSOC SUMMER SCHOOL PROGRAM 2017 ASIA PACIFIC', '<p>IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section in collaboration with Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS), UET &amp; Fast University Lahore organized a 4-day &ldquo;IEEE COMSOC Summer School Program 2017 Asia Pacific&rdquo;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July,%2017/Day%201%20Group%20Photo.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"833\" height=\"348\" /></p>\r\n<p>Other collaborators are HEC Pakistan, IEEE UET and IEEE FAST. It was much inspirational for all who attended it particularly for the young engineers in Pakistan who very actively participated in this 4-day summer school. The school was designed for the fresh graduates, MS and PhD students so that they could advance their knowledge and research activities. IEEE COMSOC Summer School has its historical background as well, as it first started two years back in 2015 in Italy.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July,%2017/IMG_3926.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"835\" height=\"503\" /></p>\r\n<p>The opening ceremony of IEEE COMSOC Summer School began with a video message by Prof. Dr Vincenzo Piuri, who is a Full Professor at the University of Milan, Italy. Prof. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, Vice Chancellor University of Engineering and Technology Lahore was the honorable chief guest. VC UET said that IEEE COMSOC was a good initiative and would surely bring lucrative results. He also mentioned that it would be beneficial for both the industry and academia. He appreciated the technological advancements in the country and emphasized on the efforts and contributions of our students who were the active parts of the smart world and smart technologies. Other guests included Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director KICS UET and Sultan Qaboos IT Chair), Prof. Dr. Noor Muhammad Shaikh, GC University Lahore and Dr. Sayyed Aaun Abbas, Dr. Tariq Jadoon, LUMS and Chair IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section Mr. Kashif Bashir.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July,%2017/Day%202%20Group%20Photo%20Technical%20Tour%20v1.1%20(1).jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"834\" height=\"503\" /></p>\r\n<p>This year IEEE COMSOC Summer School 2017 witnessed 65 research participants from 9 different universities of Pakistan. 14 speakers including 5 from abroad and 9 from national universities. International speakers were from China, Saudi Arabia, Estonia, Ireland and Malaysia whereas national speakers were from LUMS, COMSATS Lahore, UET Lahore and Mehran University Jamshoro respectively.</p>\r\n<p>A number of talks coupled with speeches by the guests were seen at this year&rsquo;s summer school.&nbsp; Featured speaker were Dr. Mohamed-Slim Alouini, Dr. Momin Uppal, Dr. Zartash Uzmi, Dr. Ghalib Shah, Dr. M. Majid Butt, Dr.&nbsp; Faisal K. Shaikh, Dr. Ubaid ullah Fiaz, Dr. Muhammad Tahir, Dr. Sobia Baig, Dr. Hussain Mahdi, Dr. Waqar Baig, Mr. He Gang and Dr. Muhammad Mahtab Alam. The topics such as Internet Censorship Research, USAID Fulbright and other Scholarship opportunities abroad, Smart Grid Communication technology, FM Radio Broadcast Using RTL Software, Internet of Things, Polar Codes, Shared Spectrum Access, 5G Wireless Communication Networks, Wireless acoustic sensor network and a number of others were discussed at the occasion in detail. Paper presentations were also presented over there. Panel discussion on the topic of how to elevate research in Pakistan was also a major highlight of the event as well.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July,%2017/Day%204%20Group%20Photo.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"837\" height=\"520\" /></p>\r\n<p>Two visits were arranged also. First visit was taken to the best eye-candy locales of the city of Lahore. Secondly the participants were taken on a technical tour of Punjab Safe City Head Quarters where they were briefed by Mr. Akbar Nasir Khan, Chief Operating Officer and Project Director PPIC3. He also showed how the city was monitored by hundreds of cameras and how all the emergency services are integrated into a single one hotline.</p>\r\n<p><br />The chief guest of the closing ceremony was Engr. Jawed Salim Qureshi, Chairman Pakistan Engineering Council. He said that Pakistan Engineering Council was closely working with the government and industry for the betterment and good future of the students who got appointed as internees. Mr. Jawed Salim Qureshi also said that Pakistani engineers had been doing great not only in Pakistan but also across the world to prove their mettle. He said that the formula of success was being a champion. Mr. Akbar Nasir Khan, Chief Operating Officer Punjab Safe City Authority said that what he learned from his education was leadership and it was what took you to the heights of success.&nbsp; Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmed Khalid, Vice Chancellor UET Lahore appreciated the efforts of KICS-UET and FAST NU Lahore for organizing this mega event successfully that lasted for 4 days from 11th to 14th July 2017.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July,%2017/DSC_0062.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"838\" height=\"480\" /></p>\r\n<p><br />Other guest included Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Director KICS UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Suhail Aftab Qureshi, Dean EE UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Amjad Hussain, Director FAST NU Lahore, Mr. Edward Zhang, Vice President Huawei Technologies China, Mr. Kashif Bashir Chair IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section and Mr. Usman Munawar Secretary IEEE Lahore Section. The guests were conferred with the souvenirs and shields whereas the participants and the events&rsquo; organizers were awarded with the certificates.</p>', NULL, '2017-07-31', 1, 1);
INSERT INTO `star_news` (`news_id`, `order`, `news_des`, `news_detail`, `newsthumb`, `news_stamp`, `group_id`, `active`) VALUES
(179, 2025, 'Stanford University\'s Professor Delivers a Talk on Finance for Entrepreneurs in KICS UET', '<p>KICS organized a seminar on the topic of &lsquo;Finance for Entrepreneurs&rsquo; on July 18th, 2017 at Seminar Hall in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore. This lucrative and comprehensive talk was arranged by Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science&rsquo;s Technology Incubation and Commercialization Center (TICK). It was attended by the horde of the participants comprising of business executives, business students, researchers and managers respectively who all took a deep interest in the talk.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July,%2017/Dr.%20Andrew_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"508\" /></p>\r\n<p>Dr. Andrew Scheuermann, a PhD from Stanford University USA, delivered this talk. He has been deeply involved in entrepreneurship education. Dr. Andrew happened to be the early team members who built StartX &ndash; one of the top startup accelerators in the world. A highly skilled in venture fundraising, Dr. Andrew is one of the &lsquo;fundraising architects&rsquo; in the StartX community that is always geared up to help other founders who have collectively raised over $2B dollars.&nbsp; Dr. Andrew is also the founder of a venture-backed company &lsquo;Arch Systems&rsquo;.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July,%2017/Dr.%20Andrew_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"578\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July,%2017/Dr.%20Andrew-03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>After the talk, there was a questions-answers session where the keen participants asked their questions from the speaker.</p>', NULL, '2017-07-19', 1, 1),
(178, 2024, 'Chairman All Pakistan Engineering Council Attends Closing Ceremony of IEEE COMSOC Summer School at UET Lahore', '<p>The closing ceremony of IEEE COMSOC Summer School 2017 took place on 13th of July at UET Auditorium, University of Engineering and Technology Lahore, where the chief guest was Chairman All Pakistan Engineering Council Mr. Eng. Jawed Salim Qureshi. Other distinguished guests included Chief Operating Officer Safe City Punjab Mr. Akbar Nasir Khan and Vice Chancellor UET Lahore Prof. Fazal Ahmad Khalid.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July,%2017/IEEE_COMSOC_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"846\" height=\"521\" /></p>\r\n<p>In his address, the chief guest Mr. Qureshi said that Pakistan Engineering Council was closely working with the government and industry for the betterment and good future of the students who got appointed as internees. He also mentioned that more than 10,000 internees were hired in the industry. Mr. Jawed Salim Qureshi also said that Pakistani engineers had been doing great not only in Pakistan but also across the world to prove their mettle. He said that the formula of success was being a champion.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July,%2017/IEEE_COMSOC_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"532\" /></p>\r\n<p>Mr. Akbar Nasir Khan, Chief Operating Officer Punjab Safe City, said that what he learned from his education was leadership and it was what took you to the heights of success.&nbsp; Mr. Khan also talked about the safe city project as to how it was all about.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July,%2017/IEEE_COMSOC_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"846\" height=\"534\" /></p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor UET Lahore appreciated the efforts of KICS for organizing this mega event successfully that lasted for 4 days from 11th to 14th July at FAST University and KICS UET Lahore. He liked how smart technologies were booming in the world and Pakistan in particular.</p>\r\n<p><br />Other speakers who contributed their views were Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director KICS) and the invited speakers who had come from around the world to attend this event.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/July,%2017/IEEE_COMSOC_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"846\" height=\"533\" /></p>\r\n<p>The ceremony concluded with the distribution of the shields and souvenirs to the honorable guests by the chief guests who was then awarded with a special shield by the Vice Chancellor. </p>', NULL, '2017-07-14', 1, 1),
(177, 2023, 'Vice Chancellor UET Inaugurates IEEE COMSOC Summer School 2017 at FAST University', '<p>The opening ceremony of IEEE COMSOC Summer School 2017 took place at FAST NU Lahore on 11th July 2017. It is for the second time that this summer school took place in Pakistan. Last year it was conducted by both Punjab University and Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science of University of Engineering and Technology Lahore and this time once again KICS UET participated in conducting this event. With a joint collaboration of KICS UET and FAST University, this year&rsquo;s event was launched, which opening ceremony witnessed a large number of participants and guest speakers from around the world.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"https://scontent-sit4-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/19959394_1397084153716564_513927863502552938_n.jpg?oh=a8ced0e6e0a00321cf5ac47c71a6eddf&amp;oe=5A0F2944\" alt=\"\" width=\"864\" height=\"576\" /></p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor University of Engineering and Technology Lahore, Prof. Fazal Ahmad Khalid was the honorable chief guest. Other guests included Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director KICS UET and Sultan Qaboos IT Chair), Prof. Dr. Noor Muhammad Shaikh (from Electrical Department, GC University Lahore) and Dr. Sayyed Aaun Abbas. Dr. Amjad Hussain, Director FAST University, hosted the event and welcomed the guests.</p>\r\n<p><br />VC UET said that IEEE COMSIOC was a good initiative and would surely bring lucrative results. He also mentioned that it would be beneficial for both the industry and academia. He appreciated the technological advancements in the country and emphasized on the efforts and contributions of our students who were the active parts of the smart world and smart technologies.</p>\r\n<p><br />Other guests too shared their views on IEEE Society and COMSOC Sumer School and how brilliantly it was being done in Pakistan.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"https://scontent-sit4-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/19959032_1397084150383231_42481936356744189_n.jpg?oh=1d82e47f2706d5fc081a0a2844414af7&amp;oe=59F9E057\" alt=\"\" width=\"867\" height=\"578\" /></p>\r\n<p>The event will last till 14th of July. First two days program is conducted at FAST University whereas the remaining two days&rsquo; activities will be done at KICS UET Lahore.</p>\r\n<p><br />The opening day was comprised of various presentations of the topics like Case Studies of ISPs, Fullbright Scholarships Programs&rsquo; Overview, An Overview of Core Smart Grid Communication Technologies and Internet of Things.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"https://scontent-sit4-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/19990404_1397084157049897_6941020073702908593_n.jpg?oh=66dad759feaa47e9d352886b8a66c0e8&amp;oe=5A10EA4D\" alt=\"\" width=\"872\" height=\"581\" /></p>\r\n<p>Opening ceremony concluded with the distribution of shields to the guests by Vice Chancellor UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Amjad Hussain (Director FAST University) and Kashif Bashir (Chair IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section and HUTIC Manager). VC UET, the chief guest of the event, was conferred with a special souvenir by Dr. Amjad.&nbsp; The guests were also taken for a tour of the city locations. </p>', NULL, '2017-07-11', 1, 1),
(176, 2022, 'TICK Proudly Launches Chargeable Electric Bike That Does 100 KM on a Single Charge', '<p>TICK has launched a Turbo Electric Bike called Simtaar that accelerates to 60 kilometer per hour. The brilliance of this electric bike is that it does more than 100 km on a single charge. All you need is to have an electric socket to charge it and the best of the best is that you can charge the bike anywhere from any electric socket. The luminous minds behind this innovation are Abdul Basit and Asra Alvi.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/June,%202017/TICK\'s%20bike.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"474\" /></p>\r\n<p>The Turbo Electric Bike Simtaar was introduced to the Vice Chancellor UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid and Director KICS, Prof. Waqar Mahmood. Other faculty members were also present at the occasion.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/June,%202017/TICK\'s%20bike_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"474\" /></p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor took a keen interest in this innovation and also took a ride enjoyably. You may visit TICK\'s Official Facebook Page for more updates at <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/tick.uet/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/tick.uet/</a></p>', NULL, '2017-06-22', 1, 1),
(175, 2021, 'Call For Paper | International Conference on Energy Conservation and Efficiency 2017 | Energy Conservation : A Smart Choice | To Be Held on 22-23 November 2017 at Faletti\'s Hotel Lahore', '<p><strong>CALL FOR PAPERS</strong><br /><br /><br /><strong>International Conference on Energy Conservation and Efficiency 2017</strong><br /><br /><strong>Energy Conservation : A Smart Choice</strong><br /><br /><strong>22-23 November, 2017 | Faletti&rsquo;s Hotel Lahore, Pakistan</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong></strong><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/June,%202017/ICECE%202017.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"754\" height=\"300\" /><br /><br /></p>\r\n<p>In the spirit of providing an opportunity and platform, FSK Pvt. Ltd&nbsp; and CERAD, UET Lahore&nbsp; organizes International Conference on Energy Conservation on 22-23 November 2017 at Faletti\'s Hotel Lahore, Pakistan in collaboration with Punjab Government PEECA and IEEE IAS (Industrial Applications Society, Lahore Section); inviting engineers, researchers, energy experts, manufacturers, and building designers to interact, discuss, explore and exchange ideas in the fastest growing field of Energy Efficiency and Conservation strategies. Demand side energy management and optimization has seen great technological advancements over the years making it viable solution in current energy situation of Pakistan. The event is intended to create a professional as well as educational network bringing interested experts and community together.<br /><br /><br />Energy Conservation is an excellent way to address the alarming electricity supply and demand gap. The increased awareness regarding renewable energies especially solar and wind energy has also stimulated the trend towards energy conservation techniques and energy efficient devices to optimize the energy demand and money saving. This forum will specifically outlook Pakistan\'s perspective over broad range of areas such as practical implementation of energy modeling, smart controls, renewable energies, resources management, combined heat and power, building design, efficient building systems, etc. Furthermore, technological advancements such as energy efficient devices, drives and controls shall also be included with the objective of practical advancements in efficient energy systems.<br /><br /><br />Convener: Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, Vice Chancellor, UET Lahore, Pakistan<br /><br />Conference Chair: Mr. Farooq Amjad Meer, President FSK Pvt Ltd. &amp; NSR Group of Companies<br /><br />Conference Technical Chair: Dr. Waqar Mehmood, Director CERAD, UET Lahore, Pakistan<br /><br />Conference Co Chair:Mr. Rao Khalid A. Khan, Managing Director, FSK Pvt. Ltd.<br /><br />Conference Secretary: Mr. Usman Munawar, Research Officer, KICS UET Lahore, Pakistan<br /><br /><br />ICECE 2017 is soliciting technical papers in technical areas which will include but not limited to:<br /><br /><br />1- Energy Conservation in Domestic, Industrial and Commercial Sector<br /><br />2- Domestic Energy Efficient Devices<br /><br />3- Commercial and Industrial Energy Efficient Equipment<br /><br />4- Smart Control System<br /><br />5- Green Building Design<br /><br />6- Building Envelope Strategies for Better Energy Performance<br /><br />7- Building Codes and Standards<br /><br />8- Energy Management System and Standards<br /><br />9- Energy Efficient Cooling and Heating System<br /><br />10- Combined Heat and Power (CHP)<br /><br />11- Power Quality Enhancement<br /><br />12- Smart Metering System<br /><br />13- Energy Efficient Lighting System<br /><br />14- Building Management System<br /><br />15- Energy System Modeling<br /><br />16- Water Management<br /><br />17- Waste to Energy Conversion<br /><br />18- Renewable Energy Technologies (Solar, Wind, Biomass etc.)<br /><br />19- Energy Storage<br /><br />20- Energy Efficient Control Drives and Cabling<br /><br />21- Load Management and Forecasting<br /><br />22- Generation, Distribution and Transmission<br /><br /><br /><strong>For Submitting Manuscripts, Please Follow</strong><br /><br />Easy Chair Link: <a href=\"http://icece.kics.edu.pk/submission/\" target=\"_blank\">Paper Submissions</a> | <a href=\"http://icece.kics.edu.pk/\" target=\"_blank\">Conference Website</a><br /><br />Manuscript submission deadline is 31st August, 2017 and acceptance/non acceptance will be on 30th September, 2017. Camera ready submission will be on 15th October, 2017. <!--[if gte mso 9]><xml>\r\n <o:OfficeDocumentSettings>\r\n  <o:TargetScreenSize>800x600</o:TargetScreenSize>\r\n </o:OfficeDocumentSettings>\r\n</xml><![endif]--></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><a style=\"text-align: right;\" href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/June,%202017/Call%20for%20Papers%20-%20ICECE.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><input class=\"btn btn-primary\" type=\"button\" name=\"button\" value=\"Download Brochure for Complete Details\" /></a></div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>For Further Detail please contact on email: <a href=\"mailto:icece.info@kics.edu.pk\">icece.info@kics.edu.pk</a>&nbsp; (For Paper Submission)<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <a href=\"mailto:info@fsk.com.pk\">info@fsk.com.pk</a> (For Sponsorship &amp; Exhibitions)</p>', NULL, '2017-06-16', 1, 1),
(174, 2020, 'Interviews for PSDF Training Courses Conducted in UET Lahore', '<p>Interviews for PSDF (Punjab Skills Development Fund) training courses have started in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore from June 15th and they will last till the following day i.e. 16th June, 2017. Large number of candidates filled applications for these training free training courses. The selected candidates will also be paid monthly stipend.</p>\r\n<p><br />Interviews were held and will be held at three locations in UET Lahore such as Auditorium Complex, Solar Lab at KICS and Conference Room at KICS UET Lahore.</p>\r\n<p><br />The experts from the respective fields were designated to conduct the interviews. Of the large number of applications, only carefully chosen 100 candidates will be selected for all courses.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/June,%202017/PSDF%20Interviews.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>', NULL, '2017-06-15', 1, 1),
(173, 2019, 'A Seminar on Entrepreneurship as a National Development Tool Taken Place at KICS,UET Lahore', '<p>KICS arranged an invited talk on &lsquo;Entrepreneurship as a National Development Tool&rsquo; on 2nd of June, 2017 at KICS Seminar Hall in UET Lahore. The invited speaker was Dr. Shahid Qureshi, who is a Program Director, CED, IBA, Karachi. The event witnessed a large amount of gathering, who all very attentively heard the views of the most luminous speaker who not only delivered a through lecture on the topic, but also gave his personal experiences and Quranic references.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/June,%202017/ent_seminar_01.JPG\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>Dr. Shahid graduated from the University of Engineering and Technology Lahore in 1990. In 1993, he went to Bangkok, Thailand where he was conferred with the Government of Holland scholarship to pursue masters in Industrial Engineering and Management at Asian Institute of Technology. Later, Dr. Shahid earned the MBA degree from LUMS. In 2006, he flied to Germany to receive the German (DAAD) scholarship to pursue PhD from the Department of Marketing at the Faculty of Business Administration at the Technical University of Berlin. Entrepreneurship and strategic management is his passion and he keeps delivering lectures on these topics not only in Pakistan, but also in other parts of the world.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/June,%202017/ent_seminar_02.JPG\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/June,%202017/ent_seminar_03.JPG\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p><br />The event concluded with a shield endowment to the speaker by Director KICS, Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood.<br /><br /></p>', NULL, '2017-06-02', 1, 1),
(172, 2018, 'UET and Tsinghua University Beijing Sign an MOU to Launch Research Collaboration Program', '<p>A delegation from the Institute of Public Safety Research Tsinghua University Beijing, China visited University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 30th May 2017 to sign an MOU to launch a joint academic and research collaboration program in Public Safety Research. MOU signing ceremony was held at Vice Chancellor Office in UET and attended by the Vice Chancellor Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, Vice Dean IPSR Tsinghua University Prof. Huang Quanyi and other key personnel from both sides.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/MOU%20China_002.JPG\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>According to the agreement, Institute of Public Safety Research Tsinghua University will be a joint venture partner for research and development projects. While talking to the attendees of the event, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid said that this joint venture would be truly beneficial for UET and Tsinghua University to extend the relations in mutual areas of development.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/MOU%20China_001.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p><br />Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Director Al Khwarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) also delivered a presentation on research and academic programs of UET Lahore.&nbsp; Following to Dr. Waqar&rsquo;s presentation, Prof. Dr. Peng Du (Senior Engineer IPSR) presented his presentation on &lsquo;Introduction to the Institute of Public Safety Research&rsquo;.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/MOU%20China_01.JPG\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"515\" /></p>\r\n<p>The delegation was also taken for a visit of the research labs of KICS such as CVML, NWN, HPCNL, Huawei and GIS where they were presented the functions of the labs. The delegation was briefed about the ongoing research projects of the labs as well. The guests were conferred with the souvenirs by the Vice Chancellor.</p>', NULL, '2017-05-31', 1, 1),
(171, 2017, 'UET Game Studio Launches App for Sehari and Iftari Timing', '<p>UET Game Studio, KICS UET&rsquo;s development team headed by Mr. Usman Ghani, has launched a Ramadan Sehri and Iftari Timings App available on both iOS and Android.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/Ramdan-Timing%20App.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"655\" height=\"580\" /></p>\r\n<p><br />Now you can keep the Ramadan Calendar in your pocket. The app updates the Sehar and Aftar timings automatically. It uses the user&rsquo;s location and gives the accurate timing for Sehar and Aftar as per the location.</p>\r\n<p><br />The premium version is available for just $1. It is ads free and you can add custom alarms for Sehar and Aftar. Download it from the app store by clicking the links below.<br /><br />Android: <a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=pk.edu.kics.uetgs.ramadan\" target=\"_blank\">https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=pk.edu.kics.uetgs.ramadan</a><br /><br />iOS: <a href=\"https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/ramadan-suhoor-aftar-timings-with-alarms/id1241291850?ls=1&amp;mt=8\" target=\"_blank\">https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/ramadan-suhoor-aftar-timings-with-alarms/id1241291850?ls=1&amp;mt=8</a><br /><br /></p>', NULL, '2017-05-30', 1, 1),
(170, 2018, 'KICS has launched Free Technical Courses Session with the collaboration of PSDF', '<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\r\n<h2><strong><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"Download Form\" href=\"http://kics.edu.pk/documents/form2017.jpg\" target=\"_self\">Download Form</a></strong></h2>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2><img src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/doc/ad2017.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" /></h2>\r\n<h2><strong>Course Content </strong></h2>\r\n<table class=\"table\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"654\">\r\n<h2><strong> Mobile Application Development </strong></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Java Application Development &ndash; Programming Fundamental</li>\r\n<li>Android Frontend Activities &ndash; GUI</li>\r\n<li>UI Customization and Custom Components</li>\r\n<li>User Interaction Components</li>\r\n<li>Interface Communication</li>\r\n<li>Background Process and Services</li>\r\n<li>Thread</li>\r\n<li>Data storage</li>\r\n<li>Dialogs Boxes and widgets</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h1>&nbsp;</h1>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"654\">\r\n<h2><strong> Solor Photovoltaic Installation and Pumping Training </strong></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Solar system designing</li>\r\n<li>Solar system installation</li>\r\n<li>Solar system troubleshooting</li>\r\n<li>Solar tube well system</li>\r\n<li>Solar Drip irrigation</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"654\">\r\n<h2><strong> Networking Technologies (Huawei)</strong><strong></strong></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Fundamental of Networks</li>\r\n<li>Huawei Certified Network Associate (HCNA) Router and switching</li>\r\n<li>Huawei Certified Network Professional (HCNP) Router and switching</li>\r\n<li>Huawei Certified Network Associate video conferencing (VC)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"654\">\r\n<h2><strong> Telecommunication Technician (Huawei) </strong></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Fundamentals of Electrical, Electronics and Communications</li>\r\n<li>Computer Networks, Wireless Technologies</li>\r\n<li>BTS/BSC Technician/Rigger</li>\r\n<li>2G, 3G, 4G Technologies</li>\r\n<li>RF Drive test and Optimization using TEMS</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"654\">\r\n<h2><strong> PLC (Programmable Logic Control) </strong></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Introduction to PLC and Control</li>\r\n<li>Introduction to Programming Languages</li>\r\n<li>Fatek PLC with programming on Winproladder</li>\r\n<li>Seimens S7-300 with programming on simetic manager</li>\r\n<li>Practical&rsquo;s</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"654\">\r\n<h2><strong> Web Design and Development </strong></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>HTML 5</li>\r\n<li>CSS3</li>\r\n<li>Bootstrap 3.+</li>\r\n<li>jQuery</li>\r\n<li>PHP</li>\r\n<li>Codeigniter</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"654\">\r\n<h2><strong> Graphic Design (Print Media)</strong><strong></strong></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Principles of Designing</li>\r\n<li>Still and Live Drawing</li>\r\n<li>Line Works</li>\r\n<li>Color Combinations</li>\r\n<li>Logo Designing</li>\r\n<li>2D Cartoon Making</li>\r\n<li>Web Banners</li>\r\n<li>Vector Based Designing Tool</li>\r\n<li>Corel Draw X7</li>\r\n<li>Pixel Based Designing Tool</li>\r\n<li>Adobe Photoshop CC</li>\r\n<li>Urdu Typing Tool</li>\r\n<li>In page</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', NULL, '2017-05-26', 1, 1),
(169, 2016, 'UET Game Studio Launches Another Mobile Game for KIDS', '<p>Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science&rsquo;s luminous development team has ventured into a new game. UET Game Studio, KICS development lab, has just released a new game titled &lsquo;Math Puzzle: Save the Frog&rsquo;. The game has been targeted to the kids and is a learning game (edutainment), but the elders too may enjoy the pleasures come out of it.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/UET%20Game%20Studio.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"628\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p><br />The game is available for download both on Google Play Store and Apple Store. You may download it by using the below links.<br /><br />Apple: <a href=\"https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/math-puzzle-save-the-frog/id1232146902?mt=8\" target=\"_blank\">https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/math-puzzle-save-the-frog/id1232146902?mt=8</a><br />Android: <a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=pk.edu.kics.uetgs.Math_Puzzle&amp;hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=pk.edu.kics.uetgs.Math_Puzzle&amp;hl=en</a><br /><br />Mr. Usman Ghani and his team have developed this game and they are highly applauded for this distinction. </p>', NULL, '2017-05-25', 1, 1),
(168, 2015, 'KICS Celebrates the World Telecom Day 2017 with Experts of Academia and Industry in UET', '<p>KICS and IEEE Communication Society organized World Telecommunication Day 2017 on 16th May 2017. The event was held at Seminar Hall in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore. High officials and the experts from academia and industry attended the event, which theme was &lsquo;Big Data for Big Impact&rsquo;.&nbsp; The purpose of WTD was to highlight the importance of communication in our lives.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/World%20Telecom%20Day%2017.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"838\" height=\"330\" /></p>\r\n<p>The event began with a video message by Prof. Dr Vincenzo Piuri IEEE President Elect 2018, who is a Full Professor at the University of Milan, Italy. He emphasized the importance of Big Data in today&rsquo;s world and thanked the organizers for conducting the World Telecom Day 2017 at KICS.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/World%20Telecom%20Day_Featured.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Chief Guest of the occasion Mr. Edward Zhang, Vice President of Huawei Enterprise Wireless Solution, uttered about the strapping friendship between Pakistan and China and how beneficial it had been since the outset in terms of business development between the two countries. He also revealed about the ICT solutions and mentioned the Huawei Pakistan&rsquo;s functions. Mr. Edward then expressed about the overview of Safe City Project Lahore. Besides, he mentioned about Smart City Services Development and IoT Services.</p>\r\n<p><br />Mr. Javed Aslam, Executive Vice President Technical PTCL, expressed his views on &lsquo;How PTCL connects us to the world?&rsquo;Mr. Amjad Hussain, Chair IEEE Lahore Section and Director FAST, presented his views on technology enhancements and communication development. Mr. Fysal Gill, Head SpeedCast (Central &amp; South Asia), talked about the topics like GPRS, Technology and Satellite Systems. Mr. Sajjad Kirmani, CEO Infogistic, revealed his views on legacy systems, advancement in technology, cloud computing and telecom explosions in Pakistan. Mr. Moeez Ahmad Faizi, Deputy Chief Telecommunication Punjab Safe City Authority, presented safe city projects and speed connectivity.</p>\r\n<p><br />Vice Chancellor UET Lahore, Prof. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, thanked the guests and expressed about the importance of technology in today&rsquo;s world. He also gave a special mention of Huawei&rsquo;s collaborations with UET.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/World%20Telecom%20Day_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Director KICS, Prof. Waqar Mahmood, too talked about the importance of Big Data and gave a presentation on IEEE Society and KICS&rsquo; Labs. The event concluded with souvenirs&rsquo; distribution among the guests.</p>\r\n<p><br />Post the event, a panel discussion followed in which the distinguished guests and the high officials of Al-Khawarazmi Institute discussed their views on the impact of Big Data. Chair IEEE Comsoc and Manager HUTIC, Mr. Kashif Bashir elaborated the Big Data impacts on the masses and told the panel about conducting more future events of these kinds.<br /><br /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '2017-05-17', 1, 1),
(167, 2014, 'KICS Organizes National Workshop on Smart Grid', '<p>National Workshop on Smart Grid (CPD) took place at Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science on 6th May, 2017. The workshop was done in collaboration with IEEE Power &amp; Energy Society &amp; IEEEP. Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Director KICS, welcomed the guests. Dean Faculty EE UET Lahore, Dr. Suhail Aftab Qureshi delivered the introduction of the workshop. The event witnessed a number of talks on the topics of &ldquo;Existing Practices and Challenges, Energy Crisis and Remedial Measures, Smart Grids in Schneider Electric, Advanced Metering Infrastructure, Towards a Smart(er) Grid in Developing Countries and Global Energy Perspective &amp; Rationale for Regional Energy Connectivity respectively.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/collage_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid was the chief guest. The guests at the occasion, who also delivered the talks, included Mr. Nauman Zafar (Associate Professor and Director Power Cluster LUMS), Dr. Suhail Aftab Qureshi (Dean Faculty EE UET Lahore), Dr. Bilal Arif (Schneider Electric, Lahore), Engr. Dr. Rana Abdul Jabbar Khan (Chief Engineer NTDC), Engr and Salis Usman (Research Fellow SAARC Energy Centre). Other distinguished guests included Syed Muhammad Mohsin (Board Of Director NTDC &amp; CEO Hybrid Technics Private Limited), Dr. Muhammad Tahir (Director ORIC, UET Lahore) and Dr. Amjad Hussain Chair (IEEE Lahore Section and Director FAST Lahore).</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/collage_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/collage_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"277\" /></p>\r\n<p>The workshop concluded with certificates&rsquo; distributions presented to the guests and the participants.</p>', NULL, '2017-05-09', 1, 1),
(166, 2013, 'A Media Delegation from HEC Visits KICS', '<p>On 28th April, 2017, a delegation from HEC (Higher Education Commission of Pakistan) paid a visit to Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science and then entire university. The delegation consisted of media team and it was headed by the Media Director. They visited all the labs at KICS and very keenly witnessed the activities being performed over there. The delegation showed interest at the labs&rsquo; functions. The managers of the labs introduced them with the staff and showed them their labs&rsquo; functions.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/hec_02%20(1).jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"846\" height=\"574\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/hec_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/hec_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"847\" height=\"544\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%202017/hec_02%20(2).jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"848\" height=\"571\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The delegation also had a meeting with the director of KICS that happened to be very beneficial for both KICS and HEC. From there on, the delegation was taken to visit the departments of the university.</p>', NULL, '2017-05-03', 1, 1),
(165, 214, 'KICS Organizes a Workshop on Patents in Collaboration with US Consulate', '<p>KICS&rsquo; incubation lab TICK in collaboration with U.S Consulate has arranged a workshop on &lsquo;Best Practices for Intellectual Property Rights in Pakistan &amp; Patents 101&rsquo; on 26th April, 2017. It was held at Conference Room at Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science, University of Engineering and Technology Lahore. The workshop was presented by the United States renowned patent lawyer Mr. Harris Zaheer Bajwa. Mr. Bajwa has developed and defended patents for world renowned companies such as Google, AOL (America Online), Samsung, Toshiba, Fuji Electronics, Alcatel, NEC and to name a few.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2017/us%20consulate_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>The workshop was attended by the high officials of KICS. Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood welcomed the guests.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2017/us%20consulate_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>In his lecture, Mr. Bajwa revealed about the patent and its system in detail such as &lsquo;What Can You Patent?&rsquo;, &lsquo;Why Acquire Patents?&rsquo;, &lsquo;Patent Application Process&rsquo;, &lsquo;Requirements of Patents&rsquo;, &lsquo;Main Types of Utility Claims in Patent&rsquo; and &lsquo;Minimalist Strategy&rsquo;.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2017/DSC_1117.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"556\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>By the end of the workshop, the questions-answers session was conducted, which proved to be much beneficial for the attendees.</p>', NULL, '2017-04-26', 1, 1),
(164, 213, 'MIT Sloan School of Management\'s (USA) Senior Faculty Member Visits KICS UET Lahore', '<p>Mr. Imran Sayyed, who is a Global Innovation Executive and a Seasoned Entrepreneur, paid a visit to Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science, University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 24th April. He was welcomed by the Director KICS Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood, who made Mr. Sayyed visit the labs at the institute. Mr. Imran took a keen interest in the functioning of the labs and appreciated the works being done over there.</p>\r\n<p><br />In 2013, he was recognized by Computer World as one of the premier 100 IT leaders. Other distinctions include being featured in Wall Street Journal, Forbes and Harvard Business Review apart from being a keynote speaker on entrepreneurship, digital technologies and innovation.</p>\r\n<p><br />Mr. Imran is currently teaching courses on Entrepreneurship and Innovation as faculty member at the MIT Sloan School of Management. He is a graduate of Brown University and did his postgraduate work at Harvard University.</p>', NULL, '2017-04-25', 1, 1),
(184, NULL, 'National Workshop on Internet of Things', '<p>IoT Labs arranged National Workshop on Internet of Things in collaboration with Sultan Qaboos IT Chair, UET Lahore.</p>', NULL, '2017-02-27', 16, 1),
(186, 2029, 'Member Energy Sadaqat Hussain Distributes Certificates to Students in UET Lahore', '<p>KICS UET Lahore has organized the certificates&rsquo; distribution ceremony at University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 12th September 2017. The students, who passed the courses offered by NAVTTC (National Vocational and Technical Training Commission) and PSDF (Punjab Skills Development Fund), were awarded with the certificates. These courses were successfully conducted at Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) UET Lahore. The honorable guests along with Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director KICS) distributed the certificates to the successful students.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/sept17/PSDF%20Cert%20Ceremony_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>The guests&rsquo; list included Mr. Ishaq Bhatti (Managing Director Read Solar Pvt. Ltd and Chairman Solar Quality Forum), Col. Shafi Salim Niazi (Managing Director Solar Tech Pvt. Ltd), Rao Khalid A. Khan (Managing Director FSK Pvt. Ltd) and Mr. Farooq Ahmad (CEO Careerz 360).&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/sept17/PSDF%20Cert%20Ceremony_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>The guests addressed to the students and attendees of the event. They shared their valuable views and experiences to the students who were going to enter into the professional life after the successful completion of the training courses. The guests were welcomed by Director KICS UET who also delivered a comprehensive presentation on CERAD (Center for Energy Research and Development) and its functions.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/sept17/PSDF%20Cert%20Ceremony_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>Distinguished guests were conferred with the souvenirs presented by the chief guest Mr. Sadaqat Hussain Khan (Member Energy/IT Planning &amp; Development Department Govt. of the Punjab). Dr. Waqar presented the shield to Mr. Sadaqat Hussain.</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-09-14', 3, 1),
(187, 2030, 'Huawei ICT Competition to Begin in Pakistani Universities & Colleges', '<p>Huawei launched &lsquo;ICT Skill Competition 2017&rsquo; worldwide. In Pakistan, it was held in collaboration with Higher Education Commission (HEC) of Pakistan. KICS UET Lahore, a Huawei Authorized Information &amp; Network Academy (HAINA), will conduct it in Lahore in other cities of the Punjab. Top 6 students from Pakistan will go to Huawei Headquarter in China for the final round of competition. Huawei will also distribute various prizes and gifts among the winners and participating students who perform very well at the competition. Registration has started from 15th of August and will continue till 30th September 2017. From 2nd year onward students from any college or university are eligible to participate in the competition that also received large entries last year in Pakistan. In order to get registered for the competition, students can log onto Huawei ICT Academy online portal at www.huaweiacad.com</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/sept17/LCWU%2011-9-2017%20(3).jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"849\" height=\"565\" /></p>\r\n<p>HUTIC and PDC team along with Huawei staff have started conducting the workshops in different universities of Lahore in order to spread awareness for this competition. More than 30 universities will be targeted and two have so far been approached where the workshops were done quite recently.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/sept17/LCWU%2011-9-2017%20(8).jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"565\" /></p>\r\n<p>First workshop was done at Lahore College for Women University on 11th September where the professional team from HUTIC (UET Lahore) guided the students thoroughly about the competition. They delivered the introduction about the Huawei competition coupled with the guidelines for the participation. Registration demo was also delivered for the ease of the students. Registrations were also done on the spot. Following day i.e. 12th September, the team did the workshop at FAST University, where the same procedure was followed.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/sept17/FAST%20Lahore%2012-9-2017%20(2).jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"416\" /></p>\r\n<p>Schedule of the event is mentioned as under:</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&bull;Registration &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 15 Aug - 30 Sep</p>\r\n<p>&bull;Preliminary Round: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 09 Oct - 13 Oct</p>\r\n<p>&bull;Regional Final &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;25 Oct - 27 Oct</p>\r\n<p>&bull;National Final &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;05 Nov - 11 Nov</p>\r\n<p>&bull;International Final in China &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 11 Dec - 15 Dec</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/sept17/FAST%20Lahore%2012-9-2017%20(3).jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"536\" /></p>\r\n<p>A number of prizes will be distributed among the winners such as Huawei mobile phones, certificates, trophies, exam vouchers and a lot more. National level winners will be awarded with China trip.</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-09-14', 6, 1),
(188, 2031, 'HUTIC UET Team Arranges a Seminar on Huawei ICT Skill Competition 2017 at UOG Sialkot', '<p>Continuing with the series of events to spread awareness about the upcoming Huawei ICT Skill Competition 2017 among the students of the universities and colleges of the Punjab province, HUTIC KICS UET&rsquo;s team conducted a seminar in University of Gujrat (UOG) Sialkot campus on 26th September 2017. Over there, around 170 students registered in IT and CS degree programs attended this event. Mr. Fahmeed Akram (Manager Research and Training) gave the introduction of the competition and let the students know all about it in his presentation.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct_17/uog_sialkot.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"843\" height=\"453\" /></p>\r\n<p>Apart from the students, the faculty members and the high officials of the university attended the seminar as well. A big gathering was witnessed at the occasion.</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-09-27', 6, 1),
(189, 2032, 'High Officials from Pakistani Universities and Huawei Technologies Attend Seminar on Pakistan\'s Biggest Engineering Competition in UET Lahore', '<p>Lahore - September 28th, 2017: KICS (Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science) UET Lahore in collaboration with Huawei Technologies is organizing ICT Skill Competition 2017 in Pakistan. The registration process of the competition has already been started from 15th of August and will go on till 30th September 2017. In a series of seminars for the awareness of this competition and registration procedure, KICS UET&rsquo;s team has been organizing seminars in various famous universities of the Punjab region. To continue with, a seminar was held at University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 28th September 2017 where noted professors from the top universities of Pakistan such as University of Agriculture Faisalabad, University of Gujrat, UET Taxila, GIK, FAST and to name a few especially made their presence. High officials from Huawei Technologies China and Pakistan also graced the event.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct_17/Students%20at%20ICT%20Skill%20Competition%20in%20UET.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"846\" height=\"564\" /></p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, welcomed the guests and delivered a speech. He acknowledged the efforts of KICS and Huawei teams to launch this stupendous event in Pakistan.</p>\r\n<p>Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Director KICS UET, described the competition and the guidelines. He also revealed about the functions of the institute to the attendees.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct_17/ICT_comp_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Large number of students from various popular universities especially came to attend this mega event who showed their keen interest in this upcoming competition and registered. Students from the universities and colleges in the Punjab region are eligible to compete and register for this competition, which preliminary round will commence from 9th October and last till 13th October. Regional final will take place from 25th October to 27th October whereas the national level final will be conducted from 5th to 11th November, 2017. Top 6 finalists from Pakistan will be awarded with a paid trip to China by Huawei where they will compete for the final from 11th to 15th December, 2017. Students, who participate in this competition, will be awarded with many other precious prizes such as Huawei mobiles, exam vouchers and a lot more.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct_17/ICT_comp_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>The delegation was taken to UET&rsquo;s newly developed branch where Huawei&rsquo;s technical courses are conducted in Model Town Lahore.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct_17/ICT_comp_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor UET also had a personal meeting with the high officials at his office later, where he distributed the shields to the guests.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-09-29', 6, 1),
(190, 2033, 'Mehwish Nadeem from KICS UET Attends International Leadership Summit 2017 in Kuala Lumpur', '<p>Lahore - October 2nd, 2017: Mehwish Nadeem, Senior Research Officer at KICS UET Lahore, attended The 2017 IEEE Women in Engineering - International Leadership Summit (2017 IEEE-WIE ILS)&nbsp; in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia on 18th and 19th September, 2017. She was invited as a guest speaker at the conference, whose topic was Bridging Engineers in Academia and Enterprise. Mehwish was invited on behalf of IEEE Women in Engineering, where she impressed the participants with her stupendous speech.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct_17/ieee_malaysia_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"839\" height=\"451\" /></p>\r\n<p>A number of other speakers also delivered their speeches at the event, which was filled with abundance of keen attendees who took deep interest in the topics talked over there.</p>\r\n<p>Mehwish was conferred with Certificate of Appreciation presented to her by Dr. Zuhaina Zakaria (General Chair IEEE, WIE ILS 2017).</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct_17/ieee_malaysia_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"420\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-10-02', 2, 1),
(191, 2034, 'HUTIC UET team visits BZU Multan to spread awareness for Huawei ICT Skill Competition', '<p>LAHORE - On 5th October, HUTIC UET team made their way to Multan where they visited Bahauddin Zakriya University to promote and spread awareness for the upcoming Huawei ICT Skill Competition 2017. The team has been promoting the competition since quite some time in a number of universities in the region of Punjab. A special big event was also organized in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 28th September where Huawei officials and universities&rsquo; professors from all over Pakistan took special part.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct_17/bzu_visit.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"475\" /></p>\r\n<p>Mr. Fahmeed Akram from HUTIC team very comprehensively revealed the competition and told the students &lsquo;how to register&rsquo; for the competition. More than 100 students attended the event where they were also told about the Huawei certifications being done at UET Lahore. The regional final of the competition will be held on 25th to 27th October whereas the national final to be held from 5th November to 11th November 2017. International final will be held in China from 11th to 15th December 2017. The national level winners will be awarded with a free trip to China to contest for the final.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct_17/bzu_visit_01.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"475\" /></p>\r\n<p>In order to commence Huawei and CISCO training courses at BZU Multan premises, a meeting with high officials of BZU was also arranged.</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-10-06', 6, 1);
INSERT INTO `star_news` (`news_id`, `order`, `news_des`, `news_detail`, `newsthumb`, `news_stamp`, `group_id`, `active`) VALUES
(192, 2038, 'KICS UET Conducts 3rd international workshop on pattern recognition applications', '<p>LAHORE &ndash; 11th October, 2017 (KICS, UET): 3rd International Workshop on Pattern Recognition Applications has been organized by Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 11th October. DAAD (The German Academic Exchange Service) from Germany sponsored this international conference. Prominent professors from the famous universities of Europe (Germany and Switzerland) and Pakistan have come to attend it. Students from UET Lahore and other universities too became the part of this mega event.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct_17/collage_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid was the chief guest. He, in his address, said that the conferences of these kinds play a vital role in spreading awareness among the learners and the students. He appreciated the efforts made by KICS to conduct this international conference in UET. Prof. Fazal Khalid then urged the organizers to continue conducting the events like this in future.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Director KICS, delivered a welcome note and revealed about the conference and its purpose in general. Dr. Sheikh Faisal Rashid, Assistant Professor UET Lahore who organized this event thoroughly, gave conference introduction and schedule.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct_17/collage_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Keynote speech was delivered by Dr. Karsten Berns (Head of Robotics Research Lab) from department of computer science university of Kaiserslautern, Germany.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Dr. Sheikh Faisal Rashid, Assistant Professor UET Lahore, gave an introductory note. The conference witnessed a number of valuable and informatively rich presentations from the professors on the topics such as recognition of people and objects around commercial vehicles, deep learning and its applications, multi-modal photo-graphics retrieval, medical and health informatics, text-to-speech for Urdu: understanding intonation and to name a few. Large number of attendees was witnessed at the occasion. The universities, which professors, delivered their presentations at the conference included University of Kaiserslautern Germany, University of Fribourg Switzerland, University of Applied Sciences Germany, NUST Islamabad and University of Central Punjab Lahore apart from UET. The professors, who delivered the presentations, included Dr. Marcus Liwicki, Dr. Adrian Ulges, Dr. Ulrich Swanchecke, Dr. Muhammad Shahbaz and others.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/oct_17/collage_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor UET distributed the shields to the guests and certificates among the participants of the conference in closing ceremony.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-10-11', 25, 1),
(193, 2036, 'KICS UET Lahore and Cybex School of IT Professionals Sign an Agreement for Professional Trainings', '<p>KICS UET Lahore (10th November, 2017) - Al-Khawarzmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore and Cybex School of IT Professionals, Faisalabad have inked an agreement to conduct network/datacom trainings on 9th November 2017. The agreement was signed by Director KICS, Dr. Waqar Mahmood and CEO Cybex Mr. Muhammad Aftab Ur Rehman. The MOU signing ceremony was held at Professional Development Center (PDC), Model Town, Lahore &ndash; a professional training center of UET Lahore. High officials of both parties attended this ceremony.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/nov_17/Kics+cybex%20FSD.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"841\" height=\"511\" /></p>\r\n<p>In the light of this agreement, KICS UET will be responsible for providing professional trainings to the students at Cybex School of IT Professionals in Faisalabad, whereas Cybex is responsible for providing training facilities coupled with marketing and promotions of the training courses in Faisalabad region.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/nov_17/Kics+cybex%20FSD_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"841\" height=\"559\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery//news/nov_17/Kics+cybex%20FSD_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"841\" height=\"559\" /></p>\r\n<p>The trainings are set to begin very soon and the teams of both the institutes will begin working on it within a short time.</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-11-10', 6, 1),
(194, 2037, 'Top Pakistani Universities’ Students Participate in the National Final Round of Huawei ICT Skill Competition at UET Lahore', '<p>KICS UET LAHORE &ndash; 9th November, 2017: National final round of Huawei ICT Skill Competition 2017, which is a joint collaboration of KICS (Al-Khawarzmi Institute of Computer Science) University of Engineering and Technology Lahore and Huawei Technologies, was held at KICS UET Lahore on 9th November 2017. Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director KICS) inaugurated the national final round along with Mr. Shahzad Akbar from Huawei Technologies. UET officials along with numerous university students also attended the event and showed their curiosity and interest to the competition. Dr. Waqar appreciated the efforts of the team and mentioned the events of these types, which enhance the intelligence level of the students, could be very beneficial for the mental as well as the educational development of the students. He urged that these kinds of events had to be promoted.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/nov_17/ICT_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>50 winners participated in this final national round. They were chosen from the universities such as COMSATS, Lahore Garrison University, University of South Asia, University of Management Technology, University of Gurjrat, Bahauddin Zakriya University, University of Sargodha, Lahore College Women University, Kinnaird College, Lahore Leads University, etc. The participating fifty students were conferred with various prestigious prizes after the competition.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>In order to spread awareness for the competition and select the winners of the competition, the expert team of HUTIC (Huawei UET Telecom and IT Center) visited the universities of Pakistan. More than 4000 students participated in the competition. Out of them, 50 top students were chosen who now participated in this national final round at UET Lahore.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/nov_17/ICT_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"839\" height=\"629\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/nov_17/ICT_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"839\" height=\"629\" /></p>\r\n<p>6 students will now be selected from these 50 contestants who participated in this national final round. These six will be awarded with paid trip to Huawei Headquarters in China for international final to be held from 11th to 15th December, 2017.&nbsp; The winners of the international final will be given big cash prizes together with many other precious prizes such as Huawei cell phones, gifts and a lot more.</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-11-09', 6, 1),
(195, 2039, '“Smart Classroom” to set up in UET Lahore in Collaboration with Southern University of Science and Weidong Cloud Education Group of China', '<p>UET Lahore (11th November 2017) &ndash; An agreement was inked among University of Engineering and Technology Lahore, Southern University of Science and Technology (International Center for Higher Education Innovation under the auspices of UNESCO Shenzhen, China) and Weidong Cloud Education Group, China to set up &lsquo;Smart Classroom&rsquo; in UET Lahore. This strategic collaboration was taken place at Vice Chancellor&rsquo;s office in UET, where the high officials from all parties attended the MOU signing ceremony particularly Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid (Vice Chancellor UET Lahore), Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director Al-Khawarzmi Institute of Computer Science), Mr. Wang Duanrui (CEO Weidong Cloud) among others present at the occasion.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/nov_17/Smartclassroom_MOU_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"836\" height=\"428\" /></p>\r\n<p>Southern University and Weidong Cloud Group will finance this project that is going to be built in UET Lahore&rsquo;s premises.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/nov_17/Smartclassroom_MOU_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"836\" height=\"548\" /></p>\r\n<p>Prior to the agreement signing ceremony, Dr. Waqar gave a brief presentation about the agreement and briefed the attendees about this to be joint collaboration. The ceremony was headed by Vice Chancellor Prof. Dr. Fazal.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/nov_17/Smartclassroom_MOU_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"834\" height=\"554\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>MOU was signed by VC UET Lahore Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid and CEO Weidong Cloud Mr. Wang Duanrui in presence of all the attendees. By the end of the ceremony Mr. Wang was presented a special souvenir by VC UET, who in return presented a special gift to him. Vice Chancellor then conferred the other Chinese guests with special souvenirs. Mr. Wang also presented a gift to Dr. Waqar Mahmood and more gifts to the attendees of the ceremony. The ceremony concluded on a special note exchanged by the parties.&nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-11-11', 6, 1),
(196, 12000, 'Two-Day international energy conference ends in Flattei’s hotel – Rana Mashood and Ch Sher Ali attend', '<p><iframe src=\"https://uetlahore.pixieset.com/icece2017/\" frameborder=\"0\" scrolling=\"no\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\"></iframe>LAHORE (23 rd November, 2017) The closing ceremony of UET Lahore and FSK (Pvt) Ltd&rsquo;s joint venture &ndash; ICECE 2017, the international conference on energy conservation, took place at Flattei&rsquo;s hotel Lahore on 23 rd November where the chief guest was Rana Mashood Ahmad Khan (education minister Punjab) and the guest of honor was Ch. Sher Ali, provincial minister for energy. Other distinguished guests included Muhammad Hamid Shwehdi (King Fahad University Saudi Arabia), Ms. Maha Kamal (Queen Marry University London), Dr. M. Akbar Hussain (Aalborg University Denmark) and Prof. Nizhie Ayas from Turkey). Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid (Vice Chancellor University of Engineering and Technology Lahore)), Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director CERAD UET) and Mr. Rao Ahmad Khalid (MD FSK Pvt Ltd) also attended the ceremony.</p>\r\n<p>26 countries participated in this international energy conference and from 13 countries, the invited speakers came to attend it. The conference featured technical talks, presentations and panel discussions on the topic of energy and conservation. Leading industries of the country placed their stalls in the industrial exhibition which was the part of this conference.</p>\r\n<p>Rana Mashood Khan, in his speech, said that overcoming on the energy crisis was the utmost need, and arranging the energy conference was required. He appreciated the efforts of the UET and FSK to conduct this international conference. He also mentioned that the government had started a number of projects to overcome energy crisis together with academia. Mashood also mentioned &ldquo;He is giving surety on behalf of chief minister Shahbaz Sharif that the government will support fully in energy crisis if the institutions and UET are willing to work together to overcome this crisis.&rdquo;</p>\r\n<p>Ch. Sher Ali said that Pakistan was suffering the energy crisis a lot. He mentioned that government had become enable to overcome this crisis. Sher Ali revealed that the government had started LNG projects which will help overcome the problems of energy in the country. He talked about the solar projects launched in Bahawalpur and in other parts of the region. He said that the government had started using the solar energy in schools, universities and offices to help conserve the energy.</p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor UET Prof Fazal Ahmad Khalid shared his views on energy crisis and energy conservation.</p>\r\n<p>Dr. Waqar Mahmood gave an overview of this two-day energy conference and also told about the technical talks done at the conference during the conference. He thanked the chief guests and the invited speakers who came from all over the world to attend the conference.</p>\r\n<p>FSK Pvt Ltd&rsquo;s Managing Director shared his views on the energy crisis in the country and also thanked the chief guests. Other honorable international guests too shared their views on the conference.</p>\r\n<p>Education minister Punjab Rana Mashood and Energy minister Punjab Ch. Sher Ali presented the souvenirs and shields to the guests, industry personnel and the organizers of the event. Vice Chancellor presented the souvenirs to Rana Mashood and Ch. Sher Ali.</p>', NULL, '2017-11-23', 2, 1),
(197, NULL, 'Free Training Courses offered by KICS UET Lahore', '<h2><img src=\"http://kics.edu.pk/doc/ad.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" /></h2>\r\n<h2><strong><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" title=\"Download Form\" href=\"http://kics.edu.pk/doc/Form1_final.pdf\" target=\"_self\">Download Form</a></strong></h2>\r\n<h2><strong>Course Content </strong></h2>\r\n<table class=\"table\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"654\">\r\n<h2><strong> Solor Photovoltaic Installation and Pumping Training </strong></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Solar system designing</li>\r\n<li>Solar system installation</li>\r\n<li>Solar system troubleshooting</li>\r\n<li>Solar tube well system</li>\r\n<li>Solar Drip irrigation</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', NULL, '2017-11-29', 3, 1),
(204, NULL, 'Rana Mashhood Khan Attends Huawei Education Summit 2018 at Flattei’s Hotel Lahore', '<p>LAHORE &ndash; 3rd January, 2018 - Minister for School Education Rana Mashhood Ahmad Khan along with Chairman Higher Education Commission Dr. Mukhtar Ahmad attended Huawei Education Summit 2018 conducted at Flattei&rsquo;s Hotel Lahore on 3rd January 2018. Vice Chancellor UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid and Director Al-Khawarzmi Institute of Computer Science UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood were also present at the occasion.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Since Education plays an integral role in maintaining and developing success for any nation and without ICT (Information and Communications Technology) in education the concept of education is simply incomplete, Huawei Technologies took the initiative to launch the education summit where the global trends in education and the importance of education were discussed.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/husummit_featured.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"563\" /></p>\r\n<p>Government dignitaries from the field of education and the representatives from universities, colleges and schools participated and shared ideas among each other.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>In the end, Rana Mashhood distributed the shields among the guests.</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-01-03', 6, 1),
(198, 12001, 'IoT Research and Innovation Lab (IRIL) journal paper is accepted in Elsevier Future Generation Computer Systems Journal.', '<p>Our IoT Research and Innovation Lab (IRIL) journal paper is accepted in Elsevier Future Generation Computer Systems Journal. The paper is co-authored by Bilal Afzal, Muhammad Umair, Dr. Ghalib from KICS and Dr. Ejaz from University of Malaya.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Paper Title:</strong>&nbsp; Enabling IoT Platforms for Social IoT Applications: Vision, Feature Mapping, and Challenges</p>\r\n<p><strong>Journal:</strong> Elsevier Future Generation Computer Systems&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Impact Factor:</strong> 3.997,&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <strong>5-Year Impact Factor:</strong> 4.78</p>\r\n<p>The paper can be cited as: </p>\r\n<p>Bilal Afzal, Muhammad Umair, Ghalib A. Shah, Ejaz Ahmed., Enabling IoT Platforms for Social IoT Applications: Vision, Feature Mapping, and Challenges; Elsevier Future Generation Computer Systems, in press, 2017.</p>', NULL, '2017-12-07', 16, 1),
(199, 2040, '3 Day International Technical Conference (11th IEEE ICOSST 2017) and Industrial Exhibition Inaugurated in UET Lahore', '<p>LAHORE (18th December, 2017) - The opening ceremony of the international conference on open source systems and technologies titled 11th IEEE ICOSST 2017 took place in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 18th December, 2017. The chief guest of the occasion was Vice Chancellor UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid and Mr. Haroon Inam (CCTO, Smart Wires, USA), who inaugurated the conference and industrial exhibition. This is an annual event which is conducted by UET Lahore every year and carries unique theme. This year&rsquo;s theme is &lsquo;Open AI&rsquo; which highlights the seriousness and business-viability that the wired and mobile community has begun to attribute towards open source software (OSS). It is the 11th season of ICOSST (International Conference on Open Source Systems and Technologies) co-organized by Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) UET and IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers) Computer Society Lahore Section.</p>\r\n<p>The conference started with the welcome notes delivered by Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid (VC UET and Conference Convener), Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director KICS UET and Conference General Chair), Dr. Ghalib Assadullah Shah (Conference Technical Chair) and Dr. Amir Mahmood (Conference Co. Chair) respectively.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The ceremony concluded with plaques distribution conferred to the guests of the occasion done by the honorable guests &ndash; Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid and Haroon Inam. Vice Chancellor also presented the shield to Haroon Inam as a token of respect.</p>\r\n<p>This 11th season of conference will last till 20th December and is set to generate a scientific venue where the participants are able to exchange ideas, strategies and policies for tackling the development, research and adaptation challenges related to open-source tools and open-source development environments for the customized and enterprise grade applications in the IEEE Region R10. The conference is equipped with technical workshops, invited talks and panel discussions on the said subject and the relevant topics.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The distinguished speakers from all over the world have been taken on board to deliver technical presentations such as from American University in Emirates, Umm Ul Qura University Saudi Arabia, University of California USA, University of Oklahoma USA, IBM USA and to name a few. There would also be technical talks from the invited speakers from leading Pakistani universities such as LUMS, ITU, NUST, IBM Karachi, UET (Lahore and Peshawar) and FAST.</p>\r\n<p>Leading industries of Pakistan too is participating in this technical conference by taking part in industry demos, roundtables and exhibition. The likes of Crescent Group, Huawei Technologies, APTECH, COMSATS, Innova Networks, Autosoft Dynamics, Northbay Solutions, LUMS, LSE, UET and a number of IoT (Internet of Things) companies are participating.</p>\r\n<p>A roundtable conference was held at Vice Chancellor&rsquo;s office later, where all leading industrialists participated and presented their views. An MOU was also signed between KICS UET and FSK Pvt Ltd at the conference.&nbsp; The delegation visited the stalls of the exhibition where they very keenly observed the products displayed there.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The conference is targeted to attract a diverse audience of open source researchers and practitioners from academia, industry, and public administration.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-12-18', 3, 1),
(200, 2041, 'Speaker Punjab Assembly Rana Iqbal Khan Attends the Closing Ceremony of UET’s 3-Day International Conference cum Industrial Exhibition', '<p>Lahore (20th December, 2017) &ndash; Speaker Punjab Assembly Rana Iqbal Khan attended the closing ceremony of UET Lahore&rsquo;s 11th Annual IEEE ICOSST 2017 taken place at the main auditorium of the University of Engineering and Technology Lahore. The 3-day conference was an utter colorful mega event where industrial exhibition was conducted and world universities&rsquo; delegation attended and delivered presentations on the theme of &lsquo;Open AI&rsquo;. It was a joint collaboration of Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) UET and IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers) Computer Society Lahore Section. Pakistan&rsquo;s leading industries such as Nestle, Unilever Pakistan, Aptech, Autosoft, etc placed their stalls at the exhibition, which were liked by the guests and the masses who took deep interest in their products. Research papers from more than 40 countries were presented at the conference whereas 12 countries&rsquo; delegation attended this mega annual conference of UET Lahore.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2017/dec/icosst44.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"748\" height=\"500\" /></p>\r\n<p>Addressing the attendance, the chief guest Rana Iqbal Khan said, &ldquo;Technology was the need of the hour. The world has progressed in a manner that now the machines does the work which human mind thinks of. It is the reflection of human behavior. Further he said that &ldquo;Open AI is a modern technology that one can see it everywhere such as the likes of Google, Facebook and other giants of technology have started working on this technology. Smart phones&rsquo; applications are working on this technology as well.&rdquo;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2017/dec/icosst55.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"748\" height=\"500\" /></p>\r\n<p>The ceremony started with the welcome notes delivered by Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid (VC UET and Conference Convener) and Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director KICS UET and Conference General Chair).</p>\r\n<p>Other distinguished guests such as Jibran Khalid (Vice President I2C Corporation) and Prof Adeil Khaleifi (Dean American University of Emirates) too delivered the speeches on the theme of Open AI.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://uet.edu.pk/newsannouncement/newssection/images/2017/dec/icosst66.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"748\" height=\"500\" /></p>\r\n<p>The ceremony concluded with shields&rsquo; distribution conferred to the guests and the organizers of the event by Rana Iqbal Khan. Vice Chancellor also presented the shield to the Speaker Punjab Assembly as a token of respect.</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-12-20', 3, 1),
(201, 2042, 'KICS UET and FSK (Pvt.) Ltd Sign an MOU for Research Activities', '<p>LAHORE &ndash; 20th December 2017 - An MOU was signed between KICS (Al-Khwarazmi Institute of Computer Science) University of Engineering and Technology Lahore and FSK (Pvt.) Ltd on December 15th 2017. In the light of this agreement, both parties will work mutually and collaboratively in the field of research. The MOU was signed by Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director KICS) and Mr. Salim Hassan (CEO, FSK). Both parties inked the deal at KICS&rsquo; mega annual event of ICOSST 2017 in the presence of Vice Chancellor of UET Lahore.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/MOU-FSK%20and%20KICS.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"564\" /></p>', NULL, '2017-12-20', 3, 1),
(202, 2043, 'CERAD UET Lahore and UPCASE UET Peshawar Agree to Work Together in Energy Sector', '<p>LAHORE &ndash; 2nd January 2018 - A Memorandum of Understanding was signed between Centre for Energy Research and Development (CERAD), University of Engineering and Technology Lahore and US Pakistan Centre for Advanced Studies in Energy UPCASE-E University of Engineering and Technology Peshawar. The agreement was inked to enhance the research and development activities collaboratively in the field of energy sector. It was signed by Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director, CERAD UET Lahore) and Dr. Najab Ullah (Deputy Director UPCASE, UET Peshawar).</p>', NULL, '2018-01-02', 3, 1),
(203, 2044, 'Solar Shaheen Wins KICS Super Sixes 2017', '<p>The second season of KICS UET&rsquo;s Super Sixes Tournament 2017 recently winded up at Junaid Jamshed Stadium in University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore. Six teams participated in this lively and fun-rich tournament attended massively by the students of the university. Solar Shaheen won the tournament beating Android Qalandars. The final was played on 28th December 2017. Results of Semi Finals and previous matches of the tournament are as follows:</p>\r\n<p><strong>Semi Finals:</strong></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <strong>Winner</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Match 1 (12:30PM):Web Night RidersVsAndroid QalandarsAndroid Qalandars</p>\r\n<p>Match 2 (01:15PM):Solar 1 (shaheen)VsSolar 3 (J7 Tigers)Solar 1 (shaheen)</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div><strong>Final:</strong></div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;<img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/super_sixes_2017.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"847\" height=\"635\" /> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Winner</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Solar 1 (Shaheen) VsAndroid QalandarsSolar 1 (Shaheen)</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Previous Matches Results:</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/super_sixes_2017_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"847\" height=\"635\" /></strong></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Winner</strong></p>\r\n<p>Match 1:Web Night RidersVsZalmi Eleven&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Web Night Riders</p>\r\n<p>Match 3:Zalmi Eleven&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; VsSolar 3 (J7 Tigers)Solar 3 (J7 tigers)</p>\r\n<p>Match 5:Web Night RidersVsSolar 3 (J7 Tigers)Web Night Riders</p>\r\n<p>Match 2:Solar 1 (shaheen)VsAndroid QalandarsSolar 1 (Shaheen)</p>\r\n<p>Match 4:Solar 2 (W4 06)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; VsSolar 1 (shaheen)Solar 1 (shaheen)</p>\r\n<p>Match 6:Android QalandarsVsSolar 2 (W4 06)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Android Qalandars&nbsp;</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-01-01', 3, 1),
(205, NULL, 'KICS UET and APTECH Computer Sign an Agreement to Deliver Professional Trainings', '<p>LAHORE &ndash; 8th January 2018 - KICS (Al-Khwarazmi Institute of Computer Science) University of Engineering and Technology Lahore and APTECH Computer Education have inked an agreement to conduct professional trainings. It was signed on 5th January 2018 by Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director KICS) and Mr. Javed Iqbal (Country Manager, APTECH) in the presence of the key personnel of both parties. The trainings will be conducted at UET Lahore by the highly trained instructor of the university. The parties also agreed to do more future ventures.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/KICS-APTECH%20Agreement.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"536\" /></p>', NULL, '2018-01-08', 17, 1),
(206, NULL, 'One Day Workshop on Communication Trends Conducted in KICS UET Lahore', '<p>LAHORE &ndash; 15th December 2017 - Al-Khawarizmi institute of Computer Science UET Lahore and IEEE COMSOC Lahore Section arranged a one day workshop on communication trends on 15th December 2017. UET students, KICS officials and a delegation from COMSAT Sahiwal accompanied by its final year students attended it. The delegation was welcomed by Director KICS Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood and Chair COMSOC Lahore Section Kashif Bashir.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>7 Sessions were conducted at the workshop and the delegation was taken on a visit to Huawei UET joint Telecom and IT Center (HUTIC) later. The participants of the workshop were also presented an introductory video of KICS UET. Kashif Bashir presented the opportunities at IEEE and COMSOC. Wireless Sensor Newtworks&rsquo; topic was discussed by Mr. Hammad Hassan (Manager NWN Lab, KICS).&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Dawer Saeed from SSR Lab of KICS UET talked about Market Oriented Final Year Projects. From Huawei Lab of KICS UET, Hafiz Tayyab presented Overview of Telecommunication Technology. The topic of cyber security and how to avoid them was discussed by Ahmed from HUTIC. Few other topics were also discussed such as Shahid Zulfiqar from KICS described the students about writing a good resume. He also shared the IEEE Resume Lab tool with the participants.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/workshop_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2017-12-15', 6, 1),
(207, NULL, 'Kashif Bashir from KICS UET Presents Research Activities at RCCC Globecom 2017 Singapore', '<p>LAHORE &ndash; 9th January 2018 - IEEE Communication Society Asia Pacific Regional Chapter Chair Congress (RCCC) took place at IEEE Globecom 2017 at Marina Bay Sands Convention Center Singapore in December 2017. The purpose of RCCC is to facilitate and encourage sharing, feedback, and networking among Chapter Chairs, staff, and ComSoc officers. The Chapter Chairs were from the countries like USA, Australia, Japan, South Korea, Malaysia, Singapore, Hong Kong, China, India, and Pakistan. A[art from Chapter Chair Meeting, there was a COMSOC board committee meeting as well.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Kashif Bashir Chair IEEE Comsoc Lahore Chapter from Al-Khawarizmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) UET Lahore represented Pakistan in this meeting. He delivered a presentation on the year 2017&rsquo;s research activities taken place in different universities of Pakistan. Bashir especially mentioned Asia Pacific IEEE COMSOC Summer School 2017, World Telecom Day 2017, All Pakistan Congress PSYWC 2017, Awards and Publications by COMSOC Lahore Chapter in his talk. The audience appreciated the work done by Kashif Bashir in Pakistan.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Kashif Bashir Chair IEEE Comsoc Lahore Chapter from KICS UET Lahore signed two MOUs at the event &ndash; with Prof. Dr. Lianfeng Shen (South East University of China) and with Prof. Dr. Pingzi (Fan Southwest Jiatong University China).&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/globecom%202017_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-01-09', 6, 1),
(208, NULL, 'KICS UET\'s Officials Make Pakistan Proud in China', '<p>LAHORE (15th January 2018) - The final of Huawei ICT Skill Competition 2017 was conducted in Huawei Headquarters in Shenzen, China where 39 students from 10 different countries participated and these students were grouped into 13. 6 students, who won the national final in Pakistan, represented the country at the final and they were grouped into 2. Among 7000 students from 22 universities and colleges, these 6 students were chosen who bagged the national level contest of Huawei. 3 out of 6 were from University of Engineering and Technology Lahore, whereas the rest of three were from NUST, Lahore Garrison University and Virtual University. The six students included Ayyaz Ahmad (UET Lahore), Muhammad Zubair (UET Lahore), Fatima Rashid Butt (UET Lahore), Malik Noor Muhammad (NUST), Shariq Malik (LGU) and Shamim Iqbal (Virtual University).&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/collageict%20china_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"563\" /></p>\r\n<p>Thirteen teams (groups) fought for the final and Pakistani teams performed brilliantly and secured second prize. Lebanon team won the first prize whereas the third prize was secured jointly by Bahrain, Jordan and Oman. Excellent Tutor and Excellent Academy Awards were also distributed among six tutors and academic institutions from Middle East region. UET Lahore&rsquo;s tutor Fahmeed Akram was awarded with the first position.&nbsp; These UETIANs (Ayyaz, Muhammad Zubair and Fahmeed Akram) also work for KICS (Al-Khawarzmi Institute of Computer Science), UET Lahore.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/ict%20china_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/ict%20china_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Senior representatives from participating countries&rsquo; embassies and consulates attended the award ceremony, in addition to other high-ranking government officials which included Mr. Ding Lianpu, Director of the Center for China-Foreign People-to-People Exchanges in China&rsquo;s Ministry of Education, Professor Zhao Jianhua, Deputy Director for the International Center for Higher Education Innovation at UNESCO, Ms. Chen Lifang, Corporate Senior Vice President of Huawei Technologies, and Mr. Simon Lacey, Vice President of Huawei Global Government Affairs Department, and Mr. Charles Yang, President of Huawei Middle East.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/ict%20china_04.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"563\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-01-15', 6, 1),
(209, NULL, 'KICS UET’s TICK and Careem Sign an Agreement ', '<p>LAHORE &ndash; 19th January 2018 - TICK (KICS UET Lahore&rsquo;s Lab) and Careem have signed an agreement to support UET&rsquo;s campus based entrepreneurial ecosystem. MOU was signed by the officials of both sides during a ceremony recently.&nbsp; Careem is a Dubai based transportation company that operates in 53 cities of Middle East. It also operates its business in Pakistan.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/MOU_signing_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"474\" /></p>', NULL, '2018-01-19', 15, 1),
(210, NULL, 'Foreign Delegation from Japan Attends Virtual Reality Workshop in UET Lahore', '<p>LAHORE (25th January 2018) - A one of its kind workshop on virtual reality and industry took place in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 24th January 2018. It was arranged by Al-Khawarzmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) UET. A Japanese delegation from STYLY Japan consisting of the high officials of the company &ndash; Nausharwan Mir (Head of Global Affairs/Chief Alliance Officer, STYLY), Michael Waite (Global Manager, STYLY), Sajid Khan (Global Manager, STYLY) and Sayaka Sagawara (Assistant Global Manager, STYLY) attended it and delivered presentations on the subject matter.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Director KICS UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood inaugurated the event and welcomed the guests. A large number of students attended this mega workshop, which subject appealed to everyone.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/VR_featured_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"412\" /></p>\r\n<p>Dr. Waqar, in his address to the attendees, briefed about the virtual reality and told the students how important it was for them and for the upcoming days. He also revealed the career prospects, which the students could relish with this education of VR. He emphasized on the importance of technology.</p>\r\n<p>Nausharwan Mir (Head of Global Affairs, STYLY) decompressed the big opportunities one could have by using virtual reality, which was fast increasing and developing in the world. &ldquo;Biggies like Google, Facebook, Amazon and YouTube are using this technology, thus one can expect how big career movements can be in ahead if succeeded in this technology&rdquo; &ndash; this is what was revealed over there. Mir also told the students to contact him directly for their projects on the subject. He offered the students paid internships in Japan and Pakistan. Besides he offered the jobs at STYLY Japan to the most intelligent students whose projects or creations the company passed.</p>\r\n<p>Michael Waite, who is the Global Manager of STYLY), expressed about the number of users of virtual reality and told how increasingly it was soaring high in the entire world. He mentioned Pakistan and India being the largest populated countries could be the biggest users of VR in near future. He also unzipped the difference between Augmented Reality (AR) and Virtual Reality (VR). Waite gave the examples of Instagram and Snapchat as to how they were using this technology by changing the faces of the people.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Global Manager STYLY, Sajid Khan, delivered the revenue figures of VR and its growth. It started working in 2016, when its revenue was 1.8 billion dollars and the estimated figure in 2020 could shoot to 37.7 billion dollars. He also depicted its use in daily life in entertainment (games, movies and live events). Khan then described how it could be used in virtual travel, education, employees training, healthcare, shopping, business meetings, socializing with friends and so on.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>A contest was also revealed at the workshop in which students could participate. It was told that the winners of the students would be awarded with a paid trip to Japan and a job at STYLY Japan. The winning amount of the contest is upto one crore rupees, which will be distributed among the lucky winners.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Dr. Waqar, at the end of the event, distributed the shields among the guests.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/Jan_18/VR_featured.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-01-25', 3, 1),
(211, NULL, 'IEEE Lahore Section’s AGM and Golden Jubilee Held at UET Lahore', '<p>LAHORE (31-01-2018) IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers) Lahore Section Annual General Meeting was held in University of Engineering and Technology Lahore. It was organized by Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science and attended by the senior technical experts from academia and industry including the CEOs, CFOs and Directors of the Universities and Institutes respectively.&nbsp; It is the 50th year of excellence of IEEE Lahore Section in Pakistan and at the AGM the golden jubilee was also celebrated. This event returned to UET Lahore after the hiatus of 20 years. Vice Chancellor UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid and Director KICS Dr. Waqar Mahmood chaired the meeting.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_18/ieee_agm_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></p>\r\n<p>Dr. Syed Zahoor Hassan (former Vice Chancellor LUMS) presented his keynote speech. The members of this annual general meeting discussed the betterment of the country in terms of technology and took initiatives in this regard. Other topics such as Robotics, Power and Energy, Control System and Communication were also discussed in detail. Dr. Amjad Hussain (Director FAST) and Dr. Shafay Shamail delivered their views very comprehensively on subject matter.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>IEEE Lahore section is very active in helping the students and the researchers. It strengthens the linkage between the industry and academia. Researchers and professionals are thoroughly helped at local and international level in their respective researches.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_18/ieee_agm_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>The event concluded with the awards&rsquo; ceremony where IEEE national awards were presented to the students and members.</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-01-31', 2, 1),
(212, NULL, 'IEEE 5G and IoT Summit on Future Trends 2018 to Be Held in KICS on 23rd February', '<p>KICS UET Lahore is going to conduct a mega one-day event titled IEEE 5G and IoT Summit on Future Trends 2018, which is unique in its kind and will be much beneficial as well as informative for those seeking knowledge on the boosting technology of 5G.&nbsp; It is the era of technology and technological advancements and the communication technology is fast turning towards 5G, promising to support 1000 times more data at 100 times more speed. Thus a deep research is required within academia and industry. In order to generate a through awareness among the students and professionals, this colossal event has been arranged at Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science in UET Lahore on 23rd February, where the speakers will confer the participants with true insight into current research dimensions in different layers of 5G.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_18/Flyer_5G%20&amp;%20IoT%20Summit-page-001.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"843\" height=\"1193\" /></p>\r\n<p>Registrations are open and being done on first come first serve basis. The deadline for the registration is 20th February. Rush your entries now. More details about the event and contact personnel can be found in the attached images. Registration process is also mentioned in the image. In order to be laced with complete details, you may visit the website at <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/ieee5giot/%20\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.kics.edu.pk/ieee5giot/&nbsp;</a></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;<img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_18/Schedule_5G%20&amp;%20IoT%20Summit-page-001.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"1089\" /></div>', NULL, '2018-02-14', 16, 1),
(213, NULL, 'NWN (KICS UET) and Safe City Authority (SCA) Lahore, Mutually Work for City-Wide Audio Surveillance ', '<p>Al-Khawarzmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS)&rsquo;s research lab NWNL (Next Generation Wireless Networks Lab) and Safe City Authority (SCA) have signed an agreement in November 2017 for providing the research-based acoustic surveillance solution at the camera sites in Lahore city.&nbsp; Under this agreement, our lab has committed a complete solution to SCA for providing audio surveillance enabled with the desired features for acoustic evidence collection at each camera location. Therefore, we have manufactured the IP65 compliance product (GSF-1) as per the specification criteria met Huawei Technologies.&nbsp; Our low powered environment-friendly product is easily integrable with the existing camera and network architecture.&nbsp; The complete solution based on the &ldquo;hardware and the Software&rdquo; will be integrated at 300 camera sites of SCA Lahore and it will be functional to monitor the incidents in real time environment of Lahore City.</p>\r\n<p>The customized solution uses the triangulation with the help of acoustic sensors to identify the exact location of the source which has to be communicated as an event at the command and control center (PPCI3) managed at SCA.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Our solution will add the following functionalities into the existing surveillance system at PPCI3:</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Continuous audio streaming from 300 camera sites.</p>\r\n<p>Web-based monitoring and hardware configurations.</p>\r\n<p>Remotely controlled surveillance with auto gain adjustment, microphone enabling/disabling and acoustic event data capturing functionality.</p>\r\n<p>Human speech reorganization in the real-time noisy environment for evidence collection.</p>\r\n<p>Audio data profiling for real-time event data.</p>\r\n<p>Gun-shot detection and source localization.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>It is the first commercial project of NWN (KICS UET). Earlier it has done numerous research projects such as multiple sensing enabled real-time intelligent wireless camera networks for secure spaces (ICT R&amp;D Fund), cluster head selection and optimization, extending Rescue 1122 through new and emerging technologies and to name a few. The lab aims to provide commercial and non-commercial solutions in the field of computer networks, excess networks, source localization, node calibration, intelligent security, and surveillance.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-02-19', 5, 1),
(214, NULL, 'CLE (KICS) and Lahore Grammar School Sign an Agreement to Use Speech Files', '<p>CLE (Centre for Language Engineering) and Lahore Grammar School, Johar Town, Lahore signed a License Agreement to use Urdu speech files synthesised by CLE Urdu TTS , on February 9, 2018.&nbsp; This agreement enables the school to integrate Urdu speech files with an RFID based student identity card solution being used at school dismissal time.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_18/CLE_kics.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"475\" /></p>', NULL, '2018-02-15', 10, 1),
(215, NULL, 'HUTIC Instructor Roped in for Training for HAINA TTT Program', '<p>LAHORE (21st February 2018) - Fahmeed Akram, Manager Research and KICS and HUTIC, has been chosen for conducting the training for the HAINA TTT (Train the Trainer Training) program at Higher Education Commission in Islamabad. This is the second batch for this training, which commenced on February 6th at R &amp; D Center at HEC Office. It will continue till two weeks. TTT session has been designed for the nominated trainers from each HAINA awarded university.</p>\r\n<p>Huawei Authorized Information and Network Academy (HAINA) is a global education program launched in Pakistan last year under the MOU signed between Higher Education Pakistan and Huawei Technologies to boost up the R &amp; D facilities in Pakistan.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_18/HAINA%20TTT%20Program_HEC.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"634\" /></p>', NULL, '2018-02-21', 6, 1),
(216, NULL, 'UET Launches Its First Web TV ‘UET NEWS’', '<p>LAHORE (23rd February 2018) - UET&rsquo;s first ever Web TV &lsquo;UET NEWS&rsquo; was launched on 23rd February at Main Auditorium of the university where a good amount of students&rsquo; participation was witnessed. Renowned artists of the country also attended the event and performed to the large audience. UET NEWS is being run by Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science UET Lahore&rsquo;s lab SMS (School of Media Studies). Vice Chancellor UET Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid, Director KICS UET Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood and other faculty members too attended the launch party. Singer Jawad Ahmad was the chief guest, who delivered a speech as well as performed to the audience.</p>\r\n<p>Talking to the students, Jawad said that we as a nation should be united in order to get progress in life. He also told that struggle and hard work were much important in shaping one&rsquo;s career. Jawad gave the example of USA&rsquo;s previous president Barack Obama.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_18/uet%20news_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Huzair Ahmad, the youngest Microsoft Certified Pakistani student, addressed the audience and let them see his robotics projects.</p>\r\n<p>The team of Kyunkay Jamhoriyat Hai (much popular comedy show on television) amused the audience. The characters of Nawaz Sharif and Asif Zardari were simply adored by the spectators.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Singers &ndash; Mehak Ali and Nadeem Abbas and the group of Qawwals stole the scene with their respective performances.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The ceremony also witnessed three MOUs signed among UET Lahore, local media groups and University of Management Technology. The event concluded with shields&rsquo; distribution. Jawad Ahmad and VC UET Lahore presented the shields to the guests and the passing out students of SMS.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/feb_18/uet%20news_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"563\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-02-23', 1, 1);
INSERT INTO `star_news` (`news_id`, `order`, `news_des`, `news_detail`, `newsthumb`, `news_stamp`, `group_id`, `active`) VALUES
(217, NULL, 'One-Day Workshop Organized on IoT and Future Trends at KICS UET', '<p>LAHORE (23rd February) - A one-day workshop titled &lsquo;IEEE 5G and IoT Summit on Future Trends&rsquo; was organized at Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science. Technology has been emerging quite high and the past two decades have seen massive increase in mobile user data rates.&nbsp; Starting from 2G and ending at 4G, we have evolved from mere 9.6 kbps to a typical of tens of Mbps for urban users. Even with 100Mbps promise of 4G, the communication industry is moving toward 5G, which at least in its definition, targets 100x data rates and 1000x channel capacity than those of 4G. Such spike in 5G technology requires interdisciplinary, multidimensional research with our academia well-aware of the challenges that 5G poses. To create this awareness among Pakistani students and faculty, KICS organized a one-day workshop on 5G. The target audience of the workshop was students who were currently pursuing or planning to pursue their graduate degrees. The speakers of the workshop provided insight into current research dimensions in different layers of 5G.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/March%2018/iot%20collage.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>The workshop attracted wide range of audience comprising industry professionals, students and faculty members representing various universities. Invited Speakers from Academia as well as Industry covered various topics on 5G and IoT, and highlighted the opportunities offered by the two paradigms to solve the various kinds of local problems. They also emphasized the potential barriers and challenges in the successful adaptation of IoT, 4G (LTE Advanced) along with 5G in future within the context of Pakistani Market considering the future requirements of relevant Industries (such as Telco\'s) and their customers. The workshop achieved the objectives such as developing an understanding of the key concepts of 5G and IoT for students and industry participants, and sharing the theoretical and practical knowledge of the two technology paradigms.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/March%2018/iot_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"848\" height=\"564\" /></div>', NULL, '2018-02-23', 16, 1),
(218, NULL, 'Delegation from Seoul National University South Korea Visits UET Lahore', '<p>LAHORE (6th March, 2018) - A delegation from Seoul National University South Korea paid a visit to Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science, University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 6th March. Dr. Kukjin Chun, who is the regional director of IEEE Region 10 Asia and Asia Pacific, represented the university. He was the Keynote Speaker at the event and delivered a comprehensive speech on the topic of &lsquo;The Benefits of IEEE Membership&rsquo;.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/March%2018/collage_001.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Dr. Kukjin Chun also serves as a professor of electrical and computer engineering department at Seoul National University and had been the head of the department during 2009 to 2011. Prior to his job at SNU, Dr Chun was the assistant professor at the electrical engineering department at Washington State University, USA. He holds a PhD degree in electrical engineering from the University of Michigan, USA.</p>\r\n<p>His speech was well-received and admired by the large audience of the students and faculty members who showed their interest in becoming the member of IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers).&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/March%2018/collage_002.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Director Al-Khwarazmi Institute, opened the event and welcomed all the guests. He presented the souvenir and a plaque to Dr. Kukjin Chun. An MOU was also signed between Al-Khawarazmi Institute and Seoul National University to promote research and development activities.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/March%2018/collage_003.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></div>', NULL, '2018-03-06', 2, 1),
(219, NULL, 'Certificates Distribution Ceremony Held at UET Lahore – Top 5 Students Awarded with Free Germany Trip', '<p>LAHORE (1st March, 2018) - Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science UET Lahore organized a certificates&rsquo; distribution ceremony on 1st March held at Chemical Hall of the university. The ceremony was conducted to award the certificates to the passing out students of the third batch of PSDF (Punjab Skill Development Fund) who successfully passed the solar, web designing and development and mobile application courses at the university. 180 successful students were awarded with the certificates.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/March%2018/psdf_collage_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>CEO Pakistan Solar Park Muhammad Amjad, Chairman Pakistan Solar Association Nuaman Khan, Director Solar Tech Colonel Irfan, Industrial Consultant Zahid Hafeez Tosi, Vice Chancellor UET Lahore Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid and Director Al-Khawarazmi Institute Dr. Waqar attended the ceremony.</p>\r\n<p>Talking to the students and the attendees, Dr. Fazal appreciated the efforts of Punjab Government for its support to the university for conducting projects mutually. He emphasized on the skill&rsquo;s importance. Dr. Fazal said that students should focus on the need of technology.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Director Solar Tech said that their organization was all set to endow 2000 schools of Punjab with solar technology very soon. He also offered the internships and jobs to the talented students of this batch.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/March%2018/psdf_collage_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"563\" /></p>\r\n<p>Chairman Pakistan Solar Association announced that he would take 5 top students on board from this batch to send to Germany on his association&rsquo;s expenditures for training. He also mentioned that the company would then sign a two year contract with these students for jobs upon their return to country so that they can serve to Pakistan.</p>\r\n<p>In the end, distinguished guests conferred the students and organizers of the ceremony with certificates. Dr. Waqar Mahmood presented the souvenirs to Vice Chancellor and all the guests.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/March%2018/psdf_collage_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-03-01', 11, 1),
(220, NULL, 'TICK from KICS UET Participates in Momentum – The Largest Startup Conference in Pakistan', '<p>KARACHI (20th February) - The largest startup conference and exhibition even the first ever technology conference was held at Expo Center in Karachi on 19-20 February 2018. It was organized on such a larger scale bringing youth and incubators from 19 cities of the country under one roof. Momentum played an important role as a catalyst in fostering entrepreneurship in Pakistan startups and linking startups with national and international mentors and investors.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/March%2018/momentum_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"473\" /></p>\r\n<p>The event carried more than 300 startups from all over Pakistan who showcased their projects in the exhibition. The speakers were from Pakistan and abroad. 7 startups from TICK (Technology Incubation Center) from KICS UET Lahore participated at the conference and 2 out of them were nominated in the top 20s. TICK&rsquo;s previously incubated startups obtained 3rd position.</p>\r\n<p>The startups gained big exposure and experience at the event.</p>\r\n<div><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/March%2018/momentum_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"473\" /></div>', NULL, '2018-02-20', 15, 1),
(221, NULL, 'FREE Solar Course at UET Lahore', '<p>UET Lahore is offering free course in solar technology.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Course Outline of Solar, Wind and UPS System Assembly</strong></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul style=\"margin-top: 0in;\" type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Solar system designing</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Solar system installation</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Solar system troubleshooting</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Wind Energy</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Batteries</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Installation of UPS</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Entrepreneurship</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>For details of the course and download the application form, click on the below bustton.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<a class=\"btn btn-success\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NfhPCPw17wbdXXyUsNxZ9Ma7HiS-42eZ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Download Form</strong></a></p>\r\n<p><strong><br /></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/March%2018/A3-1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"1191\" /></strong></p>', NULL, '2018-03-21', 11, 1),
(222, 99999, 'PSDF Merit Lists 2018', '<h4>Mobile Application Development | <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/doc/meritlist2018_mobile.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download List</a></h4>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h4>Web Design &amp; Development | <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/doc/meritlist2018_web.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download List</a></h4>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h4>Graphic Design Print Media | <a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/doc/meritlist2018_graphics.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download List</a></h4>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h4>Networking Technologies |&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/documents/psdf_network2018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Download List</a></h4>', NULL, '2018-03-26', 3, 1),
(223, NULL, 'Dr. Sarmad Hussain from KICS UET Awarded with Pride of Performance by Govt. of Pakistan', '<p>LAHORE (27th March 2018) - Professor Dr. Sarmad Hussain from Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science UET Lahore was conferred with President&rsquo;s Award for Pride of Performance for excellence in the field of science (computer) on 23rd March 2018. Dr. Sarmad was awarded for his distinguished contributions in the area of local language computing. The ceremony was held at the residence of Governor of the Punjab where the governor Malik Muhammad Rafique Rajwana bestowed the recipients with the awards. Another ceremony was held at President House in Islamabad where the President of Pakistan Mamnoon Hussain presented the awards to the people from all walks of life for their services to the country.</p>\r\n<p><code><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/xkRGyyP8n98?rel=0\" frameborder=\"0\" width=\"560\" height=\"315\"></iframe></code></p>\r\n<p>A total of 58 military and 73 civil awards were conferred to the people for the excellence in their respective fields for the country.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The ceremonies were attended by the ministers, parliamentarians, diplomats, services chiefs, military officials, high civil officials and people from all walks of life.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/March%2018/23%20March%2018_President%20Awards.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"224\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-03-27', 10, 1),
(224, NULL, 'Governor Punjab Inaugurates Industrial Open House & Career Fair’18 at UET Lahore', '<p>An Industrial Open House and Career Fair 2018 was organized by University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 4th April at University&rsquo;s auditorium. Governor Punjab Malik Muhammad Rafique Rajwana was the chief guest who inaugurated the event. In his address, Rajwana said, &ldquo;Government is taking measures to decrease the unemployment. In this line many projects are functioning to empower the youth with skills, decisions and jobs. Government is making efforts to bring the industry on the track to progress and prosperity effectively in present scenario&rdquo;. The Governor further said, &ldquo;Government is encouraging the entrepreneurship to channelize the determinations for the development of people&rdquo;.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/IOHCF.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"847\" height=\"564\" /></p>\r\n<p>Chairman Pakistan Engineering Council (PEC) Engr. Javed Saleem Qureshi said that PEC was taking measures to empower the engineering and engineers at large. He mentioned that the entrepreneurship policy had been announced to facilitate the engineers in this regard.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Many notable guest speakers such as Nayyar Ali Dada (renowned architecture of Pakistan), Mr. Levin (Director of Huawei), Engineer Mujahid Chatha (CEO LESCO), Deans, UET Chairman and a large number of students were present at the occasion.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/IOHCF_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>Vice-Chancellor Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid said, &ldquo;Industry-Academia linkage can strengthen the country and boost economy. He then also said that doing so the real objective of research and development will be fully accomplished&rdquo;.</p>\r\n<p>He further said that UET was producing quality of skilled persons thus industry should come forward to hunt the talent for the growth. He emphasized the industry to collaborate with university for betterment of economy. By the end of the ceremony, Vice-Chancellor Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid presented crest to Governor Punjab, Malik Muhammad Rafique Rajwana, Nayyar Ali Dada and Javed Saleem Qureshi and other guest of honors.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/IOHCF_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-04-05', 1, 1),
(225, NULL, 'UET Honors Dr. Sarmad Hussain, the Recipient of the Pride of Performance Award', '<p>LAHORE (9th April 2018) - Vice Chancellor UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid arranged a ceremony to honor Dr. Sarmad Hussain (from KICS UET Lahore) who was conferred with the Pride of Performance by the government of Pakistan on 23rd March 2018 on the occasion of Pakistan Resolution Day Celebrations. Dr. Sarmad was bestowed with the most prestigious award of the country for his distinguished contributions in the area of local language computing.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/Dr.%20Sarmad_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor Dr. Fazal and Director KICS Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood appreciated and applauded Dr. Sarmad&rsquo;s efforts for making UET&rsquo;s name protuberant and glorious. In his address, Dr. Sarmad explained his entire journey in language computing up to the receiving of country&rsquo;s biggest award. The attendees of the event very attentively heard and admired his success story. Dr. Sarmad heads Centre for Language Engineering (CLE) at KICS UET Lahore.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/Dr.%20Sarmad_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>At the ceremony held at Vice Chancellor&rsquo;s Office, he was presented with an award for his honor and in recognition of his exceptional efforts in the field of local language computing by Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid in presence of the faculty members, Deans and the staff.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/Dr.%20Sarmad_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"560\" /></div>', NULL, '2018-04-09', 10, 1),
(226, NULL, 'Dr. Waqar Mahmood Talks about Smart Grid at Lahore Garrison University', '<p>National Workshop on Smart Grid 2018 took place in Lahore Garrison University (LGU) on 10th April. The noted speakers attended this event and delivered their speeches on the core subject of &lsquo;Smart Grid&rsquo;. The catchline of the event was &lsquo;empowering engineers for future grids&rsquo;. The ceremony was opened by the Vice Chancellor LGU Major General (R) Obaid Bin Zakria. The entire ceremony consisted of two sessions &ndash; Existing Grid Practices and Basic Introduction to Smart Grid (First) and Challenges, Solution and Related Technologies (Second).&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/lgu_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"563\" /></p>\r\n<p>Dr. Waqar Mahmood, Director KICS UET Lahore, was the guest of honor. He talked on &lsquo;Introduction to Smart Grids&rsquo; in detail. He also revealed KICS&rsquo; projects revolving around smart grid technology. Dr. Waqar then spoke about the power sector problems and its improvements.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/lgu_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>The event featured other speeches as well such as Existing Practices and Challenges (By Director Power Cluster LUMS Mr. Nauman Zafar), Energy Crisis and Remedial Measures (By Dean Faculty EE, UET Dr. Sohail Aftab Qureshi), Short Review of Smart Grids in Schneider Electric and Smart Grid Solutions (By Dr. Bilal Arif from Schneider Electric) and Advanced Metering Infrastructure (Engr. Mr. Sultan).&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The event wrapped up with certificates&rsquo; distributions among the guests of the ceremony.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/lgu_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"420\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-04-17', 1, 1),
(227, NULL, 'KICS Personnel Attends International RF & Microwave Symposium in Islamabad', '<p>An International RF &amp; Microwave Symposium was held at Pearl Continental Hotel, Rawalpindi on 17th April 2018. It was organized by National Instruments Corporation (which is an American multinational company operating all over the world) headquartered in Austin, Texas. The research topics such as 5G Communication (Massive MIMO and mm Wave), Software Define Radio, Radar and Spectrum Monitoring, RF Automated Test and RF Precision Measurement Equipment were covered over there.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>All of these topics are aptly co-related with our telecom technology and research era. The international symposium was fully beneficial for the attendees and for all technical and research aspects.</p>\r\n<p>The keynote speech was on the topic of &ldquo;Leveraging a platform based approach for designing, testing and deploying RF systems&rdquo;. Other topics included &ldquo;Effective Automated Device Validation with NI PXI Software-Defined Platform&rdquo;, &ldquo;Software-Defined Radio &ndash; The Way for Rapid RF System Prototyping&rdquo;, &ldquo;Custom Solutions for Spectrum Monitoring and Signal Intelligence Systems&rdquo;, &ldquo;Real-Time Functional Validation of Modern RF &amp; MW Systems: 5G and FEM to ADAS and RADAR&rdquo; and &ldquo;High Performance MIMI Measurements for Prototyping and Test&rdquo;.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Muhammad Hafiz Tayyab Hashmi, Research Officer KICS UET Lahore, attended this event and is eager to implement these innovative research and technical ideas in HUTIC lab of KICS.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/Tayyab_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"1024\" /></div>', NULL, '2018-04-20', 6, 1),
(228, NULL, 'PUM Netherlands’s Delegation Visits KICS', '<p>Programma Uitzending Managers (PUM) which is Dutch for &lsquo;Manager Deployment Programme&rsquo;. The country coordinator of PUM Mr. Frans visited Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) on 19th April. The visit was specially arranged by TICK (Technology Incubation Center of KICS). Mr. Frans along with his team paid a visit on special invitation by TICK. The delegation visited all the labs at the institute and took eager interest in the functioning at all labs. Director KICS Dr. Waqar Mahmood and Program Manager TICK Frahan Riaz accompanied the delegation.</p>\r\n<p>Mutual collaborative projects between PUM and KICS were also discussed at director&rsquo;s office &ndash; some of them are now in pipeline and will soon be initiated.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>PUM Netherlands is a volunteer organization committed to the sustainable development of small and medium-sized enterprises in developing countries and emerging markets. Practical expertise within the most important sectors of the economy is offered at PUM.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/pums_netherlands.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"563\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-04-23', 15, 1),
(229, NULL, 'ESUPAK-KICS UET and Reconciliation Department of Punjab Government Ink Agreement', '<p>KICS UET Lahore and Reconciliation Department of Government of Punjab have signed an agreement for the validation of the project of AMR meters&rsquo; assessment. Punjab government has established reconciliation of energy billing cell in order to monitor and reconcile the electricity billing disputes and for this 1698 AMR meters (check meters) have been installed. These meters have been procured and installed as per WAPDA/NTDC approved specifications with the main objective of monitoring and reconciling the billing issues with concerned DISCOs of the Punjab.</p>\r\n<p>For the validation of the project and its execution appropriately and fully, a third party consultancy form has been hired. ESUPAK (Engineering Services UET Pakistan) KICS have been hired as a consultancy firm. The contract signing ceremony was held on 18th April 2018 where Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood and Imran Ali Shah (Manager AIRL Lab KICS) were present from KICS UET &lsquo;s side and Director Technical Reconciliation Muhammad Rahat Khan along with Deputy Director Reconciliation Aziz Muhammad Mazari were there from Reconciliation Department.</p>\r\n<p>Both directors &ndash; Dr. Waqar Mahmood and Muhammad Rahat Khan signed the agreement.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/KICS%20Sign%20with%20Reconciliation%20Dept%20(2).jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"843\" height=\"531\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-04-23', 11, 1),
(230, NULL, 'ESUPAK-KICS UET and Reconciliation Department of Punjab Government Ink Agreement', '<p>KICS UET Lahore and Reconciliation Department of Government of Punjab have signed an agreement for the validation of the project of AMR meters&rsquo; assessment. Punjab government has established reconciliation of energy billing cell in order to monitor and reconcile the electricity billing disputes and for this 1698 AMR meters (check meters) have been installed. These meters have been procured and installed as per WAPDA/NTDC approved specifications with the main objective of monitoring and reconciling the billing issues with concerned DISCOs of the Punjab.</p>\r\n<p>For the validation of the project and its execution appropriately and fully, a third party consultancy form has been hired. ESUPAK (Engineering Services UET Pakistan) KICS have been hired as a consultancy firm. The contract signing ceremony was held on 18th April 2018 where Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood and Imran Ali Shah (Manager AIRL Lab KICS) were present from KICS UET &lsquo;s side and Director Technical Reconciliation Muhammad Rahat Khan along with Deputy Director Reconciliation Aziz Muhammad Mazari were there from Reconciliation Department.</p>\r\n<p>Both directors &ndash; Dr. Waqar Mahmood and Muhammad Rahat Khan signed the agreement.</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-04-23', 25, 1),
(231, NULL, 'UCP Gujrat Campus Visits Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science, UET Lahore ', '<p>A delegation from University of Central Punjab&rsquo;s Gujrat Campus visited Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science on 27th April 2018. A vast majority of the students along with officials and professors were included in the delegation. Director KICS Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood and Kashif Bashir (Manager HUTIC, KICS) welcomed the guests.&nbsp; A seminar was arranged for them where Mr. Kashif Bashir delivered a presentation about KICS and its lab along with the details of the researches being done at the institute.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/ucp_001.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>The delegation was then taken to visit the labs. They took deep interest in the functioning. The students and their officials were briefed about the research projects. They were also informed about the trainings and the technical as well as IT and solar courses being carried on.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/april%2018/ucp_gujrat_05.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"632\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-04-27', 6, 1),
(232, NULL, 'PEECA in Collaboration with KICS UET Organizes 3-Day Workshop on Energy Efficiency and Conservation Tools 2018', '<p>PEECA (Punjab Energy Efficiency and Conservation Agency) &ndash; the energy department of government of the Punjab in collaboration with Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science UET Lahore organized a &lsquo;Workshop on Energy Efficiency and Conservation Tools 2018&rsquo; which was held at UET Lahore on 3rd May. The workshop will last for 3 days till 5th May. The opening ceremony was conducted at the main auditorium of the university where officials from the energy department of the Punjab along with university administration and faculty members came to attend it.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%2018/peeca_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>The workshop was attended by both officials and students in large number. Director Al-Kharawazmi Institute of Computer Science (KICS) &amp; Centre for Energy Research and Development (CERAD) delivered a welcome note to the participants. In his speech, he talked about energy efficiency and its importance and PEECA&rsquo;s role in energy management and energy efficiency.&nbsp; He also revealed UET&rsquo;s efforts in launching the energy center &lsquo;CERAD&rsquo; at UET&rsquo;s Kala Shah Kako Campus where MSc in Energy Engineering and a number of training and certificate courses in energy efficiency are being done. He then added that professional trainings on energy efficiency and conservation were being done in collaboration with GIZ Germany.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Talking to the attendees, Ms. Sadia from PEECA said that we were on energy crisis nonetheless we happened to be the nation who kept wasting energy. She also mentioned that PEECA was on way to launch the testing labs to establish on air-conditioner. PEECA official then revealed the projects done in various government universities and colleges on energy conservation.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%2018/peeca_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"563\" /></p>\r\n<p>The workshop witnessed a number of talks on the subject of &lsquo;energy efficiency and conservation&rsquo;. The topics like &lsquo;Flue Gas &amp; Combustion Analysis&rsquo;, &lsquo;HottCad Generoth Software&rsquo; and &lsquo;Opportunities in Domestic, Commercial and Industrial Sector for Energy Efficiency&rsquo;.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>By the end of the day, the speakers were conferred with the shields.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%2018/peeca_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-05-04', 21, 1),
(233, NULL, 'KICS UET Participates in CISCO Networking Academy Conference in Islamabad', '<p>CISCO Networking Academy Conference for Pakistan was held at COMSATS University, Chuk Shahzad in Islamabad on 29th April, 2018. It was conducted for the NetAcad Community in Islamabad, Punjab and KP. From KICS UET Lahore, Rafique Sultan (Research Officer) attended it. The one-day conference was organized mainly for the academy instructors but was equally beneficial for new academies and researchers. It endowed the participants with the updates in CISCO programs and courses.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The conference provided a big opportunity to all the attendees to interact with CISCO&rsquo;s top instructors in Pakistan. The participants also learnt about the new emerging technologies, programming &amp; CCNA CyberOps courses and various other interesting topics.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The main topics shared at the conference included:&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;NetAcad Evolution &amp; Technical Update</p>\r\n<p>&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Vouchers and Certifications</p>\r\n<p>&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Basics of Python,</p>\r\n<p>&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Integration Models</p>\r\n<p>&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;NetAcad in Pakistan Challenges and Opportunities</p>\r\n<p>&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Network Programmability for CCNA</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%2018/cisco_conference.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></div>', NULL, '2018-05-07', 6, 1),
(234, NULL, 'A Delegation from ODEM Switzerland Visits KICS UET and Signs MOU', '<p>A delegation from ODEM SA Switzerland was invited by ESESS (Embedded Systems &amp; Enterprise Software Solutions) Lab at KICS UET Lahore on 25th April, 2018. It was headed by Richard Maaghul (CEO ODEM). They visited all labs at the institute and took eager interest at the functioning being done in each lab. Both Dr. Zubair A. Khan and Jamshed Iqbal Janjua (Sr. Manager Research) accompanied them. The two sides &ndash; KICS UET and ODEM also discussed mutual collaborative projects.</p>\r\n<p>An MOU was also signed by the authorities from both sides for joint collaboration in Development, Research and Training Operatives through ESESS Lab.</p>\r\n<p>The delegation consisted of Richard Maaghul (CEO ODEM), Ken Finch (Director of Global Sales, ODEM) and Alexa Narma (Senior Director, Product and Marketing).&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%2018/swiss_delegation.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>', NULL, '2018-04-30', 2, 1),
(235, NULL, 'UET Lahore Conducts Certificate Distribution Ceremony for Graduating Students of PSDF', '<p>A certificate distribution ceremony was held at University of Engineering and Technology Lahore on 10th May, 2018 where the where the successful students of PSDF (Punjab Skills Development Fund) were awarded with the certificates. Punjab Skills Development Fund in collaboration with Al-Khawarazmi Institute of Computer Science has been offering the professional training courses at UET Lahore in various fields such as Web Development, Graphic Designing, Solar and to name a few. Recently graduating students were conferred with the distinctions in form of certificates. A large amount of students along with faculty members attended the ceremony.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%2018/psdf_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"563\" /></p>\r\n<p>The guests&rsquo; list included delegations from various fields such as Jordan Fast (Crown Agents, UK), Abdul Waheed (General Manager, PTCL), Moosa Nadeem Siddique (Director Accounts, Huawei Technologies) and Ayesha Zaman Hammad (Entrepreneurship Center, PITB).&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>In his address, Vice Chancellor UET Lahore, Prof. Dr. Fazal Ahmad Khalid emphasized on the importance of technology in today&rsquo;s world. He also appreciated the efforts made by PSDF and government of the Punjab in boosting up the technological advancements in the province of Punjab. Dr. Fazal then talked about the MOUs signed with Punjab government.</p>\r\n<p>The honorable guests in their respective addresses to the audience emphasized on the advancements in the field of technology and asked the students to tread along with.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%2018/psdf_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<p>Prof. Dr. Waqar Mahmood (Director Al-Khawarzami Institute of Computer Science) told the audience about the projects being run in collaboration with PSDF.</p>\r\n<p>Vice Chancellor and the honorable guests presented the certificates to the successful students. The organizers of the event were also conferred with the shields. Dr. Fazal then presented the souvenirs to the guests.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%2018/PRO_0763.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%2018/psdf_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"840\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-05-10', 11, 1),
(236, NULL, 'IEEE COMSOC Lahore Chapter Celebrates World Telecom Day 2018 in Pakistan', '<p>IEEE ComSoc Lahore chapter, KICS UET Lahore, IEEE Punjab University student branch organized World Telecom day on 16th May 2018. The event was held at Seminar Hall Faculty of Engineering and Technology, University of Punjab, attended by many high officials and the experts from academia and industry. Mr. Kashif Bashir, Chair IEEE ComSoc Lahore chapter, Prof. Dr. Taqi Zahid Butt Dean&nbsp; Faculty of Engineering and Technology University of Punjab, Dr. Amjad Hussain Chair&nbsp; IEEE Lahore Section, Dr. Vincenzo Piuri, Professor at the University of Milan, Italy, Dr. Bhawani Shankar former chair IEEE Karachi Section, Dr. Momin Uppal Lahore University of Management Sciences (LUMS) Lahore, Dr. Syed Atif Mehdi from University of Central Punjab (UCP) Lahore, Mr. Hassan Ali Senior Manager Mobilink Pakistan, Muhammad Javed Aslam Executive Vice President Technical Pakistan Telecommunication Company Limited (PTCL), Dr. Sheikh Faisal KICS, UET Lahore, Mr. Moosa Nadeem, Director Huawei Technologies Pakistan, Mr. Jawad Khalid Mirza Divisional Head Information Security &amp; Governance Allied Bank Pakistan and Dr. Ubaid Ullah Fayyaz from KICS, UET Lahore, were among the speakers.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%2018/wtd_01.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>The purpose of WTD was to highlight the importance of communication in our lives. Theme of this day was &ldquo;Enabling the positive use of Artificial Intelligence for all&rdquo;. The event began with a video message by Prof. Dr. Vincenzo Piuri, Who is a full Professor at the University of Milan, Italy. He emphasized the importance of telecommunication in today&rsquo;s world. He also talked about how we can serve humanity through better ICT technology. He thanked the organizers for conducting the World Telecom Day 2018.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Prof. Dr. Bhawani Shankar former chair IEEE Karachi Section in his video message talked about the achievements of IEEE COMSOC Lahore Chapter. He talked about the history and importance of telecommunication day.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Prof. Dr. Taqi Zahid Butt, Dean Faculty of Engineering and Technology, University of the Punjab uttered about the history of telecom and advancement in the telecommunication field. He shared his interesting and valuable personal experiences about the revolution of the mobile technology and Telecommunication industry.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Kashif Bashir explain the history of world telecom day and showed the glimpses of last year event of through a video. He also talked about COMSOC Lahore Chapter working. How world telecom day is helping the industry and academia. He also talked about the artificial intelligence and its significance in our future.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Dr. Momin Uppal from LUMS talked about: Use of artificial intelligence and Machine learning in wireless network, Internet of Things, Mobile edge caching and computing, UAVs for wireless communication.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Dr. Syed Atif Mehdi from University of Central Punjab spoke about use of Robotics in Agriculture, he talked about the detection of fungus through Artificially Intelligent Robots, and he also spoke about Progressive farmers. He share his work on agro robotics and use of drones for agriculture.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Eng. Hassan Ali from Mobilink Pakistan talked about ARPU (Average revenue per person) concepts being practiced in Mobilink. He also shared the plans of his companies for the implementation of 5G.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Muhammad Javed Aslam Executive Vice President Technical PTCL, explained how PTCL is working on artificial intelligence with smart features, and future of PTCL in Pakistan. He also share the long history of his company. He encourage students to study and do research in telecommunication, big data and artificial intelligence.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%2018/wtd_02.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"840\" height=\"560\" /></p>\r\n<p>Dr. Shiekh Faisal from KICS UET Lahore talked about Machine learning, Big data analytics, native language processing, tools for machine learning, traditional vs. big data, big data vendors, data analytics and how artificial intelligence meets IoT.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Moosa Nadeem from Huawei gave the brief introduction about Huawei and talked about historical milestones of Huawei in Pakistan. He also talked about the vision and Mission of the company. He shares about artificial intelligence technologies used in the Lahore safe City project.</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Jawad Khalid Mirza talked about importance of Cyber Security, Machine learning and Artificial Intelligence in banking sector of Pakistan.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Dr. Amjad Hussain Chair IEEE Lahore Section gave keynote of the event. He shares his personal experience about the evolution of communication.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Dr. Ubaid Ullah Fayyaz from KICS-UET gave the closing note.&nbsp; He also thanked all guests and member of IEEE Society who attended this event.</p>\r\n<p>A post panel discussion followed in which the distinguished Speaker discussed their views on the impact of telecommunication day. The event concluded with souvenirs&rsquo; and lapel pin distribution by the Chair of IEEE Comsoc Lahore chapter. A celebration cake was also cut. Group photo was taken at the end.</p>\r\n<p><img style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" src=\"http://www.kics.edu.pk/gallery/news/May%2018/wtd_03.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"845\" height=\"563\" /></p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>', NULL, '2018-05-29', 6, 1);
